#. ~ Description of furniture "chicory"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A blue flower imported from Europe, also known as a cornflower."
msgstr "一种从欧洲进口的蓝色花，也称为矢车菊。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "tulip"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A bright, colorful flower with petals forming a small cup at its top.  It can be poisonous to livestock."
msgstr "一种鲜艳的花，花瓣在顶部形成一个小杯子。对牲畜有毒。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "bluebell"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A common bluebell flower.  Pretty."
msgstr "一种常见的蓝铃花。很漂亮。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "burdock"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A common weed with a purple thistle-like flower.  Its seeds tend to stick to clothing and fur."
msgstr "一种开紫花的普通杂草。种子通过附着在衣物和毛皮上传播。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "dandelion"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A common weed with a yellow flower.  Produces seeds that get carried on the wind by thin, gray filaments."
msgstr "一种开黄花的普通杂草。种子通过灰色细丝在风中传播。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wild carrot"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A common white wildflower which could be harvested for its root."
msgstr "一株普通的白色野花，可收获胡萝卜根茎。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "chamomile"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A cute white flower with a yellow center, used to brew a soothing tea."
msgstr "一种可爱的白色花朵，中间是黄色的，可用来泡制舒缓茶。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "dam"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/misc.json
msgid "A house that beavers built.  The entrance is underwater making it harder for predators to access."
msgstr "一座河狸建造的房子。入口处在水下，捕食者更难进入。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "lotus"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A lovely flower that grows on the surface of bodies of fresh water.  A traditional symbol of many Eastern cultures."
msgstr "一种生长在淡水体表面的可爱的花。传统上与许多东方文化相联系。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "black eyed Susan"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A mildly poisonous yellow flower with a dark ball in the middle.  Sometimes known as an ox-eye daisy."
msgstr "一种带有轻微毒性的中间有暗球的黄色花朵。有时被称为牛眼雏菊。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "lily"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A pretty flower that comes in a variety of colors."
msgstr "一种漂亮的花，有多种颜色。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "datura"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A pretty moonflower."
msgstr "一朵美丽的月光花。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "purple loosestrife"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A pretty violet flower that likes water.  Unfortunately it is invasive and does not benefit the environment."
msgstr "有着美丽的紫色花朵，喜湿，不幸的是，它是一种入侵植物。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "thistle"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A prickly and invasive small plant."
msgstr "一种有着很多小刺的入侵植物。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "dahlia"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A puffy flower with many tightly-layered petals."
msgstr "一种有许多紧密分层的花瓣的蓬松的花。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "animal topiary"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A shrub with small green leaves, trimmed into a dragon shape."
msgstr "一丛高大的灌木，长着许多小绿叶，被修剪成龙的形状。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "abstract topiary"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A shrub with small green leaves, trimmed into a fanciful abstract shape."
msgstr "一丛高大的灌木，长着许多小绿叶，被修剪成奇特的抽象画的形状。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "short hedge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A shrub with small green leaves, trimmed into a squared shape."
msgstr "一丛高大的绿色灌木，被修剪成正方形。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "animal topiary"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A shrub with small green leaves, trimmed into an animal shape."
msgstr "一丛高大的灌木，长着许多小绿叶，被修剪成动物的形状。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "pile of leaves"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A sizable pile of leaves.  You could sleep on it if you don't care about comfort or warmth."
msgstr "一大堆树叶，如果你不在乎舒适和温暖，你可以睡在上面。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "common selfheal"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A small purple flower.  It got its name due to its usage in traditional medicine."
msgstr "有着紫色的小花，在世界各国的传统草药中都有应用。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wintergreen"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A small shrub native to North America.  The leaves, which remain green even in winter, are valued for medicinal purposes.  It produces edible and sweet berries, too!"
msgstr "原产于北美的一种小灌木。这些叶子即使在冬天也保持绿色，具有药用价值。它也生长可食用的甜浆果！"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wild sarsaparilla"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A small, flowering plant known as 'Aralia nudicaulis'.  It is colored in vibrant shades of orange and red in autumn, making it easy to spot."
msgstr "一种小型开花植物，学名为\"裸茎楤木\"。它在秋天会变成鲜艳的橙色和红色，很容易分辨。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "tall hedge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A tall shrub with small green leaves, trimmed into a squared shape."
msgstr "一丛高大的绿色灌木，被修剪成正方形。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "sunflower"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A tall, wide-headed flower with a large dark center.  Produces many nutritious seeds."
msgstr "一种高而宽的花，中心大而黑。产生许多营养丰富的种子。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "mustard"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A yellow flower known as Brassica Nigra.  Known for its seeds that can be used for making table mustard."
msgstr "一种黄色的花，属于十字花科芸苔属植物。它的种子可以用来做芥末。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "spurge flower"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "A yellow-green flower that grows in densely-packed bushes."
msgstr "一种黄绿色的花，生长在浓密的灌木丛中。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "wild rice"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "Also called Indian rice, Northern wild rice, or manoomin in Ojibwe, is a species of rice that has been harvested and used by Native American tribes of the northeast for hundreds of years.  It's similar to other types of wild rice, offering a fiber-rich and healthy basis of a meal."
msgstr "也被称为印第安稻、北美野生稻。奥吉布瓦美洲原住民称其为Manoomin，意为\"最好的果实\"。是一种被东北部美洲原住民部落种植并食用了数百年的水稻。它与其他类型的野生稻相似，为一顿饭提供了富含纤维且健康的主食。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "Japanese knotweed"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "An invasive species originating from Japan.  The stem looks like it might contain some water."
msgstr "原产于日本的入侵物种。根茎看起来含有些水分。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "spreading dogbane"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "It is not only toxic to dogs when eaten by them.  Humans and many other animals are affected, too.  Its fibers sure are worth salvaging though.  Despite its name, it is not actually spreading fast."
msgstr "对狗有剧毒，对人和其他动物也会有一定影响。不过，它的纤维耐磨耐拉，有着很大的用处。"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "Japanese knotweed"
msgstr "日本虎杖"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "Jerusalem artichoke plant"
msgstr "洋姜"

#. ~ Description of furniture "Jerusalem artichoke plant"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "Looking similar to a sunflower, this tall plant has a nutritious tuber."
msgstr "这株高大的植物长得很像向日葵，根茎很有营养。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "poppy flower"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "Papaver somniferum, also known as the opium poppy.  These harmless-looking flowers were once widely cultivated for decorative purposes, but in summer their heads may be harvested and used in the production of a highly addictive painkiller."
msgstr "罂粟，也就是鸦片罂粟。这些看似无害的花朵曾广泛作为观赏植物种植，但到了夏季，它们的蒴果可以被采集，并用于生产一种极易上瘾的止痛药。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "starry false Solomon's seal"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "The blossoms of this flower look like stars in the night sky.  Its crimson berries are edible."
msgstr "这株植物的花朵看起来像夜空中的星星。其深红色浆果可食用。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "lilypad"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "This lilypad doesn't look like it would support the weight of the things you've heard croaking in the swamp."
msgstr "这个睡莲看起来承受不了你在沼泽里听到的发出呱呱声音的动物的重量。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "dead plant"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "This plant has joined the billions lost in the Cataclysm, and is now little more than a dry stalk."
msgstr "这株植物已经与在灾难中丧生的无数生物一同消逝了，如今它只剩下一根干枯的茎秆了。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "cattails"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "This useful plant is available all year round.  Many parts of the plant are edible."
msgstr "这种有用的植物一年到头都有。它的许多部分是可食用的。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "salsify"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "Tragopogon porrifolius, a ragged-looking purple flower with a nutritious root."
msgstr "蒜叶婆罗门参，一种看起来参差不齐的紫色鲜花，根茎营养丰富。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "fireweed"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "Vibrant purple, it tends to be the first to appear after fires, hence its name."
msgstr "有着紫红色的花，因为常出现于火烧后的地面，因此也叫火草（Fireweed）"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "abstract topiary"
msgstr "抽象树雕"

#. ~ Furniture name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
msgid "animal topiary"
msgstr "动物树雕"

