#. ~ Description of furniture "green algae"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
msgid "A short patch of grassy green seaweed, wholly unremarkable."
msgstr "一小堆原木，不易通过。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "sugar kelp"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
msgid "Also known as kombu, this brown algae grows in a single leaflike blade that can reach more than twice the height of a man.  Young fronds make for excellent soup stock and can even be eaten raw."
msgstr "这种被称为“昆布”的褐色海藻，其生长形态为单片叶状的叶片，其高度可超过一个人的两倍。幼嫩的叶状体非常适合用来熬制汤底，甚至可以直接生吃。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "sea sponge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
msgid "An immobile, lumpy little creature that looks nothing like a square kitchen sponge.  Anchored to the sea floor, its porous body passively filters plankton from the water that freely passes through it."
msgstr "这是一种静止不动、形状不规则的小生物，与常见的方形厨房海绵完全不一样。它固定在海底，其多孔的身体会主动过滤水中的浮游生物，而水则可以自由地穿过它。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "bladderwrack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
msgid "Named for the air bladders that grow all over its leafy fronds, this leafy seaweed is technically edible and has a long history of use in folk medicine."
msgstr "这种带叶的海藻因其叶片上遍布的气囊而得名。从技术层面上讲，这种海藻是可以食用的，并且在民间医学中有着悠久的应用历史。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "red algae"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
msgid "One of the thousands of species of grassy reddish marine plants that inhabit intertidal zones the world over.  Its rubbery little fronds don't look particularly edible."
msgstr "这是全球各地潮间带环境中数以千计的草质红褐色海洋植物中的一种。它的柔软小叶看起来并不特别适合食用。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "sea lettuce"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
msgid "Sometimes known as green laver, this leafy algae from the Ulva genus grows in leafy little patches around shallows and tide pools.  Though small, it makes a tasty snack."
msgstr "这种藻类有时也被称为“青海苔”，属于石莼属。它们成片生长在浅滩和潮池周围。虽然个头不大，但吃起来却是一道美味的零食。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "sea anemone"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
msgid "This sessile polyp waves its stinging tentacles with the motion of the tides, hoping to capture a tiny fish or crab.  It's wholly inedible and poses no danger to anything bigger than a shrimp."
msgstr "这种固着生活的珊瑚虫随着潮汐的起伏摆动其带刺的触手，希望能捕获小鱼或螃蟹。它完全不可食用，对于比虾大的生物都没有威胁。"

