#. ~ Description of furniture "closed counter gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A commercial-quality swinging door made of wood that allows passage behind counters.  It's currently closed."
msgstr "一扇商用等级的弹簧门，用木头制成，让人能进出柜台后面。它是关着的。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "open counter gate"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A commercial-quality swinging door made of wood that allows passage behind counters.  It's open, allowing passage."
msgstr "一扇商用等级的弹簧门，用木头制成，让人能进出柜台后面。他是开着的，可以通过。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "fancy table"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A fancy table for a fancy person.  Functions as both a table and status symbol."
msgstr "一款专为高雅人士设计的精美餐桌。它既可用作餐桌，又可作为彰显身份地位的象征。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "fiber mat"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A large mat woven from fibrous material.  You could use it as a picnic blanket, but it's more valuable as a surface for butchering.  Too thin to be used as a comfortable sleeping mat."
msgstr "一块由纤维材料编织而成的大垫子。你可以把它当野餐毯使用，但用作屠宰的地方更有价值。因为太薄不能作为舒适的睡眠场所。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "tarp"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A large plastic tarpaulin lying on the ground.  It could be a clean place to sit, or a crude but useful surface for crafting or butchery."
msgstr "一大块放在地上的厚塑料垫，也许是个屠宰的好地方。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "leather tarp"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A large sheet of leather lying on the ground.  You could use it as a picnic blanket, but it's more valuable as a surface for butchering as it does not soak up blood."
msgstr "一大块放在地上的皮革，可以用来代替野餐毯子，但用作屠宰的地方更有价值，因为它不会渗血。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "rubber groundsheet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A large sheet of rubberized cloth lying on the ground.  It could be a clean place to sit, or a crude but useful surface for crafting or butchery."
msgstr "一大块放在地上的厚塑料垫，也许是个屠宰的好地方。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "plastic groundsheet"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A large sheet of thick plastic lying on the ground.  It could be a clean place to sit, or a crude but useful surface for crafting or butchery."
msgstr "一大块放在地上的厚塑料垫，也许是个屠宰的好地方。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "coffee table"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A low table usually found in living rooms, it makes an ideal surface for playing games, showing off some tasteful books, or presumably for putting coffee cups on.  No one cares if you use a coaster anymore."
msgstr "一张通常放在客厅里的矮桌子，是个玩游戏、展示高雅书籍或放咖啡杯的理想地方。没有人在乎你是否再使用杯垫了。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "counter"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A plain wooden countertop, either free-standing or affixed to a wall.  Makes a decent surface for storage or crafting."
msgstr "一个普通的木制柜台，可以独立放置，也可以固定在墙上。为储物和制作提供了一个不错的平面。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "metal table"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A serviceable but simple table made of scrap metal."
msgstr "一张用金属废料制成的既实用又简单的桌子。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "folding table"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A small metal folding table, ideal for off-road trips.  Can be used as a workbench in a pinch."
msgstr "一个小型金属可折叠餐桌，适合野外郊游时使用。紧急情况下可以当作工作台。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "table"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A standard wooden table.  You could sit down at it to eat like a civilized person."
msgstr "一张标准的木桌。你可以像个文明人一样坐下来吃饭。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "workbench"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A sturdy workbench built out of metal.  It is perfect for crafting large and heavy things."
msgstr "一个用金属制成的坚固的工作台。它非常适合用来制造巨大而沉重的物品。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "desk"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "A wooden desk with drawers.  You could decorate it with trinkets, eat a meal off it, use it as a workbench, read a book, write in a journal, put a laptop on it, put your feet up, rest your head for a nap if you're sitting down… who knew desks were so useful?"
msgstr "一个带有抽屉的木桌。你可以用小饰品装饰它，用它吃顿饭，把它当作工作台，看书，写日记，放一台笔记本电脑，用来架脚，如果你坐着的话可以在上面趴一会儿……桌子是如此的有用。"

#. ~ Description of furniture "cupboard"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
msgid "Store your cups.  Or other things, if you're feeling wild."
msgstr "用于存放你的杯子。如果你感觉可以，也能存别的东西。"

