#. ~ Description of terrain "closed ballistic glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A ballistic glass door, consisting of layers of laminated glass."
msgstr "一扇由多层玻璃制成的防弹玻璃门。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open ballistic glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A ballistic glass door, consisting of layers of laminated glass.  It's open."
msgstr "一扇由多层玻璃制成的防弹玻璃门。它是开着的。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged reinforced door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A battered and torn reinforced door with planks bursting from the joints.  The boarded up planks are fragmented and in pieces, this doesn't look like an easy repair."
msgstr "一扇破破烂烂的强化门，门缝处的木板都裂开了。门上的木板已经支离破碎，看起来很难修理。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A boarded up door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  Although it's been covered up in planks, you could still look through the peephole if you were close enough."
msgstr "一扇用木板封住的木门，不过有个窥视孔。虽然安上了许多木板，如果你仔细检查，仍然可以透过孔窥视。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A boarded up wooden door, except that some of the planks are fractured or coming loose.  Without repairs, it could be broken down easily."
msgstr "一扇用木板封住的木门，但大部分木板已经折断或松动了，如果不修理的话，会很快损坏。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed laminated glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A closed door made of laminated safety glass.  It's a lot tougher than regular glass, and is designed to break into fragments that are nowhere near as sharp."
msgstr "一扇由夹层安全玻璃制成的闭合门。这种玻璃比普通玻璃坚固得多，设计成破碎时产生的碎片锋利度远低于普通玻璃。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open bar door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  It's wide open.  Freedom!"
msgstr "由相互交叉的不锈钢棒所组成的牢房门。这扇门现在敞开着。终于自由了！"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bar door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  The locking mechanism appears to be engaged.  You could pick it open with enough skill."
msgstr "由相互交叉的不锈钢棒所组成的牢房门。看上去似乎已经锁上了。你可以使用开锁工具尝试开锁。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bar door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  The locking mechanism doesn't appear to be engaged."
msgstr "由相互交叉的不锈钢棒所组成的牢房门。看上去似乎并没有上锁。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open laminated glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A door made of laminated safety glass.  It's a lot tougher than regular glass, and is designed to break into fragments that are nowhere near as sharp.  It's open."
msgstr "一扇由夹层安全玻璃制成的门。这种玻璃比普通玻璃坚固得多，设计成破碎时产生的碎片远没有普通玻璃锋利。门是开着的。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A faux concrete wall positioned and joined seamlessly with the wall, this wall is capable of resisting extreme elements as well as hostile forces.  Blast load rated and extremely fire-retardant, breaching it will require specialized tools or an industrial vehicle."
msgstr "经过精心定位并以边缘密封胶无缝连接的人造混凝土墙，能抵抗极端气候与敌对力量。具备极优的爆炸负荷和抗燃性，想突破它需要专用工具或工业用载具。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A galvanized steel door, forged to withstand punishment and impede anyone or anything.  Typically used in conjunction with automated electronic locking mechanisms that require an external source to unlock."
msgstr "一扇锻造精良的镀锌钢门，坚固耐用，能阻挡任何人或事物。通常会与可远程控制的各类自动电子锁定装置一起安装。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open makeshift door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A makeshift screen consisting of planks bound together with rope, hanging from the top of the doorway.  Could be easily taken down and re-purposed.  The planks have been rolled up and attached to the top of the doorway, allowing free movement through."
msgstr "一扇用绳索将木板捆绑拼凑而成的简易门，有着几条垂直绳索将其固定在门框顶部。可以很轻松地将它拆除获得材料，或者拆下来安装在别处。这扇简易门的木板卷成一团用绳子吊在门框上。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed makeshift door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A makeshift screen consisting of planks bound together with rope, hanging vertically from the top of the doorway.  Could be easily taken down and re-purposed."
msgstr "一扇用绳索将木板捆绑拼凑而成的简易门，有着几条垂直绳索将其固定在门框顶部。可以很轻松地将它拆除获得材料，或者拆下来安装在别处。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole."
msgstr "一扇由常规木头制成的普通木门，不过有个窥视孔。如果你仔细检查，就可以透过孔窥视。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open wood door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  No need right now though, since the door is open anyway."
msgstr "一扇由常规木头制成的普通门，不过有个窥视孔。如果你仔细检查，就可以透过孔窥视。现在门已经打开，不需要窥视了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  This one has a deadbolt keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You could pry it open or pick the lock, or unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr "一扇由常规木头制成的普通门，不过有个窥视孔。如果你仔细检查，就可以透过孔窥视。上面有个门栓，应该是被锁上了。你可以用撬棍撬开这扇门，或者使用开锁工具尝试开锁，也可以从内侧将门栓打开。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  This one has a deadbolt numpad, so it's likely locked.  You could pry it open, guessing the code is out of the question, or unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr "一扇由常规木头制成的普通门，不过有个窥视孔。如果你仔细检查，就可以透过孔窥视。上面有个数字键盘，应该是被锁上了。你可以用撬棍撬开这扇门，但猜它的密码是不可能的，也可以从内侧将门栓打开。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed frosted glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A sliding door of frosted white glass."
msgstr "一扇乳白色的毛玻璃推拉门。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open glass door"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open frosted glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A sliding glass door that has been left open for all manner of things to travel through."
msgstr "一扇滑动玻璃门，它已经打开了，什么东西都可以通过。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed glass door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A sliding glass door, clear enough that an animal or a particularly dumb person could slam right into it.  This one is closed, so don't hurt yourself."
msgstr "一扇滑动玻璃门，清晰得足以让动物或特别愚蠢的人直接撞上去。 它是关着的，别伤了自己。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn easily, too."
msgstr "一扇看起来不太坚固的普通木门。多半也很易燃。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door with an electronic lock"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn easily, too.  This one has a deadbolt electronic lock, so it's likely locked.  You could pry it open, guessing the code is out of the question, or unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr "一扇看起来不太坚固的普通木门。多半也很易燃。上面有个电子锁，应该是被锁上了。你可以用撬棍撬开这扇门，但猜它的密码是不可能的，也可以从内侧将门栓打开。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn easily, too.  This one has a deadbolt keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You could pry it open or pick the lock, or unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr "一扇看起来不太坚固的普通木门。多半也很易燃。上面有个门栓，应该是被锁上了。你可以用撬棍撬开这扇门，或者使用开锁工具尝试开锁，也可以从内侧将门栓打开。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn easily, too.  This one has an electronic keypad, so it's likely locked.  You could pry it open, guessing the code is out of the question."
msgstr "一扇看起来不太坚固的普通木门。多半也很易燃。上面有个电子键盘，应该是被锁上了。你可以用撬棍撬开这扇门，但猜它的密码是不可能的，也可以从内侧将门栓打开。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn easily, too.  This one has an extra keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You could pry it open or pick the lock."
msgstr "一扇看起来不太坚固的普通木门。多半也很易燃。上面有个锁孔，应该是被锁上了。你可以用撬棍撬开这扇门，或者使用开锁工具尝试开锁。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn easily, too.  This one is wide open."
msgstr "一扇看起来不太坚固的普通木门。多半也很易燃。多半也很易燃。这是敞开的。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A standard wooden door that has several planks across it, nailed down to board it up and increase its durability.  It's still flammable, though."
msgstr "一扇标准的木门，有几块木板横穿而过，并钉牢在门框上，以增加其耐久。不过这门还是可燃的。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed corrugated metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A thin door made of corrugated steel held in a frame."
msgstr "一扇用波纹钢板制成的薄门，固定在门框内。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open corrugated metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A thin door made of corrugated steel held in a frame.  It's open, so no tools are needed to break in."
msgstr "一扇用波纹钢板制成的薄门，固定在门框内。这扇门开着，可以自由出入。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A trashed wooden door, with a large hole in the middle that you can see right through.  The doorknob is so messed up that it can't be opened anymore.  It could be fixed up with a few planks."
msgstr "一扇破旧的木门，中间有一个大洞，你可以看穿它。门把手坏得打不开了。它可以用几块木板固定起来。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "A wrecked door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole and some partly-splintered boards nailed across it.  The peephole is damaged and can't be used to see through."
msgstr "一扇由常规木头制成的普通木门，不过有个窥视孔。门上的木板大部分已经损坏了，上面的窥视孔也无法使用了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up reinforced door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "An additionally reinforced door of layered planks that has been boarded up with more wood to prevent it from opening.  It's still susceptible to fire."
msgstr "一扇用多层木板强化的门，并用更多的木板封住以防止它打开。仍然易燃。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "empty door frame"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "An empty door frame made from planks and nails.  A variety of doors could be constructed here."
msgstr "一个用木板和钉子打造的空门框。各式各样的门都可以安装在上面。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "empty metal door frame"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "An empty door frame made of steel and assorted metal.  A variety of doors could be constructed here."
msgstr "一个用钢铁和各式金属打造的空门框。各式各样的门都可以安装在上面。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "empty metal window frame"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "An empty window frame constructed from assembled metal and carefully braced with various hardware."
msgstr "一个由装配好的金属条构成的空窗框，四周仔细地用了各种五金件支撑。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into shape."
msgstr "一个十分坚固的金属门，由合金钢制成，一体冲压成型。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into shape.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the peephole."
msgstr "一扇十分坚固的金属门，由合金钢一体冲压制成，不过有个窥视孔。如果你仔细检查，就可以透过孔窥视。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "electronic locked metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into shape.  It is locked by an electronic keypad."
msgstr "一扇十分坚固的金属门，由合金钢一体冲压制成。它被电子键盘锁上了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into shape.  It's open, so no tools are needed to break in."
msgstr "一扇十分坚固的金属门，由合金钢一体冲压制成。这扇门开着，可以自由出入。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into shape.  This one has an extra keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You could probably pick the lock."
msgstr "一扇十分坚固的金属门，由合金钢一体冲压制成。上面有个锁孔，应该是被锁上了。你可以使用开锁工具尝试开锁。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open metal door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, cut and pounded into shape.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the peephole.  No need right now though, since the door is open anyway."
msgstr "一扇十分坚固的金属门，由合金钢一体冲压制成，不过有个窥视孔。如果你仔细检查，就可以透过孔窥视。现在门已经打开，不需要窥视了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bulkhead door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "An extremely resilient door made of cast metal, it is watertight and opened using the fly wheel."
msgstr "一个十分坚固的金属门，由铸铁制成，完全水密，需要用转轮开启。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open bulkhead door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "An extremely resilient door made of cast metal, it is watertight, or would be if it was closed."
msgstr "一个十分坚固的金属门，由铸铁制成，在关闭时完全水密。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "An industrially fabricated thick sheet carefully positioned and joined seamlessly with perimeter sealant, this wall is capable of resisting extreme elements as well as hostile forces.  Blast load rated and extremely fire-retardant, breaching it will require specialized tools or an industrial vehicle."
msgstr "经过精心定位并以边缘密封胶无缝连接的工业制厚板材，能抵抗极端气候与敌对力量。具备极优的爆炸负荷和抗燃性，想突破它需要专用工具或工业用载具。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open lighthouse lens hinged section"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "An intricate arrangement of glass, designed to focus light from within to be visible over long distances.  This section of the lens is hinged and is currently open."
msgstr "这组精密的玻璃结构旨在将内部光线聚焦，使其在远距离仍清晰可见。该透镜部分采用铰链连接，目前处于开启状态。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed lighthouse lens hinged section"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "An intricate arrangement of glass, designed to focus light from within to be visible over long distances.  This section of the lens is on hinges and can be opened for maintenance."
msgstr "这组精密的玻璃结构，旨在将内部光线聚焦，使其在远距离仍清晰可见。该透镜部分通过铰链连接，可开启进行维护。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged reinforced wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "Despite someone's best efforts at reinforcing this door, there are splintering planks and visible holes in the wood, it could soon be smashed apart completely if not repaired.  The doorknob is all messed up and the door can't be opened until it's fixed."
msgstr "尽管有人尽了最大的努力加固这扇门，但木板上还是出现了裂缝与明显的洞，如果不修复，它很快就会被完全砸碎。门把手全坏了，在修好之前无法打开。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed reinforced wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "Just like other wooden doors, except this one has layers of nailed-on planks and an additional hinge for reinforcement.  It might be barricaded, but it's still susceptible to fire."
msgstr "与普通木门有所不同，这扇门用木板和额外的铰链加固过，它的防护性更强，但仍然容易起火。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open reinforced wood door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "Just like other wooden doors, except this one has layers of nailed-on planks for reinforcement.  It might be fortified, but it's still susceptible to fire.  It's open, so it's not stopping anything right now."
msgstr "除了一层钉牢加固的木板，这扇木门跟其他的没啥区别。它也许经过强化，但仍然容易着火。现在是敞开的，阻挡不了任何东西。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed door curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "Repurposed curtains from a window covering a door frame.  Could be easily taken down for supplies or placed somewhere else."
msgstr "将窗帘直接吊在门框上，就成了一扇门帘。可以很轻松地将它拆除获得材料，或者拆下来安装在别处。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open door curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "Repurposed curtains from a window covering a door frame.  Could be easily taken down for supplies or placed somewhere else.  The curtains are open, bundled, and tied next to the doorway."
msgstr "将窗帘直接吊在门框上，就成了一扇门帘。可以很轻松地将它拆除获得材料，或者拆下来安装在别处。这扇门帘被卷成一团用绳子吊在门框上。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed grass curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "Sheets of grass yarn covering a door frame.  Could be easily taken down for supplies or placed somewhere else."
msgstr "将窗帘直接吊在门框上，就成了一扇门帘。可以很轻松地将它拆除获得材料，或者拆下来安装在别处。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open grass curtain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "Sheets of grass yarn covering a door frame.  Could be easily taken down for supplies or placed somewhere else.  The curtains are open, bundled, and tied next to the doorway."
msgstr "将草绳吊在门框上，就成了一扇门帘。可以很轻松地将它拆除获得材料，或者拆下来安装在别处。这扇门帘被卷成一团用绳子吊在门框上。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged wood door with peephole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "The bad news is that the peephole is broken and you can't use it to look through the door.  The good news is that the door is nearly broken down, so there's nothing blocking the view.  Also, the doorknob is so messed up that it can't be opened anymore.  A few planks, nails, and the right tools could patch up all the damage."
msgstr "坏消息是窥视孔坏了，你不能用它来透过门看。 好消息是门几乎坏了，所以没有什么挡住了视线。 此外，门把手坏得打不开了。一些木板、钉子和合适的工具可以修补所有的损伤。"

#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed bar door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "The door swings open…"
msgstr "门开了……"

#. ~ Prying failure of terrain ""
#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "The metal door is too thick."
msgstr "金属门太厚了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open secret door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "This apparently normal segment of concrete wall has opened to reveal a secret passage."
msgstr "看上去十分正常的混凝土墙中一段被打开了，露出了一条秘密通道。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open secret door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "This apparently normal segment of metal wall has opened to reveal a secret passage."
msgstr "这显然是正常的金属墙的一部分打开了，露出了一条秘密通道。"

#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed wood door"
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain ""
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed metal door"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock on the door opens."
msgstr "随着一声令人满意的咔嗒声，门上的锁被打开了。"

#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed bar door"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "locked wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "open wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "locked retractable gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed retractable gate"
