#. ~ Description of terrain "grape bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A bush of a different species invaded by grape vines, but they're fruitless."
msgstr "一丛爬满了葡萄藤的灌木。藤上没有葡萄。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "grape bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A bush of a different species invaded by grape vines."
msgstr "一丛爬满了葡萄藤的灌木。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "spicebush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A bush that features small, red berries."
msgstr "一种长有小而红色浆果的灌木。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "spicebush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A bush that usually features small, red berries but it was picked clean."
msgstr "一棵灌木通常结有小巧的红色浆果，但此刻却已经被采摘一空。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "alder tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A deciduous flowering tree with serrated, scalloped, round-obovate leaves, commonly forming dense groves alongside water."
msgstr "一种落叶开花乔木，长着锯齿状扇形纹路的倒卵形叶子，通常在水边形成密林。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pistachio tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A deciduous tree of the 'Pistacia' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is not native to this region.  Unfortunately, it looks like it has been picked clean of pistachio nuts."
msgstr "一棵落叶树，分类学上属于黄连木属。它并非本地原生物种，而是人工栽培的。看起来上面成熟的开心果都被摘完了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pistachio tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A deciduous tree of the 'Pistacia' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is not native to this region.  You could look for pistachio nuts if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr "一棵落叶树，分类学上属于黄连木属。它并非本地原生物种，而是人工栽培的。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的开心果。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "almond tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A deciduous tree of the 'Prunus' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is not native to this region.  There are no almonds left to pick on the tree."
msgstr "一棵落叶树，分类学上属于李属。它并非本地原生物种，而是人工栽培的。看起来上面成熟的扁桃仁都被摘完了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "almond tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A deciduous tree of the 'Prunus' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is not native to this region.  You could look for fresh almonds if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr "一棵落叶树，分类学上属于李属。它并非本地原生物种，而是人工栽培的。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的扁桃仁。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackjack oak"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A deciduous tree of the genus 'Quercus', with bark cracked into rectangular black plates split by narrow orange fissures.  All the usable bark has been stripped off."
msgstr "一棵落叶乔木，分类学上属于栎属。树皮开裂出橙色细缝，将其分隔成许多黑色长方块。所有可用的树皮都被剥掉了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackjack oak"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A deciduous tree of the genus 'Quercus', with bark cracked into rectangular black plates split by narrow orange fissures.  You could peel off the bark sections if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr "一棵落叶乔木，分类学上属于栎属。树皮开裂出橙色细缝，将其分隔成许多黑色长方块。靠近查看它时，可以把树皮剥下来。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hydrangea bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A dense bush of fragrant blue hydrangeas."
msgstr "一大丛长着芳香的蓝色绣球花的灌木丛。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "underbrush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A dense patch of vegetation.  Foraging here could turn up all sorts of things, and would be a bit faster with a tool for cutting plants."
msgstr "一片茂密的植被。在此觅食可能发现各种东西，若使用割草工具会稍快些。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "underbrush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A dense patch of vegetation.  It has been rummaged through and doesn't have anything useful left to forage from it."
msgstr "四散在森林中的小型植物和灌木。它已经被翻过了，没留下任何能吃能用的东西。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rose bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A fat bush of beautiful red roses, if only you could get a date!  Watch out for its thorns!"
msgstr "一大丛长着美丽红玫瑰的灌木丛，要是有个约会就好了。当心上面的刺！"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hydrangea bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A fat hydrangea bush that currently has no blooms."
msgstr "一大丛还没开花的绣球花丛。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rose bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A fat rose bush that currently has no blooms.  Watch out for its thorns!"
msgstr "一大丛还没开花的玫瑰丛。当心上面的刺！"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mega fern"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A gigantic fern like nothing you've seen before.  The leaves are a bright scarlet with a net-like structure of green veins.  The multipronged trunks have the texture of balsa wood."
msgstr "一种你从未见过的巨大蕨类植物。叶子呈明亮的猩红色，有绿色纹理的网状结构。其多刺枝干的纹理和轻木一致。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "bee hive"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A hive of bees located in a cavity inside a tree, swarming in and out at a feverish pace.  There's probably honey inside."
msgstr "一巢住在树洞里的蜜蜂，闹哄哄的飞进飞出。那儿可能有蜂蜜。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "maple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A large deciduous tree of the 'Acer' genus.  The leaves are distinctively shaped with five prongs.  A spigot is wedged into the trunk, and sweet maple sap can be extracted."
msgstr "一棵高大的大型落叶树，分类学上属于槭属。长着形似手掌的独特树叶。树干被被楔入一根插管，可以收获甜蜜的枫树树汁。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "maple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A large deciduous tree of the 'Acer' genus.  The leaves are distinctively shaped with five prongs.  It could be tapped in order to extract maple sap."
msgstr "一棵高大的大型落叶树，分类学上属于槭属。长着形似手掌的独特树叶。可以安装插管来收获枫树树汁。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mushroom colony"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A large pile of organic matter which has molded over with fungus.  The caps of many mundane mushrooms spring from the top, you can even recognize some.  The fungi growing here don't seem edible, though."
msgstr "一大堆被真菌覆盖的有机物。 许多平凡的蘑菇的菌盖从顶部冒出来，你甚至可以认出一些。 不过，这里生长的真菌似乎不可食用。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "cottonwood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A large tree belonging to the 'Populus' genus, commonly found throughout the New England region.  All the cottonwood tree bolls have been harvested."
msgstr "一棵体型巨大的树，分类学上属于杨属，在新英格兰地区四处可见。上面的杨絮都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "cottonwood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A large tree belonging to the 'Populus' genus, commonly found throughout the New England region.  You see some cottonwood tree bolls that can be harvested."
msgstr "一棵体型巨大的树，分类学上属于杨属，在新英格兰地区四处可见。你在上面看到一些可以摘下来的杨絮。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "elm tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A large tree belonging to the 'Ulmus' genus, commonly found throughout the New England region."
msgstr "一棵体型巨大的树，分类学上属于榆属，在新英格兰地区四处可见。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sycamore tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A long-lived tree with flaky bark and a broad trunk."
msgstr "一棵长寿的树，树皮呈鳞片状，树干粗壮。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apiary"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A man-made wooden box designed to hold honeybees and facilitate the care for a hive.  The modular construction allows for inspecting the bees and harvesting their bounty without destroying the hive completely.  This year's harvest should be ready by now."
msgstr "一个人造木箱，设计来承载蜂巢和蜜蜂。其分离式设计允许你观察蜜蜂、收集蜂蜜而不完全摧毁蜂巢。它已经准备好丰收了！"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apiary"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A man-made wooden box designed to host honeybees and facilitate the care for a hive.  The modular construction allows for inspecting the bees and harvesting their bounty without destroying the hive completely.  It will be some time before this one is ready to harvest."
msgstr "一个人造木箱，设计来承载蜂巢和蜜蜂。其分离式设计允许你观察蜜蜂、收集蜂蜜而不完全摧毁蜂巢。这个蜂箱离收获还要等些时日。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "oak tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive deciduous tree belonging to the 'Quercus' genus, commonly found throughout the New England region."
msgstr "一棵体型巨大的落叶树，分类学上属于栎属，在新英格兰地区四处可见。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "oak tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive deciduous tree belonging to the 'Quercus' genus, commonly found throughout the New England region.  If you look closely, you can see some acorns the squirrels haven't gotten yet."
msgstr "一棵体型巨大的落叶树，分类学上属于栎属，在新英格兰地区四处可见。靠近看时可以发现一些还没有被松鼠摘取的橡实。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "chestnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Castanea' genus."
msgstr "一棵巨大的树木，分类学上属于栗属。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "chestnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Castanea' genus.  If you look closely, you can see some unharvested chestnuts."
msgstr "一棵巨大的树木，分类学上属于栗属。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的栗子。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "beech tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Fagus' genus."
msgstr "一棵巨大的树木，分类学上属于山毛榉属。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "beech tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Fagus' genus.  If you look closely, you can see some unharvested beech nuts."
msgstr "一棵巨大的树木，分类学上属于山毛榉属。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的榉实。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "butternut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus, but with lighter bark and more elongated fruits than the more common black walnut."
msgstr "一棵巨大的树木，分类学上属于胡桃属，但与更常见的黑胡桃木相比，有着颜色更浅的树皮和更细长的果实。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "butternut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus, but with lighter bark and more elongated fruits than the more common black walnut.  If you look closely, you can see some unharvested butternuts."
msgstr "一棵巨大的树木，分类学上属于胡桃属，但与更常见的黑胡桃木相比，有着颜色更浅的树皮和更细长的果实。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的白胡桃。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "walnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus."
msgstr "一棵巨大的树木，分类学上属于胡桃属。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "walnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus.  If you look closely, you can see some unharvested walnuts."
msgstr "一棵巨大的树木，分类学上属于胡桃属。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的核桃。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "ash tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A member of the 'Fraxinus' genus, these hardwood trees have long been prized for their lumber."
msgstr "作为梣属植物的一员，这些硬木树种因其木材而备受珍视。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "young tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A relatively young sapling of an indeterminate species.  It could take decades before reaching maturity, so there's no use waiting around."
msgstr "一个过于年幼而难以分辨物种的小树。长大成熟可能需要几十年，所以在这里干等着可没用。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "tree trunk"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A section of trunk from a tree that has been cut down.  Can be sawn into logs with the right tool."
msgstr "一截树干，来自一棵被砍倒的树。使用合适的工具可以锯成原木。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "fern"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A short plant with thousands of leaves which grow in a fractal pattern from the stem."
msgstr "一株低矮的植物，茎秆上长着成千上万的分形般的叶片。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "fern"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A short plant with thousands of leaves which grow in a fractal pattern.  All of the curled shoots have been harvested."
msgstr "一株低矮的植物，上面长着成千上万的分形般的树叶。上面的嫩芽都被收割了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small blackberry bush that's fruitless.  Watch out for its thorns!"
msgstr "一小丛没有果实的黑莓丛。当心上面的刺！"

#. ~ Description of terrain "blueberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small blueberry bush that's fruitless."
msgstr "一小丛没有果实的蓝莓丛。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "peanut bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of crunchy peanuts."
msgstr "一小丛长着香脆花生的灌木丛。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of delicious blackberries.  Watch out for its thorns!"
msgstr "一小丛长着美味黑莓的灌木丛。当心上面的刺！"

#. ~ Description of terrain "raspberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of delicious raspberries.  Watch out for its thorns!"
msgstr "一小丛长着美味树莓的灌木丛。当心上面的刺！"

#. ~ Description of terrain "huckleberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of huckleberries, often mistaken for blueberries."
msgstr "一小丛长着香甜越橘的灌木丛。经常被误认为蓝莓。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "strawberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of juicy strawberries."
msgstr "一小丛长着多汁草莓的灌木丛。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "blueberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small bush of sweet blueberries."
msgstr "一小丛长着香甜蓝莓的灌木丛。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "huckleberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small huckleberry bush that's fruitless."
msgstr "一小丛没有果实的越橘丛。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "peanut bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small peanut bush that's fruitless."
msgstr "一小丛没有果实的花生丛。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "golf hole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small plastic cup embedded in an area of very short, neat grass."
msgstr "一个埋进一片又短又匀整的草坪里的小塑料杯。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "raspberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small raspberry bush that's fruitless.  Watch out for its thorns!"
msgstr "一小丛没有果实的树莓丛。当心上面的刺！"

#. ~ Description of terrain "shrub"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small shrub."
msgstr "一丛小灌木。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "strawberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small strawberry bush that's fruitless."
msgstr "一小丛没有果实的草莓丛。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hazelnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A stubby tree belonging to the 'Corylus' genus."
msgstr "一棵粗矮的树木，分类学上属于榛属。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hazelnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A stubby tree belonging to the 'Corylus' genus.  If you look closely, you can see some unharvested hazelnuts."
msgstr "一棵粗矮的树木，分类学上属于榛属。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的榛子。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "tall bamboo"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A tall bamboo thicket about head high."
msgstr "一颗高高的竹子，大概有头那么高。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A tall deciduous tree of the 'Betula' genus, with the characteristic peeling bark.  Species like 'B. alleghaniensis', 'B. papyrifera', and 'B. populifolia' are the most common in the New England region.  Looks like there isn't enough rhytidome to peel off yet."
msgstr "一棵高大的落叶树，分类学上属于桦属，在新英格兰地区主要由北美黄桦、北美白桦、北美灰桦组成。看起来桦树皮都被撕光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A tall deciduous tree of the 'Betula' genus, with the characteristic peeling bark.  Species like 'B. alleghaniensis', 'B. papyrifera', and 'B. populifolia' are the most common in the New England region.  You could tear off some strips of bark if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr "一棵高大的落叶树，分类学上属于桦属，在新英格兰地区主要由北美黄桦、北美白桦、北美灰桦组成。靠近查看它时，可以撕下一些树皮。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pecan tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  It doesn't look like there are any pecan nuts left on the tree."
msgstr "一棵高大落叶树，分类学上属于山核桃属。看起来上面成熟的美洲山核桃都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  It looks like the tree has been picked clean of hickory nuts."
msgstr "一棵高大落叶树，分类学上属于山核桃属。看起来上面成熟的山核桃都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  You could look for hickory nuts if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr "一棵高大落叶树，分类学上属于山核桃属。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的山核桃。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pecan tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  You could look for pecan nuts if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr "一棵高大落叶树，分类学上属于山核桃属。靠近看时可以发现一些还没被摘掉的美洲山核桃。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "willow tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A tall, wide deciduous tree of the 'Salix' genus, with long, thin, leafy branches that hang down like curtains.  Looks like all usable bark has been torn off, and new rhytidomes have not formed yet."
msgstr "一棵又高又壮的落叶树，分类学上属于柳属。叶子长而薄，如窗帘一般垂下。看起来树皮都被撕掉了，还没形成新皮层。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "willow tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A tall, wide deciduous tree of the 'Salix' genus, with long, thin, leafy branches that hang down like curtains.  You could tear off some bark."
msgstr "一棵又高又壮的落叶树，分类学上属于柳属。叶子长而薄，如窗帘一般垂下。靠近查看它时，可以撕下一些树皮。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  If you examined the tree more closely, you might find usable sticky whorls, resin clumps, and pinecones."
msgstr "一棵高耸入云的针叶树，分类学上属于松属，在新英格兰地区主要由刚松、北美红松、北美乔松组成。靠近查看它时，可以找到粘稠的松香、树脂和松塔。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  Some of the branches and resin clumps have been stripped away and many of the pinecones aren't developed fully yet, but given a season, it could be harvestable again."
msgstr "一棵高耸入云的针叶树，分类学上属于松属，在新英格兰地区主要由刚松、北美红松、北美乔松组成。看起来它的枝干被人折走了许多，成熟的松塔和树脂都被摘光了，不过再过一季就应该能再次收获了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  This tree's branches are bare, and it appears to be dead."
msgstr "一棵高耸入云的针叶树，分类学上属于松属，在新英格兰地区主要由刚松、北美红松、北美乔松组成。这棵树的枝干都秃了，看起来已经枯萎了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apricot tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A transplanted species of 'Prunus armeniaca', rarely found in New England.  It produces apricots in the summer.  If you examined the spurs more closely, you could probably find some mature apricots."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出杏子的树，分类学上属于李属杏种。由于是移植树种，在新英格兰地区很少能见到。顺着枝干仔细观察的话，应该可以找到几个成熟的杏子。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apricot tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A transplanted species of 'Prunus armeniaca', rarely found in New England.  It produces apricots in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe apricots have been picked."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出杏子的树，分类学上属于李属杏种。由于是移植树种，在新英格兰地区很少能见到。看起来上面成熟的杏子都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "tree stump"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A tree stump, a remnant of a tree that has been cut down."
msgstr "一截树桩，砍倒树木的残余物。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "lilac bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A wide bush of bright pinkish-purple lilacs."
msgstr "一大丛长着鲜亮粉紫色丁香花的灌木丛。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "lilac bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A wide lilac bush that currently has no blooms."
msgstr "一大丛还没开花的丁香花丛。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "shorn grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of grass clipped nearly down to the roots."
msgstr "一片被修剪得又短又匀整的草坪。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "white grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of grass covered in white latex-based paint, with neat lines designed for recreational sports."
msgstr "一片被白色乳胶漆覆盖的肯塔基蓝草，线条整齐，适合休闲运动。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "golf green"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of grass mowed very short and neat."
msgstr "一片被修剪得又短又匀整的草坪。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of hardy grass about ankle high."
msgstr "一片茂密的草丛，大概有头那么高。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "long bamboo shoots"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of long bamboo shoots about shin high."
msgstr "一片长长的竹笋，大概有小腿那么高。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead bamboo"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of long, brown, dead bamboo shoots covered in white fungus."
msgstr "一片长长的褐色的枯死的竹子，上面覆盖着白色的真菌。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "long grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of long, shaggy grass about shin high."
msgstr "一片长而杂乱的草，大概有小腿那么高。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "tall grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of tall grass about head high."
msgstr "一片茂密的草丛，大概有头那么高。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "young bamboo shoots"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of young bamboo shoots about ankle high.  Many shoots are just barely pushing above the ground."
msgstr "一片大约脚踝高的竹笋地。许多嫩笋只是勉强露出地面。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "young bamboo shoots"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An area of young bamboo shoots about ankle high.  The smallest shoots have already been harvested."
msgstr "一片大约脚踝高的竹笋地。能食用的嫩笋都被收过了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An indiscernible tree that has withered away due to weather, fire, or otherworldly causes."
msgstr "一棵受天气、火焰、或是异界的影响而枯萎且难以分辨物种的枯树。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An indiscernible tree that has withered away due to weather, fire, or otherworldly causes.  Someone or something has broken most of its dead branches, leaving little but its gnarled trunk."
msgstr "一棵隐约可见的树，因天气、火灾或其他超自然原因而枯萎了。有什么人或物破坏了它的大部分树枝，只留下长着木瘤的扭曲树干。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "autumn olive"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An invasive species from Japan which is also called silverberry.  Widely planted in the 1940s to combat erosion, it spread far and wide, often even displacing native plants.  As it name says, it bears fruits in autumn, which are quite unlike olives, but this particular plant has been harvested already."
msgstr "一种来自日本的入侵物种，亦称银莓。1940年代为防治水土流失而广泛种植，此后迅速蔓延，常将本土植物挤占殆尽。正如其名，它在秋季结果，果实与橄榄截然不同，但这株特定植株的果实已被采收。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "autumn olive"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "An invasive species from Japan which is also called silverberry.  Widely planted in the 1940s to combat erosion, it spread far and wide, often even displacing native plants.  As it name says, it bears fruits in autumn, which are quite unlike olives."
msgstr "一种来自日本的入侵物种，亦称银莓。1940年代为防治水土流失而被广泛种植，此后迅速蔓延至广阔区域，甚至常取代本土植物。正如其名，它在秋季结果，果实与橄榄截然不同。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hobblebush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "Called hobblebush because it may hinder and trip, hobbles, unwary hikers with its branches bending over and taking root.  It also bears surprisingly sweet berries in autumn, if it hadn't been picked clean already."
msgstr "因其枝条下垂生根，常绊倒不慎的徒步者而得名\"绊脚灌木\"。若未被采摘殆尽，秋日里它还会结出出人意料的甜美浆果。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hobblebush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "Called hobblebush because it may hinder and trip, hobbles, unwary hikers with its branches bending over and taking root.  It also bears surprisingly sweet berries in autumn."
msgstr "因其枝条下垂生根，常绊倒不慎的登山者而得名\"绊脚灌木\"。秋日里它竟会结出出人意料的甜美浆果。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "black chokeberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "Drooping black berries adorn the shrub during autumn.  These have a distinctive star-shaped fold and look quite juicy."
msgstr "在秋天，这种灌木丛上会挂满低垂的黑色浆果。这些浆果有着独特的星形褶皱，看起来十分多汁"

#. ~ Description of terrain "black chokeberry bush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "Drooping black berries adorned this shrub, but the shrub was picked clean."
msgstr "这丛灌木上挂着一些下垂的黑色浆果，但这些灌木已经被采摘一空了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "tupelo tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "Its name, originating from Native American tongues and garbled by the settlers, approximately means \"swamp tree\".  During autumn it bears cherry-like fruits, but someone picked this one clean already."
msgstr "它的名字源自美洲原住民的语言，后来又被殖民者随意改写，大致意思是“沼泽树”。到了秋天，它会结出类似樱桃的果实，但有人已经把这棵树上的果实全部摘光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "tupelo tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "Its name, originating from Native American tongues and garbled by the settlers, approximately means \"swamp tree\".  During autumn it bears cherry-like fruits."
msgstr "它的名字源自美洲原住民的语言，后来被殖民者随意改写，大致意思是“沼泽树”。在秋天，它会结出类似樱桃的果实。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "cherry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears cherries in the summer.  If you examined the foliage more closely, you could probably find some viable clusters."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出樱桃的树，分类学上属于李属，是新英格兰地区的本土种类。顺着枝干仔细观察的话，应该可以找到几串成熟的樱桃。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "cherry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears cherries in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe bunches of cherries have been picked."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出樱桃的树，分类学上属于李属，是新英格兰地区的本土种类。看起来上面成熟的樱桃都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "peach tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears peaches in the summer.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could probably find some mature peaches."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出桃子的树，分类学上属于李属，是新英格兰地区的本土种类。顺着枝干仔细观察的话，应该可以找到几个成熟的桃子。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "peach tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears peaches in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe peaches have been picked."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出桃子的树，分类学上属于李属，是新英格兰地区的本土种类。看起来上面成熟的桃子都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "plum tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it produces plums in the summer.  If you examined the spurs more closely, you could probably find some ripe plums."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出李子的树，分类学上属于李属，是新英格兰地区的本土种类。顺着枝干仔细观察的话，应该可以找到几个成熟的李子。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "plum tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it produces plums in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe plums have been picked."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出李子的树，分类学上属于李属，是新英格兰地区的本土种类。看起来上面成熟的李子都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "juniper tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "One of the species of 'Juniperus' that grows in New England, juniper berries grow over two to three years.  It flowers in the first year, produces a green berry the second, and in the third produces the more famed blue varieties.  If you examined the foliage more closely, you could probably find some viable clusters."
msgstr "一棵新英格兰地区的杜松子树，分类上属于刺柏属。杜松子从开花算起需两到三年才能成熟。它在第一年开花，第二年结出绿色的浆果，第三年才产出广为人知的蓝色浆果。顺着枝干仔细观察的话，应该可以找到几串成熟的杜松子。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "juniper tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "One of the species of 'Juniperus' that grows in New England, juniper berries grow over two to three years.  It flowers in the first year, produces a green berry the second, and in the third produces the more famed blue varieties.  Looks like all the ripe bunches of berries have been picked."
msgstr "一棵新英格兰地区的杜松子树，分类上属于刺柏属。杜松子从开花算起需两到三年才能成熟。它在第一年开花，第二年结出绿色的浆果，第三年才产出广为人知的蓝色浆果。看起来上面成熟的杜松子都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "magnolia tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "Part of an ancient lineage of broadleaf trees known for their large white flowers."
msgstr "属于一种古老的阔叶树种，以其硕大的白色花朵而闻名。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead grass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "Patchy grass which has withered and died."
msgstr "一片枯死、斑驳的草地。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "woodchips"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "Small splinters of wood laid out in a layer to prevent unwanted plants from growing."
msgstr "地上铺了一层碎木屑，用于避免杂草生长。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "basswood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "The American linden.  It has pretty and sweet-smelling flowers in the summer, and its edible young leaves have already been harvested."
msgstr "一棵美洲椴树。夏天它会开着美丽而芬芳的花朵，它上面的嫩叶已经被采光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "basswood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "The American linden.  It has pretty and sweet-smelling flowers in the summer, and you might be able to eat its young leaves in the spring."
msgstr "一棵美洲椴树。夏天它会开出美丽而芬芳的花朵，而春天你可以吃它的嫩叶。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped dead pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "The branches of this pine tree have been twisted into a shape that remind you of Sierpinski triangles.  It did not survive being warped like this."
msgstr "这棵枯松树的树枝被扭曲成某种让你想起谢尔宾斯基三角形的形状。它没法被扭曲成这样后继续存活。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "The dead remnants of a tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  Nothing useful can be foraged from this poor, dead tree."
msgstr "一棵枯萎的高大落叶树，分类学上属于山核桃属。从这棵贫瘠的枯萎的树上收获不到任何果实。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sweet birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "The sweet birch lacks the paper bark of its cousins in the 'Betula' genus.  It gets its name from its sweet sap, which can be tapped with a spile and used to make syrup."
msgstr "甜桦树不像同属的其他桦树那样具有纸质树皮。其名源于甜美的树液，可用钻孔器采集树液制成糖浆。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sweet birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "The sweet birch lacks the paper bark of its cousins in the 'Betula' genus.  This one's tapped with a spile."
msgstr "甜桦树没有其同属桦木属（Betula）近亲那种纸质树皮。这种树是用钻孔器钻孔采集树液的。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This deciduous tree's branches are warped into a spiral.  This appears to have killed it."
msgstr "这棵落叶树的树枝被某种力量扭曲成螺旋状，而且让它枯萎了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "coffee tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This is 'Gymnocladus dioicus', or the Kentucky coffee tree, which produces roastable coffee pods and brewable leaves in the fall.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could probably find a few mature ones."
msgstr "一棵在秋天能够结出豆荚和叶子的肯塔基咖啡树，分类学上属于豆科肥皂荚属，其豆荚可以烘烤成咖啡豆的替代品，而叶子可以酿酒。顺着枝干仔细观察的话，应该可以找到几个成熟的豆荚。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "coffee tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This is 'Gymnocladus dioicus', or the Kentucky coffee tree, which produces roastable coffee pods and brewable leaves in the fall.  Looks like all the ripe pods have been picked."
msgstr "一棵在秋天能够结出豆荚和叶子的肯塔基咖啡树，分类学上属于豆科肥皂荚属，其豆荚可以烘烤成咖啡豆的替代品，而叶子可以酿酒。看起来上面成熟的豆荚都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pear tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This is 'Pyrus communis', or the common pear tree, which produces fruit in the fall.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could probably find a few mature ones."
msgstr "一棵在秋天能够结出梨子的树，分类学上属于梨属西洋梨种。顺着枝干仔细观察的话，应该可以找到几个成熟的梨子。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pear tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This is 'Pyrus communis', or the common pear tree, which produces fruit in the fall.  Looks like all the ripe pears have been picked."
msgstr "一棵在秋天能够结出梨子的树，分类学上属于梨属西洋梨种。看起来上面成熟的梨子都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hemlock tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This is an evergreen tree from the 'Tsuga' genus, superficially similar to a pine."
msgstr "这是一棵属于“杜鹃松属”的常绿树，其外观与松树颇为相似。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hemlock tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This is an evergreen tree from the 'Tsuga' genus, superficially similar to a pine.  Some of the branches and resin clumps have been stripped away and many of the cones aren't developed fully yet, but given a season, it could be harvestable again."
msgstr "一棵高耸入云的针叶树，分类学上属于松属，在新英格兰地区主要由刚松、北美红松、北美乔松组成。看起来它的枝干被人折走了许多，成熟的松塔和树脂都被摘光了，不过再过一季就应该能再次收获了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "nannyberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This small tree, it could almost be a large shrub, bears clusters of dark blue berries in autumn, but someone picked this one clean already."
msgstr "这棵小树几乎可以算作是一棵大型灌木了，到了秋天会结出一簇簇深蓝色的浆果，但已经有人大肆采摘，把这棵树上的果实都摘光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "nannyberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This small tree, it could almost be a large shrub, bears clusters of dark blue berries in autumn."
msgstr "这棵小树几乎可以算作是一棵大型灌木了，到了秋天会结出一簇簇深蓝色的浆果。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, producing fruit commonly known as apples.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could probably find a few mature ones in autumn."
msgstr "一棵能够结出苹果的树，分类学上属于苹果属。在秋天顺着枝干仔细观察的话，应该可以找到几个成熟的苹果。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, producing fruit commonly known as apples.  There do not appear to be any ripe apples now."
msgstr "一棵能够结出苹果的树，分类学上属于苹果属。看起来上面成熟的苹果都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "crabapple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, though unlike popular cultivars, its fruits are small and sour.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could probably find a few mature ones in autumn."
msgstr "一棵分类学上属于苹果属的树，但是和常见的栽培种相比，这种树结的果实又小又酸。在秋天顺着枝干仔细观察的话，应该可以找到几个成熟的野苹果。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "crabapple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, though unlike popular cultivars, its fruits are small and sour.  There do not appear to be any ripe crabapples now."
msgstr "一棵分类学上属于苹果属的树，但是和常见的栽培种相比，这种树结的果实又小又酸。看起来上面成熟的野苹果都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mulberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This tree is a member of the 'Morus' genus, producing fruit commonly known as mulberries.  In the summer, many berries can be picked."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出许多桑椹的树，分类学上属于桑属。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mulberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This tree is a member of the 'Morus' genus, producing fruit commonly known as mulberries.  There do not appear to be any ripe mulberries now."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出许多桑椹的树，分类学上属于桑属。看起来上面成熟的桑椹都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "elderberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This tree is a member of the 'Sambucus' genus, producing fruit commonly known as elderberries.  In the summer, many berries can be picked."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出许多接骨木果的树，分类学上属于接骨木属。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "elderberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This tree is a member of the 'Sambucus' genus, producing fruit commonly known as elderberries.  There do not appear to be any ripe elderberries now."
msgstr "一棵在夏天能够结出许多接骨木果的树，分类学上属于接骨木属。看起来上面成熟的接骨木果都被摘光了。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sassafras tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This tree is a member of the 'Sassafras' genus, known for its aromatic qualities.  In the winter and spring, the sap rich roots can be harvested to make a sweet beverage."
msgstr "这棵树是黄樟属的一员，以其芳香的品质而闻名。 在冬季和春季，可以收获富含汁液的根来制作甜味饮料。"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sassafras tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "This tree is a member of the 'Sassafras' genus, known for its aromatic qualities.  This tree's roots have been harvested, any more and the tree will die."
msgstr "这棵树是黄樟属的一员，以其芳香的品质而闻名。 这棵树的根已经被砍掉了，再砍下去树就会死。"

