#. ~ Description of "dragon skin vest"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A ballistic vest made of disc-shaped ceramic scales arranged in an overlapping pattern, like the scales of a mythical dragon.  The design allows it to absorb many more impacts without becoming fully compromised like a ballistic plate might, but it was never widely adopted due to its failure to meet high-temperature operational tests.  While well past its warranty date, it remains a highly sought after collecter's item."
msgstr "防弹背心由圆盘状陶瓷鳞片制成，呈重叠图案，就像神话中龙的鳞片一样。  该设计使其能够吸收更多的冲击力，而不会像防弹板那样完全受到损害，但由于无法满足高温操作测试，它从未被广泛采用。  虽然早已过了保修期，但它仍然是备受收藏家追捧的物品。"

#. ~ Description of "soft ballistic vest"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A bulky but comfortable armor vest.  It lacks pockets for ballistic plate inserts, but the IIIa rating on its label suggests that it should stand up to everything short of high-powered rifle rounds."
msgstr "笨重但舒适的装甲背心。  它没有用于弹道板插入物的口袋，但其标签上的 IIIa 等级表明它应该能够承受除高威力步枪弹之外的所有情况。"

#. ~ Description of "scrap ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A crudely-hammered piece of sheet metal, wrapped in rags in an attempt to prevent spalling.  If used in a ballistic vest, it might offer some protection."
msgstr "一块粗略锤打过的金属板，用破布包裹以减少碎裂飞溅。如果装入防弹背心，或许能提供一定的防护。"

#. ~ Description of "scrap ballistic side plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A flat piece of salvaged steel, crudely cut and bent into the shape of an ESBI ballistic plate."
msgstr "一块扁平的废钢，经过粗略切割并弯曲成 ESBI 弹道板的形状。"

#. ~ Description of "paper ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A great many layers of paper stacked and laminated together with a generous portion of glue to form an armor plate for the front or back of the torso.  This could be used in a plate carrier in lieu of an ESAPI plate, though it probably won't stand up to much."
msgstr "将许多层纸堆叠并用大量胶水层压在一起，形成躯干正面或背面的装甲板。  这可以在板载体中代替 ESAPI 板使用，尽管它可能无法承受太多。"

#. ~ Description of "paper ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A great many layers of paper stacked and laminated together with a generous portion of glue to form an armor plate for the front or back of the torso.  This could be used in an oversized plate carrier, though it probably won't stand up to much."
msgstr "大量纸张层层堆叠，并用大量胶水粘合压制而成，用于覆盖躯干前部或后部的装甲板。可用于超大号载板战术背心，不过估计也扛不住什么重击。"

#. ~ Description of "paper ballistic side plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A great many layers of paper stacked and laminated together with a generous portion of glue to form an armor plate for the sides of the torso.  This could be used in a plate carrier in lieu of an ESBI plate, though it probably won't stand up to much."
msgstr "将许多层纸堆叠并用大量胶水层压在一起，形成躯干侧面的装甲板。  这可以在板载体中代替 ESBI 板使用，尽管它可能经不起太多考验。"

#. ~ Description of "steel ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A hand-forged steel ballistic plate more than double the standard size.  It can't be worn on its own, and would need to be inserted into an equally gigantic plate carrier vest to be of any benefit."
msgstr "一块手工锻造的钢制防弹板，尺寸超过标准两倍以上。它无法单独穿戴，必须插入同样巨大的载板战术背心中才能发挥防护作用。"

#. ~ Description of "steel ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A hand-forged steel ballistic plate, designed to be used in a ballistic vest."
msgstr "手工锻造的钢制防弹板，设计用于防弹背心。"

#. ~ Description of "plate carrier"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A heavy-duty vest with specialized pockets to hold hard armor plates, the sort of thing you see on soldiers and armored car drivers.  A soft kevlar liner provides protection against spalling and low-caliber firearms.  It sports MOLLE webbing for attaching compatable accessories."
msgstr "一种重型背心，设有专用口袋用于容纳硬质防弹插板，常见于士兵和装甲车驾驶员所装备的防护具。内部配有凯夫拉软质衬里，可提供对破片和低口径枪弹的防护。表面配备 MOLLE 织带系统，便于挂载兼容的外挂配件。"

#. ~ Description of "steel ballistic side plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A hexagonal piece of steel forged into a side insert for a plate carrier and padded with synthetic fabric."
msgstr "一块六边形钢片锻造成板载体的侧插入件，并用合成纤维填充。"

#. ~ Description of "compromised ceramic front plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A large ballistic plate that has been cracked by damage.  It no longer provides reliable protection, but it's still just as heavy."
msgstr "一块损坏破裂的大型防弹装甲板。它不再提供可靠的保护，但仍然很重。"

#. ~ Description of "concealable ballistic vest"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A level II Kevlar vest, rated for low-caliber pistol rounds and designed to be worn under clothing.  Concerningly, it is sized for a toddler."
msgstr "一件II级凯夫拉防弹背心，可抵御小口径手枪弹，设计为可穿在衣物内。令人担忧的是，它是给幼童穿的尺码。"

#. ~ Description of "concealable ballistic vest"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A lightweight ballistic armor vest, suitable for wearing under clothing.  Its level II rating suggests that it should help against lower-caliber pistol rounds."
msgstr "轻质防弹背心，适合穿在衣服里面。  其二级评级表明它应该有助于对抗较小口径的手枪弹。"

#. ~ Description of "stab vest"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A lightweight soft armor vest.  The level II rating on the label suggests it will protect from knife attacks and low caliber handguns, provided it has its matching stab plate inserts."
msgstr "轻质软甲背心。  标签上的 II 级评级表明，只要有匹配的防刺板插件，它就可以防止刀具攻击和小口径手枪。"

#. ~ Description of "compromised ceramic side plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A medium-sized ballistic plate that has been cracked by damage.  It no longer provides reliable protection, but it's still just as heavy."
msgstr "一块损坏破裂的中型防弹装甲板。它不再提供可靠的保护，但仍然很重。"

#. ~ Description of "deltoid ballistic plates"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A pair of NIJ Level III ballistic plates with a concave profile, made of UHMW polyethylene.  \"STRIKE FACE\" is printed on its outer surface.  These plates are designed to be worn in the shoulder pockets of suitable plate carriers or combat shirts, and can resist several high-energy rifle rounds before breaking.  Deltoid plates such as these are very infrequently worn due to their marginal utility in improving survivability."
msgstr "一对 NIJ III 级防弹板，具有凹形轮廓，由 UHMW 聚乙烯制成。  其外表面上印有“STRIKE FACE”字样。  这些板片设计用于佩戴在合适的板甲携带者或战斗衬衫的肩部口袋中，并且可以在断裂前抵抗数个高能步枪子弹。  诸如此类的三角肌板很少磨损，因为它们在提高生存能力方面作用不大。"

#. ~ Description of "wooden ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A panel of wood cut into an irregular hexagon, slightly concave.  It would fit in a plate carrier sized for a giant, and while by no means capable of stopping gunfire, it may still hold up against other threats."
msgstr "一块切成了不规则六边形的木板，略微内凹。它适合插入为巨人尺寸设计的载板背心，虽然绝对挡不住枪弹，但或许能抵御其他威胁。"

#. ~ Description of "ESBI ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A polygonal ballistic plate with a slightly concave profile, made of ceramic.  \"STRIKE FACE\" is printed on its outer surface.  This is designed to be worn in the sides of a plate carrier, and can withstand several high-energy rifle rounds before breaking."
msgstr "一块有轻微凹面的多边形陶瓷防弹板。外表面标记着\"打击面\"的字样。它需要放进防弹背心后穿着使用，在完全破碎之前可以承受几次高能步枪子弹打击。"

#. ~ Description of "ESAPI ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A polygonal ballistic plate with a slightly concave profile, made of ceramic.  Its inner surface is coated with UHMW polyethylene and is labeled \"TOP\", while the outer surface is labeled \"STRIKE FACE\".  This is intended to be worn in a ballistic vest, and can withstand several high-energy rifle rounds before breaking."
msgstr "一块有轻微凹面的多边形防弹装甲板，由陶瓷制成。其内表面涂有超高分子量聚乙烯，并印着\"顶部\"的字样，而在外表面印着着\"打击面\"的字样。它需要放进防弹背心后穿着使用，在完全破碎之前可以承受几次高能步枪子弹打击。"

#. ~ Description of "EOD fragmentation plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A polygonal fragmentation plate with a slightly concave profile, made of thin layers of steel, UHMW polyethylene, foam, and Kevlar.  Though certified to provide protection from fragmentation, it will not provide much protection from firearms.  This is intended to be inserted into an EOD suit, and can't be worn on its own."
msgstr "具有轻微凹形轮廓的多边形破碎板，由薄层钢、超高分子量聚乙烯、泡沫和凯夫拉尔制成。  虽然经过认证可以提供防碎片保护，但它无法提供太多针对枪支的保护。  它旨在插入 EOD 套装中，不能单独穿着。"

#. ~ Description of "concealable ballistic vest"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A preposterously sized Kevlar vest faced with ballistic nylon  Its low-profile design is perfect for wearing under clothing."
msgstr "一件尺寸大得离谱的凯夫拉防弹背心，外层为防弹尼龙。其低轮廓设计非常适合穿在衣物内。"

#. ~ Description of "wooden ballistic side plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A sheet of wood cut into a small irregular hexagon.  It would fit in the side pockets of a plate carrier, and while by no means capable of stopping gunfire, it may still hold up against other threats."
msgstr "一块木头切成不规则的小六边形。  它可以装在板载车的侧袋中，虽然无法阻止炮火，但它仍然可以抵御其他威胁。"

#. ~ Description of "wooden ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A sheet of wood cut into an irregular hexagon, slightly concave.  It would fit in a plate carrier, and while by no means capable of stopping gunfire, it may still hold up against other threats."
msgstr "一块切成不规则六边形、略微凹陷的木板。它可以塞进防弹背心的插板槽里。虽然它绝无可能挡住子弹，但或许仍能抵御其他威胁。"

#. ~ Description of "half plate carrier"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A simple plate carrier vest covering just the upper torso, with a soft kevlar liner and a front and back pockets for armor plates to keep your organs from being perforated by small-arms fire.  It features a MOLLE cummerbund that you can tuck a few magazines into."
msgstr "一款结构简单的插板背心，仅覆盖上半身。内衬为软质凯夫拉材料，前后设有装甲插板袋，可防止内脏被轻武器火力贯穿穿透。其 MOLLÉ 腰带侧翼可用于收纳少量弹匣。"

#. ~ Description of "lightweight plate carrier"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A slimmed-down kevlar vest with inserts for hard ballistic armor plates in front and back.  It offers plenty of protection without any accessories or extra bits to get in the way."
msgstr "一件精简设计的凯夫拉背心，前后设有硬质防弹插板槽。在不牺牲防护性能的前提下，去除了所有冗余配件，确保行动无碍。"

#. ~ Description of "soft stab panel"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A soft armor insert designed to protect against stab wounds.  This is intended to be inserted into a ballistic vest, and can't be worn on its own."
msgstr "一个柔软的防弹背心插板，用来防刺伤。虽然防护称不上优秀，但同时也不会增加多少累赘。它需要放进防弹背心后穿着使用，无法直接穿着。"

#. ~ Description of "EOD jacket"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "A thick armored jacket constructed from Kevlar, Nomex, and foam padding, for use by explosive ordnance disposal technicians.  It features a central pocket for a large plate, and near complete coverage in fragmentation resistant materials.  Aside from the plate, it offers insufficient protection from ballistic threats."
msgstr "由 Kevlar、Nomex 和泡沫填充物制成的厚装甲夹克，供爆炸物处理技术人员使用。  它的特点是有一个可容纳大盘子的中央口袋，并且几乎完全覆盖了防碎片材料。  除了钢板之外，它还不足以抵御弹道威胁。"

#. ~ Description of "tactical EOD jacket"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "An armored jacket constructed from Kevlar, Nomex, and foam padding, for use by explosive ordnance disposal technicians in 'non-permissive environments'.  It is lighter than normal EOD armor to allow for wearing a plate carrier beneath it.  It features two pockets in the arms covering the deltoids for additional optional protection."
msgstr "由 Kevlar、Nomex 和泡沫填充物制成的装甲夹克，供爆炸物处理技术人员在“不允许的环境”中使用。  它比普通的排爆装甲轻，可以在其下方佩戴板甲。  它的手臂上有两个口袋，覆盖三角肌，提供额外的可选保护。"

#. ~ Description of "plate carrier"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "An enormous handmade ballistic vest with MOLLE webbing for attaching accessories.  No factory ever made ESAPI plates that would fit in this thing, but it ought to be possible to make some out of steel or other materials."
msgstr "一件巨大的手工防弹背心，带有MOLLE织带用于挂载附件。没有哪家工厂生产过能塞进这玩意儿里的ESAPI防弹板，不过用钢材或其他材料自制一些应该是可行的。"

#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "heavy plate carrier"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "Attachment for a collar."
msgstr "衣领附件。"

#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "heavy plate carrier"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "Attachment for a groin protector."
msgstr "腹股沟保护器的附件。"

#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "heavy plate carrier"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid "Attachment for shoulder protectors."
msgstr "肩部保护装置的附件。"

