#. ~ Description of "kufi cap"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A brimless, short and rounded cap."
msgstr ""
"一个短短的圆圆的无沿小帽子，是流行于西北非、中东等地的男性用帽，也同时在非洲裔男性中被广泛使用。\n"
"\"不要和犹太男子在祷告时戴的小帽子混淆了。\""

#. ~ Description of variant "pilgrim hat" of item "wizard hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A broad-brimmed black hat with a buckled belt around the crown.  It's a cheap replica of the kind ahistorically associated with the pilgrims who settled at Plymouth Rock."
msgstr "一顶宽边黑色帽子，帽冠周围有一条带扣的带子。  这是与定居在普利茅斯岩的朝圣者相关的廉价复制品。"

#. ~ Description of "kerchief"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A cotton bandana worn over the head.  It can be adjusted to cover the mouth and nose instead."
msgstr "一条可以覆盖在嘴上的棉制方巾，可以保暖并减少吸入尘土和有害物质。"

#. ~ Description of "baseball cap"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A cotton cap with a rounded crown, an adjustable strap, and a long visor.  It shields your eyes from the sun and provides a little bit of warmth.  Traditionally worn by baseball players."
msgstr "一顶圆顶棉帽，有条可调节的带子和长长的帽舌。它能保护你的眼睛不受阳光直射，而且也能稍微保暖。通常由棒球运动员穿戴。"

#. ~ Description of "tricorne"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A design that goes back to the founding of the thirteen colonies, this is a wide-brimmed oiled leather hat pinned up on three sides to make a distinctive three-pointed design."
msgstr "这种设计可以追溯到十三个殖民地的建立时期，这是一顶宽边涂油皮帽，三边用别针固定，形成独特的三尖设计。"

#. ~ Description of "golf cap"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A flat, short-brimmed cap, commonly worn by golfers."
msgstr "一种扁平的短边帽，高尔夫球手通常佩戴。"

#. ~ Description of "porkpie hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A flat-topped hat with circular indent and a narrow brim.  Most popular in the 40s and 50s, still common among those in the mod scene, hipsters, and people named Heisenberg."
msgstr "一顶有着圆形凹槽和狭窄帽檐的平顶帽。在上世纪四五十年代很流行，现在仍然常在摩德文化客，嬉皮士以及被叫做\"海森堡\"的那家伙头上见到。（注：《绝命毒师》）"

#. ~ Description of "French maid hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A frilly white headpiece."
msgstr "一个有着白色镶边的头饰。"

#. ~ Description of "summer hard hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A hard plastic hat worn at construction and industrial sites, with a sun shield tucked on top to keep the glare out of your eyes.  Protects your eyes from the harsh sun, although it makes ear muffs unattachable to the hard hat itself."
msgstr "一顶供工地和工厂的工人穿戴的硬塑料帽，能有效提供头部对斩击与钝击的保护。下方塞了块棉布作为临时兜帽使用，这让它戴起来更舒适一些，同时保护颈部免受日晒雨淋。"

#. ~ Description of "hard hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A hard plastic hat worn at construction and industrial sites.  Provides excellent protection from cuts and percussion."
msgstr "一顶供工地或工厂的工人穿戴的硬塑料帽，能有效提供头部对斩击与钝击的保护。"

#. ~ Description of "fur hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A hat made from the pelts of animals.  Extremely warm."
msgstr "一顶由动物毛皮制成的帽子。保暖效果非常好。"

#. ~ Description of "straw hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A hat woven out of straw.  Its brim helps keep the sun out of your eyes."
msgstr "一顶由麦秸或其他坚韧植物编织而成的帽子，宽大的帽檐能够保护你的眼睛不受太阳直射。"

#. ~ Description of "eboshi"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A high, black cap with a very narrow top.  Traditionally worn by Shinto priests."
msgstr "一顶通常由神道教的祭司穿戴的黑色尖顶高帽。"

#. ~ Description of variant "witch hat" of item "wizard hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A pointed black hat with a broad brim."
msgstr "一顶适合女巫戴的尖顶帽。"

#. ~ Description of "wizard hat"
#. ~ Description of variant "wizard hat" of item "wizard hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A pointed blue hat with stars stitched into it."
msgstr "一顶镶有许多星星的蓝色尖顶帽。戴着它可以增加你的最大魔力值。"

#. ~ Description of "Santa hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A red hat with white faux fur trim, commonly used by bearded men on Christmas."
msgstr "一顶装饰着白色人造毛皮的红色帽子，常被那个在圣诞节出现的长胡子男人使用。"

#. ~ Description of "hunting cap"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A red plaid hunting cap with ear flaps.  Notably warm."
msgstr "一顶扁扁的、两侧有御寒耳罩的毛毡制猎帽，非常保暖。"

#. ~ Description of "aluminum foil hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A sheet of aluminum foil that has been molded into a form-fitting hat.  Perfect for protecting yourself from the government, Illuminati, aliens, and THEM."
msgstr "用一块铝箔纸折折叠叠而成的一顶合身的帽子。保护你免受来自政府、神棍、外星人，还有\"他们\"对你的伤害。"

#. ~ Description of "patrol cap"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A simple round cap in a camouflage pattern.  Often used by the military when helmets aren't needed.  Its brim helps keep the sun out of your eyes."
msgstr "迷彩图案简约圆形帽子。  军队在不需要头盔时经常使用。  它的边缘有助于防止阳光照射到您的眼睛。"

#. ~ Description of "newsboy cap"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A slouching wool cap with a short front brim, traditionally associated with newspaper delivery boys.  Quite warm."
msgstr ""
"一顶低檐、软帽包裹住整个后脑勺的报童帽，曾经是送报童们的标志性帽子，比较保暖。\n"
"\"我亲眼看到一个骑着自行车的报童丢报纸把我家玻璃砸碎了。\""

#. ~ Description of "zucchetto"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A small, crimson skullcap.  Traditionally worn by Catholic priests."
msgstr "一顶较小的深红色无檐帽。一般是天主教神父常戴着它。"

#. ~ Description of "knit hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A snug-fitting wool hat.  Very warm."
msgstr "一顶贴身的羊毛帽。保暖效果非常好。"

#. ~ Description of "beret"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A soft cap that fits snugly about the head with a bit of slack on top."
msgstr "柔软的帽子，紧贴头部，顶部有一点松弛。"

#. ~ Description of "wool beret"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A soft felt cap that fits snugly about the head with a bit of slack on top."
msgstr "柔软的毡帽，紧贴头部，顶部稍宽松。"

#. ~ Description of "faux fur hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A stylish hat made of faux fur.  Like real fur, but without the suffering, if the tag is to be believed.  Very warm."
msgstr "一顶用人造毛皮制成的时髦帽子。像真正的毛皮，如果真如标签所说的话，制造过程不会杀害野生动物。十分保暖。"

#. ~ Description of "kippah"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A thin, rounded skullcap.  A traditional headdress in Judaism."
msgstr "一顶轻薄的圆形无边便帽，是犹太教教徒的传统服饰。"

#. ~ Description of "toque"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A traditional chef's hat, standing tall and proud against the vulgarities of the world."
msgstr "一定传统的厨师帽，高耸而骄傲地对抗着尘世的凡俗。"

#. ~ Description of "mail carrier hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A traditional mail carrier's cap, with the US postal service logo embroidered on the front above the plastic brim.  A symbol of a bygone world."
msgstr "一顶塑料帽檐上方印着美国邮政服务标志、传统样式的邮差帽。"

#. ~ Description of "beanie"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A warm knit hat."
msgstr "针织帽"

#. ~ Description of "chaplet"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "A wreath headdress made from plant material woven into a ring."
msgstr "一种由植物材料制成的环状头饰。"

#. ~ Description of "boonie hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "Also called a \"bucket hat.\" Often used in the military.  Its wide brim helps keep the sun out of your eyes."
msgstr ""
"一顶有一圈较为宽大、略成梯形的遮阳边缘的帽子，多为特战部队使用于各个恶劣的作战环境之中。\n"
"\"永别了，普莱斯上尉。\""

#. ~ Description of "eight point cap"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "Also known as a utility cover or utility cap, this is an eight pointed hat with a baseball-style visor at the front.  Commonly worn by Marines and sailors, this hat is the standard headwear of both the United States Marine Corps and Navy."
msgstr "也被称为工作帽或作训帽，这是一顶八角帽，前面有棒球风格的帽舌。这顶帽子常见于海军陆战队和水手，是美国海军陆战队和海军的标准头饰。"

#. ~ Description of "drinking hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "An improvised harness that can be worn over other headgear or by itself, made from two small liquid containers, a rubber hose, a bundle of steel wire, and some cordage.  A convenient and simple device for hands-free drinking, though it's not watertight and would spill if you put it into your backpack."
msgstr "这套简单的自制装置由两个小型容器、一根塑胶管、一捆铁线和一些绳索制成，戴在头上之后不需要用手就可以方便地喝水。不过，如果你把它放进背包，里面的水就会洒掉。"

#. ~ Description of "bowler hat"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "An old-fashioned gentleman's cap with a domed crown and a short, rounded brim."
msgstr "老式绅士帽，有圆顶帽冠和短圆形帽檐。"

#. ~ Description of "sombrero"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "An orange felt sombrero with traditional white and yellow hand stitching.  The wide brim keeps the sun out of your eyes, and a thin strap hooks around your chin."
msgstr "一顶橙色的墨西哥毛毡宽边帽，装饰着传统白黄相间的手工刺绣图案。宽大的帽檐能够保护你的眼睛不受阳光直射，同时还有一条细细的绑带钩住你的下巴。"

#. ~ Description of "turban"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "Cloth wound around the head, worn by people of many cultures worldwide."
msgstr "世界各地不同文化背景的人们都佩戴缠绕在头上的布。"

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "kerchief"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "Cover mouth"
msgstr "覆盖嘴部"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "French maid hat"
msgid_plural "French maid hats"
msgstr[0] "法式女仆头饰"

#. ~ Description of "noise canceling headgear"
#: data/json/items/armor/hats.json
msgid "Padding over your ears, kept in place by some string.  Blocks incoming sounds."
msgstr "一个用来隔绝外界噪音的头戴式耳罩。"

