#. ~ Description of "clip-on tie"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A clip-on necktie with blue and silver stripes.  It's quick and easy to put on, and really, who's going to know the difference?"
msgstr "一根有着蓝色和银色条纹的夹式领带。夹式领带便于穿戴，而且说真的，谁会知道它们的差别呢？"

#. ~ Description of "clown wig"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A colorful and ridiculous wig fit for a clown."
msgstr "一顶五颜六色的滑稽搞笑的小丑假发。"

#. ~ Description of "golden crown"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A delicate golden crown."
msgstr "金冠"

#. ~ Description of "gum blanket"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A fabric sheet which has been coated in liquid rubber, allowing it to serve as a raincoat, a work surface, or with a little know-how, part of an improvised shelter."
msgstr "一块涂了液体橡胶的布，可以用作雨衣、工作台，或者稍微懂点技巧的话，还能当临时的简易庇护所的一部分。"

#. ~ Description of "golden crown"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A golden crown for the monarch of survivors."
msgstr "一顶幸存者之王的金冠。"

#. ~ Description of "wedding veil"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A lacy white wedding veil."
msgstr "一个带有花边的结婚面纱。"

#. ~ Description of "rolled fur sleeping bag"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A large sleeping bag lined with fur, with a strap for carrying it on your back when not in use.  Who needs a tent?  Activate it to unroll it so you can use it for warmth."
msgstr "一个可以把你从头到脚包住的内衬毛皮的大睡袋，不用时可以用袋子扎起来背在背上。谁还需要帐篷呢。它现在绑好了；使用它来取暖。"

#. ~ Description of "fur sleeping bag"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A large sleeping bag lined with fur, with a strap for carrying it on your back when not in use.  Who needs a tent?  It is currently unrolled; activate it roll it up for easy storage."
msgstr "一个可以把你从头到脚包住的内衬毛皮的大睡袋，不用时可以用袋子扎起来背在背上。谁还需要帐篷呢。当前已展开；使用它把它绑好，便于存放。"

#. ~ Description of "rolled sleeping bag"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A large sleeping bag that covers you head to toe, with a strap for carrying it on your back when not in use.  This one is medium weight.  Activate it to unroll it so you can use it for warmth."
msgstr "一个可以把你从头到脚包住的大睡袋，不用时可以用带子扎起来背在背上。这个是中等重量的型号。它现在绑好了；使用它来取暖。"

#. ~ Description of "necktie"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A length of fabric typically looped around the collar of a dress shirt.  Knowing how to properly tie it takes some practice, but it's an important skill to learn.  Clip-ons are for children."
msgstr "一根普通的绿色领带，知道如何正确地打领带需要一些练习，但这是一项需要学习的重要技能。夹式领带是给孩子们戴的。"

#. ~ Description of "Boston-Chan wig"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A long blue hair wig for the Boston-Chan costume."
msgstr "波士顿酱cosplay套装中的蓝色长假发。"

#. ~ Description of "skinny tie"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A necktie much narrower than usual, popularized by mid-century rock musicians and an enduring symbol of subculture ever since, it can nonetheless still serve as a high-class accessory."
msgstr "一种比平常窄得多的领带，由二十世纪中期的摇滚音乐家推广，自此成为亚文化的持久象征，然而它仍然可以作为高雅的配饰使用。"

#. ~ Description of "plastic vampire fangs"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A pair of white vampire fangs made of plastic."
msgstr "一对白色的塑料吸血鬼尖牙。"

#. ~ Description of "tarpaulin"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A plastic sheet with several grommets for securing it with rope or cord.  Useful for improvised rain protection."
msgstr "用绳子或线固定的塑料片，还算有效的临时防雨措施。"

#. ~ Description of "protective mouthpiece"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A protective piece of equipment commonly used by athletes, worn inside the mouth to protect your teeth."
msgstr "一个拳击运动员常用的保护性装备。戴在嘴里以保护牙齿。"

#. ~ Description of "clown nose"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A red rubber nose, the sort often worn by clowns."
msgstr "一个小丑常戴的红色乳胶假鼻子。"

#. ~ Description of "tefillin (head)"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A set of leather straps attached to a wooden box, to fulfil the commandment written in Deuteronomy that states \"And you shall set these words of Mine upon your heart and upon your soul, and bind them for a sign upon your hand and they shall be for ornaments between your eyes.\"  This one is for the forehead."
msgstr "一套皮带系在一个木盒子上，以履行在申命记写下的戒律: “你们要把我的这些话放在你们的心上和灵魂上，绑在你们的手上作记号，在你们的眼睛之间作装饰品。” 这个是头部使用的。"

#. ~ Description of "tefillin (left arm)"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A set of leather straps attached to a wooden box, to fulfil the commandment written in Deuteronomy that states \"And you shall set these words of Mine upon your heart and upon your soul, and bind them for a sign upon your hand and they shall be for ornaments between your eyes.\"  This one is for the left arm."
msgstr "一套皮带系在一个木盒子上，以履行在申命记写下的戒律: “你们要把我的这些话放在你们的心上和灵魂上，绑在你们的手上作记号，在你们的眼睛之间作装饰品。” 这个是给左臂用的。"

#. ~ Description of "tefillin (right arm)"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A set of leather straps attached to a wooden box, to fulfil the commandment written in Deuteronomy that states \"And you shall set these words of Mine upon your heart and upon your soul, and bind them for a sign upon your hand and they shall be for ornaments between your eyes.\"  This one is for the right arm."
msgstr "一套皮带系在一个木盒子上，以履行在申命记写下的戒律: “你们要把我的这些话放在你们的心上和灵魂上，绑在你们的手上作记号，在你们的眼睛之间作装饰品。” 这个是给右臂用的。"

#. ~ Description of "bow tie"
#: data/json/items/armor/misc.json
msgid "A simple black bow tie.  Best worn with a suit."
msgstr "一个简单的领结，搭配西装更佳。"

