#. ~ Description of "boiled large human stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A boiled stomach from a large humanoid creature, nothing else.  It looks all but appetizing."
msgstr "一个煮熟的人型动物胃囊，看起来丝毫不能引起食欲。"

#. ~ Description of "large boiled stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A boiled stomach from an animal, nothing else.  It looks all but appetizing."
msgstr "一个煮熟的动物胃囊，看起来丝毫不能引起食欲。"

#. ~ Description of "putrid heart"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A cartliginous knot of flesh the size of a small pumpkin, superficially resembling a mammalian heart and covered in ribbed grooves.  It's still full of whatever passes for blood in jabberwocks, and is heavy in your hands.  After everything you've seen lately, you can't help but remember old sayings about eating the hearts of your enemies…"
msgstr "一个巨大而沉重的肉块，无疑比你的头还要大，看上去外形和哺乳动物的心脏一个样，上面布满了凸起的纹路。它仍然充满了伽卜沃克的血液，握起来沉甸甸的。在见识过最近所发生的这一切景象后，你不禁想起了那个吃下敌人心脏的传说……"

#. ~ Description of "cooked piece of lung"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A chewy, grayish lump of flavorless connective tissue.  It doesn't look any tastier than it did raw, but any parasites are all cooked out."
msgstr "一块无味且很难嚼的灰色结缔组织。看起来并不比生的好吃，但起码寄生虫都被煮熟了。"

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw human brain"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A chunk of brain from a human.  Eating this may cause kuru, but you probably won't live long enough to care about that anyway."
msgstr "一块人类大脑。吃这个可能会导致库鲁病，但不管怎么算你都不太可能活得足够长来担心这个。"

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw brain"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A chunk of brain from an animal.  You wouldn't want to eat this raw…"
msgstr "一块来自某种动物的大脑。你可不想生吃这玩意……"

#. ~ Description of "cooked fatty meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A chunk of cooked fatty meat.  Although absent of vitamins, it is very filling and delightfully greasy."
msgstr "一块刚煮好的猪肚腩肥肉，虽然缺乏维生素，但很管饱且非常油腻。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A chunk of cooked meat.  It's filling and nutritious, but unseasoned and a bit bland."
msgstr "一块经过简单烹饪的肉。能够填饱肚子，营养也还丰富，但没有调过味，吃上去有点枯燥乏味。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked lobster"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A chunk of delicious cooked lobster meat."
msgstr "一大块煮熟的美味龙虾肉。"

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw human kidney"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A chunk of kidney from a human, which appears to have been extracted too crudely to ever be useful as a transplant."
msgstr "一块人肾的一部分。割取手法太粗糙了，无法用作器官移植。"

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw kidney"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A chunk of kidney from an animal.  Preparing it for cooking is a challenge unless you want the kitchen to smell strongly of urine."
msgstr "一块来自某种动物的肾脏。如何烹饪它是一个挑战，除非你希望整个厨房充满那种强烈的尿骚味。"

#. ~ Description of "human flesh"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A chunk of raw meat, butchered from a human body."
msgstr ""
"一块从人身上切下来的生肉。\n"
"\"生人勿扰\""

#. ~ Description of "chunk of meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A chunk of raw meat.  You could eat it as-is, but cooking it is better."
msgstr "一块生肉。你可以就这样吃掉，但煮熟更好。"

#. ~ Description of "chunk of lobster meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A chunk of uncooked lobster meat."
msgstr "一大块未煮过的龙虾肉。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked foul meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A cooked chunk of meat from a mutated animal.  It still looks and smells all wrong."
msgstr "一块煮熟的变异动物肉。它看起来和闻起来都不太对劲。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked fish"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A cooked fish fillet.  Very nutritious."
msgstr "一份煮熟的鱼片，营养非常丰富。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked human flesh"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A cooked portion of human flesh."
msgstr "异形熟碎肉"

#. ~ Description of "chunk of porkbelly"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A fatty cut of pork from the belly, popular in some cuisine.  With proper technique, it can be used to create bacon.  Not safe to consume in its current raw form."
msgstr "一块来自猪肚腩的肥肉，是用来烹饪某些特定菜肴的原料，在经过特殊腌制处理后，也可以用来熏制成培根。不适合直接生吃，加工一下会更安全。"

#. ~ Description of "tainted hide"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A ghastly skin marred by decay.  It sloughs apart like wet newspaper when handled, and the smell is intolerable."
msgstr "可怕的皮肤已腐烂。  处理时它会像湿报纸一样脱落，而且气味令人难以忍受。"

#. ~ Description of "purged gastropods"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A handful of lucky gastropods that have been prepared for cooking by repeatedly boiling and washing them to remove their mucus and pathogens."
msgstr "一把幸运的腹足类动物，通过反复煮沸和清洗以去除粘液和病原体，已经准备好用于烹饪了。"

#. ~ Description of "large slab of uncut bacon"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A huge slab of uncut smoked bacon.  You can eat it as is, but it would be more efficient to cut it into smaller portions with a knife."
msgstr "一大块未切开的熏培根肉。可以直接吃，但用刀把它切片后食用不会太浪费。"

#. ~ Description of "pickled offal"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A mass of entrails and organ meat, preserved in brine.  Packed with essential vitamins, and although it looks like a lab specimen, it actually tastes pretty palatable."
msgstr "一份在盐水中保存的内脏和肠子。富含人体所需的各种维生素，虽然它看起来像一个实验室标本，但其实尝起来味道还行。"

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw human liver"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A piece of liver from a human, which appears to have been extracted too crudely to ever be useful as a transplant."
msgstr "一块人肝的一部分。割取手法太粗糙了，无法用作器官移植。"

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw liver"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A piece of liver from an animal.  Although many dislike its texture, it's one of the more vitamin-rich parts of the animal.  It is very good in sausages, but maybe a little less appetizing when cooked on its own."
msgstr "一块来自某种动物的肝脏。虽然许多人不喜欢这种口感，但它是动物中维生素含量较高的部位之一。制成香肠会很美味，但如果仅仅是煮熟的话，就不那么可口了。"

#. ~ Description of "chunk of tainted meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A piece of meat that's obviously unhealthy.  You could eat it, but it will poison you."
msgstr "一块散发着恶心的味道的肉，一看就非常不健康。你可以吃，但是会让你中毒。"

#. ~ Description of "chunk of mi-go flesh"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A piece of spongelike pink flesh.  It's nearly as hard as wood at its core, with an armored crust lining the exterior.  The smell suggests it is definitely not edible."
msgstr "一块海绵状的粉红色血肉。其核心坚硬如木，外层覆盖着装甲般的硬壳。气味表明它绝对不可食用。"

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw human sweetbread"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A piece of the thymus or pancreas of a human, which appears to have been extracted too crudely to ever be useful as a transplant."
msgstr "一块人胸腺或是胰腺的一部分。割取手法太粗糙了，无法用作器官移植。"

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw sweetbread"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A piece of the thymus or pancreas of an animal.  These are a delicacy, if prepared properly."
msgstr "一块动物的胸腺或胰腺。如果料理得当，会是美味佳肴。"

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw heart"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A portion of an animal's heart.  It's tough but not that chewy, and it spoils very quickly."
msgstr "动物的心脏切片。口感偏韧但不算难嚼，腐败速度极快。"

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw human heart"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A portion of heart from a human.  It's tough but not that chewy, and it spoils very quickly.  It appears to have been extracted too crudely to ever be useful as a transplant."
msgstr "一块人肺的一部分。看上去像粉红色的海绵状物体，而且很容易腐败。割取手法太粗糙了，无法用作器官移植。"

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw human lung"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A portion of lung from a human.  It's spongy and pink, and spoils very quickly.  It appears to have been extracted too crudely to ever be useful as a transplant."
msgstr "一块人肺的一部分。看上去像粉红色的海绵状物体，而且很容易腐败。割取手法太粗糙了，无法用作器官移植。"

#. ~ Description of "piece of raw lung"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A portion of lung from an animal.  It's spongy and pink, and spoils very quickly.  It can be a delicacy if properly prepared - but if improperly prepared, it's a chewy lump of flavorless connective tissue."
msgstr "一块来自某种动物的肺脏。看上去像粉红色的海绵状物体，而且很容易腐败。如果料理得当，它也能够变成一道美味；但如果料理不当，它就是一大块枯燥乏味的结缔组织。"

#. ~ Description of "frog legs"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A raw pair of frog legs.  Tastes like chicken when cooked or smoked."
msgstr "一对生的蛙后腿。烹调或熏制之后尝起来像鸡肉。"

#. ~ Description of "raw pelt"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A raw skin harvested from a fur-bearing animal.  You can cure it for storage and tanning, or scrape the fur off to get a clean hide."
msgstr "从毛皮动物身上采集的生皮。  您可以将其固化以便储存和晒黑，或者刮掉毛皮以获得干净的皮革。"

#. ~ Description of "raw human pelt"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A raw skin harvested from a fur-bearing mutant human.  It still has the fur attached.  You can cure it for storage and tanning, or eat it if you're desperate enough."
msgstr "一块从有毛皮的变异人身上仔细地削下来的生皮。还连着毛。你可以加工它来存储并进一步的鞣制，或者直接吃掉它，如果你的肚子里真的是一根毛都没有了的话。"

#. ~ Description of "raw hide"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A raw skin harvested from an animal.  You can cure it for storage and tanning, or eat it if you're desperate enough."
msgstr "从动物身上获取的生皮。  你可以将它处理起来储存和晒黑，或者如果你足够绝望的话可以吃掉它。"

#. ~ Description of "desiccated putrid heart"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A red-black strip of muscle - all that remains of a putrid heart that has been sliced open and drained of blood.  It could be eaten if you're hungry, but looks *disgusting*."
msgstr "一个巨大的肉块——这是将一颗腐化之心割开放血后所残存的部分。如果你实在是饿得发慌的话可以吃掉它，但是看上去*真的*很恶心。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked piece of heart"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A roasted piece of heart.  It doesn't look any tastier than it did raw, but any parasites are all cooked out."
msgstr "一块无味且很难嚼的灰色结缔组织。看起来并不比生的好吃，但起码寄生虫都被煮熟了。"

#. ~ Description of "tainted limb"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A rotted and then shredded arm.  Not much use unless you want to scrape the meat from the bones."
msgstr "一条腐烂然后被撕碎的手臂。  除非你想把骨头上的肉刮下来，否则没什么用。"

#. ~ Description of "tainted pelt"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A rotting pelt from some long-dead furry creature.  It's already too far gone to be tanned, and rapidly getting worse."
msgstr "一些死去已久的毛茸茸的生物的腐烂毛皮。  它已经太严重了，无法晒黑，而且还在迅速恶化。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked mutant bug organs"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A selection of cooked mutant bug organs.  Looks awful, but if you give it a try, you'll find -- that it's worse than it looks."
msgstr "一些煮熟的变异昆虫器官。看起来很糟糕，但如果你尝一尝，你会发现——它比看起来更糟糕。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked offal"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A selection of cooked organs and entrails.  Filled with essential vitamins, but pretty unappetizing in this form."
msgstr "一些煮熟的器官和内脏。富含必需的维生素，但就以这种形式吃下，令人有些反感。"

#. ~ Description of "raw offal"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A selection of uncooked internal organs and entrails.  Filled with essential vitamins, but most people consider it a bit gross unless it's very carefully prepared."
msgstr "一些屠宰时挑选出来的内脏，还未经烹饪。富含必需的维生素，但大多数人认为它有点恶心，除非它经过精心料理。"

#. ~ Description of "chunk of tainted human meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A slab of human flesh that stinks to high heaven.  The tissue is breaking down far too quickly."
msgstr "一块臭气熏天的人肉。组织分解得实在太快了。"

#. ~ Description of "boiled human stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A small boiled stomach from a human, nothing else.  It looks all but appetizing."
msgstr "一个煮熟的人胃，看起来丝毫不能引起食欲。"

#. ~ Description of "boiled stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A small boiled stomach from an animal, nothing else.  It looks all but appetizing."
msgstr "一个煮熟的某种动物的胃，看起来丝毫不能引起食欲。"

#. ~ Description of "portion of raw bone marrow"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A soft, spongy substance found in bones, rich in fat.  Chock-full of good stuff and doesn't taste too bad even raw, but beware of parasites."
msgstr "一种柔软的海绵状物质，存在于骨骼中，富含脂肪。包含各种营养，即使生的味道也不会太差，但要提防寄生虫。"

#. ~ Description of "seeping heart"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A thick mass of flesh superficially resembling a mammalian heart.  It's the size of your fist and covered in dimpled grooves."
msgstr "一块厚厚的肉，表面看起来像哺乳动物的心脏。它有你的拳头那么大，上面覆盖着多处凹陷。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked scrap of foul meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A tiny scrap of cooked meat from a mutated animal.  It still smells unappealing."
msgstr "一小片煮熟的变异动物肉。闻起来依然让人提不起食欲。"

#. ~ Description of "scrap of fish"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A tiny scrap of edible fish.  It's not much, but it'll do in a pinch."
msgstr "一小片可食用的鱼肉。虽然不多，但足以应急。"

#. ~ Description of "scrap of human flesh"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A tiny scrap of raw human flesh."
msgstr "一小块生的碎人肉。"

#. ~ Description of "scrap of foul meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A tiny scrap of raw meat from a heavily mutated animal.  It smells unappealing, to say the least."
msgstr "从严重变异的生物身上切下的一小块生肉。客气点说，闻起来不太诱人。"

#. ~ Description of "scrap of meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A tiny scrap of raw meat.  It's not much, but it'll do in a pinch."
msgstr "一小块生的碎肉。虽然量不多，但在紧要关头也是肉。"

#. ~ Description of "portion of tainted bone marrow"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A wet, green chunk of spongy goop extracted from a rotten bone.  It looks and smells all wrong."
msgstr "一块从腐骨中提取的湿漉漉的绿色海绵状黏糊糊的东西。看起来和闻起来都很不对劲。"

#. ~ Description of "portion of tainted bone marrow"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "A wet, green chunk of spongy goop extracted from a rotten bone.  You could eat it, but it will poison you."
msgstr "潮湿的绿色海绵状黏液，从腐烂的骨头中提取得来。你可以吃下它，但它会让你中毒。"

#. ~ Description of "fillet of fish"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "An uncooked fish fillet.  Makes a passable meal raw."
msgstr "一份生鱼片，生吃起来味道还过得去，但要当心寄生虫。"

#. ~ Description of "tainted innards"
#. ~ Description of "tainted human innards"
#. ~ Snippet in category "tainted_innards_desc"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json data/json/snippets/zombie_anatomy.json
msgid "An unidentifiable selection of rotted innards that barely hold their form.  It is revolting and certainly no longer healthy to eat."
msgstr "一些无法辨认的腐烂内脏，几乎无法保持其形状。  这是令人反感的，而且吃起来肯定不再健康。"

#. ~ Description of "mutant blood"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Blood extracted from a heavily mutated creature."
msgstr "从严重变异的生物身上提取的血液。"

#. ~ Description of "mutant human blood"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Blood extracted from a heavily mutated human."
msgstr "从严重变异的人类身上提取的血液。"

#. ~ Description of "human blood"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Blood extracted from a human being."
msgstr "从人体中提取的血液。"

#. ~ Description of "animal blood"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Blood extracted from a living creature."
msgstr "从活物中提取的血液。"

#. ~ Description of "roasted bone marrow"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Bone marrow, fully cooked to eliminate any parasites.  Tasty!"
msgstr "被完全烤熟以消除任何寄生虫的骨髓。好吃！"

#. ~ Description of "cooked piece of liver"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Chock-full of A- and B-Vitamins!  Cooked liver isn't all that bad, depending on how you feel about the texture, but this is probably the least fancy way to do it."
msgstr "一块来自某种动物的肝脏。富含维生素A和维生素B！煮熟的肝脏可能并不是最糟糕的，这取决于你是否喜欢这种口感，但这肯定是最不花哨的烹饪方式。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked gastropods"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Cooked gastropods.  A bit low on calories, but high in protein."
msgstr "煮熟的腹足类动物肉。热量有点低，但蛋白质含量高。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked cretin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Cooked meat from a heavily mutated humanoid.  Now that the worst bits have been picked out, it's probably digestible, if not very appetizing."
msgstr "一块煮熟的变异人肉。里面不好的部分已经被处理干净，虽然倒人胃口，不过大概是可以食用了。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked mollusk"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Cooked mollusk meat.  Devoid of any parasites or bacteria due to heat, the only thing left to do is add sauce."
msgstr "新煮熟软体动物肉。高温杀死了寄生虫和细菌，只需要加入些酱汁。"

#. ~ Description of "canned offal"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Cooked organ meat and entrails, preserved by canning.  Unappetizing, but filled with essential vitamins."
msgstr "一份密封在罐头里保存的熟内脏和肠子。看着很恶心，但富含人体所需的各种维生素。"

#. ~ Description of "fried meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Delicious oil-fried meat."
msgstr "一份美味的油煎肉。"

#. ~ Description of "butchery refuse"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Eugh.  This is a mess of dirt, excreta, connective tissue, and bits of matter like hair and claws, leftover from the butchering process.  Eating it isn't even worth thinking about."
msgstr "呕。一团泥土、粪便、结缔组织、以及诸如毛发爪子之类物质的混合物，屠宰之后留下来的残渣。吃下它连想都不要想。"

#. ~ Description of "smoked fish"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Fish that has been heavily smoked for long term preservation.  It could be further smoked to dehydrate it completely."
msgstr "为长期保存而经过重度熏制的鱼。可以进一步熏制使其完全脱水。"

#. ~ Description of "tainted blood"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Foul blood that's rapidly getting worse.  Separated from its owner, it seems intent on congealing into a disgusting jelly as fast as possible.  You could drink it, but it will poison you."
msgstr "污血正在迅速恶化。  与主人分离后，它似乎一心想尽快凝结成恶心的果冻。  你可以喝它，但它会让你中毒。"

#. ~ Description of "tainted human blood"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Foul human blood that's rapidly getting worse.  Separated from its owner, it seems intent on congealing into a disgusting jelly as fast as possible."
msgstr "恶臭的人血，正在迅速恶化。离开主人之后，它似乎急着要凝固成恶心的胶状物。"

#. ~ Description of "mi-go ichor"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Goo from inside a mi-go, perhaps some kind of blood?  It's obviously alien, given its pink color and strange, nostril-stinging odor.  It would not be advisable to try to drink it."
msgstr "米戈体内的粘液，也许是某种血液?鉴于其粉红的颜色和刺鼻的怪味，显然是外星生物的体液。不要尝试吃掉它，这并不明智。"

#. ~ Description of "smoked lobster"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Lobster that has been heavily smoked for long term preservation.  It could be further smoked to dehydrate it completely."
msgstr "为长期保存而经过重度熏制的龙虾。可以进一步熏制使其完全脱水。"

#. ~ Description of "smoked meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Meat that has been heavily smoked for preservation.  It could be further smoked to dehydrate it completely."
msgstr "为长期保存而经过重度熏制的肉。可以进一步熏制使其完全脱水。"

#. ~ Description of "smoked mollusk"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Mollusk meat that has been heavily smoked for long term preservation.  It could be further smoked to dehydrate it completely."
msgstr "为长期保存而经过重度熏制的软体动物肉。可以进一步熏制使其完全脱水。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked piece of kidney"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "No, this is not beans."
msgstr "一块来自某种动物的肾脏。不，它们不是豆子。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked piece of sweetbread"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Normally a delicacy, but this style of preparation is missing something."
msgstr "大体上味道不错，但这种烹饪方式还是缺了什么东西。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked piece of brain"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Now you can emulate those zombies you love so much!  Preparing brain for eating is challenging, and this doesn't seem to be the best way to do it."
msgstr "一块来自某种动物的大脑。现在煮熟后你可以模仿那些你所深爱的丧尸了！如何烹饪大脑很有挑战，而这看上去并不是最好的烹饪方式。"

#. ~ Description of "slab of raw curing porkbelly"
#. ~ Description of "slab of raw curing porkbelly (obsolete)"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json data/json/obsoletion_and_migration/obsoletion.json
msgid "Porkbelly in the process of becoming fully cured with salt and sugar, capable of becoming bacon.  The flavor is slowly developing at this stage, and is significantly unpleasant due to the residual salt.  Activate it once completed to make use of the final product."
msgstr "一块正在用盐和糖腌制的五花肉，腌制后能被熏制成培根。在这个阶段，风味物质正在其中缓慢积累，但仍然残留着多到令人咋舌的盐。腌制完成后使用它以获得成品。"

#. ~ Description of "slab of raw cured porkbelly"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Porkbelly that has been preserved and flavored with salt and sugar to draw out the moisture from the first layer.  Still raw, it is ready for smoking into bacon."
msgstr "用盐和糖腌制并调味过的五花肉，表皮已经略微脱水。仍然是生的，但可以用来熏制培根了。"

#. ~ Description of "mutant humanoid meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Raw meat butchered from the body of a heavily mutated creature that was unsettlingly humanoid in appearance.  It has odd bits of fur and other tissue lodged in it that clearly don't belong.  You'd have to be crazy or starving to eat this."
msgstr "从严重变异的人形生物身上切下的生肉块，内部散布着小块毛皮和其它显然不该长出来的组织。除非你疯了，否则在饿死之前你不会考虑吃这个。"

#. ~ Description of "chunk of foul meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Raw meat obviously taken from a heavily mutated animal.  It looks and smells all wrong."
msgstr "一块显然来自重度变异动物的生肉。它看起来和闻起来都不对劲。"

#. ~ Description of "mutant organs"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Raw organs from a giant mutant bug."
msgstr "从巨大的变异昆虫身上切下的奇怪器官，还是生的。"

#. ~ Description of "smoked tainted mutant meat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Rotten mutant meat that has been heavily smoked for preservation."
msgstr "腐烂的变异熏肉，为了保证质量经过烟熏处理，可以长期保存。"

#. ~ Description of "meat jerky"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Salty dried meat that lasts for a long time, but will make you thirsty."
msgstr "一块可以长期保存的咸肉干，会使人越吃越渴。"

#. ~ Description of "tainted skin scraps"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Shredded scraps of raw skin from an unnatural creature.  It can't have much use."
msgstr "从怪物身上剥下来的生皮碎片。它没有什么用。"

#. ~ Description of "portion of raw mutant bone marrow"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Soft, spongy and oddly-colored marrow tissue from the bone of a heavily mutated animal."
msgstr "柔软、海绵状和颜色奇特的骨髓组织，从某种高度变异动物骨骼中提取得来。"

#. ~ Description of "portion of raw mutant human bone marrow"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Soft, spongy and oddly-colored marrow tissue from the bone of a heavily mutated creature that was unsettlingly humanoid in appearance."
msgstr "柔软、海绵状和颜色奇特的骨髓组织，从某种高度变异类人生物骨骼中提取得来。"

#. ~ Description of "portion of raw human bone marrow"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "Soft, spongy marrow tissue from a human bone."
msgstr "柔软、海绵状骨髓组织，从人骨中提取得来。"

#. ~ Description of "raw human skin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "The flayed hide of a human being.  You can cure it for storage and tanning, or eat it if you're desperate enough."
msgstr "一张小心翼翼从人类身上剥下并折叠起来的生皮。你可以加工它以方便储存和鞣制，如果你饿疯了也可以就这样吃掉。"

#. ~ Description of "fillet of mollusk"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "The raw flesh of a mollusk.  Must be cleaned and cooked before eating."
msgstr "软体动物的生肉。食用前必须清洗和煮熟。"

#. ~ Description of "human stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "The stomach of a human.  It is surprisingly durable."
msgstr "人的胃囊，令人意外的耐磨。"

#. ~ Description of "mutant human stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "The stomach of a large humanoid creature.  It is surprisingly durable."
msgstr "大型人型生物的胃囊，令人意外的耐磨。"

#. ~ Description of "large mutant stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "The stomach of a large mutated creature.  It is surprisingly durable."
msgstr "大型变异生物的胃。  它出奇地耐用。"

#. ~ Description of "large stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "The stomach of a large woodland creature.  It is surprisingly durable."
msgstr "一个大型林地生物的胃囊，十分的耐磨，经过加工后可以用作简单的工具，或有其它用途。"

#. ~ Description of "mutant stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "The stomach of a mutated creature.  It is clearly malformed and smells revolting."
msgstr "变异生物的胃。  它明显畸形并且散发出令人作呕的气味。"

#. ~ Description of "stomach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json
msgid "The stomach of a woodland creature.  It is surprisingly durable."
msgstr "一个林地生物的胃囊，十分的耐磨，经过加工后可以用作简单的工具，或有其它用途。"

#. ~ Description of "tainted limb"
#. ~ Snippet in category "leg_zed_desc"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/carnivore.json data/json/snippets/zombie_anatomy.json
msgid "What's left of some zombie's limb.  Most likely a leg based on the proportions.  Though it's rotted, there is quite a bit of meat still on it."
msgstr "一些僵尸的肢体剩下的部分。  根据比例最有可能是一条腿。  虽然已经腐烂了，但上面还是有不少肉的。"

