#. ~ Description of "large cattle fodder bundle"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A big heap of cattle fodder, enough to feed a cow for a day."
msgstr "一大捆家畜饲料，可以让一头牛吃一天。"

#. ~ Description of "earthworm"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A common earthworm."
msgstr "一条普通的蚯蚓。"

#. ~ Description of "boiled earthworms"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A handful of common earthworms, boiled to remove impurities."
msgstr "一把普通的蚯蚓，煮过后去除杂质。"

#. ~ Description of "fried earthworms"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A handful of fried earthworms, cooked in salt."
msgstr "一把用盐烹制的炸蚯蚓。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked beans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A hearty serving of cooked beans."
msgstr "一份热腾腾香喷喷的野生米饭。"

#. ~ Description of "chunk of beeswax"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A large chunk of beeswax.  Despite being used in some cooking recipes, beeswax in itself is indigestible to humans."
msgstr "一大块蜂蜡。尽管会在一些食谱中使用，但蜂蜡本身对人类而言是难以消化的。"

#. ~ Description of "honey comb"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A large chunk of wax filled with honey.  Very tasty."
msgstr "一大块涂满了蜂蜜的蜡，超级美味。"

#. ~ Description of "slime glob"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A little hunk of glop that fell off a slime monster.  It doesn't seem hostile, but it does wiggle occasionally."
msgstr "一小块从变形怪身上掉下的糊状物，似乎已经没有了敌意，但偶尔会蠕动几下。"

#. ~ Description of "seed paste"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A mass of ground seeds that are ready to be pressed into oil."
msgstr "一大团磨碎的种子，准备用来榨油。"

#. ~ Description of "napkin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A napkin.  Can be used for fires."
msgstr "一张纸巾。可以用来生火。"

#. ~ Description of "chamomile tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A paper sachet with dried chamomile inside.  Put it into boiling water to make a cup of chamomile tea."
msgstr "一个装满了干洋甘菊的小纸袋。把它丢进一杯开水里就能泡出甘菊茶了。"

#. ~ Description of "dandelion tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A paper sachet with dried dandelion roots inside.  Put it into boiling water to make a cup of dandelion tea."
msgstr "一个装满了干蒲公英根茎的小纸袋。把它丢进一杯开水里就能泡出蒲公英茶了。"

#. ~ Description of "herbal tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A paper sachet with dried wild herbs inside.  Put it into boiling water to make a cup of herbal tea."
msgstr "一个装满了干草药的小纸袋。把它丢进一杯开水里就能泡出草药茶了。"

#. ~ Description of "fruit tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A paper sachet with leaves and fruit parts inside.  Put it into boiling water to make a cup of fruit tea."
msgstr "一个装满了草叶和干果的小纸袋。把它丢进一杯开水里就能泡出果茶了。"

#. ~ Description of "black tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A paper sachet with tea leaves inside.  Put it into boiling water to make a cup of black tea."
msgstr "一个装满了茶叶的小纸袋。把它丢进一杯开水里就能泡出红茶了。"

#. ~ Description of "green tea bag"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A paper sachet with tea leaves inside.  Put it into boiling water to make a cup of green tea."
msgstr "一个装满了茶叶的小纸袋。把它丢进一杯开水里就能泡出绿茶了。"

#. ~ Description of "piece of cardboard"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A piece of cardboard."
msgstr "硬纸板"

#. ~ Description of "cattle fodder bundle"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A pile of cattle fodder, about enough to feed a goat or a sheep for a day."
msgstr "一捆家畜饲料，基本可以让一只山羊或者绵羊吃一天。"

#. ~ Description of "yeast"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A powder-like mix of cultured yeast, good for baking and brewing alike."
msgstr "一份人工培育的粉末状酵母，可以用于烘培或者酿造。"

#. ~ Description of "yogurt starter culture"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A powder-like mix of cultured yogurt bacteria, good for fermenting yogurt."
msgstr "一种由用于发酵酸奶的细菌混合而成的粉末状混合物，用于发酵酸奶。"

#. ~ Description of "garden snail"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A small gastropod harvested from the bushes.  These are dangerous to consume raw, but could be worth cooking if you got enough of them."
msgstr "一只从灌木丛中找到的小型腹足动物。生吃十分危险，但如果你找到足够多的蜗牛，可以把它们洗净处理。"

#. ~ Description of "instant coffee mix"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A small packet of commercial instant coffee powder.  No creamer or sweetener added."
msgstr "一小包商品化的速溶咖啡粉。未添加奶油或甜味剂。"

#. ~ Description of "small plant"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A small plant or flower, edible by grazers and ruminants only.  Seeing this item is a bug."
msgstr "一株小型植物或花卉，只能被食草动物和反刍动物食用。该物品不应该出现在正常游戏中。"

#. ~ Description of "honeydew"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A sugar-rich sticky substance, produced by aphids from plant sap.  Ants and bees love it."
msgstr "一种富含糖的粘性物质，由吸取植物汁液的蚜虫产生。蚂蚁和蜜蜂都喜欢它。"

#. ~ Description of "swarm of bees"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A swarm of honey bees, displaced from the hive.  Without the support and nutrients of an apiary, or taking root somewhere, they will die in a few days."
msgstr "从蜂巢或蜂箱里取出来的一群蜜蜂。如果没有蜂房的补给和营养，或者没有在某个地方筑巢，它们将在几天内死亡。"

#. ~ Description of "nut paste"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A thick mass of ground nuts that are ready to be pressed into oil."
msgstr "一大团磨碎的浓稠坚果，准备用来榨油。"

#. ~ Description of "royal jelly"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A translucent hexagonal chunk of wax, filled with dense, milky, bitter and acidic-tasting jelly.  Though some hold it as a panacea, it doesn't have any medical benefit.  Still it is rich with the most beneficial substances the hive can produce."
msgstr "一大块涂满了粘稠 、乳白色液体的半透明蜂窝蜡，尝起来有点苦涩和酸味。虽然有些人认为它是灵丹妙药，但它其实没有任何疗效。不过尽管如此它依然富含蜂群能制造的营养物质。"

#. ~ Description of "dried bottle gourd"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "A vegetable from the gourd family, bottle gourds were brought to the Americas by the first Native American settlers crossing the Bering strait.  This one has been dried for processing into a watertight container."
msgstr "一种葫芦科的蔬菜，由第一批穿越白令海峡的美洲土著定居者带到美洲。这个葫芦已经烘干，准备加工成一个水密容器。"

#. ~ Description of "akutaq"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Also called Inuit or Alaskan ice cream, this is a dense mix of solid fat and sugar that makes for a sweet dessert reminiscent of cake frosting.  It is a traditional food of people throughout the arctic, providing a massive amount of energy to fuel a difficult lifestyle in grueling conditions."
msgstr "这种冰淇淋也被称为因纽特冰淇淋或阿拉斯加冰淇淋，是由固体脂肪和糖的浓稠混合物制成，吃起来像蛋糕上的糖霜一样甜。它是北极地区人们的传统食物，能为他们在艰苦的环境中艰难的生活方式提供大量能量。"

#. ~ Description of "akutaq with fruit"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Also called Inuit or Alaskan ice cream, this is a dense mix of solid fat, fruit, and sugar that makes for a sweet dessert reminiscent of cake frosting.  It is a traditional food of people throughout the arctic, providing a massive amount of energy to fuel a difficult lifestyle in grueling conditions."
msgstr "这种冰淇淋也被称为因纽特冰淇淋或阿拉斯加冰淇淋，是由固体脂肪、水果和糖混合而成的浓稠混合物，吃起来像蛋糕上的糖霜一样甜。它是北极地区人们的传统食物，为他们在艰苦的环境中艰难的生活方式提供了大量的能量。"

#. ~ Description of "dried soybeans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Beige colored beans, dried until rock hard.  They'll need to be cooked or processed before use."
msgstr "干燥的米黄色的豆子，坚如磐石。它们在使用前需要经过烹饪或加工。"

#. ~ Description of "raw soybeans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Beige colored beans.  They have many uses, but in their raw form are fairly poisonous to humans."
msgstr "米黄色的豆子。它们有很多用途，但生吃对人类来说有剧毒。"

#. ~ Description of "blood rice pudding"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Blood rice pudding is a pastry made from blood and rice grains.  Best with chopped peanuts, but also good to eat with various seasonings."
msgstr "血米布丁是一种用血和大米做成的糕点。最好搭配花生碎，也可以搭配各种调料食用。"

#. ~ Description of "canned beans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Canned beans.  A staple among canned goods, these are reputedly good for one's coronary health."
msgstr "罐装豆子。罐头食品的标志性产品，据说有利于冠动脉健康。"

#. ~ Description of "canned tomato"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Canned tomato.  A staple in many pantries, and useful for many recipes."
msgstr "罐装番茄。厨房里常见的罐头食品，可以做很多种菜。"

#. ~ Description of "Kentucky coffee grounds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Coffee grounds created through washing, cleaning, and roasting the pods from a Kentucky coffeetree.  They can be used to create coffee."
msgstr "通过清洗、清洁和烘烤来自肯塔基州咖啡树的豆荚而形成的咖啡粉。它们可以用来制造类似咖啡的饮品。"

#. ~ Description of "dried beans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Dehydrated beans.  Tasty and nutritious when cooked, virtually inedible when dry."
msgstr "脱水的大北豆。煮熟以后美味又营养，但是干燥状态几乎不能食用。"

#. ~ Description of "dehydrated tofu"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Dehydrated tofu, sealed and still extra firm to last a long time."
msgstr "脱水豆腐，被密封保存。可以保存相当久的时间不腐坏。"

#. ~ Description of "powdered gelatin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Dried and powdered gelatin, used as a gelling agent when mixed with water."
msgstr "经过烘干的粉状明胶，当与水混合后变成凝胶。"

#. ~ Description of "dried earthworms"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Dried, cooked and ground earthworms."
msgstr "将蚯蚓晒干、煮熟并磨碎。"

#. ~ Description of "dry cat food"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Dry kibbles of cat food with a long shelf life.  Made from dried processed meats and grains, and enriched with vitamins and minerals."
msgstr "有较长保质期的干猫粮。由加工过的肉类和谷物制成，富含维生素和矿物质。"

#. ~ Description of "press cake"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Dry leftovers that remain after extracting the oil from nuts or seeds."
msgstr "一份坚果或种子榨油后留下的干燥残渣。"

#. ~ Description of "dry dog food"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Dry morsels of dog food with a long shelf life.  Made from dried processed meats and grains, and enriched with vitamins and minerals."
msgstr "有较长保质期的干犬粮。由加工过的肉类和谷物制成，富含维生素和矿物质。"

#. ~ Description of "fresh gelatin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Fresh gelatin.  Not vegan-friendly!"
msgstr "新鲜的明胶。不适合素食主义者！"

#. ~ Description of "extracted gelatin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Freshly extracted gelatin in a dilute acid solution.  It needs to be strained to separate the gelatin from the acid."
msgstr "在稀酸溶液中新鲜提取出的明胶。它需要过滤以将明胶和酸液分开。"

#. ~ Description of "coffee powder"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Ground coffee beans.  You can boil it into a mediocre stimulant, or something better if you had a coffee pot."
msgstr "研磨好的咖啡豆。你可以将其煮沸制成一杯普通的提神饮品，如果有咖啡壶的话，味道会更好。"

#. ~ Description of "candied honey"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Honey, that stuff the bees make.  The sugars have crystallized, but this doesn't affect the flavor or anything."
msgstr "亲爱的，那是蜜蜂做的东西。  糖已经结晶，但这不会影响味道或任何东西。"

#. ~ Description of "Mycus fruit"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Humans might call this a Gray Delicious apple: large, gray, and smells even better than the Marloss.  If they didn't reject it for its alien origins.  But we know better."
msgstr "人类也许称其为美味灰苹果：大且灰白，香味更甚于马洛斯梅。若那些人类不因其起源于异界而排斥，将会更加美妙。但吾等更清楚。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Kentucky coffee grounds"
msgid_plural "Kentucky coffee grounds"
msgstr[0] "肯塔基咖啡粉"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Marloss berry"
msgid_plural "Marloss berries"
msgstr[0] "马洛斯变异梅"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Marloss gelatin"
msgid_plural "Marloss gelatin"
msgstr[0] "马洛斯凝胶"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Mycus fruit"
msgid_plural "Mycus fruits"
msgstr[0] "马卡斯果"

#. ~ Description of "acid soaked hide"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Raw hide soaking in a dilute acid solution to extract collagen.  After 24 hours the solution can be strained to extract fresh gelatin."
msgstr "一块浸泡在稀酸溶液中提取胶原蛋白的生皮。在24小时后，将溶液过滤就能够提取出新鲜明胶。"

#. ~ Description of "raw edamame"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Raw soybeans still in their pod.  They can be cooked as-is or shelled for further processing, but in their raw form, they're toxic to humans."
msgstr "未去荚的豆子。它们可以直接烹饪，或者去壳进行进一步加工，但生吃对人类来说有毒。"

#. ~ Description of "grass"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Some grass, edible by grazers and ruminants only.  Seeing this item is a bug."
msgstr "一些草，只能被食草动物和反刍动物食用。该物品不应该出现在正常游戏中。"

#. ~ Description of "koji"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Some ground rice covered with a special kind of mold used for saccharification and fermentation in Japanese cuisine."
msgstr "一些表面覆盖着一种特殊的霉菌的碎米，在日本料理中用于糖化和发酵。"

#. ~ Description of "underbrush"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Some underbrush, edible by ruminants only.  Seeing this item is a bug."
msgstr "一些矮灌木丛，只能被反刍动物食用。该物品不应该出现在正常游戏中。"

#. ~ Description of "chewing gum"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "That gum you liked is probably not going to come back in style."
msgstr "你喜欢的口香糖可能不会再流行了。"

#. ~ Description of "chitin powder"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "This chitin powder can be used to craft fertilizer and some other things."
msgstr "一份甲壳粉，可以用来制造肥料和其他物品。"

#. ~ Description of "embalmed human brain"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "This is a human brain soaked in a solution of highly toxic formaldehyde.  Eating this would be a terrible idea."
msgstr "一个浸泡在含有剧毒的福尔马林中的人脑。吃下它会是个十分糟糕的主意。"

#. ~ Description of "wet cat food"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "This is wet food for cats, made from canned fresh meats.  It has a pungent aroma that cats seem to love."
msgstr "半湿猫粮，用罐装鲜肉制成。闻起来有点刺鼻，但是猫猫喜欢。"

#. ~ Description of "wet dog food"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "This is wet food for dogs, made from canned fresh meats.  It smells strange, but dogs seem to love it."
msgstr "半湿犬粮，用罐装鲜肉制成。闻起来很奇怪，但是狗狗喜欢。"

#. ~ Description of "Marloss berry"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "This looks like a blueberry the size of your fist, but pinkish in color.  It has a strong but delicious aroma, but is clearly either mutated or of alien origin."
msgstr "这看起来像拳头大小的蓝莓，但却有粉红色的颜色。香气浓郁，芬芳扑鼻，但显然经过了变异，或许是外星产物也说不准。"

#. ~ Description of "Marloss gelatin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "This looks like a handful of lemon-colored liquid which has taken a set, much like pre-Cataclysm Jello.  It has a strong but delicious aroma, but is clearly either mutated or of alien origin."
msgstr "这看起来就像凝固住的柠檬色液体，活像末日前的果冻。香气浓郁，芬芳扑鼻，但显然经过了变异，或许是外星产物也说不准。"

#. ~ Description of "tofu"
#. ~ Description of "fried tofu"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Tofu, a soy protein crucial to East Asian cuisine.  It absorbs flavors very well and can be used as a meat alternative in many dishes."
msgstr "豆腐，一道在东亚菜系中占据重要地位的菜肴，富含蛋白质。它能很好地吸收风味，在许多菜肴中可作为肉类替代品。"

#. ~ Description of "cooked lentils"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "Wet, cooked lentils.  Humble and nutrient-rich, but pretty bland."
msgstr "水煮熟的扁豆。简单且营养丰富，但味道寡淡。"

#. ~ Description of "bird food"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "What birds eat.  Mainly made of seeds, silage or legumes.  It's perfect for small birds."
msgstr "一些主要由种子、青贮或一些豆类制成的鸟食，小型鸟类非常喜欢吃。"

#. ~ Description of "cattle fodder"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "What cattle eat.  Mainly made of grass, silage or legumes.  It's perfect for ruminants."
msgstr "一些喂养家畜用的饲料，主要由草、青贮饲料或豆类等制成，适合奶牛等牲畜食用。"

