#. ~ Description of "starry false Solomon's seal berries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A bunch of deep red berries with a pleasant bittersweet flavor.  Can have a laxative effect if eaten in large quantities."
msgstr "一把深红色的浆果，有股令人愉悦的甘苦回甜的味道。大量食用可以通便。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of blackberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A darker cousin of the raspberry.  The color isn't actually what sets them apart - the identifying characteristic is whether the stem stays connected to the fruit when it's first picked."
msgstr "树莓的深色近亲。颜色并不是区分它们的关键——重点特征是首次采摘时，果梗是否与果实相连。"

#. ~ Description of "watermelon"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A deep green melon, bigger than your head.  It is very juicy!  You should be able to take it apart with a knife."
msgstr "一个深绿色的比你的头还大的多汁甜瓜！你应该能够用刀把它切开。"

#. ~ Description of "mango"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A fleshy tropical fruit with a large pit.  Better enjoy it soon, you're pretty sure more of these aren't going to be imported for a long time."
msgstr "多肉的热带水果，带有一个大果核。最好赶快吃掉，你十分确定，在很长一段时间内，再也不会有人进口这种东西了。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of chokeberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of black chokeberries.  They look similar to blackcurrant.  Big and juicy but actually exceedingly sour."
msgstr "一把黑色苦莓。  它们看起来与黑加仑相似。  又大又多汁，但实际上非常酸。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of cantaloupe melon chunks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of cantaloupe melon chunks.  A great snack by itself or in a fruit salad."
msgstr "一把哈密瓜块。可以直接吃，也可以用于制作水果沙拉。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of coconut flesh"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of coconut flesh.  It's surprisingly calorie-dense."
msgstr "椰子的果肉，卡路里含量惊人。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of nopales"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of edible pads from a cactus."
msgstr "一种仙人掌的肉质茎，可以作为蔬菜食用。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of elderberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of elderberries, toxic when eaten raw but great when cooked."
msgstr "一把接骨木果，生吃有毒，但煮熟后很美味。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of rose hips"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of fruits grown from pollinated rose flowers.  Full of irritating hairs and hard seeds, they'll need to be disassembled before eating."
msgstr "一些授粉成功的玫瑰花长成的果实。里面充满了扎人的毛刺和坚硬的种子，食用前需要先拆解。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of huckleberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of huckleberries, often times confused for blueberries."
msgstr "一把美洲越橘，经常会和蓝莓混淆。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of grapes"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of juicy grapes.  Quite calorie-dense compared to most fruit, and you might be able to make them into wine if you're ambitious enough."
msgstr "一串多汁的葡萄，与大多数水果相比，它的热量相当高。如果你有雄心壮志——以及耐心，还可以把它们酿成酒。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of pineapple chunks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of pineapple chunks.  Delicious and a great source of Vitamin C, though a bit sour."
msgstr "一捧菠萝果肉，十分美味，而且富含维生素C，就是有点酸。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of apricots"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of smooth-skinned fruits related to the peach."
msgstr "一把杏子，表皮很光滑，有着味甜多汁的暗黄色果肉，是桃子的近亲。"

#. ~ Description of "juice pulp"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of stringy pulp, left-over from juicing some kind of fruit.  It's not very tasty, but contains a lot of healthy fiber."
msgstr "一把粘稠的果肉，某种水果榨汁后剩下的。不太好吃，但富含膳食纤维。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of raspberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of sweet red berries, each with a hollow core."
msgstr "一把红色甜浆果，每颗都有一个空的果核。"

#. ~ Description of "wintergreen berries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of sweet, brilliant red berries of the wintergreen shrub."
msgstr "一把冬青灌木所结出的芬芳而鲜艳的红色浆果。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of blueberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of tasty sweet-tart berries.  They're blue, but that doesn't mean they're sad."
msgstr "一把美味的酸甜浆果。它们是蓝色的，但这并不意味着它们很伤心（blue）。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of strawberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of tasty, juicy red berries with visible seeds on the outside of the skin.  Often found growing wild in fields."
msgstr "一把美味多汁的红色浆果，果皮外面有可见的种子。经常可以在田野中找到野生的。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of cranberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of very bitter red berries, probably grown locally in Massachusetts.  Good for urinary tract health."
msgstr "一把红色的酸浆果，主要在马萨诸塞州当地生长。有益于泌尿道健康。"

#. ~ Description of "grapefruit"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A hybrid citrus fruit descended from the orange, whose taste ranges from sour to semi-sweet, and a little bitter."
msgstr "一种由橙子杂交而来的柑橘类水果，有酸味又有一点甜味，还略带苦味。"

#. ~ Description of "pear"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A juicy, bell-shaped pear.  Yum!"
msgstr "一个味美汁多，铃铛外形的梨子。甜中带酸，营养丰富，含有多种维生素和纤维素。"

#. ~ Description of "cantaloupe melon"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A large and very sweet orange fruit.  Technically a berry, like all melons are.  You should be able to take it apart with a knife."
msgstr "一种大而甜的橙色水果。严格地说是一种浆果，就像所有的甜瓜一样。你应该能够用刀把它切开。"

#. ~ Description of "plum"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A large purple plum.  Tasty and good for your digestion."
msgstr "一把紫色的大李子，饱满圆润，玲珑剔透，形态美艳，口味甘甜，美味又有助于消化。"

#. ~ Description of "kiwi"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A large, brown, and fuzzy-skinned berry.  Its delicious insides are green."
msgstr "一个大大的，有着棕色毛绒外皮的水果，绿色的果肉有着奇异的味道。"

#. ~ Description of "pineapple"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A large, spiky tropical fruit.  A tough rind protects the tasty flesh inside, and digging into it as-is would be pretty inefficient and messy.  You should find a knife or something vaguely knife-like to cut it up with."
msgstr "大而尖的热带水果。坚硬的外皮可以保护里面美味的果肉。想完整去掉果皮可是个技术活。当然也可以用\"迪拜刀法\"，前提是你有刀。"

#. ~ Description of "mutant fruit"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A leathery skin covers this purplish-brown little fruit.  It will need to be deconstructed before anything can be done with it."
msgstr "这个暗紫色小型水果上面覆盖着坚韧的果皮。需要将其拆解才能用它做别的事情。"

#. ~ Description of "banana"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A long, curved yellow fruit in a peel.  Some people like using them in desserts.  Those people are probably dead."
msgstr ""
"一种长弧形黄色可剥皮的水果，一些人喜欢拿来当饭后甜点。\n"
"\"但那些人已经死了。\""

#. ~ Description of "mayapple"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A small, edible fruit of an otherwise toxic plant.  You should not eat too many of them."
msgstr "一种小型可食用的浆果，来自有毒植物。你不应该吃太多。"

#. ~ Description of "orange"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A sweet citrus fruit.  Also comes in juice form.  In case you were wondering, the color is named after the fruit, not the other way around."
msgstr "一种甜柑橘类水果。可以榨成果汁。以免你真的会好奇为什么橙子是橙色：\"橙\"色是从水果得来的，而不是反过来。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of cherries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A sweet red fruit that grows on trees.  If you have some time on your hands, maybe you could figure out how to do that trick where you tie a knot in the stem with your tongue."
msgstr "一种长在树上的甜红色果实。如果你手头有一些时间，也许可以练习一下那个用舌头给樱桃梗打结的技巧。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of passionfruit"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A sweet, acidic fruit originating from South America.  It grows on vines and is filled with seeds like a pomegranate.  Also known as the maracuya."
msgstr "一种味道酸甜的水果，原产于南美洲，生长在藤蔓上，果实内长满了种子，像石榴一样。也被称为马拉库亚。"

#. ~ Description of "guava"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A sweet, sandy-textured fruit with pink flesh native to the Caribbean, Central America, and South America.  Great for making milkshakes."
msgstr "一种甜美的沙质水果，果肉呈粉红色，原产于加勒比海、中美洲和南美洲。非常适合制作奶昔。"

#. ~ Description of "crabapple"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A term used to describe both wild apples native to North America as well as less appetizing feral varieties, these are rather small and far too sour."
msgstr "北美本土的野生苹果属植物果实，或者苹果的味道不佳的野化品种。这些野苹果很小，而且太酸了。"

#. ~ Description of "coconut"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A tropical fruit with a hard, hairy shell and a hollow inside full of liquid and edible flesh.  If you want to eat it, you'll have to find something heavy to crack open the shell and something sharp to remove the 'meat'."
msgstr ""
"一种热带水果，外壳坚硬而多毛，保护着里面装着的汁水与果肉。想吃的话，要先找个钝器把壳砸开，再找个锐器把果肉刮下来。\n"
"\"从小喝到大\""

#. ~ Description of "lemon"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A very sour citrus fruit.  Can be eaten if you're desperate, but you should probably look for some other cooking application for this."
msgstr "一种非常酸的柑橘类水果。如果你真的很想直接吃，也不是不行，但你或许应该为它寻找一些别的料理用途。"

#. ~ Description of "papaya"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A very sweet and soft tropical fruit."
msgstr ""
"一个香甜软嫩的热带水果，由于有丰胸作用所以常常受到女性喜爱。\n"
"\"大！大！大！\""

#. ~ Description of "watermelon wedge"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A yummy wedge of watermelon.  A handheld snack that tastes like summer."
msgstr "一片美味的西瓜。一种有夏日味道的手持式小吃。"

#. ~ Description of "lulo"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "An acidic fruit found in South America and the Caribbean, it looks like a hairy orange and is used mainly for juice and desserts.  Also known as the naranjilla."
msgstr "一种产于南美洲和加勒比海的酸性水果，看起来像多毛的橘子，主要用于果汁和甜点。也被称为纳兰吉拉。"

#. ~ Description of "apple"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "An iconic and delicious fruit grown and enjoyed across the world, used for generations in folk medicine as doctor repellant."
msgstr ""
"一种\"标志性\"的美味水果，在世界各地都有种植和食用，世世代代在民间医学中用作医生驱避剂。\n"
"\"一天一苹果，医生远离我。\""

#. ~ Description of "peeled mutant fruit"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "Divested of its skin, this mutated fruit is revealed to be a nonsensical jumble of plant and animal matter.  Human hair and teeth grow from pithy blood-slick flesh, redolent with the scent of rotting mangoes."
msgstr "剥去果皮后，你发现这个变异水果是一团植物和动物组织的怪异混合体，人的头发和牙齿从多孔的带血肉块中长出，散发出如同腐烂芒果一般的气味。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of autumn olives"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "Not tasting anything like olives, this sweet, red and very nutritious fruit can also be used as a tomato-substitute in some cases."
msgstr "这种甜的、红色的、营养丰富的水果尝起来不像橄榄，在某些情况下也可以用作番茄的替代品。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of hobbleberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "Some black hobbleberries.  They are quite sweet.  Before they ripened, they were deceptively red and utterly bitter."
msgstr "一些黑色的霍贝尔莓。  他们很甜蜜。  在它们成熟之前，它们看起来是红色的，而且非常苦。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of nannyberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "Some dark blue nannyberries, tasting like prunes mixed with banana."
msgstr "一些深蓝色的南莓，尝起来像李子和香蕉的混合。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of tupelo fruits"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "Some dark blue tupelo fruits.  They are tart and feature a hard seed but are still enjoyable."
msgstr "一些深蓝色的图珀洛果实。  它们很酸，种子很硬，但仍然很美味。"

#. ~ Description of "cut rose hips"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "Tart little fruits grown from a rose bush, now separated from their inedible seeds and spines."
msgstr "玫瑰丛里长出的酸味小果实，已经去掉了不可食用的种子和毛刺。"

#. ~ Description of "cholla bud"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "The edible bud of a cholla cactus, with its spines removed; the candy of the Mojave indigenous peoples.  Tastes similar to asparagus."
msgstr "可食用的仙人掌花蕾，刺已经去掉了，是莫哈维沙漠土著的最爱。尝起来有点像芦笋。"

#. ~ Description of "peach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "This fruit's large pit is surrounded by its tasty flesh."
msgstr "一个近球形带条沟纹的桃子，表面有毛茸，肉质香甜可口，非常美味。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of mulberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "This red variety of mulberries is unique to eastern North America, and is said to have the strongest flavor of any variety in the world."
msgstr "一把北美桑椹，这种红色品种是北美东部所独有的，据说是世界上所有品种中风味最浓的一个品种。"

#. ~ Description of "pomegranate"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "Under this pomegranate's spongy skin lie hundreds of fleshy seeds."
msgstr "一个石榴，海绵一样的果皮下面有着数以百计被果肉包裹的种子，甘甜可口。"

