#. ~ Description of "dried wild rice stalks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A bunch of dry wild rice stalks.  Threshing these would knock the grains loose."
msgstr "一捆干燥的野生稻稻穗，需要脱粒后才能使用。"

#. ~ Description of "corn cob"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A corn cob full of delicious golden kernels.  You can eat them on the cob or shell it for cooking."
msgstr "一个装满美味的金色果仁的玉米棒子。你可以直接抓住棒子吃，也可以把它剥下来煮。"

#. ~ Description of "dried buckwheat stalks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A heap of dried buckwheat.  It'll need to be threshed before eating, unless you're a cow."
msgstr "一堆干燥的荞麦麦穗。除非你是一头牛，否则在吃之前需要把它脱粒。"

#. ~ Description of "wheat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A heap of dried wheatberries, ready for planting.  They're hard as gravel, but could be boiled for food or ground into flour."
msgstr "一堆干小麦，可以用于种植。它们像砾石一样坚硬，但可以煮成食物或磨成面粉。"

#. ~ Description of "canola seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A heap of round black seeds, typically milled and pressed for their oil."
msgstr "一堆圆形的黑色种子，通常用于碾磨和压榨以获得油。"

#. ~ Description of "dried lentils"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A humble but nutrient-rich legume.  They should be cooked prior to consumption, unless you're planning to plant them."
msgstr "一种不起眼但富含营养的豆类。食用前应该先煮熟，除非你想拿去种。"

#. ~ Description of "threshed buckwheat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A pile of buckwheat seeds with some chaff still mixed in.  Once it's winnowed, it'll be ready for use."
msgstr "混着谷壳的荞麦，它必须经过扬谷才能使用。"

#. ~ Description of "barley"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A pile of dried barleycorn, a staple of brewing everywhere.  It can be planted, boiled, or ground into flour."
msgstr "一堆干大麦，世界各地都用它当主食。它可以种植，也可以煮成食物或磨成面粉。"

#. ~ Description of "oats"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A pile of raw oats."
msgstr "一堆生燕麦。"

#. ~ Description of "dried lentil stalks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A pile of short stalks with lentils rattling in their pods.  These plants dried in the field and didn't need a tool to harvest, but they'll still need to be threshed and winnowed."
msgstr "一捆长着豆荚的短茎，扁豆在豆荚里嘎嘎作响。这些植物可以直接在田里晾干，不需要用工具收割，但仍需要脱粒和扬谷。"

#. ~ Description of "popcorn cob"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A popcorn cob full of popcorn kernels.  You can eat them on the cob or shell it for cooking."
msgstr "一个装满美味的金色果仁的玉米棒子。你可以直接抓住棒子吃，也可以把它剥下来煮。"

#. ~ Description of "dried barley stalks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A sheaf of dried barley stalks.  These will require threshing before anything can be done with them."
msgstr "一捆干燥的大麦麦穗。在使用它们做任何事情之前，你都需要取下上面的麦子。"

#. ~ Description of "dried oat stalks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A sheaf of dried oat stalks.  These will require threshing before anything can be done with them."
msgstr "一捆干燥的燕麦麦穗。在使用它们做任何事情之前，你都需要取下上面的麦子。"

#. ~ Description of "dried wheat stalks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A sheaf of dried wheat stalks.  These will require threshing before anything can be done with them."
msgstr "一捆干燥的小麦麦穗。在使用它们做任何事情之前，你都需要取下上面的麦子。"

#. ~ Description of "dried canola stalks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A sheaf of dry grass, it must be threshed to separate out the seeds."
msgstr "一捆干草，必须经过脱粒才能从中分出种子。"

#. ~ Description of "barley stalks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A sheaf of freshly-cut barley, now ready for drying in a stook or smoker."
msgstr "一捆刚刚收割的大麦，现在可以放在炉灶或烟熏架里烘干了。"

#. ~ Description of "oat stalks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A sheaf of freshly-cut oats, now ready for drying in a stook or smoker."
msgstr "一捆刚刚收割的燕麦，现在可以放在炉灶或烟熏架里烘干了。"

#. ~ Description of "wheat stalks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A sheaf of freshly-cut wheat, now ready for drying in a stook or smoker."
msgstr "一捆刚刚收割的小麦，现在可以放在炉灶或烟熏架里烘干了。"

#. ~ Description of "canola stalks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A sheaf of tall grass with slender little seed pods, now ready for drying."
msgstr "一捆有着细长的小籽荚的长穗，现在可以拿去烘干了。"

#. ~ Description of "wild rice stalks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A sheaf of wild rice stalks, ready for drying."
msgstr "一捆野生稻稻穗，可以拿去干燥了。"

#. ~ Description of "raw popcorn"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "A special variety of corn which could be used for making popcorn, after it's dried.  Unlike normal corn, it's not sweet and is more dry."
msgstr "一种特殊的玉米，干燥后可以用来做爆米花。不像普通的玉米，它不甜，而且更干。"

#. ~ Description of "empty corn cob"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "An empty corn cob.  No longer contains any edible kernels, but it can be used to make stock or as fuel."
msgstr "一个脱粒的玉米芯。不再包含任何可食用的玉米粒，但可以用来制作物品或作为燃料。"

#. ~ Description of "threshed barley"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "Barley with the chaff still mixed in.  It will have to be winnowed before it's usable."
msgstr "混着谷壳的大麦，它必须经过扬谷才能使用。"

#. ~ Description of "corn kernels"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "Delicious golden kernels of corn."
msgstr "美味的金黄色玉米粒。"

#. ~ Description of "popcorn kernels"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "Dried kernels from a particular type of corn.  Inedible raw, they can be cooked to make a tasty snack."
msgstr "这种干燥过的玉米粒来自于一种特殊种类的玉米。不能生吃，但是加以烹饪就会成为美味的佳肴。"

#. ~ Description of "buckwheat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "Dry seeds from a wild buckwheat plant.  Inedible in their present state, they are commonly cooked or ground into flour."
msgstr "从野生荞麦里收获的干荞麦，不能生吃，通常要把他们磨成粉或者放在水里煮熟。"

#. ~ Description of "threshed lentils"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "Lentils with chaff mixed in.  These will have to be winnowed before they're usable."
msgstr "混着豆荚的燕麦，它必须经过扬谷才能使用。"

#. ~ Description of "chaff"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "Loose bits of dried straw and seed casings from winnowed grain.  There are a few fragments of seeds still mixed in, a big enough pile of this stuff could be made into bird food or cattle fodder."
msgstr "松散的干稻草和筛过的谷壳。里面仍有混着一些种子碎屑，可以收集起来制成鸟食或牛饲料。"

#. ~ Description of "threshed oats"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "Oats with the chaff still mixed in.  They will have to be winnowed before they're usable."
msgstr "混着谷壳的燕麦，它必须经过扬谷才能使用。"

#. ~ Description of "popcorn"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "Plain, unseasoned popcorn.  Not as tasty as other kinds, but healthier as a result."
msgstr "一份质朴且毫无味道的\"原味\"爆米花，味道不如加料的爆米花，但是相比之更加绿色健康无污染。"

#. ~ Description of "buttered popcorn"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "Popcorn with a light covering of butter for extra flavor."
msgstr ""
"一份抹上薄薄一层黄油晶莹剔透的爆米花。\n"
"\"好吃到爆！\""

#. ~ Description of "salted popcorn"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "Popcorn with salt added for extra flavor."
msgstr "一份咸味爆米花，最早期的爆米花就是以玉米黄油还有盐为主，19世纪开始风靡。在二战期间，糖又成了管制用品，欧美爆米花咸的口味就因此延续至今了。"

#. ~ Description of "wild rice"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "Raw wild rice, still in its fibrous shell.  It'll need to be milled before it's edible for humans."
msgstr "生的野生稻，仍被包裹在其纤维状的外壳中。它需要经过研磨才能供人类食用。"

#. ~ Description of "threshed canola"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "Round black seeds mixed in with dry chaff."
msgstr "和干谷壳混合在一起的圆形的黑色种子。"

#. ~ Description of "buckwheat stalks"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "These leafy stalks only get about waist-high and technically aren't a grass, but thanks to their long stems and nutritious seeds, they can still be farmed like any other cereal crop."
msgstr "这些多叶的茎秆只有齐腰高，严格意义上讲也不是草，但由于它们的长茎和营养丰富的种子，它们仍然可以像其他谷物作物一样用于种植。"

#. ~ Description of "threshed wheat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
msgid "Wheat with the chaff still mixed in.  It will have to be winnowed before it's usable."
msgstr "混着谷壳的小麦，它必须经过扬谷才能使用。"

