#. ~ Description of "broccoli"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A big stalk of broccoli.  It's a bit tough, but rich in Vitamin C and quite delicious when properly cooked."
msgstr ""
"一大根西兰花。有点硬，但富含维生素C，煮熟后非常美味。\n"
"\"即使是非常有营养的食物，无脑向别人推荐也是不对的。\""

#. ~ Description of "handful of spinach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A bunch of spinach leaves.  Their ability to provide one with superhuman strength has been greatly exaggerated by popular media."
msgstr "一束菠菜叶。和大众媒体宣传的不同，吃了并不会拥有超人的力量。"

#. ~ Description of "cut chili pepper"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A chili pepper that's been cut into pieces.  The seeds have been removed."
msgstr "被切成块的辣椒，里面的种子已被摘除。"

#. ~ Description of "cut bell pepper"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A chopped up bell pepper with the seeds removed."
msgstr "去掉籽的切好的灯笼椒。"

#. ~ Description of "cut salad cucumber"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A chopped-up salad cucumber."
msgstr "一份切好的黄瓜。"

#. ~ Description of "cut zucchini"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A chopped-up summer squash.  The seeds have been removed."
msgstr "一种切碎的夏日瓜果。种子已被摘除。"

#. ~ Description of "fungal chunk"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A chunk of fungal matter.  Eating unfamiliar mushrooms is a bad idea."
msgstr "一大块外星真菌物质。乱吃陌生蘑菇小心躺板板哦。"

#. ~ Description of "hops flower"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A cluster of small cone-like flowers, indispensable for brewing beer."
msgstr "一簇小圆锥状的花，它是啤酒酿造不可缺少的原料。"

#. ~ Description of "lettuce head"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A crisp head of iceberg lettuce.  You should probably prepare it before eating."
msgstr "脆脆的卷心生菜头。  你可能应该在吃之前准备好。"

#. ~ Description of "cut eggplant"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A cut-up eggplant with many of the seeds picked out."
msgstr "切好的茄子，里面的种子已经被去除。"

#. ~ Description of "cut tomato"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A cut-up tomato with the seeds removed."
msgstr "去掉籽的切好的番茄。"

#. ~ Description of "triffid flesh"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A dense chunk of rubbery plant matter.  Though flexible and succulent, it's far too fibrous for a person to eat."
msgstr "一块致密的橡胶状植物物质。  Though flexible and succulent, it's far too fibrous for a person to eat."

#. ~ Description of "bell pepper"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A green bell pepper.  Eating it whole and raw would be kind of a hassle, considering all the seeds."
msgstr "一个青椒。考虑到里面有那么多种子，把它整个生吃会有点麻烦。"

#. ~ Description of "sea lettuce"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A handful of edible green seaweed.  It makes a good snack as-is, but can be dried or prepared in a number of ways."
msgstr "一把可食用的绿色海藻。  它本身就是一种很好的零食，但可以干燥或以多种方式制备。"

#. ~ Description of "dandelion"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A handful of freshly-picked yellow dandelions.  In their current raw state they are quite bitter."
msgstr ""
"一把新摘取的黄色蒲公英。\n"
"\"别想让我生吃这苦玩意。\""

#. ~ Description of "fiddleheads"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A handful of immature fern fronds, still curled up like the head of a fiddle.  Delicious when cooked, but consuming them raw can cause food poisoning."
msgstr "一把未成熟的蕨菜叶子，仍像小提琴头一样蜷曲着。烹饪后味道鲜美，但生吃会引起食物中毒。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of shredded cabbage"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A handful of shredded cabbage."
msgstr "一头洁白脆嫩的卷心菜。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of shredded lettuce"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A handful of shredded iceberg lettuce."
msgstr "脆头卷心的莴苣，也叫生菜。"

#. ~ Description of "seaweed"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A handful of slimy seaweed.  It doesn't look edible, but properly dried, it might make for decent kindling."
msgstr "一把粘糊糊的海藻。  它看起来不可食用，但如果干燥得当，它可能会成为不错的引火物。"

#. ~ Description of "cabbage head"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A head of crisp white cabbage.  You should probably prepare it before eating."
msgstr "一头脆白卷心菜。  你可能应该在吃之前准备好。"

#. ~ Description of "carrot"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A healthy root vegetable.  Rich in vitamin A!"
msgstr "健康的根菜。富含维生素A！"

#. ~ Description of "salsify root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A highly nutritious root, it is tough and bland until cooked, at which point it tastes strangely similar to oysters."
msgstr "一种营养丰富的根，在煮熟之前又韧又无味，此时它的味道很奇怪地与牡蛎非常相似。"

#. ~ Description of "tomato"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A juicy red tomato.  It gained popularity in Italy after being brought back from the New World."
msgstr "一个鲜美多汁的番茄，从新大陆引入之后就在意大利广泛被食用。"

#. ~ Description of "pumpkin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A large gourd, about the size of a person's head.  It'll require some disassembly before use."
msgstr "一个有大约一个人的头那么大的瓜。在使用前需要先切开。"

#. ~ Description of "horseradish root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A large white tapered root of a horseradish plant.  Way too spicy to eat in this form, but can be used for making condiments."
msgstr "一根巨大的白色锥形辣根根茎。这样直接吃太辣了，但可以用来做调味品。"

#. ~ Description of "bladderwrack"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A leafy bunch of seaweed covered in air bladders.  Many claims are made about its health benefits, but at least as a foodstuff, it's no better or worse than other edible seaweed."
msgstr "一束绿叶海藻，上面覆盖着气囊。  许多人声称它对健康有益，但至少作为一种食品，它并不比其他食用海藻更好或更差。"

#. ~ Description of "cooking banana"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A much less sweet and more starchy relative of the banana; unlike dessert bananas, they usually are eaten cooked rather than raw, and can be processed into flour.  They are a staple food in tropical regions of the world.  Also known as plantains."
msgstr "香蕉的近亲，没那么甜，但淀粉含量更高；与水果香蕉不同，芭蕉通常煮熟后食用，而非生吃，也可以加工成面粉。它们是世界热带地区的主食。又名普拉塔恩。"

#. ~ Description of "eggplant"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A normal and healthy purple eggplant.  Needs to be disassembled before being useful for cooking."
msgstr "正常健康的紫茄子。  在用于烹饪之前需要拆卸。"

#. ~ Description of "raw potato"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A potato, mildly toxic and not very tasty raw.  Delicious and filling when properly cooked."
msgstr "一种马铃薯，微毒，生的不太好吃，但适当烹饪后美味可口又管饱。"

#. ~ Description of "garlic bulb"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A pungent garlic bulb, popular as a seasoning for its strong flavor.  Can be disassembled into cloves or planted as is."
msgstr "一块味道刺鼻的大蒜鳞茎。因其浓郁的气味，是常见的香辛调味料。可以拆解为可种植的蒜瓣。"

#. ~ Description of "cut pumpkin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A quarter section of a pumpkin.  The seeds and stringy inner pulp have been removed."
msgstr "南瓜的四分之一块。种子和粘稠的内果肉已被去除。"

#. ~ Description of "celery"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A single stalk of celery.  Neither tasty nor very nutritious, but it goes well with salad."
msgstr "一种既不好吃也不很有营养的蔬菜，但它的口感很适合沙拉。"

#. ~ Description of "sugar kelp"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A sizable strip of new growth harvested from a sugar kelp.  While these are most often dried, it seems edible enough as is."
msgstr "从糖海带中收获的一大片新生长物。  虽然这些通常是干的，但看起来就足够食用了。"

#. ~ Description of "Jerusalem artichoke"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A slightly sweet tuber.  Contains much inulin which may cause some minor issues with your digestive tract, so it should be cooked."
msgstr "一种略带甜味的块茎。含有大量菊糖，可能会导致消化道出现一些小问题，所以应该煮熟后食用。"

#. ~ Description of "pile of seaweed"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A slimy heap of seaweed.  It doesn't look edible, but properly dried, it might make for decent kindling."
msgstr "一堆粘糊糊的海藻。  它看起来不可食用，但如果干燥得当，它可能会成为不错的引火物。"

#. ~ Description of "cattail rhizome"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A small tuber-like root from a cattail plant.  Its crisp white flesh is very starchy and fibrous, but you really ought to cook it before you attempt to eat it."
msgstr "香蒲植物的块状小根。其脆嫩的白色肉质富含淀粉和纤维，但食用前最好先煮熟。"

#. ~ Description of "bee balm"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A snow-white flower also known as wild bergamot.  Smells faintly of mint."
msgstr "一种雪白的花，也被称为野薄荷。散发着淡淡的薄荷气味。"

#. ~ Description of "rhubarb"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A sour stalk of the rhubarb plant, often used in baking pies."
msgstr "一些北美菜用大黄的肉质叶柄，很酸，烤馅饼时常用它。"

#. ~ Description of "chili pepper"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A spicy chili pepper.  Not the best on its own, but adds great flavor when used in cooking."
msgstr "一种辣椒。单吃不怎么样，但在烹饪中使用能增添超棒的风味。"

#. ~ Description of "dogbane"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A stalk of dogbane.  It has very fibrous stems and is mildly poisonous."
msgstr "一株罗布麻。有非常厚的植物纤维，并且有点毒性。"

#. ~ Description of "mugwort"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A stalk of mugwort.  Smells wonderful."
msgstr "一种艾草。闻起来很棒。"

#. ~ Description of "cattail stalk"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A stiff, green stalk from a cattail plant.  It is starchy and fibrous, but it would be much better if you cooked it."
msgstr "来自香蒲的绿色硬茎。它富含淀粉和纤维，但如果你把它煮熟会更美味。"

#. ~ Description of "plant stalk"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A stiff, green stalk from a plant.  It is starchy and fibrous, but it would be much better if you cooked it."
msgstr "来自一株植物的绿色硬茎。它富含淀粉和纤维，烹饪后会更美味。"

#. ~ Description of "zucchini"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A tasty summer squash."
msgstr "一个看上去挺好吃的夏日瓜类蔬菜，皮薄、肉厚、汁多，含有较多维生素、葡萄糖等营养物质。"

#. ~ Description of "cotton boll"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A tough protective capsule bulging with densely-packed fibers and seeds, this cotton boll can be processed into usable material with the right tools."
msgstr "一个充满了浓密的纤维和种子的坚硬保护荚，可以用适当的工具加工成有用的材料。"

#. ~ Description of "raw bottle gourd"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A vegetable from the gourd family, bottle gourds were brought to the Americas by the first Native American settlers crossing the Bering strait.  It can be further prepared to produce a hard, watertight shell, usable as a biodegradable liquid container.  Eating it doesn't look worth it."
msgstr "葫芦科的一种蔬菜，由第一批穿越白令海峡的美洲土著定居者带到美洲。它可以进一步制备出坚硬的、不透水的外壳，能制成可降解的液体容器。没必要吃这个。"

#. ~ Description of "chicory root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A very bitter root, not meant to be eaten raw."
msgstr "一朵普通的蓝色花。这朵花的根很苦，不能生吃。"

#. ~ Description of "wild garlic"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Also called ramps, this delicate leafy vegetable is healthy and a tasty ingredient for many dishes."
msgstr "这株纤细的多叶蔬菜也被称为北美野韭，是许多菜肴的健康美味配料。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of ground nuts"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "An almost forgotten staple of the native tribes, called the Indian potato by some.  Very nutritious, but mildly toxic unless cooked."
msgstr "几乎被遗忘的土著部落主食，一些人称之为\"印第安土豆\"。非常有营养，但未煮熟时有轻微毒性。学名\"美洲土圞儿\"。"

#. ~ Description of "onion"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "An aromatic onion used in cooking.  Cutting these up can make your eyes sting!"
msgstr ""
"一种香料洋葱，适合用于烹饪。\n"
"\"在我未变异成吸血鬼前，洋葱只会对我的眼睛造成点刺激。\""

#. ~ Description of "wild vegetables"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "An assortment of edible-looking wild plants.  Most are quite bitter-tasting.  Some are inedible until cooked."
msgstr "一些可食用的野菜，据说大部分野菜都含有苦味，一些只有在加工后才可以进行食用。"

#. ~ Description of "burdock"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Burdock, a bitter thistle-like vegetable.  Can be eaten raw or cooked."
msgstr "牛蒡，一种苦涩的蓟类蔬菜。可以生吃或煮熟。"

#. ~ Description of "garlic clove"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Cloves of garlic, useful as a seasoning."
msgstr "用大蒜、油和调味料烤制的面包。"

#. ~ Description of "green tea leaves"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Dried leaves of a tropical plant.  You can boil them into green tea, or you can just eat them raw.  They're pretty gross and not too filling that way, though."
msgstr "热带植物的晒干的叶子，可以泡成绿茶，还可以直接嚼着吃，只是不饱肚子而且令人恶心。"

#. ~ Description of "black tea leaves"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Dried leaves of a tropical plant.  You can boil them into tea, or you can just eat them raw.  They're pretty gross and not too filling that way, though."
msgstr "热带植物的晒干的叶子，可以当茶叶泡，还可以直接嚼着吃，只是不饱肚子而且令人恶心。"

#. ~ Description of "grape leaves"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Edible leaves of the grape vine.  Typically used in salads or as a food wrapping."
msgstr "葡萄藤上结出的可食用的叶子。通常用于沙拉或食品包装。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "Japanese knotweed stems"
msgid_plural "Japanese knotweed stems"
msgstr[0] "日本虎杖茎秆"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Jerusalem artichoke"
msgid_plural "Jerusalem artichokes"
msgstr[0] "洋姜"

#. ~ Description of "horseradish greens"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Leaves of a horseradish plant with a sharp, bitter and peppery taste.  They're edible, but not commonly eaten."
msgstr "辣根的叶子，有一股刺激的苦辣味道。它们虽然可以食用，但并不常见人吃这些叶子。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of bamboo shoots"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Raw woody bamboo shoots, they require some preparation before they can be eaten safely."
msgstr "生竹笋，在能够被安全食用前，需要先做一些处理。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of raw beans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Raw, uncooked beans.  They are mildly toxic to humans in this form, but you could cook them to make them tasty."
msgstr "生的，没有经过烹煮的菜豆。生豆子对人类来说有点毒性，但是熟了就好吃了。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of chicory greens"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Some chicory greens.  They are quite bitter but high in calcium."
msgstr "一些菊苣叶。它们相当苦，但富含维生素。"

#. ~ Description of "Japanese knotweed stems"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Some young Japanese knotweed stems.  They taste a bit like rhubarb and contain good amounts of vitamin A.  Refreshing."
msgstr "一些日本虎杖的嫩茎秆。它们尝起来有点像大黄，含有大量的维生素A。十分提神。"

#. ~ Description of "handful of young leaves"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Some young leaves from miscellaneous plants.  They're tender enough to eat, but not very tasty on their own."
msgstr "来自各种植物的嫩叶。很嫩，可以吃，单独食用时味道不怎么样。"

#. ~ Description of "poppy pod"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "The fruit of the poppy flower, a seed-bearing head left over after the petals have dropped off."
msgstr "罂粟花掉瓣后留下的带籽果实。"

#. ~ Description of "dahlia root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "The large, tuberous root of a dahlia flower.  It smells spicy, but is too starchy to eat without cooking."
msgstr "大丽花的大块根。它闻起来挺辣，但是由于含有太多淀粉，不做熟就不能吃。"

#. ~ Description of "salad cucumber"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "The larger cousin of a pickle.  A vegetable from the gourd family.  Not especially flavorful, but very refreshing."
msgstr "葫芦科的一种蔬菜。不是特别香，但是很清爽。"

#. ~ Description of "lotus root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "The rhizome of the lotus, which has many tubular cavities inside, can be eaten both raw and cooked."
msgstr "带有许多管状空腔的莲花根茎，可以生吃也可以烹调后食用。"

#. ~ Description of "wild root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "These are often wild carrots, but beware of poisonous lookalikes.  In any case, the root is tough and is not as tasty as a real raw carrot."
msgstr "这些通常是野生胡萝卜，但要当心某些会有毒。无论如何，这些根茎都很硬，不像真正的生胡萝卜那么好吃。"

#. ~ Description of "pile of wintergreen leaves"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "These leaves smell strongly medicinal.  When chewed, they first taste sweet but the aftertaste is incredibly bitter.  These leaves contain good amounts of methyl salicylate and merely chewing them may have a similar effect to aspirin."
msgstr "这些叶子闻起来有股草药味。咀嚼时，它们最初尝起来有点甜，但回味却极其苦涩。这些叶子中含有大量的水杨酸甲酯，仅仅咀嚼它们可能会产生与阿司匹林相似的效果。"

#. ~ Description of "wild sarsaparilla root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "This aromatic rhizome can be eaten as is in an emergency, but it is much better used for making beverages.  Its taste is pleasant but it is also tough and stringy."
msgstr "这种芳香的根茎可以在紧急情况下食用，但它最好用于制作草药茶。它的味道沁人心脾，但也硬而多筋。"

#. ~ Description of "sugar beet"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "This fleshy root is ripe and flowing with sugars; it'll just take some processing to extract them."
msgstr "这块新鲜的根茎已经成熟并且充满了糖分。只差最后一些步骤，赶紧把它们都榨出来吧。"

#. ~ Description of "wheat-free flour"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "This wheat-free white flour is useful for baking items for those with grain intolerances."
msgstr "不含小麦的白面粉，用于烘烤供谷物不耐的人食用的食物。"

#. ~ "activation_message" action message of item "pile of wintergreen leaves"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "You chew the wintergreen leaves."
msgstr "你咀嚼着吃下了冬青叶。"

