#. ~ Description of gun "Mosin carbine"
#. ~ Description of "Mosin carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid "A later produced and substantially shortened version of Imperial Russia's original service rifle, this variant of the Mosin features a notably more compact barrel and an integral side-folding bayonet.  Produced during the latter days of the Second World War for the Soviet Union, the weapon exhibits less overall stopping power than its full-length older brother thanks to the former's stubbier barrel.  Despite the arm being somewhat weaker than its forefather, the 7.62x54mm round that it chambers still packs a hefty punch, whilst its smaller size helps to make the weapon wieldier."
msgstr "莫辛的这种变体是俄罗斯帝国原始服役步枪的后来生产和大幅缩短的版本，具有明显更紧凑的枪管和一体式侧折叠刺刀。  该武器是在第二次世界大战后期为苏联生产的，由于枪管较粗，因此该武器的整体制动力低于其全长武器。  尽管手臂比其前身稍弱，但其所装的 7.62x54 毫米子弹仍然具有强大的打击力，而其较小的尺寸有助于使武器更易于使用。"

#. ~ Description of gun "Mosin battle rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Mosin battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid "Developed by the Russian Empire prior to the onset of the First World War, the Mosin is a bolt-action military battle rifle chambered for 7.62x54mm rounds.  Powerful, unwieldy, and prolific across the world as military surplus, this sizable rifle is a Soviet updated version of the venerable Mosin."
msgstr "莫辛纳甘步枪，于第一次世界大战前夕由俄罗斯帝国所研制，是一种口径为7.62x54mm的栓动步枪。这种威力大、不够便携，产量巨大的步枪作为军备剩余品而遍布全球。这款长莫辛是苏联时期的改进型。"

