#. ~ Description of "stone axe head"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "A broad piece of stone with an edge narrow enough to roughly chop wood."
msgstr "边缘狭窄的宽阔石头，勉强可以用来砍树。"

#. ~ Description of "metal axe head"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "A chunk of steel with one edge hammered down to something resembling a cutting edge.  It works passably well, but really can't compare to a proper axe."
msgstr "一大块钢材，一边被锤成类似于刀刃的东西。它的使用效果还可以，但完全不能与一把真正的斧子相提并论。"

#. ~ Description of "fire axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "A hefty two-handed axe normally used by firefighters.  It makes a powerful melee weapon, but is a bit slow to recover between swings.  Thanks to its prying head, it can also be used to force locked doors and windows open."
msgstr ""
"一把用于清理着火或易燃材料，切断火势蔓延的大斧，还可以劈开被烧变形的门窗，解救被困的人，如今可以用来解救受困于腐烂身体中的痛苦灵魂。\n"
"\"烈火雄心，尸海纵横。\""

#. ~ Description of "street sign"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "A large street sign, its aluminum pole uprooted.  An unreasonably strong person might be able to wield it like a crude axe."
msgstr "一个巨大的路牌，其铝杆被连根拔起。  一个异常强大的人也许可以像使用粗糙的斧头一样使用它。"

#. ~ Description of "wood axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "A large, two-handed wood axe.  It makes a good melee weapon, but is a bit slow to recover between swings."
msgstr "巨大的双手木斧。是个优秀的近战武器，至于速度比较慢，请不要在意这些细节。"

#. ~ Description of "hatchet"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "A one-handed hatchet.  Makes a great melee weapon, and is useful both for chopping things and hammering them."
msgstr "一柄单手的短斧，是一件不错的近战武器，也可以用于砍柴与捶打。"

#. ~ Description of "copper hatchet"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "A primitive axe made from a small wedge of copper affixed to a short haft."
msgstr "一把原始的斧，楔形的铜质斧头下方装有较短的手柄。"

#. ~ Description of "crash axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "A short, lightweight emergency tool with a quarter-circular blade, a short pick opposite the blade, and an insulated handle.  Used on airplanes to chop down or pry walls or cabinets to gain access in case of a fire."
msgstr "一个轻便应急用短斧，由一个扇形的斧刃、与斧刃相对的锄尖和一根绝缘手柄组成。用于在飞机火灾时砍开或撬开墙壁或机舱。"

#. ~ Description of "bronze axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "A socketed bronze axe with a work-hardened edge, tightly bound to the shaft with cords."
msgstr "一把带銎的青铜斧，刃口经过加工硬化，斧头像用绳索紧紧地绑在斧柄上。"

#. ~ Description of "stone adze"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "A stone adze, a primitive tool for smoothing or scraping wood objects."
msgstr "石锛，用来削平木头的原始工具。"

#. ~ Description of "stone axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "A stone with a narrow edge affixed to a stick.  It can chop wood, but requires much more effort than a modern axe."
msgstr "一块固定在棍子上的窄边石头。它勉强能砍木头，但比现代斧头要费劲得多。"

#. ~ Description of "battle axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "An axe designed for medieval warfare, the head secured to the haft with langets.  Though formidable, it's lighter than the sort you'd use for felling trees, and would make an inferior tool for that purpose."
msgstr "专为中世纪战争设计的斧头，头部用长柄固定在斧柄上。  尽管它很强大，但它比用来砍伐树木的那种工具要轻，并且是一种较差的工具。"

#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "fire axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/axes.json
msgid "Marrying strap for a Halligan bar."
msgstr "用于固定消防破拆棍的绑带"

