#. ~ Description of "foam rubber bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A baseball bat made of foam rubber with a plastic handle.  Light and easy to wield, but almost completely ineffective if your goal is to hurt someone."
msgstr "一根用泡沫橡胶制成的棒球棒，带一个塑料手柄。轻巧且趁手，但如果你打算用来打人，这东西完全造成不了什么伤害。"

#. ~ Description of "nail bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A baseball bat with several nails driven through it.  The spikes look dangerous, but they're sure to make it less durable."
msgstr "一根棒身插了几根钉子的棒球棒，强力的近战武器。"

#. ~ Description of "barbed wire bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A baseball bat wrapped with barbed wire, giving it a little extra oomph without compromising its durability."
msgstr "一根在顶部缠绕了几道带刺铁丝网的棒球棒，野蛮的近战武器。"

#. ~ Description of "soaking stone war club"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A curved wooden club cradling a stone head.  It is currently soaking in oil and won't be properly fit for combat for a while longer."
msgstr "一根弯曲的木棍，上面托着一个石头头。  它目前正浸泡在油中，一段时间内无法正常战斗。"

#. ~ Description of "stone war club"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A curved wooden club cradling a stone head.  These weapons were once used by indigenous peoples across North America."
msgstr "一种弯曲的木棍，前端嵌有石质杖头。这种武器曾被北美各地的原住民使用。"

#. ~ Description of "soaking wooden war club"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A curved wooden club with a ball head carved from a root burl.  These devastating weapons were once used by indigenous peoples across North America."
msgstr "一种弯曲的木制球杆，其球头由根节雕刻而成。  这些毁灭性武器曾经被北美各地的土著人民使用过。"

#. ~ Description of "wooden war club"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A curved wooden club with a ball head carved from a root burl.  These weapons were once used by indigenous peoples across North America."
msgstr "一种弯曲的木棍，杖头由树根瘤雕刻而成。这种武器曾被北美各地的原住民使用。"

#. ~ Description of "hockey stick"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A curved wooden stick with with a flat paddle at one end, commonly used by hockey players."
msgstr "一端弯曲扁平的木棍，冰球和曲棍球运动员的常用器材。"

#. ~ Description of "quarterstaff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A fighting staff carved out of wood.  Lightweight and good for defense, it is surprisingly easy to handle."
msgstr "一根用木头制成的结实棍棒。既轻且长，易于操作。"

#. ~ Description of "tooth-bladed macuahuitl"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A flat wooden club with impossibly-sharp teeth stuck to both sides, a postapocalyptic facsimile of the weapons once used by Aztec warriors."
msgstr "一个两边镶有磨尖玻璃碎片的扁平木棍。在某种程度上与原版实物相符。"

#. ~ Description of "glass-bladed macuahuitl"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A flat wooden club with sharpened flakes of stone, ceramic, or glass stuck to both sides, a reasonable facsimile of the weapons once used by Aztec warriors."
msgstr "一个两边镶有磨尖玻璃碎片的扁平木棍。在某种程度上与原版实物相符。"

#. ~ Description of "tonfa"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A hard plastic truncheon commonly employed by police.  Originally an Okinawan weapon, it consists of a stick with a perpendicular handle attached a third of the way down its length."
msgstr "一根通常被警察所使用的硬质塑料警棍。源自冲绳的土著武器，由棍身及垂直连接在主体的三分之一处的握把组成。"

#. ~ Description of "pool cue"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A hardwood stick designed for hitting colorful balls around a felt table.  Truly, the coolest of sports."
msgstr ""
"一个前细后粗的硬木台球杆，用于在桌面上击打一些五颜六色的台球。\n"
"\"酒吧混斗的常规武器。\""

#. ~ Description of "sledgehammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A heavy steel head on a long shaft, designed for demolition work.  It's a very hard-hitting melee weapon, but slow to swing and will probably exhaust you quickly."
msgstr "一把大而重的锤子，非常粗暴的近战武器。但它挥舞起来很慢，而且可能很快让你筋疲力尽。"

#. ~ Description of "nail board"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A hefty plank of wood.  The nails driven through one end look nasty enough, but it remains a very awkward weapon."
msgstr "一块厚重的木板。  穿过一端的钉子看起来很恶心，但它仍然是一种非常尴尬的武器。"

#. ~ Description of "Mjölnir"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A large hammer, forged from the heart of a dying star.  It bears the inscription:\n"
"\n"
"Whosoever holds this hammer,\n"
"If he be worthy,\n"
"Shall possess the power to…\n"
"CRUSH!'"
msgstr ""
"一把名为妙尔尼尔的神锤，用白矮星的星核打造。上面有着一道铭文：\n"
"\n"
"执此锤者，\n"
"如其适格，\n"
"当承神威以……\n"
"摧毁！！"

#. ~ Description of "ironshod quarterstaff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A long wooden staff reinforced with steel langets and ferrules."
msgstr ""
"一根木质长棍，两端箍上金属圈并装上金属包头来加固。\n"
"\"吃俺老孙一棒！\""

#. ~ Description of "walking stick"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A long, thin stick carved smooth for an easy grip.  These are commonly used by hikers to help navigate steep slopes, and could serve as a fighting staff, though this one looks too thin to last for long."
msgstr "一根细长的棍子，雕刻光滑，易于抓握。  这些通常被徒步旅行者用来帮助穿越陡峭的斜坡，并且可以用作战斗人员，尽管这个看起来太薄而不能持续很长时间。"

#. ~ Description of "war hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A medieval hammer with a spike on one end, made for battle.  Its odd shape and balance make it an excellent weapon, but an ineffective tool."
msgstr "一把中世纪风格的战锤，一端有根尖刺。它古怪的外形和平衡使它成为一把优秀的武器，不过敲起钉子来就没有五金店里的锤子好用了。"

#. ~ Description of "morningstar"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A medieval weapon consisting of a wood handle with a spiked metal ball on the end.  It is bigger and heavier than a typical mace, and its spikes can deal serious damage to soft targets."
msgstr ""
"一柄中世纪的武器，木柄上面附有一个满是尖刺的金属球，步兵对付具甲骑兵的主要武器之一，亦是骑兵间流行的杀敌利器。它能造成毁灭性的钝击伤害，而且尖刺很容易刺穿软体目标。\n"
"\"带钉之锤形如晨星，耀眼且致命的诗意。\""

#. ~ Description of "mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A medieval weapon consisting of a wooden handle with a knob-shaped steel head."
msgstr "一把中世纪武器，由一根非常长的木杆与钢制矛尖结合而成。"

#. ~ Description of "steel bladed macuahuitl"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A modern reimagining of the ancient Aztec weapon, made of a flat wooden club inset along its edges with steel razor blades."
msgstr "对古代阿兹特克武器的现代重新想象，由一根扁平的木棍制成，其边缘嵌有钢制剃须刀刀片。"

#. ~ Description of "aluminum crutches"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A pair of aluminum rods with a brace and padding designed to help support the body using the arms.  These would make for an abysmal weapon, but they'd help you get around on a broken leg."
msgstr "一对带有支架和衬垫的铝杆，旨在帮助使用手臂支撑身体。  这些将是一件糟糕的武器，但它们可以帮助你在断腿的情况下行走。"

#. ~ Description of "mismatched crutches"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A pair of rods, one wood and one aluminum, with braces designed to help support the body using the arms.  These would make for an abysmal weapon, but they'd help you get around on a broken leg."
msgstr "一对杆，一根是木头，一根是铝，带有支架，旨在帮助使用手臂支撑身体。  这些将是一件糟糕的武器，但它们可以帮助你在断腿的情况下行走。"

#. ~ Description of "wooden crutches"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A pair of wooden rods with a brace designed to help support the body using the arms.  These would make for an abysmal weapon, but they'd help you get around on a broken leg."
msgstr "一对带有支架的木杆，旨在帮助使用手臂支撑身体。  这些将是一件糟糕的武器，但它们可以帮助你在断腿的情况下行走。"

#. ~ Description of variant "plastic wizard cane" of item "plastic toy cane"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A plastic cane designed to look like a wizard's staff.  They shall not pass!"
msgstr "一根塑料手杖，设计得像巫师的手杖。  他们不会通过！"

#. ~ Description of variant "plastic fairy wand" of item "plastic toy cane"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A plastic cane festooned with ribbons and glitter."
msgstr ""
"塑料吸管，用于喝饮料以及变成干垃圾。\n"
"\"也许还是可回收垃圾？\""

#. ~ Description of "tactical tonfa (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A reinforced plastic tonfa; the core is filled with capacitors and a high-yield rechargeable storage battery.  When a switch on the handle is pressed, a high-voltage current is transmitted to the two electrodes mounted in the end of the tonfa, and by extension to anyone unfortunate enough to be in contact with them.  It also has a nifty flashlight, which is off at the moment."
msgstr "一把强化的塑料警棍，内部装着电容与电池仓。当握把上的开关被按下去时，一股高压电流会被传导至安装在警棍顶端的两个电极上，然后输出给任何接触到电极的倒霉蛋身上。它还有个别致的小手电筒，现在处于关闭的状态。"

#. ~ Description of "tactical tonfa (on)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A reinforced plastic tonfa; the core is filled with capacitors and a high-yield rechargeable storage battery.  When a switch on the handle is pressed, a high-voltage current is transmitted to the two electrodes mounted in the end of the weapon, and by extension to anyone unfortunate enough to be in contact with them.  The integral flashlight is turned on, continually draining power and lighting the surrounding area."
msgstr "一根强化的塑料警棍，内部装着电容与电池仓。当握把上的开关被按下去时，一股高压电流会被传导至安装在警棍顶端的两个电极上，然后输出给任何接触到电极的倒霉蛋身上。它上面的手电筒已经开启，不断耗电来产生光亮。激活它来关闭。"

#. ~ Description of "spiked cudgel"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A short bit of wood with nails driven through the business end to create a menacing, if inelegant, weapon."
msgstr "一小段木头，钉子穿过其末端，打造出一种威胁性的武器，尽管并不优雅。"

#. ~ Description of "jitte"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A short steel baton employed by Japanese police in the 17th and 18th century.  A small hook forks from the weapon just above the hilt, intended to aid in snagging or disarming opponents."
msgstr "一种17至18世纪日本警方使用的短钢制警棍。握柄上方分出一支小钩，用于钩挂或缴械对手。"

#. ~ Description of "blackjack"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A short, easily concealed bludgeoning weapon consisting of a weight embedded at the end of a short leather shaft.  Formerly used by law enforcement, this weapon is meant to stun or knock out the subject, although head strikes have a high risk of causing a permanent, disabling brain injury or being fatal."
msgstr "一把便于藏匿的短槌，由皮革制成的手柄加上顶端的配重制成。以前被执法部门使用，主要用于眩晕或击晕目标，但是对头部的攻击仍然有很高的概率造成永久性致残的脑损伤，甚至致命。"

#. ~ Description of "plastic toy cane"
#. ~ Description of variant "plastic villain's cane" of item "plastic toy
#. cane"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A sinister looking cane made of plastic.  It has a shiny red orb gripped by claws at the handle."
msgstr "一根看起来很邪恶的塑料手杖。它的把手上有个爪子，抓着一颗闪亮的红球。"

#. ~ Description of "bokken"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A solid wood training katana, exactingly crafted to mimic the weight and balance of the real thing.  Despite its lack of a sharp metal edge, it's still quite capable as a blunt weapon."
msgstr ""
"一柄训练用的木刀，严格模仿真正武士刀的重量和平衡，尽管缺乏一个锋利的刀锋，但它仍然有相当的能力去造成致命的伤害。\n"
"\"洞 爷 湖\""

#. ~ Description of "bowling pin"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A standard bowling pin.  This could make a decent weapon, if it came to that."
msgstr "一只标准保龄球瓶。你非要当成武器去砸丧尸也行，就是有点短。"

#. ~ Description of "bronze mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A stick with a lump of bronze at one end.  While not as durable as steel, its heft makes it every bit as effective."
msgstr "一根一端有一块青铜的棍子。  虽然不像钢那么耐用，但它的重量却使其同样有效。"

#. ~ Description of "lump hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A stout and hefty hammer, more akin to a mini sledge than a claw or ball-peen.  It's useful for portable demolition work, but unwieldy as a weapon."
msgstr "一把结实而有分量的锤子，相比于一般的圆头锤，更像一把大钢锤。作为一把便携工具，在拆除工作中十分有用，但作为武器用起来十分笨拙。"

#. ~ Description of "loaded stick"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A stout knotty stick with a large knob at the top that has been left to cure in a chimney.  A traditional Irish weapon, the shillelagh was originally used for settling disputes in a gentlemanly manner.  The knob has been hollowed and filled with molten heavy metal to pack more of a punch."
msgstr "一根短粗的木棍，顶端有一个巨大的突起，在烟囱内熏制而成。这是一种传统的爱尔兰武器，最初用于以具有绅士风度的方式解决争端。这把木槌的突起被挖空浇铸了金属，具有更强的攻击力。"

#. ~ Description of "wooden tonfa"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A stout wooden truncheon of the sort commonly employed by police.  Originally an Okinawan weapon, it consists of a stick with a perpendicular handle attached a third of the way down its length."
msgstr "一个通常为警用的木头结实短棍。原本是源于冲绳的武器，在棍身三分之一处有着一个垂直的握柄。"

#. ~ Description of "shillelagh"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A stout, knotty stick with a large knob at the top that has been left to cure in a chimney.  A traditional Irish weapon, the shillelagh was originally used for settling disputes in a gentlemanly manner."
msgstr "一根短粗木棍，顶端有一个巨大的突起，在烟囱内熏制而成。这是一种传统的爱尔兰武器，最初用于以具有绅士风度的方式解决争端。"

#. ~ Description of "soaking shillelagh"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A stout, knotty stick with a large knob at the top that is presently soaking in oil.  When it's done, it should be ready to bust some heads."
msgstr "一根粗壮、多节的棍子，顶部有一个大旋钮，目前正浸泡在油中。  当它完成后，它应该准备好打破一些人的头。"

#. ~ Description of "baseball bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A sturdy wooden cudgel once essential to the great American pastime."
msgstr "坚固的木棍曾经是美国伟大消遣的必备品。"

#. ~ Description of "expandable baton (extended)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A telescoping baton that's extended and ready to bust some heads.  Activate to collapse."
msgstr "一把叠缩式短棍，缩小后更易于携带。这是一件不错的的近战武器。激活以收回。"

#. ~ Description of "expandable baton (collapsed)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A telescoping baton.  Right now, it's collapsed for easy storage.  Activate to expand."
msgstr "一把叠缩式短棍，缩小后更易于携带。现在已经被折叠起来，激活以伸出。"

#. ~ Description of "golf club"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A thin aluminum rod with a heavy head on one end for hitting golf balls.  It looks quite fragile, but it could do a fair bit of damage before the shaft got too bent."
msgstr "一根细铝杆，一端有一个重头，用于击打高尔夫球。  它看起来很脆弱，但在轴过度弯曲之前它可能会造成相当大的损坏。"

#. ~ Description of "kanabō"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A two-handed war club used in feudal Japan by samurai against armored opponents, it's made from hardwood studded with metal."
msgstr "一种日本封建时期武士用来对付全副武装的对手的双手战棍。由硬木制成，镶有金属钉。"

#. ~ Description of "lucerne hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A versatile polearm with a spiked hammer head, a spike, and a hook attached to a beefy wooden pole."
msgstr "一把多功能的长柄武器，上面有一个钉锤头（又称鸦喙），一个矛头，和一道弯钩。由于其针对各种目标的广泛适应性，在骑兵作战中大放异彩，实用主义派冷兵器的顶尖之作。"

#. ~ Description of "walking cane"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A walking stick designed to lean on, whether for mobility assistance or puttin' on the ritz."
msgstr "一款专为倚靠而设计的手杖，无论是作为行动辅助还是放在床上。"

#. ~ Description of "wooden crutch"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A wooden rod with a brace designed to help support the body using the arm.  It could be combined with another like it, or used on its own."
msgstr "带有支架的木杆，旨在帮助使用手臂支撑身体。  它可以与其他类似的产品结合使用，也可以单独使用。"

#. ~ Description of "bō staff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A wooden staff weapon used in Okinawan martial arts.  It has been finely sanded and treated with oil for integrity."
msgstr "冲绳传统武术中所使用的木制棍棒。被人精细打磨并上油处理，确保其完好。"

#. ~ Description of "aluminum crutch"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "An aluminum rod with a brace and padding designed to help support the body using the arm.  It could be combined with another like it, or used on its own."
msgstr "带有支架和衬垫的铝杆，旨在帮助使用手臂支撑身体。  它可以与其他类似的产品结合使用，也可以单独使用。"

#. ~ Description of "aluminum bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "An aluminum version of the tapered club used to play baseball.  It's lighter, stronger, and hits harder than the wooden variety."
msgstr "用于打棒球的锥形球杆的铝制版本。  它比木制品种更轻、更坚固、打击力更强。"

#. ~ Description of "powered quarterstaff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "An ironshod quarterstaff that has a high-voltage stun gun built into the handle.  The stun gun is wired to the metal caps at either end of the staff, allowing you to zap a dangerous opponent should beating them senseless with it prove too hazardous."
msgstr ""
"一柄铁头木棒，内置有高压电击枪。电击枪发出的电流能传导至棍棒两端的金属帽上，如果碰到了光是用棍打不太安全的对手，可以不讲武德地把它电晕，再一顿痛殴。\n"
"\"电子兵器，小子。\""

