#. ~ Description of "monomolecular blade"
#: data/json/items/melee/fake.json
msgid "A foot-long blade made from high-tech alloy and edged with bonded nanocrystals."
msgstr "使用尖端科技打造的约一尺长的合金刀片，号称只有一个分子宽的纳米晶体组成了它的锋刃。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/fake.json
msgid "monomolecular blade"
msgid_plural "monomolecular blades"
msgstr[0] "单分子刀刃"

#. ~ Description of "butterfly sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A Shaolin butterfly sword, short, with a handguard and an unusually wide blade.  These are traditionally used in pairs, but just one is more than enough."
msgstr "少林蝴蝶剑，短，有护手，剑刃异常宽。  传统上，它们是成对使用的，但仅一个就足够了。"

#. ~ Description of "kilij"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A Turkish sabre, the kilij is quite a bit heavier than most Middle Eastern sabres and has a distinctive wide tip called a yelman, which gives it vicious cutting power but means it requires a special scabbard."
msgstr ""
"基利杰是一种土耳其军刀，比大多数中东军刀都要重一些，被称为\"耶尔曼\"的宽大刀尖赋予了它强悍的切割能力，但也意味着它需要一个特殊的刀鞘。\n"
"\n"
"这把刀有一个合适的握把，由高碳钢制成。"

#. ~ Description of "cutlass"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A broad saber known for its use by sailors and pirates, as its short blade is easy to handle in close quarters."
msgstr "一把因被水手与海盗广泛使用而闻名的阔刃军刀，偏短的刀刃让它在近身时得心应手。"

#. ~ Description of "xiphos"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A bronze sword of ancient Greek origin."
msgstr "一把源自古希腊的青铜剑，希腊长枪以外的副武器。"

#. ~ Description of "hollow cane"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A cane designed to conceal a blade.  This was a popular fashion accessory for the wealthy during the 18th and 19th centuries."
msgstr "藏了一把剑的手杖。这在18至19世纪的欧洲是富人之间流行的时尚装备。"

#. ~ Description of "kirpan"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A ceremonial dagger carried by Sikh men.  This one is sharp and could be an effective weapon."
msgstr "锡克教徒使用的礼仪匕首，它十分锋利，也许是一种有效的武器。"

#. ~ Description of "longsword"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A classic medieval sword, in between the lighter arming sword and later two-handed swords in size.  It's well-balanced and surprisingly easy to use due to its two-handed grip, but requires a larger baldric or scabbard compared to smaller swords."
msgstr "一把经典中世纪长剑，体积介乎于骑士剑和后期的双手剑之间。相较于其他较小的剑，它的平衡性很好，而且因为使用了双手握把，非常容易使用，但需要剑鞘（背）或剑鞘（肩）来收起。"

#. ~ Description of "arming sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A classic medieval sword, just the right size to use one-handed."
msgstr "一把经典的中世纪剑，大小正好可以单手使用。"

#. ~ Description of "wakizashi"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A comparatively-common Japanese short sword.  Smaller and lighter than a katana, but still effective in combat."
msgstr "一柄短刀，日本武士用于室内及其他狭小空间贴身战斗，通常随身携带，遭遇袭击时，在打刀、太刀不利于使用的情况下自卫。"

#. ~ Description of "cavalry saber"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A curved sword associated with cavalry from the Early Modern period onward.  Lightweight, but a deadly slashing weapon."
msgstr "一把骑兵用弯刀，从近代起就成为骑兵的近战武器。轻便，但同时又是致命的斩击武器。"

#. ~ Description of "scimitar"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A curved sword associated with various Middle Eastern and Central Asian countries.  Designed for slashing, and quite deadly against unarmored targets."
msgstr "一把弯刀，源于多数中东及中亚国家。专门为斩击而设计，而且对无护甲的目标相当致命。"

#. ~ Description of "talwar"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A curved sword used by the Raj of India in the 16th century, a talwar is usually impeccably decorated and able to take off a limb with a single swipe."
msgstr ""
"塔瓦弯刀是十六世纪时印度统治者常用的武器。它通常被装饰得极为精美，能够在一挥之间斩断肢体。\n"
"\n"
"这把是由硬化碳钢制成的，有着不错的握柄，从各种方面来说都是把不错的武器。"

#. ~ Description of "falx"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A distinct Dacian sword that curves forward, allowing you to bypass shields or hook and pull enemies, while delivering decent chopping damage."
msgstr "一种曾经由达西安人使用的独特弯刀，让你可以绕过盾牌并钩拉敌人，同时提供不错的斩击伤害。"

#. ~ Description of "glass shiv"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A glass shard with wrapping at one end so it can be safely wielded."
msgstr "一片碎玻璃，一端已经被包扎好，可以安全地手持。"

#. ~ Description of "crude sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A hand-forged approximation of a medieval weapon.  It's certainly sharp enough to get the job done, but the simplistic design is clearly inferior to the real thing."
msgstr "手工锻造的中世纪武器的近似品。  它确实足够锋利来完成工作，但简单的设计显然不如真实的东西。"

#. ~ Description of "zweihänder"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A huge two-handed sword from Germany.  It packs a real wallop."
msgstr "一柄起源于德国，十三世纪初登场的双手巨剑，造型威武、重量惊人，多为骑士一对一决斗中使用，而后特别受到德国与瑞士的佣兵们的喜爱。"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift machete"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A large blade with one end wrapped in duct tape to make a crude handle, making it easier to wield as a rough machete."
msgstr "一把大刀，一端用胶带缠住，做成一个粗糙的刀柄，使其更容易作为一把粗糙的砍刀挥舞。"

#. ~ Description of "crude greatsword"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A large, crudely-forged blade.  It's too big to be called a sword.  Too massive, too thick, too heavy, and far too rough."
msgstr "一把粗劣锻造制成的大刀，大到不能称之为剑。太大、太厚、太沉，而且太粗糙。"

#. ~ Description of gun mod "sword bayonet"
#. ~ Description of "sword bayonet"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A long, knife bladed bayonet that can be attached to the front of a rifle, converting it into a pike.  It is long enough to be used as a short sword when unmounted."
msgstr "一种长长的带刃刺刀，可以连接在步枪的前部，当作一只长矛使用。这柄刺刀足够长，可以以在卸下时当短剑用。"

#. ~ Description of "welded greatsword"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A long-handled single-edged sword made out of sheet metal layered thrice over itself then welded together.  The extra length and weight makes it a tad awkward, but gives it a lot of slashing power."
msgstr "一把长柄单刃剑，由金属板折叠成三层后焊接而成。额外的长度和重量使它有点笨拙，但也带来了更强的劈砍能力。"

#. ~ Description of "wooden greatsword"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A plank with a handle and a whittled-down point, left large enough to require two hands.  It's only a facsimile of a sword, but might serve for training or just knocking heads."
msgstr "一块带有握柄的木板，顶部被削尖，个头不小，需要双手持握。虽然依旧不太适合挥砍，但比木板本身要好得多。"

#. ~ Description of "wooden sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A plank with a handle and a whittled-down point.  It's only a facsimile of a sword, but might serve for training or just knocking heads."
msgstr "一块木板，装上护手后削尖了头做成木剑。不太适合拿来挥砍，但总比赤手空拳要好。"

#. ~ Description of "punch dagger"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A short, sharp double-edged dagger made to be gripped in the palm, with the blade protruding between the fingers."
msgstr "一把短而锋利的双刃匕首，可以紧握在手心，刀刃从指缝中露出来。它是起源于印度的冷兵器。"

#. ~ Description of "bronze sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A simple short sword made of bronze."
msgstr "一堵被漆成棕色的简易混凝土墙。"

#. ~ Description of "kriegsmesser"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A single-edged two-handed sword of German design, with a long, curved blade.  It became popular across Europe due to its low cost while maintaining strong cutting power in comparison to the more sophisticated longsword."
msgstr "起源于德国的双手巨剑，带有长而弯曲的刀片。与更复杂的长剑相比，它成本低廉，同时仍有强大的切割力，因此在欧洲广受欢迎。"

#. ~ Description of "katana"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A slightly curved sword from Japan, world-famous for its artistic design and association with the age of the samurai."
msgstr "来自日本的略微弯曲的剑，因其艺术设计和与武士时代的联系而闻名于世。"

#. ~ Description of "broadsword"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A straight sword that was ubiquitous during the Early Modern era, with a wide blade suitable for slashing or stabbing.  These were called \"broad\" to contrast with the slimmer rapiers of the day."
msgstr "近代早期普遍存在的直剑，刀刃较宽，适合砍杀或刺刺。  这些被称为“宽幅”，以与当时较细的剑杆形成鲜明对比。"

#. ~ Description of "sword cane"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A sword with a thin blade designed to be hidden inside a hollow cane."
msgstr "一把薄刃的短剑，能藏在空心手杖里面。"

#. ~ Description of "rapier"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A thin, straight sword of the type once preferred by musketeers, masked gentlemen, and swashbucklers of all sorts."
msgstr "一把薄而直的剑，曾经是火枪手、蒙面绅士和各种虚张声势的人所喜爱的类型。"

#. ~ Description of "machete multitool"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A thin, wobbly steel blade with sawteeth on one side and a flat chisel tip for digging.  More of a jackass of all trades than a jack of them."
msgstr "细长又摇摇晃晃的的钢刃的一侧有着锯齿，顶部是一个能用来挖掘的凿头。门门精通，样样稀松。"

#. ~ Description of "karambit"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A traditional Indonesian knife.  The blade is very short, but its curved design is perfect for precision attacks."
msgstr "传统的印尼小刀。它十分锋利，也许是一种有效的武器。"

#. ~ Description of "nodachi"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A two-handed sword from Japan resembling an extremely long katana."
msgstr "来自日本的双手剑，类似极长的武士刀。"

#. ~ Description of "welded sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A vicious single-edged sword made out of sheet metal layered twice over itself then welded together.  It's not as robust as a proper forged sword, but the edge is wickedly sharp."
msgstr "一把十分狂野的单刃剑，由金属板折叠后焊接而成。它不像正规的锻造剑那样坚固，但其边缘却非常锋利。"

#. ~ Description of "fencing foil"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A weapon used for fencing, the most noble of all sports.  Unfortunately, a fencing foil is rather useless as a weapon due to its flexible shaft and dull tip."
msgstr "一把用于击剑的武器，击剑运动被认为是所有运动中最为高贵的。但是在大灾变后，这把剑身软又钝的剑没什么用。"

#. ~ Description of "fencing épée"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "A weapon used for fencing, the most noble of all sports.  While not designed for combat the épée is the heaviest and stiffest of the fencing weapons, and therefore perhaps still useful in your situation."
msgstr "一把用于击剑的武器，击剑运动被认为是所有运动中最为高贵的。虽然并非专为战斗而设计，但这种剑是各种比赛用剑中最为沉重和坚固的一种，因此在实战中仍然有效。"

#. ~ Description of "estoc"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "Also called a tuck, the estoc is a very long thrusting sword designed for piercing armor on the battlefield."
msgstr "estoc 也称为 Tuck，是一把很长的刺剑，设计用于在战场上刺穿盔甲。"

#. ~ Description of "jian"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "An ancient Chinese doubled-edged straight sword, with an ornate guard and a tassel attached to the pommel.  One of the four major weapons in folklore, alongside the dao sabre, qiang spear, and gun staff."
msgstr "一把古中国剑，双刃开锋，剑身长直，护手带有装饰，柄端附有流苏。民间传说中四大武器之一，其余三个是：刀、枪和棍。"

#. ~ Description of "dao"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "An ancient Chinese saber consisting of a curved blade and a guard with a cupped design.  This one is made of bronze."
msgstr "一把古中国刀，由青铜制成，刀身微曲，配以杯形护手。源自商代的设计。民间传说中四大武器之一，其余三个是：剑、枪和棍。"

#. ~ Description of gun mod "Type 30 bayonet"
#. ~ Description of "Type 30 bayonet"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "An essential tool within any 20th-century Japanese soldier's toolbox, the Type 30 is a massive, single-edged sword-style bayonet intended for use with Arisaka rifles and even light machineguns.  Possessing a J-shaped quillon guard for hooking an opponent's weapon during combat, the bayonet, when dismounted, acts like a particularly sizable machete."
msgstr "30 型是 20 世纪日本士兵工具箱中的必备工具，是一种巨大的单刃剑式刺刀，适用于有坂步枪甚至轻机枪。  刺刀具有 J 形刺刀护手，用于在战斗中钩住对手的武器，卸下后就像一把特别大的砍刀。"

#. ~ Description of "tanto"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "An ornate knife that dates back to the Heian period in Japan.  Originally a backup weapon for samurai, these blades took on a ceremonial purpose, becoming the instrument used for seppuku."
msgstr "一把华丽的刀，可以追溯到日本平安时代。  这些刀片最初是武士的备用武器，后来具有仪式用途，成为切腹的工具。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Gun mod name
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "Enfield No. 4 bayonet"
msgid_plural "Enfield No. 4 bayonets"
msgstr[0] "恩菲尔德四号步枪刺刀"

#. ~ Description of "razorbar katar"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "Five pieces of rebar sharpened to cruel points and strapped to a brace fastened at the wrist and forearm on both arms.  The next bub better watch out."
msgstr "一把传统武器，5根磨尖了的钢筋被焊接在拳套支架上，支架固定在手腕和前臂上。"

#. ~ Description of "electrified foil"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "The modifications made to this fencing foil may not be sporting, but they might give you an edge in this final competition.  Extra effort has been made to insulate the grip and a high voltage stun gun has been attached to the guard, wired through the electronic scoring circuit to the tip.  Thrusting the sharpened tip into a foe and activating the momentary switch will deliver a painful electric shock."
msgstr "这把花剑的改装可以说毫无体育精神，但是能够给你在这场末日比赛中带来一点优势。这把花剑的把手经过了充分绝缘改装，剑格上接上了一把高压电击枪，并通过电子计分器的电路连到了花剑末端。如果你在击打敌人时按下电击开关，就可以释放出一道强烈的电击。"

#. ~ Description of "electrified saber"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "The modifications made to this fencing saber may not be sporting, but they might give you an edge in this final competition.  Extra effort has been made to insulate the grip and a high voltage stun gun has been attached to the guard, wired to the tip along the saber's groove.  Thrusting the sharpened tip into a foe and activating the momentary switch will deliver a painful electric shock."
msgstr "这把佩剑的改装可以说毫无体育精神，但是能够给你在这场末日比赛中带来一点优势。这把佩剑的把手经过了充分绝缘改装，剑格上接上了一把高压电击枪，并沿着佩剑的血槽连到了剑的末端。如果你在击打敌人时按下电击开关，就可以释放出一道强烈的电击。"

#. ~ Description of "electrified épée"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "The modifications made to this fencing épée may not be sporting, but they might give you an edge in this final competition.  Extra effort has been made to insulate the grip and a high voltage stun gun has been attached to the guard, wired through the electronic scoring circuit to the tip.  Thrusting the sharpened tip into a foe and activating the momentary switch will deliver a painful electric shock."
msgstr "这把重剑的改装可以说毫无体育精神，但是能够给你在这场末日比赛中带来一点优势。这把重剑的把手经过了充分绝缘改装，剑格上接上了一把高压电击枪，并通过电子计分器的电路连到了重剑末端。如果你在击打敌人时按下电击开关，就可以释放出一道强烈的电击。"

#. ~ Description of "khopesh"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "This ancient bronze weapon features a curved, sickle-like blade sharpened on the outside edge.  Associated with the New Kingdom period of Ancient Egypt, it was designed mainly to hack through the light armor common to the region."
msgstr "这把古老的青铜兵器有一个弯曲、镰刀状的锋利外刃。发源于古埃及新王国时期，它的主要目的是砍开当地盛行的轻装甲。"

#. ~ Description of "machete"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "This intimidating blade makes an excellent tool for chopping through vegetation, or anything else you don't want in your yard."
msgstr "这把令人生畏的刀片是砍伐植被或院子里任何你不想要的任何东西的绝佳工具。"

#. ~ Description of gun mod "Enfield No. 4 bayonet"
#. ~ Description of "Enfield No. 4 bayonet"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "This is a vintage spike bayonet for the British Lee Enfield No. 4 rifle, featuring a distinct cruciform blade and socket-based mounting system."
msgstr "这是柄用于英国李恩菲尔德四号步枪的复古刺刀，具有独特的十字形刀片和一个基于插座的安装系统。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Gun mod name
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "Type 30 bayonet"
msgid_plural "Type 30 bayonets"
msgstr[0] "30式刺刀"

#. ~ Description of "fencing saber"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "Unlike most cavalry sabers, the fencing saber is straight, and stouter than the foil or épée.  Designed for sport rather than real combat, it has a rounded tip and dull edges."
msgstr "与大多数骑兵军刀不同，击剑军刀是直的，并且比花剑或重剑更坚固。  它专为运动而不是真正的战斗而设计，具有圆形尖端和钝边。"

#. ~ Description of "sharpened foil"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "What was once a mostly-harmless fencing foil has had its electrical plunger assembly removed and has been crudely sharpened to a point.  Though it still lacks a cutting edge, it is now somewhat more lethal, yet still familiar to the practiced fencer."
msgstr "这把曾经人畜无害的花剑的压力感应器已经被移除，末端被粗糙地磨尖。虽然它还是没有剑刃，但磨尖的末端已经使它带有一定程度的致命性，对于熟悉击剑的人来说还是比较有用的。"

#. ~ Description of "sharpened saber"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "What was once a mostly-harmless fencing saber has had its rounded tip snapped off and has been crudely sharpened to a point.  Though it still lacks a cutting edge, it is now considerably more lethal, yet still familiar to the practiced fencer."
msgstr "这把曾经人畜无害的佩剑的钝尖已经被折断，末端被粗糙地磨尖。虽然它还是没有剑刃，但磨尖的剑尖已经使它带有相当程度的致命性，对于熟悉击剑的人来说还是比较有用的。"

#. ~ Description of "sharpened épée"
#: data/json/items/melee/long_blades.json
msgid "What was once a mostly-harmless fencing épée has had its electrical plunger assembly removed and has been crudely sharpened to a point.  Though it still lacks a cutting edge, it is now considerably more lethal, yet still familiar to the practiced fencer."
msgstr "这把曾经人畜无害的重剑的压力感应器已经被移除，末端被粗糙地磨尖。虽然它还是没有剑刃，但磨尖的末端已经使它带有相当程度的致命性，对于熟悉击剑的人来说还是比较有用的。"

