#. ~ Description of "chain whip"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid "A long spool of chain with a steel weight at one end.  What a terrible night it'll be for anyone who gets hit by this thing."
msgstr "一长链轴，一端有钢重物。  对于任何被这个东西击中的人来说，这将是一个多么可怕的夜晚。"

#. ~ Description of "rock in a sock"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid "A pair of nested socks with a stone tied inside.  A true weapon of desperation."
msgstr "一对套在一起的袜子，里面装了个石头。绝对是绝境下才会使用的武器。"

#. ~ Description of "riding crop"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid "A rod ending in a leather popper originally used to stimulate a horse and give them orders."
msgstr "一种皮制头部的杆子，最初用来刺激马并给它们下达命令。"

#. ~ Description of "rope dart"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid "A sharp metal spike tied to the end of a long rope, used primarily in Chinese martial arts.  Though often used for show, there's little doubt that a skilled fighter could do real damage with this thing."
msgstr "绑在长绳末端的锋利金属钉，主要用于中国武术。  尽管经常用于表演，但毫无疑问，熟练的战士可以用它造成真正的伤害。"

#. ~ Description of "horseman's flail"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid "A short pole with a spiked steel ball attached to it by a chain."
msgstr "一根短杆，上面有一个用链条连接的尖刺钢球。"

#. ~ Description of "grappling hook"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid "A steel hook attached to a long rope.  Deploying this next to a wall might give you a way to climb up."
msgstr "一种连接于长绳的钢制钩爪。在墙边使用，或许能提供一种攀爬途径。"

#. ~ Description of "war flail"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid "A stout pole with a spiked mace head attached to the end with a chain, a purpose-made combat version of the peasant flail.  It specializes in threshing people in metal armor, rather than grain."
msgstr "一根结实的杆子，末端用一条短链连接着一个带凸缘的大锤矛，是农民连枷的特制战斗版本。它专门用来给穿着金属盔甲的人脱粒，而不是谷物。"

#. ~ Description of "peasant flail"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid "A stout pole with a wooden club attached to the end with a leather cord.  This farming tool was historically used to thresh grain, but was frequently pressed into service as a weapon."
msgstr "一根结实的杆子，末端用皮绳连接着一根木棒。这种农具在历史上被用来给小麦脱粒，当农民对他们的封建领主感到愤怒时，偶尔也用来打人。"

#. ~ Description of "urumi"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid "A thin ribbon of flexible steel attached to a handle, the whip sword is an Indian weapon long renowned for its bizarre design and the skill required to properly use it."
msgstr "一条连接于握柄的柔性钢制薄带，鞭剑是一种印度武器，长期以来以其奇特的设计及正确使用所需的技巧而闻名。"

#. ~ Description of "bullwhip"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid "A very long strip of braided leather with a handle on one end.  Originally developed to settle disagreements with cattle, it's better used now for flaying the rotten flesh off of walking corpses.  Great for when a problem comes along."
msgstr ""
"一端有手柄的狭长皮鞭，本来是用来驱赶不听话的牛羊，但是现在可以防止行尸走肉靠近你。\n"
"\"你可以称之为吸血鬼杀手，但这个世界没有吸血鬼。\""

#. ~ Description of "nunchaku"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid "A weapon originating from East Asia consisting of a pair of short sticks connected by a shorter rope or chain.  The design is a bit unwieldy, but fast and deadly in the right hands."
msgstr "一种起源于东亚的武器，由一对用较短的绳子或链条连接的短棍组成。  这个设计有点笨拙，但在正确的人手中却是快速且致命的。"

#. ~ Description of "scourge"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid "The \"cat 'o nine tails\", a handle with nine short leather whips, each sporting a razor-sharp metal tip.  This ancient instrument of torture can cause bleeding, but by design is inefficient as a weapon."
msgstr "九尾鞭，又被人称为\"九尾猫\"。一个带着九根短皮鞭的手柄，每根皮鞭的顶端都有锋利的金属尖刺。这种古老的酷刑手段能够导致大量出血，但作为武器使用时并不出色。"

