#: data/json/items/resources/glass.json
msgid "A big triangular shard of glass, sharp all over.  You could use it as a weapon, but you might want to wear gloves."
msgstr "这是一块巨大的三角形玻璃碎片，四周都很锋利。你可以把它当作武器使用，但最好戴上手套。"

#. ~ Description of "sheet of glass"
#: data/json/items/resources/glass.json
msgid "A large sheet of glass, easily shattered.  Useful for repairing windows."
msgstr "一整块玻璃，大约90×120厘米，超级容易碎。用于维修窗户。"

#. ~ Description of "sheet of tempered glass"
#: data/json/items/resources/glass.json
msgid "A large, durable sheet of tempered glass, the kind used in windshields.  This safety glass has the curious property of breaking into small, non-lethal pieces upon shattering."
msgstr "一整块耐用的钢化玻璃，约有六毫米厚。这是一种常见的安全玻璃，它的奇特之处在于破碎时只会碎成不致命的小碎块。"

#. ~ Description of "broken glass"
#: data/json/items/resources/glass.json
msgid "A pile of broken glass.  The pieces are sharp, but too small to use for cutting as they are. They must be prepared before they can be scattered on the ground."
msgstr "一堆碎玻璃。这些碎片虽然锋利，但因为太小，无法直接用于切割。必须先进行处理，才能撒在地上。"

#. ~ Description of "reinforced sheet of tempered glass"
#: data/json/items/resources/glass.json
msgid "A plate of safety glass reinforced with metal brackets and slats to give it a bit more durability without sacrificing too much visibility."
msgstr "一种由金属支架和横条加固的安全玻璃板，在不牺牲太多透明度的情况下提供更强的耐用性。"

#. ~ Description of "glass fragments"
#: data/json/items/resources/glass.json
msgid "When tempered glass breaks, the result is these little gravel-shaped pieces.  They're not sharp at all, which is where it gets the name safety glass. "
msgstr "当钢化玻璃破裂时，会产生这些小砾石状的碎片。它们一点也不锋利，这就是它被称为安全玻璃的原因。"

