#. ~ Description of "ballistic Kevlar panel"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "16 layers of ballistic Kevlar sheets stacked and stitched together into a soft, flexible panel.  Ballistic Kevlar is precision-made by machine and features an extremely tight and uniform weave which cannot be replicated by hand.  Given that the material isn't useful for cut-resistant applications and relies on being stackeed in layers to function, there's no reason to try and take it apart."
msgstr "16层防弹凯夫拉片堆叠缝合而成的柔软柔性面板。防弹凯夫拉由机器精密制造，具有极其紧密均匀的编织结构，无法手工复制。鉴于该材料不适用于防切割用途，且需多层堆叠才能发挥作用，因此没有必要尝试将其拆解。"

#. ~ Description of "Kevlar plate"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A compressed panel of layered Kevlar fabric saturated with epoxy or other adhesive to make it stiff as a board."
msgstr "层状凯夫拉纤维织物的压缩面板，浸有环氧树脂或其他粘合剂，使其像木板一样坚硬。"

#. ~ Description of "wool staple"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A natural cluster of wool fibers.  It could be processed into felt patches or spun into yarn."
msgstr "一簇天然羊毛纤维。可以加工成毛毡补丁或毛纱。"

#. ~ Description of "fur patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A palm-sized piece of preserved fur from an animal."
msgstr "一块手掌大小的保存下来的动物毛皮。"

#. ~ Description of "denim patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A palm-sized square of densely-woven cotton.  Denim is usually used for making jeans, but the fabric is both tough and soft enough for a variety of uses."
msgstr "手掌大小的方形密织棉布。  牛仔布通常用于制作牛仔裤，但这种面料既坚韧又柔软，足以满足多种用途。"

#. ~ Description of "Kevlar patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A palm-sized square of loosely-woven Kevlar fabric.  This variety lacks in ballistic protection, but would be great for making cut-resistant garments."
msgstr "手掌大小的方形松散凯夫拉纤维织物。  该品种缺乏防弹保护，但非常适合制作防割服装。"

#. ~ Description of "nylon patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A palm-sized square of synthetic fabric."
msgstr "由化纤织物制成的柔软汽车座椅。"

#. ~ Description of "canvas patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A palm-sized square of tough canvas fabric.  It could be used to repair items made of canvas or stitched into patchwork sheets for tailoring projects."
msgstr "一块6英寸(约15厘米)见方的坚韧帆布片，可以用来修理用帆布制品，或缝制成帆布拼布面料。"

#. ~ Description of "gambeson batting"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A pile of shredded fabric, dry grass, hair or other cheap materials which could be used to stuff the fabric layers of a gambeson to create armor more cheaply and easily than properly layering and quilting the entire product."
msgstr "一块由碎织物、干草、毛发或其他廉价材料组成的布料，可以用来填充软铠的织物层，使用它制作铠甲可以比以如分层和缝合等正常制作流程的速度更快，成本更低。"

#. ~ Description of "cured pelt"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A rolled-up animal hide which has been scraped of extraneous hair and flesh and treated to prevent decay.  It still requires tanning to become usable fur."
msgstr "一张卷起来的硬化毛皮皮。相比生皮去除了多余的毛皮和残留肌肉脂肪组织，并且进行了防腐处理。依旧需要鞣制才能变成有用的毛皮。"

#. ~ Description of "cured hide"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A rolled-up animal hide which has been scraped of extraneous hair and flesh and treated to prevent decay.  It still requires tanning to become usable leather."
msgstr "一张卷起来的硬皮。相比生皮去除了多余的毛皮和残留肌肉脂肪组织，并且进行了防腐处理。依旧需要鞣制才能变成有用的皮革。"

#. ~ Description of "leather patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A roughly six-inch square patch of leather, could be used to repair clothing and make smaller leather crafts."
msgstr "一块约6英寸(约15厘米)见方的皮革片。可制成小型皮革制品或用于修补皮革物品。"

#. ~ Description of "Nomex sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A sheet of Nomex synthetic fabric, suitable for making heat-resistant clothing."
msgstr "一片芳纶化纤织物面料，可以用来制造耐热衣物。"

#. ~ Description of "denim sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A sheet of densely woven cotton.  Denim is usually used for making jeans, but the fabric is both tough and soft enough for a variety of uses."
msgstr "一层密织的棉布。  牛仔布通常用于制作牛仔裤，但这种面料既坚韧又柔软，足以满足多种用途。"

#. ~ Description of "canvas sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A sheet of durable and waterproof waxed canvas fabric, suitable for making tough bags and clothing."
msgstr "一张12英寸x24英寸(约30厘米×61厘米)的打蜡帆布，耐用且防水，适合制作坚韧的袋子和衣物。"

#. ~ Description of "cloth sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A sheet of fabric made from a plant like cotton or linen.  It can be used to stop bleeding, but it would be better to actually make some bandages."
msgstr "由棉花或亚麻等植物制成的织物。  可以用来止血，不过最好还是实际做一些绷带。"

#. ~ Description of "felt sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A sheet of fabric made from combed wool."
msgstr "一件棉制吊带背心。"

#. ~ Description of "Kevlar sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A sheet of loosely-woven Kevlar fabric.  This variety lacks in ballistic protection, but would be great for making cut-resistant garments."
msgstr "一张松散编织的凯夫拉纤维织物。  该品种缺乏防弹保护，但非常适合制作防割服装。"

#. ~ Description of "neoprene sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A sheet of neoprene, a synthetic rubber, suitable for making underwater gear."
msgstr "一片氯丁橡胶（一种合成橡胶）面料。可以用来制造水下作业的衣物。"

#. ~ Description of "spandex sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A sheet of stretchy synthetic fabric made of highly elastic fibers."
msgstr "一片化纤织物面料，可以用来制造衣物。"

#. ~ Description of "nylon sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A sheet of synthetic fabric."
msgstr "化纤织物捆"

#. ~ Description of "faux fur sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A sheet of synthetic fur."
msgstr "化纤织物捆"

#. ~ Description of "leather sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A sheet of tanned animal hide."
msgstr "过道上的一块布。"

#. ~ Description of "tanned pelt"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A sheet of tanned animal pelt with the fur intact."
msgstr "一张鞣制的动物毛皮，毛皮完好无损。"

#. ~ Description of "Nomex patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A six-inch square patch of fire-resistant Nomex fabric."
msgstr "一块约6英寸(约15厘米)见方的防火芳纶纤维布片。"

#. ~ Description of "spandex patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A six-inch square patch of synthetic fabric blended with stretchy spandex fibers.  It could be used to make flexible yet strong clothing.  Stylish, but bad for the environment; at least you're recycling it."
msgstr "一块6英寸（约15厘米）见方的合成面料，混纺了高弹力的氨纶纤维。可用作制作灵活且坚韧服装的材料。虽然这种材质时尚但污染环境，不过好在你现在是在回收利用它。"

#. ~ Description of "neoprene patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A small neoprene patch.  It can be used to repair neoprene clothing."
msgstr "一个小的氯丁橡胶贴片。  它可用于修复氯丁橡胶服装。"

#. ~ Description of "faux fur patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A small piece of faux fur, roughly six inches square."
msgstr "一小块人造毛皮，大约六英寸见方。"

#. ~ Description of "felt patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A small, six-inch square patch of felt."
msgstr "一块6英寸(约15厘米)见方的小毛毡片。"

#. ~ Description of "fabric strap"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "A strip of broad, flat cloth with a metal adjustment buckle threaded in the centre.  Normally used as a shoulder strap for bags, its ends are usually sown about a corresponding container's D-rings."
msgstr "一条宽而平的布，中间有一个金属调节扣。  通常用作包袋的肩带，其末端通常围绕相应容器的 D 形环。"

#. ~ Description of "Nomex thread"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "Heat-resistant Nomex thread that would be particularly useful for making heat protection gear, though it's fine to use in place of normal thread too, in most cases."
msgstr "防火的芳纶纤维，在制造防火装甲时特别有用，不过在大多数情况下也能用来替代普通的缝衣线。"

