msgid "Primitive yarn made from coarse plant fibers like straw or grass.  It's too thick to sew with, but could be woven into a crude sheet of fabric."
msgstr "用干草一类的粗糙植物纤维制作的简单丝线。太粗了，没法用来缝纫，但是可以编织成简易的织物。"

#. ~ Description of "heavy duty thread"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "Some tough canvas-weight thread, sturdier than ordinary thread.  You could meticulously weave this into a sheet of canvas cloth.  It would also be useful for stitching such sheets together, though it's fine to use for normal tailoring projects too."
msgstr "一些坚韧的帆布用纺织线，比普通的线更结实。你可以把它细致地编织成一张帆布，或者用来缝合帆布面料，不过用于普通的裁缝项目也是可以的。"

#. ~ Description of "Kevlar thread"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "Very durable Kevlar thread that would be particularly useful for making ballistic armor, though it's fine to use in place of normal thread too, in most cases.  Making armor-grade Kevlar sheets from this would need a particularly tight weave, and so would require some specialized machinery."
msgstr "非常耐用的凯夫拉纤维，在制造防弹装甲时特别有用，不过在大多数情况下也能用来替代普通的缝衣线。盔甲级凯夫拉面料需要特别紧密编织而成，因此需要专门机器才能制造。"

