#. ~ Description of "deployable antenna"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A directional antenna and accompanying tripod, folded into a shape vaguely resembling an umbrella."
msgstr "一台定向天线和配套的三脚架，折叠成类似雨伞的形状。"

#. ~ Description of "manual tire changer"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A floor-mounted machine containing all the levers, clamps, and mounts required to remove or fit a tire, plus an integrated foot pump to inflate it."
msgstr "一台落地式机器，包含拆卸或安装轮胎所需的各类杠杆、夹具和安装件，以及一个内置脚压式充气泵。"

#. ~ Description of "portable stove"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A foldable wood stove to safely lit fires while camping in the wilderness.  Activate it to deploy."
msgstr "用于野外露营时安全点火的可折叠柴炉。激活以作为家具放置。"

#. ~ Description of "camp chair"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A folded chair for camping.  Activate it to set it down for a place to sit."
msgstr "露营用的折叠椅子。激活以作为家具放置。"

#. ~ Description of "fiber mat"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A large mat woven from fibrous material.  You could use it as a picnic blanket, but it's more valuable as a surface for butchering.  Too thin to be used as a comfortable sleeping mat.  It's rolled and ready for carrying."
msgstr "一块由纤维材料编织而成的大垫子。你可以把它当野餐毯使用，但用作屠宰的地方更有价值。因为太薄不能作为舒适的睡眠场所。它已经被卷起以便于携带。"

#. ~ Description of "fire barrel (200 L)"
#. ~ Description of "fire barrel (100 L)"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A large metal barrel used to contain a fire.  It has multiple holes punched in its walls for air supply.  Fires set in a fire barrel will not spread to surrounding flammable objects."
msgstr "用来烧火的大金属桶。它的桶壁上有多个孔以保障空气供应。火桶中的火不会蔓延到周围的易燃物品。"

#. ~ Description of "brazier"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A large metal stand used to contain a fire.  Fires set in a brazier will not spread to surrounding flammable objects."
msgstr "一个巨大的金属支架，用于容纳篝火。火盆内的篝火不会引燃周围的易燃物。"

#. ~ Description of "screw press"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A large screw press for manually pressing oil out of fruit or seed paste.  Needs to be placed via the construction menu."
msgstr "一种大型螺旋压榨机，用于手动从果实或种子糊中榨油。需要通过建造菜单放置。"

#. ~ Description of "leather tarp"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A large sheet of leather.  You could use it as a picnic blanket, but it's more valuable as a surface for butchering as it does not soak up blood.  It's rolled and ready for carrying."
msgstr "一大块缝制的皮革，你可以用它来代替野餐毯子，但用作屠宰工具更有价值，因为它不会渗血。它已经被卷起以便于携带。"

#. ~ Description of "butter churn"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A large wooden container used to turn raw milk into butter and buttermilk.  This model uses a foot crank and holds three gallons of raw milk."
msgstr "一个大木桶，能够将生乳制成黄油和奶油。这个型号有个脚踏曲柄，能够装下三加仑生乳。"

#. ~ Description of "metal butchering rack"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A metal butchering rack designed to hang a carcass in the air.  It is folded for easy transportation."
msgstr "一个金属屠宰架子，可以将清理内脏后的胴体悬挂在半空中。它已经被折叠起来以便携带。"

#. ~ Description of "folding table"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A metal folding table for off-road trips.  It is currently folded for easy transportation."
msgstr "用于野外旅行的金属餐桌，目前已被折叠起来方便携带。"

#. ~ Description of "metal smoking rack"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A metal rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste.  It is folded for easy transportation."
msgstr "设计用于熏制食物的金属架，可以获得更好的保存和口感。它已经被折叠起来以便携带。"

#. ~ Description of "cot"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A military-style folding cot.  While it may not be quite as comfortable as a bed, it's better than slumming it on the ground."
msgstr "一张折叠起来的行军床，虽然没家里的床舒服，但至少比睡在地上好多了。"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift brazier"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A portable brazier fashioned from a steel bucket by punching small holes on the sides to improve the air supply.  It is too small to fit any fuel item larger than some splintered wood.  Fires set in this bucket will not spread to surrounding flammable objects."
msgstr "一种便携式火盆，由钢桶制成，在侧面打小孔以改善空气供应。  它太小，无法容纳任何比一些碎木头更大的燃料物品。  该桶中发生的火灾不会蔓延到周围的易燃物体。"

#. ~ Description of "water mill"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A small water-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour.  Needs to be placed via the construction menu."
msgstr "小型水动力磨，可将含淀粉的物品加工成面粉。需要通过建造菜单放置。"

#. ~ Description of "wind mill"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A small wind-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour.  Needs to be placed via the construction menu."
msgstr "小型风动力磨，可将含淀粉的物品加工成面粉。需要通过建造菜单放置。"

#. ~ Description of "hobo stove"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "A small, improvised wood stove, made from a metal can or similar container of the right size.  It's too small to fit anything much larger than splintered wood.  Activate it to deploy."
msgstr "小型的流浪汉火炉，用金属罐或大小合适的类似容器制成。它太小了，装不下任何比碎木体积更大的柴火。激活以作为家具放置。"

#. ~ Description of "deck chair"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "Folded deck chair, deploy to sit down."
msgstr "已折叠的日光浴躺椅，展开它来坐下。"

#. ~ Description of "folding chair"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "Folded plastic chair on a metal frame, deploy to sit down."
msgstr "已折叠的金属框架塑料椅，展开它来坐下。"

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "cot"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "You unfold the cot and place it on the ground."
msgstr "你打开床并把它放在地上。"

#. ~ Name of a trap
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json data/json/traps.json
msgid "cot"
msgid_plural "cots"
msgstr[0] "行军床"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "deployable antenna"
msgid_plural "deployable antennas"
msgstr[0] "可展开天线"

#. ~ Description of "professional camera"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A 35 mm digital SLR (single-lens reflex) camera with optical and digital viewfinders, a zoom lens with auto-focus and stabilizer, and flash.  You can look at your photos on the digital screen or transfer them with any standard electronic device.  Before the Cataclysm, you could have taken professional-grade photos using this."
msgstr "35 mm 的数码单反（单镜头反光）相机，带光学/数字取景器，具有自动对焦的变焦镜头、防抖功能和闪光灯。你可以使用它查看已拍摄的照片，或者将照片存储至存储卡上；它使用普通电池供电。在大灾变之前，专业级照片都是使用这种相机拍摄出来的。"

#. ~ Description of "older USB drive"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A USB thumb drive.  Maybe a decade out of date, but still useful for holding electronic data."
msgstr "USB 拇指驱动器。  也许已经过时了十年，但对于保存电子数据仍然有用。"

#. ~ Description of "USB drive"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A USB thumb drive.  Useful for holding electronic data."
msgstr "一个U盘，用于存储电脑软件与数据。"

#. ~ Description of "cellphone"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A cellphone, an older cousin of the smartphone that is still popular in certain circles due to its reliability and sturdiness.  Using the phone will turn it on and provide light, assuming it is sufficiently charged.  It also tells the time and has an alarm feature."
msgstr "这是一款手机，是现在智能手机的堂兄，但由于它的可靠性、坚固性和使用普通电池的特点，它仍然在某些圈子里很受欢迎。当电量足够时，使用它就能开启并提供照明。它也有一个时钟应用程序，其中包括闹钟功能。"

#. ~ Description of "noise emitter (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A device constructed by 'enhancing' a speaker with some amplifier circuits.  It has no other use besides emitting loud crackling static noise that could distract zombies."
msgstr "这个装置主要是一个增强的扬声器，这个扬声器连接着一些放大器电路。除了发出刺耳的噪音之外，它没有其他用途。噪音会分散丧尸的注意力。"

#. ~ Description of "methanol fuel cell UPS"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A direct methanol fuel cell which can provide power to UPS-compatible electronic devices by oxidizing methanol supplied from a specialized fuel tank to produce electricity."
msgstr "一种直接使用甲醇作为燃料的电池，通过氧化从特殊燃料罐中提供的甲醇产生电能，并提供给兼容 UPS 接口的电器。"

#. ~ Description of "hand-crank charger"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A hand-powered battery charger.  It has an adjustable receptacle designed to accept a wide variety of rechargeable battery cells."
msgstr "一个手摇电池充电器。它有一个可调节的插座，可以插入各种型号的可充电电池。"

#. ~ Description of "noise emitter (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A homemade device that is emitting horrible crackles, pops, and other loud static sounds.  Quick, get away from it before it draws zombies to you!"
msgstr "这个便携装置正在发出可怕的噼啪声、碰撞声和其他嘈杂的声音。快点，在它把丧尸吸引过来之前离开它！"

#. ~ Description of "memory card"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A memory card, can be used to store data."
msgstr "一张存储卡，可以用来存放数据。"

#. ~ Description of "memory card (CLASSIFIED)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A memory card, can be used to store data.  This one has a label on which is written 'CLASSIFIED' followed by a long string of numbers."
msgstr "一张存储卡，可以用来存放数据。这张存储卡上有一个标签，上面写着“XEDRA”，后面跟着一长串数字。"

#. ~ Description of "older memory card"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A memory card.  Maybe a decade out of date, but can still be used to store data."
msgstr "一张存储卡，可以用来存放数据。"

#. ~ Description of "electronic handcuffs"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"A pair of electronic handcuffs, used by police and riot bots to detain captives.  Their continuous siren clearly identifies the wearer as an arrested criminal and alerts human police.  Wait for their arrival, don't try to escape or to remove the cuffs - they will administer an electric shock.\n"
"However, since the only police likely to respond are undead, you may have a long wait ahead, unless you get creative…"
msgstr ""
"一副电子手铐，警察和机器人用来限制嫌疑人行动的常用工具。它会持续的发出警报并且不停的呼叫警官过来将犯人带回警局关押。如果试图挣脱或者逃跑，手铐将主动电击疑犯。\n"
"\"鉴于目前的治安情况，请在被电击和被吃掉脑子之间选择一个吧，亲。\""

#. ~ Description of "camera"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A point-and-shoot digital camera with a digital viewfinder, a backup 'iron-sight', and flash.  You can look at your photos on the digital screen, or transfer them with any standard electronic device."
msgstr "一台傻瓜式数码相机，带有数字取景器，辅助的手动取景器以及闪光灯。你可以在液晶屏幕上查看你的照片，或是传到存储卡里。使用普通电池供电。"

#. ~ Description of "smartphone (locked)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A popular, fancy smartphone.  Sadly for you, its previous user used its security features, rendering you unable to use most of its qualities.  You are still able to check the time and use a flashlight.  Runs on a small, rechargeable power cell compatible with a Unified Power Supply."
msgstr "一款广受欢迎的时尚智能手机。当电量足够时，能够使用内置摄像头拍摄照片，或者打开闪光灯当作手电筒照明。手机里还安装了时钟程序，其中包括闹钟功能，以及能记录热量摄入的程序。它使用一个兼容UPS的小型可充电电池供电。"

#. ~ Description of "laptop computer"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A portable computer, ubiquitous tool both before and after the cataclysm.  While it is little you can do with it nowadays, mostly from lack of internet, you still can load it with books (or even scan using frontal camera)"
msgstr "便携式计算机，灾难前后无处不在的工具。  虽然现在你能用它做的事情很少，主要是因为缺乏互联网，但你仍然可以在里面装书（甚至使用前置摄像头扫描）"

#. ~ Description of "portable hard drive"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A portable external hard drive, the best in affordable mass storage.  Useful for holding lots of electronic data."
msgstr "便携式外置硬盘，经济实惠的大容量存储中的最佳选择。  对于保存大量电子数据很有用。"

#. ~ Description of "handheld game system"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A portable video game console, with a backlit screen allowing you to play in the dark.  Multiple game systems can be linked together for multiplayer games."
msgstr "一个便携式游戏机，它有一个可以在黑暗中使用的背光屏幕，你需要电池才能玩游戏。多台游戏机可以连接在一起进行多人游戏。"

#. ~ Description of "NRE recorder"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A strange apparatus, seemingly consisting of a glass-encased microphone linked to a small thermal printer and digital screen.  The screen remains perpetually blank, save for a battery indicator on its upper right, and on its left side lies a single red button: \"PRINT DATA\"."
msgstr "一个奇怪的仪器，似乎由一个玻璃包裹的麦克风连接到一个小型热敏打印机和数字屏幕组成。屏幕始终保持空白，除了右上角的电池指示灯，左侧有一个红色按钮：\"打印数据\"。"

#. ~ Description of "e-ink tablet PC"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A tablet PC using an efficient color e-ink display.  Before the Cataclysm, these were nifty gadgets; now, it's an almost priceless resource.  Runs on conventional batteries."
msgstr "一台拥有高清彩色电子墨水屏的平板电脑。大灾变前的俏玩意，现如今的无价宝。它需要电池进行供电。"

#. ~ Description of "Geiger counter (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A tool for measuring radiation.  It is in continuous scan mode, and will produce quiet clicking sounds in the presence of ambient radiation.  Using it allows you to turn it off, or scan yourself or the ground."
msgstr "本产品适用于监测辐射。提示：本产品正处于持续扫描模式下，一旦检测到强辐射会发出无声警报。再次使用可以切换模式，转为一次性扫描，或是终止运行。"

#. ~ Description of "Geiger counter (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A tool for measuring radiation.  Using it will prompt you to choose whether to scan yourself or the terrain, or to turn on continuous scan, which will provide continuous feedback on ambient radiation.  It is currently off."
msgstr "本产品适用于监测辐射，可以用于持续监测周围环境的辐射，也可以扫描一次你的身体或是周围的地形，检测辐射是否超标。"

#. ~ Description of "smartphone"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A ubiquitous communication device that once connected users to the internet via a worldwide cellular network, now reduced to a mere computer.  Capable of taking photos with its integrated camera and illuminating an area with its flashlight app, assuming it has enough charge.  The smartphone also has a clock app that includes an alarm and an app for tracking consumed calories.  Runs on a small, rechargeable power cell compatible with a Unified Power Supply."
msgstr "一款广受欢迎的时尚智能手机。当电量足够时，能够使用内置摄像头拍摄照片，或者打开闪光灯当作手电筒照明。手机里还安装了时钟程序，其中包括闹钟功能，以及能记录热量摄入的程序。它使用一个兼容UPS的小型可充电电池供电。"

#. ~ Description of "UPS"
#. ~ Description of "UPS (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A unified power supply, or UPS.  It is a device developed jointly by military and scientific interests for use in combat and the field.  The UPS is designed to power tools, smartphones, armor, and some guns, but drains batteries quickly."
msgstr "这是一个统一化电源，简称UPS。这种装置由军方和科学界共同研制，用于战斗和野外使用。UPS的设计目的是为装甲和某些枪支提供动力，但它的电力会很快耗尽。"

#. ~ Description of "UPS (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A unified power supply, or UPS.  It is a device developed jointly by military and scientific interests for use in combat and the field.  The UPS is designed to power tools, smartphones, armor, and some guns, but drains batteries quickly.  Use it to turn it on."
msgstr "这是一个统一化电源，简称UPS。这种装置由军方和科学界共同研制，用于战斗和野外使用。UPS的设计目的是为装甲和某些枪支提供动力，但它的电力会很快耗尽。使用以打开。"

#. ~ "description" action message of item "NRE recorder"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "Activate the recorder's printer"
msgstr "激活记录器的打印功能"

#. ~ Description of "directional antenna"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "An antenna designed to pick up signals better when pointed at the source.  You could use this with a radio to receive faint signals."
msgstr "天线，可以用来收集信号。当然，你要是把天线对准了信号源，信号强度会更高。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "EMF detector (off)"
msgid_plural "EMF detectors (off)"
msgstr[0] "EMF探测器（关）"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "EMF detector (on)"
msgid_plural "EMF detectors (on)"
msgstr[0] "EMF探测器（开）"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "Geiger counter (off)"
msgid_plural "Geiger counters (off)"
msgstr[0] "盖革计数器（关闭）"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "Geiger counter (on)"
msgid_plural "Geiger counters (on)"
msgstr[0] "盖革计数器（开）"

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "EMF detector (off)"
#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "radio (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json data/json/items/tool/radio_tools.json
msgid "It's dead."
msgstr "它没电了。"

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "laptop computer"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "Light up the screen"
msgstr "点亮屏幕"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "NRE recorder"
msgid_plural "NRE recorders"
msgstr[0] "NRE记录器"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "Otherworldly measuring device"
msgid_plural "Otherworldly measuring devices"
msgstr[0] "超凡脱俗的测量装置"

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "smartphone (locked)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "Recover"
msgstr "能量恢复"

#. ~ Description of "mp3 player (off)"
#. ~ Description of "mp3 player (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "Small enough to fit in your pocket, this device includes a pair of earbuds that allow you to listen to music without anyone else hearing."
msgstr "该设备体积小，可以放入口袋，配有一对耳塞，可让您在没有其他人听到的情况下听音乐。"

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "cellphone"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "The cellphone's batteries need more charge."
msgstr "手机没电了。"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "UPS (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "The charger is turned off."
msgstr "充电器已关闭。"

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "UPS (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "The charger's battery is empty."
msgstr "充电器的电量耗尽了。"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "Geiger counter (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "The geiger counter's SCANNING LED turns off."
msgstr "盖革计数器的工作状态灯灭了。"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "noise emitter (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "The infernal racket dies as the noise emitter turns off."
msgstr "你关闭了噪音发生器，同时可怕的噪音也随之消失了。"

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "laptop computer"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "The laptop's batteries need more charge."
msgstr "笔记本电脑没电了。"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "EMF detector (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "The noise of your EMF detector slows to a halt."
msgstr "EMF探测器所发出噪音渐渐停了。"

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "smartphone"
#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "smartphone (locked)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "The smartphone's charge is too low."
msgstr "智能手机没电了。"

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "e-ink tablet PC"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "The tablet batteries are dead."
msgstr "电纸书的电池耗尽了。"

#. ~ Description of "vibrator"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "This battery-devouring device is just the thing to knead the tension out and help you relax.  Use it to take a break and unwind."
msgstr ""
"一个具有振动、加热等功能的用于保健按摩的按摩器械，激活它来使用。\n"
"\"好舒服，要变得奇怪了。\""

#. ~ Description of "EMF detector (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "This device detects and reads out different electromagnetic wave lengths.  It beeps with proximity and is sensitive enough you could use it to get a sense of direction."
msgstr "该设备检测并读出不同的电磁波长度。它接近目标时发出嘟嘟声，足够灵敏，你可以用它来获得方向感。"

#. ~ Description of "EMF detector (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "This device detects and reads out different wave lengths.  It is currently on, humming and beeping with proximity.  It is sensitive enough you could use it to get a sense of direction."
msgstr "该设备检测并读出不同的电磁波长度。它目前正在工作，嗡嗡作响，足够灵敏，你可以用它来获得方向感。"

#. ~ Description of "electrohack"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "This device has many ports attached, allowing it to connect to almost any control panel or other electronic machine (but not computers).  With a little skill, it can be used to crack passwords and more."
msgstr "该设备有许多连接端口，允许它连接到几乎任何控制面板或其他电子机器（但不包括计算机）。只需一点技巧，它就可以用来破解密码等。每次使用需要消耗25点电池电量。"

#. ~ Description of "smartphone - music"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "This phone is playing music, steadily raising your morale.  You can't hear anything else while you're listening."
msgstr "这款手机正在播放音乐，稳步提升你的士气。你在听音乐的时候，听不到其他的声音。"

#. ~ Description of "Otherworldly measuring device"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "This strange contraption appears to be little more than a laminated box built around a battery, a poorly backlit screen, and a wound spool of cloth netting.  The letters \"X E D R A\" are emblazoned on the side.  To operate the device, unfurl the netting and place it around the object to analyze.  Despite not appearing to do anything, it consumes an enormous amount of electricity and provides a brief numerical readout."
msgstr "这个奇怪的装置看起来只不过是一个围绕着电池、背光屏幕和缠绕的布网线轴构建的层压盒子。  侧面印有字母“X E D R A”。  要操作该设备，请展开网并将其放置在要分析的物体周围。  尽管看起来没有做任何事情，但它消耗大量的电力并提供简短的数字读数。"

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "smartphone - Flashlight"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "smartphone (locked) - Flashlight"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "Turn off flashlight"
msgstr "关闭手电筒"

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "e-ink tablet PC (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "Turn off the screen"
msgstr "关闭屏幕"

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "smartphone"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "smartphone (locked)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "Turn on flashlight"
msgstr "开启手电筒"

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "e-ink tablet PC"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "Turn on the screen"
msgstr "点亮屏幕"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "UPS"
msgid_plural "UPSes"
msgstr[0] "UPS"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "UPS (off)"
msgid_plural "UPSes (off)"
msgstr[0] "UPS（关）"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "UPS (on)"
msgid_plural "UPSes (on)"
msgstr[0] "UPS（开）"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "USB drive"
msgid_plural "USB drives"
msgstr[0] "U盘"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "smartphone"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "smartphone (locked)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
