#. ~ Description of "booby trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "A crude explosive device triggered by a piece of string.  Use it to set it up and wait for some poor bastard to trigger it."
msgstr "由一小截绊线触发的简易爆炸装置。激活它来安装，并等待某个可怜的小混蛋在经过时触发吧。"

#. ~ Description of "loose glass caltrops"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "A handful of glass shards glued together to expose all their sharp edges.  If an unsuspecting victim steps on one, they'll get cut."
msgstr "这些碎玻璃片用胶水粘在一起，露出锋利的边缘。如果哪个倒霉蛋踩上去，就会被割伤。"

#. ~ Description of "loose teeth caltrops"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "A handful of small impossibly-sharp teeth glued together.  If an unsuspecting victim steps on one, they'll get a tooth through the foot."
msgstr "一把极其锋利的小牙齿粘在一起。  如果毫无戒心的受害者踩到一个人，他们的脚就会被牙齿咬穿。"

#. ~ Description of "loose caltrops"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "A handful of small metal objects covered with many sharp points.  If an unsuspecting victim steps on one, they'll get a spine through the foot."
msgstr "一些金属小刺猬，如果哪个倒霉蛋踩上去，就得担心破伤风的问题了。"

#. ~ Description of "tripwire trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "A length of thin string with some affixing tools on either end.  It must be placed across a doorway or other thin passage to function.  Its purpose is to trip up trespassers, causing them to stumble and possibly hurt themselves slightly."
msgstr "一个绊索陷阱，只能设置在门口或是狭窄的走廊。入侵者将触发它，将其绊倒的同时也可能造成轻微伤害。"

#. ~ Description of "M14 land mine"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "A pressure-activated explosive device colloquially known as a \"toepopper.\"  These small land mines were once only found along the Korean demilitarized zone, but were quite controversially deployed en masse across the United States in an attempt to deter the inexorable advance of the walking dead."
msgstr "一种压力启动爆炸装置，俗称“脚趾爆破器”。  这些小型地雷曾经只在朝鲜非军事区发现，但后来在美国各地大规模部署，试图阻止行尸走肉的无情推进，颇具争议。"

#. ~ Description of "bubble wrap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "A sheet of plastic covered with air-filled bubbles.  Use it to set it on the ground, creating a trap that will warn you with noise when something steps on it."
msgstr "一层充满气泡的塑料薄膜，如果有东西踩过它的话，会发出足够的响声以提醒在附近活动的你。"

#. ~ Description of "light snare kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "A simple loop snare, comprising a carefully wound loop of string, two anchor points, and a tool to hammer them in.  It is suitable for immobilizing only small animals.  It has no means of harming its target, as live meat lasts longer."
msgstr "一种简单的套圈陷阱，由一根精心缠绕的绳环，两个锚点组成，并用工具将其敲入地里。它只适合抓捕小型动物，没有伤害能力，防止动物死亡导致肉快速变质。"

#. ~ Description of "crossbow trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "A simple tripwire attached to the trigger of a loaded crossbow.  When the tripwire is pulled, the crossbow fires.  Only a single bolt can be used, after which the trap is disabled."
msgstr "一根轻巧的棉线轻柔地连在了弩的扳机之上，绊线拉动后致命的短矢就会直奔目标而去。但只有一发弩矢，之后就需要重新填装了。"

#. ~ Description of "shotgun trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "A simple tripwire attached to the trigger of a loaded double slam-fire shotgun.  When the tripwire is pulled, the shotgun fires.  Two shells are loaded; the first time the trigger is pulled, one or both shells may be discharged."
msgstr "一根轻巧的棉线轻柔地连在了一把双管霰弹枪的扳机之上，绊线拉动后霰弹枪就会双管齐发，给那位不幸的家伙一个痛快。"

#. ~ Description of "bear trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "A spring-loaded pair of steel jaws connected to a sensitive pressure plate.  Use it to set it on the ground, creating a trap that will ensnare and damage anything that steps on it.  If you are carrying a shovel, you will have the option of burying it."
msgstr "一副弹簧驱动的钢制夹子，连着灵敏的压力板。布置在地面上做成陷阱，可以保证每个失足踩上来的家伙喝上一壶。如果你随身带着铁锹，你还能把它埋在土里。"

#. ~ "bury_question" action message of item "bear trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "Bury the beartrap?"
msgstr "确定埋下捕熊陷阱？"

#. ~ "bury_question" action message of item "M14 land mine"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "Bury the land mine?"
msgstr "埋下地雷？"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "M14 land mine"
msgid_plural "M14 land mines"
msgstr[0] "地雷"

#. ~ Description of "broken glass trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "Same glass shard as before, now prepared to be spread on the ground. It will make noise when stepped on."
msgstr "和之前一样的玻璃碎片，现在准备铺在地上。踩上去会发出声音。"

#. ~ Description of "nailboard trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "Several pieces of wood nailed together, with some nails sticking straight up.  If an unsuspecting victim steps on it, they'll get nails through the foot."
msgstr "这是一块厚实的木板，其中一端上有几枚长长的钉子。你可以邀请你的敌人享受脚板的\"愉悦\"。"

#. ~ bury trap message of item "bear trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You bury the beartrap."
msgstr "你埋下了捕熊陷阱。"

#. ~ bury trap message of item "M14 land mine"
#: data/json/items/tool/traps.json
msgid "You bury the land mine."
msgstr "你埋下了地雷。"

