#. ~ Description of monster "moorhen"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A bird belonging to the Rallidae family.  They are relatives of the coots but have a distinctive red coloration on their heads and brownish plumage."
msgstr "一种属于秧鸡科的鸟。它们是白骨顶鸡的近亲，但头顶是独特的红色，羽毛呈褐色。"

#. ~ Description of monster "coot"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A bird belonging to the Rallidae family.  They can be found worldwide on freshwater habitats, including many islands in the not so distant past."
msgstr "一种属于秧鸡科的鸟。它们可以在世界各地的淡水栖息地发现，包括近海岸的许多岛屿。"

#. ~ Description of monster "robin"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A brown songbird with a reddish-orange breast.  Their eggs are a distinctive shade of blue."
msgstr "一只棕色鸣禽，胸部呈桔红色。它们的蛋有一种独特的蓝色，很好分辨。"

#. ~ Description of monster "grouse"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A common game bird resembling a quail or a very small chicken."
msgstr "一种常见的猎鸟，类似鹌鹑或很小的鸡。"

#. ~ Description of monster "chicken"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A domesticated descendant of junglefowl, it may still be the most numerous bird in the world.  Before the Cataclysm, it was raised by humans as a source of meat, eggs, and early morning wakeup calls."
msgstr "由野鸡驯化的家禽，它可能依旧是世界上数量最多的鸟类，是大灾变前人类的主要肉食来源。母鸡产蛋，公鸡打鸣。"

#. ~ Description of monster "crow"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A fairly large, elegant black bird, famous for its distinctive call.  An intelligent bird, there is a glitter of mischief behind its eyes."
msgstr "一只羽毛大多黑色或黑白两色的乌鸦，长喙，有的有鲜明的白色颈圈，黑羽具紫蓝色金属光泽，嘴、腿及脚大多是纯黑色，十分聪明。"

#. ~ Description of monster "pigeon"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A gentle, plump, small-billed bird with a skin saddle, or cere, between its bill and forehead.  On the ground, it struts about with a characteristic bobbing of the head.  It is a strong, swift flier thanks to its long wings and powerful flight muscles."
msgstr "一只圆润优雅的小喙鸟类，在喙和额之间长着一层隆起的皮肤，又称蜡膜。在地上时，它昂首阔步地走着，头不停地前后摇晃。由于具有较长的翼和强大的飞行肌群，它们能够长时间灵活飞行。"

#. ~ Description of monster "oversized crow"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A horrible bird grown three or four times bigger than ought to be possible and sporting a swollen gut that might look comical if it weren't for the razor sharp beak and the madness in its beady eyes."
msgstr "这只可怕的鸟长得比你想象中的体型要大三到四倍，它的腹部十分肿胀，如果不是因为它那锋利的喙和眼里的疯狂，它可能会显得有些滑稽可笑。"

#. ~ Description of monster "turkey"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A large and colorful game bird native to the forests of North America.  Its head and beak are covered in fleshy protuberances."
msgstr "一种原产于北美森林的大型美腻的鸟类。头和喙有着迷样的肉质棒状凸起。鸡盒的常客。"

#. ~ Description of monster "duck"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A mallard duck, often seen around rivers and other bodies of water.  It feeds primarily on insects, seeds, roots, and, pre-Cataclysm, bread scraps."
msgstr "一只野鸭，常见于河流或其他水体附近，主要以昆虫、种子、植物根为食。当然，在大灾变之前，还有面包屑。"

#. ~ Description of monster "grebe"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A medium sized aquatic bird with a long neck.  These birds can be distinguished by their strange leg placement which makes them great at diving."
msgstr "一种脖子很长的中型水鸟。这种鸟可以通过它们奇怪的腿的位置来区分，这使它们擅长潜水。"

#. ~ Description of monster "pheasant"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A medium-sized game bird that can have bright feathers depending on the sex and species."
msgstr "一只体型中等的猎禽，根据性别和品种不同，会有颜色不同的彩色羽毛。"

#. ~ Description of monster "sparrow"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A small bird with brown and gray feathers.  Introduced to North America in the 1850s, it is now one of the most abundant birds in the continent."
msgstr "一只长着棕灰色羽毛的小鸟。它于19世纪50年代被引入北美，现在是北美大陆数量最多的鸟类之一。"

#. ~ Description of monster "woodpecker"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A small bird with woody colors and a colored crest on its head.  These birds are well known for their ability to poke holes on trees while looking for grubs."
msgstr "一种长着木质颜色羽毛，头上有彩色羽冠的小鸟。这种鸟以它能在树上戳洞寻找害虫而闻名。"

#. ~ Description of monster "cardinal"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A small songbird, famous for its distinctive crest and facial markings.  A well-known example of sexual dimorphism, the males are colored much more vibrantly than the females."
msgstr "一只小型鸣禽，以其独特的羽冠和面部斑纹而闻名。作为众所周知的雌雄异形例子，雄鸟的羽毛比雌鸟要鲜艳得多。"

#. ~ Description of monster "raven"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A small, elegant black bird, famous for its distinctive call.  A clever bird, there is a glitter of mischief behind its eyes."
msgstr "一只小巧优雅的黑鸟，以其独特的叫声而闻名。是只聪明的鸟，眼睛中闪烁着淘气的光芒。"

#. ~ Description of monster "blue jay"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A small, noisy bird with distinctive blue feathers."
msgstr "一只小而吵闹的鸟，长着独特的蓝色羽毛。"

#. ~ Description of monster "brown chick"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A tiny darkly-colored chick, it could be from a number of different species."
msgstr "一只体型很小的深色雏鸟，太小了以至于你无法分辨它的物种，它可能来自几种不同的物种。"

#. ~ Description of monster "grey chick"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A tiny dull-colored chick, it could be from a number of different species."
msgstr "一只体型很小的深色雏鸟，太小了以至于你无法分辨它的物种，它可能来自几种不同的物种。"

#. ~ Description of monster "yellow chick"
#. ~ Description of monster "mon_grouse_chick"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A tiny yellow and brown chick, it could be from a number of different species."
msgstr "一只体型很小的黄棕色的雏鸟，太小了以至于你无法分辨它的物种，它可能来自几种不同的物种。"

#. ~ Description of monster "waterfowl chick"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A tiny yellow and brown waterfowl chick, it could be from a number of different species."
msgstr "一只体型很小的黄棕色的水禽雏鸟，太小了以至于你无法分辨它的物种，它可能来自几种不同的物种。"

#. ~ Description of monster "goose"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "A waterfowl well known for its loud honking and aggressive behavior."
msgstr "一只家鹅。一种以大声鸣叫和攻击性行为而闻名的水禽。"

#. ~ Description of monster "cormorant"
#: data/json/monsters/bird.json
msgid "An aquatic bird with a long snake-like neck.  They are considered coastal birds but many species can also be found on freshwater habitats."
msgstr "一种脖子像蛇一样长的水鸟。它们被认为是沿海鸟类，但许多物种也可以在淡水栖息地找到。"

