#. ~ Description of monster "kokanee salmon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A Kokanee salmon.  A very fatty, nutritious fish.  Tastes great smoked."
msgstr "一条内陆红鲑。非常肥美并且营养丰富。烟熏后味道好极了。"

#. ~ Description of monster "banded sunfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A banded sunfish.  A small fish related to bass and bluegill."
msgstr "一条暗色九棘日鲈。与鲈鱼和蓝鳃太阳鱼是近亲。"

#. ~ Description of monster "black crappie"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A black crappie.  A medium-sized fish also known as a 'calico bass'."
msgstr "一条黑莓鲈（黑斑刺盖太阳鱼），体型中等，经常被与大口副鲈（calico bass）混淆。"

#. ~ Description of monster "bluegill"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A bluegill, an invasive species in Japan.  Commonly gutted and cooked whole."
msgstr "一条蓝鳃太阳鱼，被引进日本后成为当地危险的入侵物种。一般把内脏去掉整条鱼烧了吃。"

#. ~ Description of monster "bowfin"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A bowfin.  These fish are related to gar but without the huge teeth, skin-rending scales, and aggression."
msgstr "一条弓鳍鱼。这些鱼和颌针鱼有亲缘关系，但是没有大尖齿、能切破皮的鳞片和凶暴的天性。"

#. ~ Description of monster "brook trout"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A brook trout.  A fish made popular by father-son fishing trips, except for the part where you have to gut it."
msgstr "一条溪鳟。因为\"父子垂钓之旅\"节目而家喻户晓，嗯，只要吃的时候尽量别去想挖内脏的过程就行。"

#. ~ Description of monster "brown bullhead"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A brown bullhead, a type of catfish.  Delicious when battered and fried."
msgstr "一条云斑鮰，又名褐首鲇，属于鲇形目。裹浆油炸后很美味。"

#. ~ Description of monster "brown trout"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A brown trout.  A fish made popular by father-son fishing trips, except for the part where you have to gut it."
msgstr "一条褐鳟。因为\"父子垂钓之旅\"节目而家喻户晓，嗯，只要吃的时候尽量别去想挖内脏的过程就行。"

#. ~ Description of monster "chain pickerel"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A chain pickerel.  It looks like a pike, but slightly smaller."
msgstr "一条暗色狗鱼（链纹狗鱼），看起来和白斑狗鱼（北方狗鱼）很像，但体型较小，体表也覆盖有一层黏液。"

#. ~ Description of monster "channel catfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A channel catfish.  It has a forked tail and long whiskers."
msgstr "一条斑点叉尾鮰。它长着分叉的尾巴和长长的胡须。"

#. ~ Description of monster "lobster"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A dark greenish crustacean in its natural habitat.  These were once considered pests barely worth eating, then some marketing genius started selling them to people as a delicacy and they took off in popularity… and price."
msgstr "一只暗绿色甲壳动物，生活在其自然栖息地之中。它们曾被认为是不堪食用的害虫，直到某些营销天才把它们当作美食来宣传，从此这玩意儿的知名度……还有价格……开始蹭蹭地飞涨。"

#. ~ Description of monster "fallfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A fallfish.  These fish are small cyprinids, related to carp."
msgstr "一条小眼须雅罗鱼，与鲤鱼同属鲤科，但体型更小。"

#. ~ Description of monster "summer flounder"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A flatfish, the summer flounder, also known as a fluke, likes to stay camouflaged against the ocean floor."
msgstr "一只大西洋牙鲆，是一种比目鱼，喜欢贴近海床来伪装自己。"

#. ~ Description of monster "European carp"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A golden-yellow common carp.  Some people think they don't taste great, but you can't afford to be choosy in the Cataclysm."
msgstr "一条金黄色的普通鲤鱼。有人觉得它们不好吃，但是你在大灾变的时候实在没有太多选择。"

#. ~ Description of monster "green sunfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A green sunfish.  A small fish related to bass and bluegill."
msgstr "一条蓝太阳鱼。一种跟鲈鱼及蓝鳃太阳鱼关系较近的小鱼。"

#. ~ Description of monster "mutant fish fry"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A half-translucent fish larva… though this one is far larger than the usual.  Impossible to identify which species it belongs to but you can safely tell that it is going to outgrow normal fish you're used to seeing."
msgstr "一条半透明的鱼苗……但是这条比一般的鱼苗要大得多。你无法确定它属于哪个物种，但你可以确认它将长成超过你所见过的大部分正常鱼类的体型。"

#. ~ Description of monster "huge fish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A huge fish."
msgstr "一条巨型鱼。"

#. ~ Description of monster "grass carp"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A huge grass carp.  A golden, herbivorous fish."
msgstr "一条大草鱼。一种金色的食草鱼类。"

#. ~ Description of monster "huge salmon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A huge mutant salmon grown almost to the size of an alligator."
msgstr "一条几乎和鳄鱼一样大的变异鲑鱼。"

#. ~ Description of monster "leaper salmon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A huge mutant salmon, one that outgrows even the other ones present.  On its sides, beneath the fins, are visible two flesh-colored tubes which propel water as it leaps."
msgstr "一条巨大的变异鲑鱼，它的体型甚至超过了其他的鲑鱼。  在其两侧的鳍下方，可以看到两根肉色的管子，在水跳跃时推动水流。"

#. ~ Description of monster "lake trout"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A lake trout.  A fish made popular by father-son fishing trips, except for the part where you have to gut it."
msgstr "一条湖鳟。因为\"父子垂钓之旅\"节目而家喻户晓，嗯，只要吃的时候尽量别去想挖内脏的过程就行。"

#. ~ Description of monster "lake whitefish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A lake whitefish, closely related to salmon.  One can assume they taste just as nice when smoked."
msgstr "一条湖白鲑（鲱形白鲑），在北美水域广泛分布，栖息地延伸至北极圈。因为是鲑鱼的近亲，你可以认为它们烟熏了之后也一样好吃。"

#. ~ Description of monster "longnose gar"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A large ancient type of fish with a mean jaw and poisonous eggs."
msgstr "一种古老的大型鱼类，有着健壮的下颚和有毒的卵。"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant crayfish larva"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A large crayfish larva already larger than non-mutated adults of its kind."
msgstr "一只巨型鳌虾的幼虫，已经比没有变异过的成年人还要大了。"

#. ~ Description of monster "large fish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A large fish."
msgstr "一条大型鱼。"

#. ~ Description of monster "seweranha"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A large, mutant variety of carp.  It has shimmering green scales and a mouth lined with three jagged rows of razor-sharp teeth."
msgstr "一只巨大的变异鲤鱼，它身上长满了闪闪发光的绿色鳞片，三瓣嘴充满了锯齿状的牙齿。"

#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic cod"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A large, white-meat fish known for its mild flavor and flaky texture.  Highly prized in both commercial and recreational fishing."
msgstr "一种大型白肉鱼类，以其较淡的风味和片状的肉质而闻名，在商业捕捞和休闲垂钓中具有极高价值。"

#. ~ Description of monster "largemouth bass"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A largemouth bass.  Very popular with sport fishermen."
msgstr "一条大嘴鲈。很受钓鱼爱好者的喜爱。"

#. ~ Description of monster "razorclaw"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A man-sized crustacean clad in iron-like chitin, capable of emitting horrible shrieking noises.  Often spotted near shipwrecks or other dark, damp places, which it uses as nesting grounds."
msgstr "一只人型大小的甲壳类生物，浑身覆盖着铁一样甲壳，能发恐怖的尖叫声。经常在它用作筑巢地点沉船或其他黑暗潮湿的地方附近被发现。"

#. ~ Description of monster "medium fish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A medium fish."
msgstr "一条中型鱼。"

#. ~ Description of monster "pollock"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A member of the cod family, pollock is a versatile fish known for its white, delicate meat and mild taste."
msgstr "狭鳕是鳕鱼的一种，用途广泛，以其白色细嫩的肉质和较淡的风味为人所知。"

#. ~ Description of monster "crustacean larva"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A minuscule half-translucent crustacean larva.  Impossible to identify which species it belongs to."
msgstr "一种微小的半透明甲壳类动物幼虫。无法确定它属于哪个物种。"

#. ~ Description of monster "fish fry"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A minuscule half-translucent fish larva.  Impossible to identify which species it belongs to."
msgstr "一条微小的半透明幼鱼。无法确定它属于哪个物种。"

#. ~ Description of monster "muskellunge"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A muskellunge.  Closely related to pike but even larger, it shares the same aggression and sharp teeth."
msgstr "一条大梭鱼，与狗鱼是近亲，但生活在纬度更低的地方。它的体型更大，而且同样有尖锐的牙齿和强烈的攻击性。"

#. ~ Description of monster "oversized crayfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A mutant crayfish the size of a dog, with a brown carapace, claws, and long antennae."
msgstr "一只体型和狗一般大小的变异鳌虾，长着棕色的躯壳、爪子和长长的触须。"

#. ~ Description of monster "alpha razorclaw"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A mutated crustacean the size of a horse.  With its bulky body and sword-like pincers, it serves as a protector of the nest."
msgstr "一只浑身血红色，体型巨大的利爪怪。它用那剑一般的钳子来守护自己的巢穴。"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant salmon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A mutated salmon roughly the size of a person.  Quite dangerous to the inexperienced angler."
msgstr "一条和人一般大小的变异鲑鱼，对于经验不足的渔夫来说非常危险。"

#. ~ Description of monster "northern pike"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A northern pike.  Pike can be pretty aggressive fish, careful around those teeth."
msgstr "一条北美梭鱼。梭鱼是一种攻击性很强的鱼，当心它们的牙齿。"

#. ~ Description of monster "haddock"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A popular food fish, the haddock is recognized by its dark lateral line and a black blotch above the pectoral fin."
msgstr "黑线鳕是一种知名的食用鱼类，可通过两侧的黑色线条和胸鳍上方的黑斑来辨认。"

#. ~ Description of monster "pumpkinseed"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A pumpkinseed sunfish.  A small fish related to bass and bluegill."
msgstr "一条驼背太阳鱼。一种跟鲈鱼及蓝鳃太阳鱼关系较近的小鱼。"

#. ~ Description of monster "rainbow trout"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A rainbow trout.  A fish made popular by father-son fishing trips, except for the part where you have to gut it."
msgstr "一条虹鳟。因为\"父子垂钓之旅\"节目而家喻户晓，嗯，只要吃的时候尽量别去想挖内脏的过程就行。"

#. ~ Description of monster "redbreast sunfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A redbreast sunfish.  A small fish related to bass and bluegill."
msgstr "一条红胸太阳鱼。一种跟鲈鱼及蓝鳃太阳鱼关系较近的小鱼。"

#. ~ Description of monster "burbot"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A relatively large fish that looks like a cross between a catfish and an eel, and is the only freshwater fish from the order that cods hail from."
msgstr "一种相对较大的鱼，看起来像是鲶鱼和鳗鱼的杂交体，是鳕鱼目中唯一的淡水鱼。"

#. ~ Description of monster "rock bass"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A rock bass.  Related to sunfish, this tiny fish has a camouflage-like patterning and red eyes."
msgstr "一条岩钝鲈。这种形似太阳鱼的小鱼，有着迷彩状的伪装和红色的眼睛。"

#. ~ Description of monster "round whitefish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A round whitefish, closely related to salmon.  One can assume they taste just as nice when smoked."
msgstr "一条圆白鲑，与鲑鱼亲缘关系密切。可以想象，它们经过烟熏后的味道也一样好。"

#. ~ Description of monster "small fish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A small fish."
msgstr "一条小型鱼。"

#. ~ Description of monster "black sea bass"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A small, robust fish, the black sea bass is known for its dark, mottled color and meaty texture."
msgstr "黑海鲈是一种耐受性强的小型鱼类，以其斑驳的深色外皮和结实的口感为人所知。"

#. ~ Description of monster "yellow perch"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A small, sprightly perch.  It is a very bony fish, still has some tasty meat on it though."
msgstr "一条活蹦乱跳的小鲈鱼。刺特别多，但肉也还挺好吃的。"

#. ~ Description of monster "smallmouth bass"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A smallmouth bass.  Infamously intolerant to pollution, the presence of smallmouth bass is a good indicator of how clean a body of water is."
msgstr "一条小口黑鲈。由于无法忍受水污染，小口黑鲈的存在是衡量水质清洁与否的好指标。"

#. ~ Description of monster "striped bass"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A striped bass.  Mostly a saltwater fish, they migrate to fresher water to spawn."
msgstr "一只条纹鲈。一般生活在咸水里，但在产卵期会游到淡水中。"

#. ~ Description of monster "tiny fish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A tiny fish."
msgstr "一条微型鱼。"

#. ~ Description of monster "lake sturgeon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A very large armored bottom-feeder, the lake sturgeon is one of the largest unmutated fish one can find in the freshwater regions of New England."
msgstr "湖鲟是一种非常大的带甲底食性鱼类，是新英格兰地区最大的未变异淡水鱼类之一。"

#. ~ Description of monster "walleye"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A walleye.  A green-brown medium-sized fish with a white belly."
msgstr "一条碧古鱼。一种绿褐身体、白色肚腩的中型鱼。"

#. ~ Description of monster "warmouth"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A warmouth, similar to a rock bass.  This small fish is related to the sunfish."
msgstr "一条大口突鳃太阳鱼，类似于岩钝鲈，这种小鱼属于太阳鱼。"

#. ~ Description of monster "white catfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A white catfish.  A small whiskered fish with a broad head."
msgstr "一条白叉尾鮰。一种长着细长胡须的宽头鱼类。"

#. ~ Description of monster "white sucker"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A white sucker.  It has a streamlined body with a round mouth."
msgstr "一条白亚口鱼，有着流线型的身体和一张圆嘴巴。"

#. ~ Description of monster "yellow bullhead"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A yellow bullhead, a type of catfish.  Delicious when battered and fried, though smaller than its brown cousin."
msgstr "一条黄鮰鱼，属于鲶鱼的一种。捣碎油炸后味道鲜美，不过体型比它的表亲云斑鮰小。"

#. ~ Description of monster "scup"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "Also known as porgy, the scup is a small fish commonly found in Atlantic coastal waters, recognizable by its silver body with blue and purple tinges."
msgstr "门齿鲷是一种常见于大西洋海岸水域的小型鱼类，可通过其银色的身体及蓝色和紫色的色泽来分辨。"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "American eel"
msgid_plural "American eels"
msgstr[0] "美洲鳗鲡"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "American pickerel"
msgid_plural "American pickerels"
msgstr[0] "北美狗鱼"

#. ~ Description of monster "American eel"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "An American eel.  They used to be quite common in these parts until the dams were built.  They'll get a second chance now that those aren't running."
msgstr "一条美洲鳗鲡。它们在水坝修成之前还是挺常见的。现在大坝不再运作了，也许它们能有二次繁衍的机会。"

#. ~ Description of monster "American pickerel"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "An American pickerel.  It looks like a pike, but unlike its chain pickerel cousin, this one is way smaller."
msgstr "一条美国狗鱼。它看起来像一条长矛，但与它的表亲暗色狗鱼不同，这条要小得多。"

#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic mackerel"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "An Atlantic mackerel, known for its distinctive striped pattern."
msgstr "一只大西洋鲭，因其独特的条纹为人所知。"

#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic salmon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "An Atlantic salmon.  A very fatty, nutritious fish.  Tastes great smoked."
msgstr "一条大西洋鲑。非常肥美并且营养丰富。烟熏后味道好极了。"

#. ~ Description of monster "colossal crayfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "An enormous mutated gray crayfish with pincer claws and long antennae."
msgstr "一只体型巨大的灰色变异鳌虾，长着大大的钳爪和长长的触须。"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "Atlantic bluefin tuna"
msgid_plural "Atlantic bluefin tuna"
msgstr[0] "大西洋蓝鳍金枪鱼"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "Atlantic cod"
msgid_plural "Atlantic cod"
msgstr[0] "大西洋鳕"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "Atlantic halibut"
msgid_plural "Atlantic halibut"
msgstr[0] "大比目鱼"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "Atlantic mackerel"
msgid_plural "Atlantic mackerel"
msgstr[0] "大西洋鲭"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "Atlantic salmon"
msgid_plural "Atlantic salmon"
msgstr[0] "大西洋鲑"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "European carp"
msgid_plural "European carp"
msgstr[0] "欧洲鲤"

#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic bluefin tuna"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "One of the largest and fastest fish in the waters of New England, the bluefin tuna is a streamlined predator with a dark blue back and silvery sides."
msgstr "蓝鳍金枪鱼是新英格兰水域最大和速度最快的肉食性鱼类，具有流线型的身体、深蓝色的背部和银色的侧面。"

#. ~ Description of monster "lakebed creeper"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "Pink and translucent, with all of its otherworldly organs visible through its skin, this meter-high conical creature creeps along the seabed with its stubby, furry legs.  It contracts some kind of retracted barbed filaments into an orifice at its rear as it aims it at potential prey."
msgstr "这种一米高的圆锥形生物呈粉红色半透明，透过皮肤可以看到所有超凡脱俗的器官，它用粗短、毛茸茸的腿沿着海底爬行。  当它瞄准潜在的猎物时，它会将某种缩回的带刺细丝收缩到其后部的孔中。"

#. ~ Death message of monster "fish fry"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#, c-format
msgid "The %s is smashed to non-recognizable pieces."
msgstr "%s 被碾碎成了无法辨别的碎肉。"

#. ~ Description of monster "bluefish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "The bluefish, a moderately proportioned marine fish, is known for its aggressive nature and sharp teeth.  It sports a distinct blue-green coloration."
msgstr "扁鲹是一种中等大小的海鱼，以其天生的攻击性和锋利的牙齿而出名，带有独特的蓝绿色泽。"

#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic halibut"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "The largest flatfish in the ocean, known for its dense, firm texture and mild flavor."
msgstr "大比目鱼是海洋中最大的比目鱼，以其结实的肉质和较淡的风味为人所知。"

#. ~ Description of monster "crayfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "This crustacean looks like a tiny lobster, but is actually a completely different species.  If you could get ahold of a bunch more of these, a hefty pot of boiling water, and some spicy seasonings…"
msgstr "这种甲壳动物看起来像一只小号的龙虾，但实际上两者是完全不同的物种。要是你能找到一大堆这玩意，烧一大锅开水，再加一些足够辣的调味品……"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant crayfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "This crustacean, larger than a man, resembles a mud-colored lobster."
msgstr "这种甲壳类动物比人还大，类似于泥色的龙虾。"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant carp"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "This thing looks like a carp, but huge and very, very angry.  Death is the gift of the carp god."
msgstr "这只怪物看起来很像是鲤鱼，只是体型十分巨大，而且非常暴躁。死亡是鲤鱼王送给你的礼物。"

#. ~ Description of monster "shortnose sturgeon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "While the shortnose sturgeon is still large, it is nothing compared to its cousin - the lake sturgeon.  What really sets it apart, however, is its signature shorter snout."
msgstr "虽然短吻鲟确实很大，但与它的表亲湖鲟相比，只能说是小巫见大巫。然而，真正让它与众不同的是它标志性的短吻。"

#. ~ Description of monster "goldfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "Yes, this is that common pet fish.  Though, given its size and the fact that it's still alive, you can take a wild guess that this one is feral."
msgstr "是的，就是那个及其常见的宠物鱼。不过，考虑到它的体型，以及它还活着，你可以大胆地猜测这条鱼是野生的。"

