#. ~ Description of monster "dog"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A (usually) four-legged omnivorous mammal, man's best friend since time immemorial.  This specimen is of average size, like a labrador or a pit bull."
msgstr "一种（通常）四足杂食性哺乳动物，自古以来就是人类最好的朋友。  该标本中等大小，如拉布拉多犬或斗牛犬。"

#. ~ Description of monster "llama calf"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A baby llama.  Unlike their parents, the calves tend to be more friendly in demeanor."
msgstr "一只小羊驼。与它们的父母不同，小犊子在举止上往往更加友好。"

#. ~ Description of monster "wild bunny"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A baby rabbit with a cute wiggling nose and long ears.  It is extremely skittish."
msgstr "一只小兔子，有着可爱的会动的鼻子和长长的耳朵。  它非常胆怯。"

#. ~ Description of monster "bunny"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A baby rabbit with a cute wiggling nose and long ears.  This one is of the domesticated variety, commonly kept as a pet, a research subject, or a source of food."
msgstr "一只小兔子，有着可爱的会动的鼻子和长长的耳朵。  这是一种驯养品种，通常作为宠物、研究对象或食物来源饲养。"

#. ~ Description of monster "llama"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A big and wooly herbivore domesticated by the Andean cultures of South America.  Llamas and their kin are distant relatives to camels and are adapted to mountain environments."
msgstr "一种体大毛长的食草动物，被南美安第斯文明驯化。羊驼和它们的同类是骆驼的远亲，适应了山区气候环境。"

#. ~ Description of monster "kitten"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A cuddly kitten scampering amid the ruins of human civilization."
msgstr "一只可爱的幼年猫，喵喵叫着在死亡的夹缝间流窜。看上去是野猫。"

#. ~ Description of monster "wolf"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A cunning pack predator, once extinct in the New England area, the wolf was successfully reintroduced and their numbers reached record highs in the decade before the Cataclysm.  Lucky you."
msgstr "一只生活在新英格兰地区的狡猾捕猎者，曾经一度灭绝。但是大灾变让他们成功的恢复了种群数量，有着出色的团队协作捕猎能力。祝你面对它们时还能好运。"

#. ~ Description of monster "guard dog"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A dog of intimidating size and bearing, it looks like it's had some training and could be fairly dangerous."
msgstr "这只狗的体型和举止令人生畏，看起来受过一些训练，可能相当危险。"

#. ~ Description of monster "fancy rat"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A domesticated Norway rat, bred by rat fanciers to be far less skittish than the wild type.  These clever animals were omnipresent in modern biomedical research, and were commonly kept as pets."
msgstr "一种家养的挪威鼠，由老鼠爱好者培育而成，比野生型要容易受惊得多。  这些聪明的动物在现代生物医学研究中无处不在，并且通常被当作宠物饲养。"

#. ~ Description of monster "pig"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A domesticated omnivore descended from the wild boar, intelligent and inquisitive.  Left to its own devices, it has gone feral."
msgstr "一种源自于野猪的杂食性驯养后裔，既聪明又好奇，还很美味。现在它已恢复了野性，蓄势待发。"

#. ~ Description of monster "piglet"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A domesticated omnivore descended from the wild boar, intelligent and inquisitive.  Left to its own devices, it has gone feral.  Unlike the fully grown version, this juvenile can be tamed."
msgstr "一种源自于野猪的杂食性驯养后裔，既聪明又好奇，还很美味。现在它已恢复了野性，蓄势待发。不同于成年个体，它还能被再次驯服。"

#. ~ Description of monster "great tusked moose"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A gargantuan ungulate sporting a huge rack of antlers and a pair of curving tusks.  It tosses its head as it stampedes across the landscape, spattering foam from its quivering jaw."
msgstr "一种巨大的有蹄类动物，拥有巨大的鹿角和一对弯曲的獠牙。  当它在大地上奔跑时，它会抬起头，颤抖的下巴溅出泡沫。"

#. ~ Description of monster "goat"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A hooved browsing mammal known for climbing and eating just about anything.  Either gender can have horns."
msgstr "一种胆小的四蹄食草哺乳动物，以攀爬和吃任何东西而闻名。山羊不论公母都会长角。"

#. ~ Description of monster "kid"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A hooved browsing mammal known for climbing and eating just about anything.  The young are famously cute and cuddly."
msgstr "一种胆小的四蹄食草哺乳动物，以攀爬和吃任何东西而闻名。幼年山羊以可爱著称。"

#. ~ Description of monster "horse"
#. ~ Description of monster "Scott's horse"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Megafauna/monsters/mf_domestic.json
msgid "A hooved grazing mammal with a mane of hair, a sweeping tail, and powerful-looking muscles.  A stalwart companion to humans for longer than recorded history, with some effort you should be able to get this one to trust you enough to ride it."
msgstr "一匹拥有浓密的鬃毛，摇晃的尾巴和强壮的肌肉的哺乳动物。作为比有记录的历史更长时间以来人类坚定的伴侣，通过一些努力，你应该能够让它足够信任你来驾驭它。"

#. ~ Description of monster "mon_horse_police"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A hooved grazing mammal with a mane of hair, a sweeping tail, and powerful-looking muscles.  This one has been trained to have less of a fear reaction in order to assist with riot control and standard police work.  With some effort, you should be able to get this one to trust you enough to ride it."
msgstr "一匹拥有浓密的鬃毛，摇晃的尾巴和强壮的肌肉的哺乳动物。这个个体经过训练减少了惊恐，辅助参与镇暴及标准的出警工作。通过一些努力，你应该能取得它的信任并骑上它。"

#. ~ Description of monster "foal"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A hooved grazing mammal with a mane of hair, a sweeping tail, and powerful-looking muscles.  This one is still a juvenile; it'll take a while before it can be ridden."
msgstr "一匹拥有浓密的鬃毛，摇晃的尾巴和强壮的肌肉的哺乳动物。它还未成年；需要过一段时间才能骑乘。"

#. ~ Description of monster "black bear cub"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A juvenile American black bear.  This one isn't much of a threat, but be wary of its parent; black bears are known for their protectiveness."
msgstr "美国黑熊的幼体。这个小家伙虽然看上去没啥威胁，但是你需要当心它的父母；人人都知道黑熊有保护幼崽的习性。"

#. ~ Description of monster "reindeer fawn"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A juvenile caribou, it is smaller than its adult counterparts, as well as having shorter antlers."
msgstr "一只幼年北美驯鹿，比成年驯鹿体型更小，角也更短。"

#. ~ Description of monster "fawn"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A juvenile northern woodland white-tailed deer, a quick and strong grazing animal.  Favored prey of coyotes, wolves, and giant spider mutants."
msgstr "北方森林中的栖居的白尾鹿的幼体，快速灵敏且健壮，狼和巨型变异蛛最喜爱的猎物。"

#. ~ Description of monster "muskrat"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A large omnivorous rodent with a thick furry pelt, found in wetlands across the Northern Hemisphere.  It marks its territory with a musky odor for which it is named."
msgstr "一只大型杂食性啮齿动物，浑身长着浓密的毛皮，在整个北半球的湿地中均有出没。它用一种类似麝香的气味来标记自己的领地，而这也正是它的名字的由来。"

#. ~ Description of monster "big dog"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A particularly big dog, weighing as much as some adult humans.  It looks formidable, though no more aggressive than any other breed."
msgstr "这是一只体型特别大的狗，体重堪比一些成年人。它看起来很威猛，但并不比其他品种更具攻击性。"

#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "skunk"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A skunk raises its tail and squirts!"
msgstr "%s举起了胳膊！"

#. ~ Description of monster "squirrel"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A small granivorous rodent with a long bushy tail, often seen darting amid the branches of trees.  A skittish varmint with an expression of unwavering austerity, it is the mortal enemy of cat and dog alike."
msgstr "一只小型食谷类啮齿动物，长有浓密毛发的尾巴，经常可以看到它在树枝间穿梭，表情坚定又淘气，惧怕猫和狗。"

#. ~ Description of monster "raccoon"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A small mammal native to North America, distinctive for its dexterous paws and facial markings.  It is resourceful and agile enough to open sealed containers in search of food."
msgstr "北美本土的小型哺乳动物，具有灵巧的爪子和显著的面部特征。它足智多谋，且足够灵活，据说为了觅食能打开密封的容器。"

#. ~ Description of monster "wild rabbit"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A small mammal with a cute wiggling nose and long ears.  It is extremely skittish."
msgstr "一只小型哺乳动物，鼻子可爱地翕动着，长着软绵绵的球形尾巴，而且肉质鲜美。"

#. ~ Description of monster "rabbit"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A small mammal with a cute wiggling nose and long ears.  This one is of the domesticated variety, commonly kept as a pet, a research subject, or a source of food."
msgstr "一种小型哺乳动物，鼻子可爱地扭动着，耳朵长长的。这种动物是家养品种，通常被作为宠物饲养、研究对象或食物来源。"

#. ~ Description of monster "fox"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A small, omnivorous canine with almost cat-like mannerisms.  It is a solitary hunter, and one of the only canids able to climb trees."
msgstr "一种小型杂食性犬科动物，但几乎有着猫一样的习性。它是一个孤独的猎手，也是唯一一种会爬树的犬科动物。"

#. ~ Description of monster "bobcat"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Megafauna/monsters/mf_predators.json
msgid "A spotted wild cat living across much of North America.  It is not a serious threat to humans, but it can be aggressive when threatened."
msgstr "一种生活在北美大部分地区的斑点野猫。它对人类而言没有严重的威胁，但它在受到威胁时可能具有攻击性。"

#. ~ Description of monster "sheep"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A timid, hooved grazing mammal, and one of the first animals ever domesticated.  Its body is covered in a thick layer of wool, and the males have long, spiraling horns."
msgstr "一种胆小的四蹄食草哺乳动物，是人类最早驯化的动物之一。它的身体覆盖着一层厚厚的毛皮，雄性有长长的螺旋状的角。"

#. ~ Description of monster "lamb"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A timid, hooved grazing mammal, and one of the first animals ever domesticated.  Its body is covered in a thick layer of wool."
msgstr "一种胆小的四蹄食草哺乳动物，是人类最早驯化的动物之一。它的身体覆盖着一层厚厚的毛皮。"

#. ~ Description of monster "little dog"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A tiny dog, surviving the cataclysm against all odds."
msgstr "一只小狗，在灾难中克服重重困难幸存下来。"

#. ~ Description of monster "ferret kit"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A young domesticated ferret, known as a kit."
msgstr "一只年轻的家养雪貂，或者说雪貂幼崽。"

#. ~ Description of monster "reindeer"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "Also known as the caribou, this deer is native to North America and parts of Eurasia.  Although usually friendly, they can be aggressive during the autumn and winter mating season as well as when hungry."
msgstr "这种鹿也被称为北美驯鹿，原产于北美和欧亚大陆的部分地区。尽管它们通常很温顺，但它们在秋冬交配季节以及饥饿时会表现出攻击性。"

#. ~ Description of monster "groundhog"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "Also known as the woodchuck, this ground squirrel has no actual talent for chucking wood."
msgstr "被称为土拨鼠，这只生活在地面上的松鼠科动物喜欢掘土，神出鬼没，会\"啊啊啊\"的叫。"

#. ~ Description of monster "little puppy"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "An adorable, defenseless puppy.  It's tiny now, and it doesn't seem like it's going to get much bigger."
msgstr "一只可爱又无助的小狗。它现在很小，看起来也不会长得很大。"

#. ~ Description of monster "big puppy"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "An adorable, defenseless puppy.  It's tiny now, but it looks like it could grow up to be pretty big."
msgstr "一只可爱的小狗，毫无防备。它现在很小，但看起来长大后可能会很大。"

#. ~ Description of monster "puppy"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "An adorable, defenseless puppy.  Much safer to tame than an adult dog."
msgstr "一只可爱而无助的幼年拳师獒犬。驯服起来比一只成年狗要安全得多。"

#. ~ Description of monster "wolf puppy"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "An adorable, defenseless wolf pup that will, in time, grow into a not-so-defenseless and debatably-adorable wolf.  Be careful of its parents, who are sure to be around nearby!"
msgstr "一只可爱而无助的小狼仔，终有一天会长成一只不再毫无防备且并非可爱的大灰狼。小心它的父母，他们肯定就在附近！"

#. ~ Description of monster "rat"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "Considered vermin by many, maybe even harbingers of the Cataclysm, this diminutive rodent looks pretty harmless up close."
msgstr "这种小型啮齿动物被许多人视为害虫，甚至可能是大灾难的预兆，但近距离观察时却显得相当无害。"

#. ~ Description of monster "ferret"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "Domesticated from the European polecat, this sleek and energetic mammal was commonly kept as a pet before the Cataclysm."
msgstr "由欧洲鼬驯化而来，这只毛光油亮精力旺盛的哺乳动物在大灾变之前往往被当作宠物饲养。"

#. ~ Description of monster "cat"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "In the absence of human stewardship, this tiny domesticated predator has grown wary of humans.  Harried by the rigors of survival, it has become very skittish but is still motivated by food."
msgstr "在没有人类照料的情况下，这种小型家养捕食动物对人类变得十分警惕。迫于生存的严酷考验，它变得异常敏感，但仍受食物驱使"

#. ~ Description of monster "bat"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "One of the vesper bats, a family of winged insect-eating mammals.  It roosts in caves and other hollows, and uses a form of echolocation to aerially navigate through tricky terrain at rapid speeds."
msgstr "昼伏夜出的蝙蝠，可以飞行的哺乳动物，以昆虫为食，一般群居在山洞或者其他凹陷处，使用超声波定位和导航，移动非常迅速。"

#. ~ Description of monster "wild boar"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "Originally not native in the U.S., this wild omnivore is a crossbreed between the Eurasian wild boar escaped from hunting reserves and the domesticated pig gone feral in the wilderness.  Its population has skyrocketed during the last few decades."
msgstr "这种野生杂食性动物并非原产于美国，是由从狩猎保护区逃出来的欧亚野猪和野外野化后的家猪杂交而成的品种。在过去的几十年里，它们在美国的种群数量猛增。"

#. ~ Description of monster "wild boar piglet"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "Originally not native in the U.S., this wild omnivore is a crossbreed between the Eurasian wild boar escaped from hunting reserves and the domesticated pig gone feral in the wilderness.  This one is just a baby, and is surprisingly cute."
msgstr "这种野生杂食性动物并非原产于美国，是由从狩猎保护区逃出来的欧亚野猪和野外野化后的家猪杂交而成的品种。它还只不过是个婴儿，非常可爱。"

#. ~ Description of monster "sick deer"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "Patchy fur stretches over this animal's ribs.  Its legs wobble and it continually tosses its head as it plods on, seemingly unaware that it's dying."
msgstr "这只动物的肋骨上长着斑驳的皮毛。它步履蹒跚，一边艰难前行，一边不停地摇头，似乎并未意识到自己正在走向死亡。"

#. ~ Description of monster "charred human"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "Placeholder for charred human corpses.  If you see this, it's a bug."
msgstr "该物品用于烧焦的人类尸体的占位符。如果你看到这个，说明游戏出bug了。"

#. ~ Description of monster "child"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "Placeholder for children corpses.  If you see this, it's a bug."
msgstr "该物品用于儿童尸体的占位符。如果你看到这个，说明游戏出bug了。"

#. ~ Description of monster "human"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "Placeholder for human corpses.  If you see this, it's a bug."
msgstr "该物品用于人类尸体的占位符。如果你看到这个，说明游戏出bug了。"

#. ~ Description of monster "tusked moose calf"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "Standing taller than a fully grown deer, this mutated moose calf has a pair of curved tusks that look quite out of place."
msgstr "这只突变的麋鹿幼崽比一只成年鹿还要高，长着一对弯曲的鹿角，看起来非常不协调。"

