#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/out_of_town_2.json
msgid "What happened after the acid mist?"
msgstr "酸雾过后发生了什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/out_of_town_2.json
msgid "What happened to your friend?"
msgstr "你朋友怎么了？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"&<npc_name> inhales sharply and breaks eye contact.\n"
"\n"
"\"I…  I mean, I can sympathize with someone who thinks that way…  The government lies all the time and they're probably out there somewhere STILL lying.  But nah, I wouldn't leave my computer laying around, unprotected.\""
msgstr ""
"&<npc_name> 猛吸一口气，视线游移。\n"
"\n"
"\"我……我的意思是，我同情有这种想法的人……政府总是撒谎，在外面的某些地方，他们可能依旧在撒谎。但不行，我不能让我没有锁定的电脑随意放置。\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid ""
"&<npc_name> sighs and pauses for a moment.\n"
"\n"
"\"Listen…  I know what you think I am, but the threats are real.  The dead are walking, strange hellspawn crawling out of…  well, I can't even talk about it.  Whatever demonic, technological abomination, bio-weapon the communists unleashed on the world is definitely out of their control.  Look around you!  Isn't it obvious something bigger is going on?\""
msgstr ""
"&<npc_name>叹了口气，停顿了片刻。\n"
"\n"
"\"听着……我知道你认为我是哪种人，但威胁真实存在。死人横行，奇怪的地狱族裔爬出……好吧，我甚至无法谈论它。无论那是什么恶魔的、邪恶技术的，还是贡铲党放到这个世界上的生物兵器，显然都已经失控了。看看你周围！明显有更大的事情正在发生，不是吗？\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "'War of the Worlds', baby!  That's what I like to hear!  Let's get moving…"
msgstr "\"世界大战\"，宝贝！这就是我喜欢听的！让我们动起来吧……"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "*tenses up and stares in disbelief.  \"You're playing with me.  The government doesn't exist anymore…  You better be messing around or I-\""
msgstr "*紧张起来，难以置信地凝视着。\"你在玩我。政府已经不存在了……你最好是在胡闹，否则我——\""

#. ~ Player message in an effect
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "<npc_name> marks the location of the LMOE shelter on your map."
msgstr "<npc_name>在地图上标出了LMOE避难所的位置。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "A Marshal, huh?  I could tell there was something a bit square about you.  Or… round, I suppose, ha!  In my experience, when people at that level start talking stuff like that, there's at least some truth to it."
msgstr "执法官？我看得出来你有点正经，或者说……圆滑，哈！根据我的经验，当那种级别的人开始讨论那样的话题时，至少说的会有些道理。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgid "A contractor?  How much does something like a survivalist shelter cost?"
msgstr "外包雇员？这么一个生存避难所要多少钱？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid "Almost as much as my house, in the end.  I think they realized they could make a lot of money as things got worse and worse.  But it's nicer than my house, too.  They said the ventilation system was built to withstand a month of anything: nuclear fallout, biological attack, you name it.  Concrete and soil above me to absorb radiation, appliances and supplies…  I even brought some old books I've never read.  I always knew it would come to this."
msgstr "最终花费和我家差不多。我觉得他们意识到了随着事情变糟，能赚的钱也越来越多。但是这里也比我家好多了。他们说通风系统能在任何情况下坚持一个月——核尘埃、生物武器，之类的。头顶上的混凝土和泥土能吸收辐射，还有各式家电和补给……我甚至还带了一些从来没读过的旧书。我就知道事情会变成这样。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
