#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Bryan Rooters, Reception Manager\n"
" TO: Joe Shert, Receptionist\n"
" RE: Performance Eval\n"
"\n"
" Hi Joe.\n"
" Your 90-day performance evaluation is due.  Please plan to meet with me in my office on Tuesday.\n"
" Thanks."
msgstr ""
"&来自：布莱恩·鲁特斯，接待经理\n"
"发往：乔·舍特，接待员\n"
"主题：绩效评估\n"
"\n"
"嗨，乔。\n"
"你的季度绩效评估时间要到了。请按计划在周二到我的办公室面谈。\n"
"谢谢。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Bryan Rooters, Reception Manager\n"
" TO: Receptionists\n"
" RE: Housekeeping\n"
"\n"
" Hi team,\n"
" Please be aware that the decision has been made to let go some of the housekeeping staff.\n"
" This decision was made by management to ensure that our operation can run as smoothly and efficiently as possible by passing on these cost savings to the residents.\n"
" To keep up with our high standards of elder care, I will be assigning some additional small tasks to you in the near future.\n"
" As you know, here at Shady Hills we value each and every employee and see this as an excellent opportunity to grow, learn, and provide for the Shady Hills family.\n"
" Please let me know if you have any questions.\n"
" Thanks."
msgstr ""
"&来自：布莱恩·鲁特斯，接待经理\n"
"发往：全体接待员\n"
"主题：家政\n"
"\n"
"嗨，亲们，\n"
"请注意，公司已决定为部分家政人员办理毕业手续。\n"
"管理层做出这一决定是为了确保我们的运营能够尽可能顺利和高效地进行，并为住户节省成本。\n"
"为了跟上我们高标准的老年护理，我会在不久的将来分配一些额外的小任务给你们。\n"
"如你们所知，在 Shady Hills，我们重视每一位员工，并将其视为成长、学习和为 Shady Hills 大家庭提供服务的绝佳机会。\n"
"如果你有任何问题，请告诉我。\n"
"谢谢。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Connie Malackey, Receptionist\n"
" TO: Joe Shert, Receptionist\n"
" RE: Ghosts!?\n"
"\n"
" Joe!  After we heard those weird noises the other night, I talked to some of the nurses.\n"
" We aren't the only ones!  Everyone has heard weird noises coming from the walls.\n"
" Do you think this place is haunted!?"
msgstr ""
"&来自：康妮·马拉奇，接待员\n"
"发往：乔·舍特，接待员\n"
"主题：幽灵！？\n"
"\n"
"乔！那天晚上我们听到那些奇怪的声音后，我和一些护士聊了一下。\n"
"不光是我们听到了！每个人都听到过从墙后面传来的奇怪声音。\n"
"你不觉得这地方闹鬼吗！？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Connie Malackey, Receptionist\n"
" TO: Joe Shert, Receptionist\n"
" RE: Mrs.  Palmero\n"
"\n"
" Hi Joe.\n"
" So - you know how Mrs.  Palmero has been acting weird and constantly talking about baking cookies?\n"
" I was talking to one of the nurses and they said that Mrs.  Palmero was prescribed this new medicine?\n"
" It's this weird powder stuff.  Apparently the nurses aren't even qualified to give it to her - she needs a special doctor to come in every day!\n"
" Crazy, right?  I wish all I had to worry about was baking cookies…"
msgstr ""
"&来自：康妮·马拉奇，接待员\n"
"发往：乔·舍特，接待员\n"
"主题：帕尔梅罗夫人\n"
"\n"
"嗨，乔。\n"
"所以——你知道帕尔梅罗夫人是为什么表现得那么奇怪，总是在说烤饼干的事情吗？\n"
"我正在和一位护士交谈，他们说帕尔梅罗夫人开了这种新药？\n"
"就是这种奇怪的粉末。而护士们连给她送药的资格都没有——她需要一位专科医生每天进来喂药！\n"
"疯了吧？我真希望我只需担心烤饼干的事情……"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Joe Shert, Receptionist\n"
" TO: Bryan Rooters, Reception Manager\n"
" RE: Housekeeping\n"
"\n"
" Hi Mr. Rooters, with all due respect I feel that I may have been assigned more of these tasks than the other Receptionists.\n"
" Jim said he hasn't had to do any cleaning in two weeks, yet I have been on cleaning duty 3 times.\n"
" To be clear, I certainly do not mind the extra work!  I just want to ensure you're aware in case there is a computer glitch.\n"
" Thank you and have a great day!"
msgstr ""
"&来自：乔·舍特，接待员\n"
"发往：布莱恩·鲁斯特，接待经理\n"
"主题：家政\n"
"\n"
"嗨，鲁斯特先生，恕我直言，我觉得我可能被分配了比其他接待员更多的任务。\n"
"吉姆说他已经两个星期不用打扫了，但我已经当了三回班了。\n"
"先说清楚，我当然不介意加班工作！我只是想确保您知道，万一是有电脑故障呢。\n"
"谢谢，祝您有美好的一天！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Joe Shert, Receptionist\n"
" TO: Bryan Rooters, Reception Manager\n"
" RE: Performance Evaluation\n"
"\n"
" Hi Mr. Rooters, I look forward to seeing you Tuesday for my evaluation.  I've been working really hard to show that I am Shady Hills material!"
msgstr ""
"&来自：乔·舍特，接待员\n"
"发往：布莱恩·鲁特斯，接待经理\n"
"主题：绩效评估\n"
"\n"
"嗨，鲁特斯先生，我很期待星期二和您进行绩效面谈。我一直在努力证明我是块 Shady Hills 的料！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Kristi Gordee, SVP Operations\n"
" TO: Bryan Rooters, Reception Manager\n"
" RE: Connie Malackey\n"
"\n"
" Bryan,\n"
" Connie has been asking a lot of weird questions about 'Ghosts' and other such nonsense.\n"
" This could look bad for us.  To make it worse, she is hanging out with Joe Shert a lot.\n"
" Shut it down."
msgstr ""
"&来自：克里斯蒂·戈迪，运营高级副总裁\n"
"发往：布莱恩·鲁斯特，接待经理\n"
"主题：康妮·马拉奇\n"
"\n"
"布莱恩，\n"
"康妮一直在问很多关于\"幽灵\"和诸如此类的奇怪问题。\n"
"这会让我们难堪的。更糟糕的是，她经常和乔·舍特呆在一起。\n"
"把这事压下来。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Kristi Gordee, SVP Operations\n"
" TO: Bryan Rooters, Reception Manager\n"
" RE: Do Your Job\n"
"\n"
" Bryan,\n"
" Do you not conduct thorough background checks and reviews on new hires?  Joe is related to the Mayor of Springfield.  His 90 day New Employee evaluation is coming up.  Do your job."
msgstr ""
"&来自：克里斯蒂·戈迪，运营高级副总裁\n"
"发往：布莱恩·鲁特斯，接待经理\n"
"主题：做好你的工作\n"
"\n"
"布莱恩，\n"
"你难道不对新员工进行彻底的背景调查吗？乔可是斯普林菲尔德市长的人。他的季度新员工绩效评估马上就到时间了。做好你的工作。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Kristi Gordee, SVP Operations\n"
" TO: Peter St. Travers, SVP Research & Development\n"
" RE: Budget\n"
"\n"
" Peter,\n"
" You need to find a way to reverse what you did ASAP.\n"
" What exactly do you expect me to do to get us out of this?\n"
" The police are investigating us now for foul play."
msgstr ""
"&来自：克里斯蒂，戈迪，运营高级副总裁\n"
"发往：彼得·圣特拉弗斯，研发高级副总裁\n"
"主题：解决这一切\n"
"\n"
"彼得，\n"
"你需要找到一种方法来尽快扭转你所做的事情。\n"
"你到底希望我做什么才能让我们摆脱困境？\n"
"警方现在正在调查我们是否有违法行为。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Kristi Gordee, SVP Operations\n"
" TO: Peter St. Travers, SVP Research & Development\n"
" RE: Shepherds\n"
"\n"
" Peter,\n"
" Leah Shepherds keeps sending me emails, and we just received the papers for yet another lawsuit.\n"
" I don't know what you're thinking but this one is going to be really difficult and could cost us.\n"
" The Board is going to be furious."
msgstr ""
"&来自：克里斯蒂·戈迪，运营高级副总裁\n"
"发往：彼得·圣特拉弗斯，研发高级副总裁\n"
"主题：谢菲尔德\n"
"\n"
"彼得，\n"
"利亚·谢菲尔德不断给我发电子邮件，我们刚刚又收到了一张法院传票。\n"
"我不知道你在想什么，但这样真的很难办，可能会让我们花费不少。\n"
"董事会会大发雷霆的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Leah Shepherds\n"
" TO: Kristi Gordee, SVP Operations\n"
" RE: I am going to sue you\n"
"\n"
" I don't know what kind of sick game your sham of a home is playing, but I am getting to the bottom of it.\n"
" I've hired a lawyer and we are going to sue you.\n"
" I should never have left grandpa in your care.\n"
" How does a PERSON go missing from a NURSING HOME!?  I have pictures of how dirty and disgusting that place is.\n"
" You should be ashamed!"
msgstr ""
"&来自：利亚·谢菲尔德\n"
"发往：克里斯蒂·戈迪，运营高级副总裁\n"
"主题：我要起诉你\n"
"\n"
"我不知道你的假疗养院在玩什么样的恶心游戏，但我马上就要找出谜底了。\n"
"我已经聘请了律师，我们要起诉你。\n"
"我就不该把爷爷交给你们这群人照顾。\n"
"一个大活人怎么会从疗养院失踪！？我已经掌握了这个魔窟中许多肮脏和恶心的照片。\n"
"你们应该感到羞耻！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Peter St. Travers, SVP Research & Development\n"
" TO: Kristi Gordee, SVP Operations\n"
" RE: Budget\n"
"\n"
" Hi KRISTI GORDEE,\n"
"\n"
" Kristi, please see attached for my budget proposal.\n"
" We need more jet injectors.\n"
"  I am on the verge of a breakthrough - you need to run interference on this Shepherds issue.\n"
" - Peter"
msgstr ""
"&来自：彼得·圣特拉弗斯，研发高级副总裁\n"
"发往：克里斯蒂·戈迪，运营高级副总裁\n"
"主题：预算\n"
"\n"
"嗨，克里斯蒂·戈迪，\n"
"\n"
"克里斯蒂，请参阅附件中的我的预算提案。\n"
"我们需要更多的注射器。\n"
"我正处于突破的边缘——而你需要马上插手解决那个叫谢菲尔德的问题。\n"
"——彼得"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Unknown Sender\n"
" TO: Peter St. Travers, SVP Research & Development\n"
" RE: Results\n"
"\n"
" Looking forward to your report at the next meeting.\n"
" I put a lot on the line for you, don't disappoint me, Peter.\n"
" Get me results."
msgstr ""
"&来自：未知发件人\n"
"发往：彼得·圣特拉弗斯，研发高级副总裁\n"
"主题：结果\n"
"\n"
"期待你在下次会议上的报告。\n"
"我为你付出了很多，别让我失望，彼得。\n"
"给我结果。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Vincent Fuels, Researcher\n"
" TO: Peter St. Travers, SVP Research & Development\n"
" RE: This is bad!\n"
"\n"
" While you were gone last night, the old man started to wake up and become cranky.\n"
" We had to give him another dose of that elephant tranquilizer!\n"
" I think he might actually be strong enough to break out of his cell now.\n"
" We really need to do something before he kills someone!\n"
" I know this experiment meant a lot to you, but it isn't worth the risk anymore!"
msgstr ""
"&来自：文森特·福尔斯，研究员\n"
"发往：彼得·圣特拉弗斯，研发高级副总裁\n"
"主题：情况很糟糕！\n"
"\n"
"昨晚你不在的时候，老人开始清醒，变得暴躁。\n"
"我们不得不再给他注射一剂大象镇静剂！\n"
"我想他现在可能真的强壮到可以冲出牢房了。\n"
"在他杀人之前，我们真的需要做点什么！\n"
"我知道这个实验对你来说意义重大，但现在不值得这么冒险了！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Will Higgins, VP Information Technology\n"
" TO: Peter St. Travers, SVP Research & Development\n"
" RE: Security\n"
"\n"
" Hello sir,\n"
" I understand your concerns about security.  Rest assured, myself and my team take this very seriously.  I assure you that high-level encryption protects all of our systems.\n"
" Nobody will be able to access any of our PCs without use of the owner's fingerprint authentication, even in the event that the main power supply is cut.\n"
" Nobody unauthorized will ever be able to read our emails or documents."
msgstr ""
"&来自：威尔·希金斯，信息技术副总裁\n"
"发往：彼得·圣特拉弗斯，研发高级副总裁\n"
"主题：安全性\n"
"\n"
"您好先生，\n"
"我理解您对信息安全有所担忧。请放心，我和我的团队非常重视这一点。我向您保证，高级加密可以保护我们所有的系统。\n"
"如果不使用所有者的指纹认证，任何人都无法访问我们的任何个人电脑，即使是主电源被切断的情况下也是如此。\n"
"未经授权的任何人都无法阅读我们的电子邮件或文件。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid "JAMES NEONDORTHALL; RECEPTIONIST"
msgstr "詹姆斯·尼奥多尔；接待员"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid "JOSEPH SHERT; RECEPTIONIST"
msgstr "乔·舍特；接待员"

