msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "Hey, did you notice that there's working wi-fi here?  Not that anything else is online anymore, but still."
msgstr "嘿，你注意到这里有无线网络吗？虽然说其他地方都没网上了，但这里还有。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "Hey, did you notice that there's working wi-fi here?  Not that anything else is online anymore, but still."
msgstr "嘿，你注意到这里有无线网络吗？虽然说其他地方都没网上了，但这里还有。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Hey, it can wait."
msgstr "嘿，可以以后再聊。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return to Hub 01"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Hey, you have a map, don't you?  You can use mine, if you need."
msgstr "嘿，你有张地图，不是吗？如果你需要的话，还可以用我的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Hmm?  Nothing, I guess I just like resting in this place.  I feel good today."
msgstr "嗯？没什么，我想我只是喜欢在这个地方休息。我今天感觉还好。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Hold on, government documents?"
msgstr "等等，政府文件？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Honestly, sometimes I feel like an ATM."
msgstr "说实话，有时候我觉得自己像台ATM。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Hoo boy, yes they did, and let me tell you, they were not happy campers about me crashing on their couch.  Now, these people don't tell me who they are, but they tell me to get off the premises immediately.  I wasn't having that.  I had been through hell and come out the other end, and I don't remember what I said to them, but it was along the lines of 'I have nowhere to go, and your building is nice and cozy, so if you want me to leave, you can come out here and make me.'\"  They laugh.  \"They weren't expecting me to bite back.  So I turn off the intercom and I go eat lunch.  When I go back again, the first thing they ask is if I want a job."
msgstr "哦，兄弟，是的，他们确实这样做了，让我告诉你，他们对像我这样的不速之客占用他们的沙发感到不满。现在，这些人没有告诉过我他们是谁，但他们告诉我立即离开这里。我才不买账。我经历了地狱，从另一端出来了，我不记得我对他们说了什么，但总之是'我无处可去，而你们的大楼又好又舒适，所以如果你们想让我离开，你们可以到这里来试试。'之类的话\"他笑了。\"他们没想到我会反击。所以我挂掉对讲机，去吃午饭。当我再次回去时，他们问的第一件事是我是否想要一份工作。"

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Appears in the the surface of Hub 01 as an external mercenary.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Hub Mercenary"
msgstr "Hub 01 雇佣兵"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I appreciate it.  Here's the scrip; don't spend it all in one place."
msgstr "我很感激。这是金币；不要把所有的钱都花在一个地方。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I bought fruit and veggies from the store for my greens, but I figured those didn't really have enough calories for the long-term, so I hunted.  To be more accurate, I poached in the park I worked at.  It was never anything huge; I had to be able to conceal this stuff, remember.  But we were on a shoestring budget as it is and we never had the people we needed, so it was trivial to bag an animal using a rifle from one of the ranger stations.  I'd dress the carcass, then leave it in a place that I could either bring with me in my truck that day or come back later to sneak it out.  I never got caught.  I'm not proud of it, but I'm not really ashamed of it, either.  Besides, venison is great."
msgstr "我一开始从商店里买水果和蔬菜做绿叶蔬菜，但我觉得这些蔬菜并没有足够的热量长期食用，所以我开始打猎。更准确地说，我在我工作的公园里偷猎。这从来都不是什么大家伙；记住，我必须能够藏起这些东西。但我们公园当时的预算很低，而且我们缺少足够人手，所以用放在巡逻站的步枪偷猎动物很简单。我会给尸体清理内脏，然后把它藏在某个地方，直到我可以把它当天带到我的卡车里，或者以后再回来偷偷把它带出去。我从来没有被抓住过。我并不为此感到骄傲，但我也不为此感到羞耻。话说回来，鹿肉很棒。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I don't have 200 gold for you right now."
msgstr "我现在没有200金币给你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I don't know what I was expecting."
msgstr "我也不知道自己在期望什么。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I don't remember the video."
msgstr "我不记得那段视频了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I guess I am, yeah.  Feels like a stupid chore.\"  They suddenly pause.  \"Hey.  If you happen across any gold out in the world, I'll pay you to bring it back for me.  Right now my assignment stipulates eight scrip per kilo, and I'd be willing to give you all of that.  I just want something else to do.  Just maybe don't mention it to the intercom, alright?  This is supposed to be my job."
msgstr "我想我是的，是的。  感觉就像是一件愚蠢的苦差事。” 他们突然停了下来。“嘿。  如果你在世界上发现了任何黄金，我会付钱给你，让你帮我带回来。  现在我的任务规定每公斤八个通票，我愿意把这些都给你。  我只是想做点别的事。  只是也许不要在对讲机上提及这件事，好吗？  这应该是我的工作。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"I guess I am, yeah.  It feels nice to be putting all my skills to use instead of working an underpaid job to walk around the same woods flying a quadcopter around and being a glorified PR rep to cranky parents who are only at the park because they promised their kids they'd go.  Mind you, I'd still go back to it if I could.\"  Their expression falters a little.  \"We all had our struggles, but things are different now, you know?  We get to worry about the future in a whole new way; an existential way that we never had to consider before, not really.  Sure, there was the occasional nuke scare, but as a society, we had things pretty good.  Unless the dead stop getting back up, I… don't think things are going to ever go back to normal.\"\n"
"\n"
"Cranberry pauses for a moment, then shakes it off.  \"But… right now, I'm feeling at peace with everything, despite it all.  Maybe I'm just in shock, and it'll all come crashing down one of these days.  Things might get worse, and they may never get better.  But I feel alright.  And I think that's enough for me."
msgstr ""
"我想是的。我很高兴能把我所有的技能都用上，而不是做一份报酬微薄的工作，在同一片树林里转来转去，开着四轮直升机，做一名光荣的公关代表，给那些暴躁的父母看，只因为他们答应孩子要去公园。不过话说回来，如果可以的话，我还是想回去的。\"他的表情有些犹豫。\"我们都有过自己的挣扎，但现在一切都不一样了，你知道吗？我们得以一种全新的方式担心未来；一种我们从未考虑过的事关生死的方式，从没这么严重过。当然，以前偶尔也会有核战的恐慌，但作为一个社会，我们曾经过的还行。而现在除非死者停止复活，否则我……认为一切都不会恢复正常。\"\n"
"\n"
"克兰伯里停顿片刻，然后把这个念头抖掉。\"但是……现在，我觉得与世无争了，尽管发生这么多事情。也许我只是受到了惊吓，也许某天一切都会崩溃。这一切也许会变得更糟，永远不会好转。但我现在感觉还好。我觉得这对我来说已经够了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I guess I could stay for a while."
msgstr "我想我可以在这里呆一阵子。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I guess so.\"  They beam sheepishly.  \"Uh, call me Cranberry.  Cran is fine too.  It's nice to meet someone else from here.  I guess having some company for once wouldn't be awful."
msgstr "我想是的。\"他羞怯地笑着。\"叫我克兰伯里（译注：Cranberry 蔓越莓 小红莓）吧。叫克兰也行。很高兴在这里认识其他人。我想有人陪我一次也不会很糟糕。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I just realized, we've been in touch for a while now and I don't actually know; are you a man or a woman?"
msgstr "我刚刚意识到，我们已经认识了好一段时间，可我还不知道你是男是女？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I kind of lost track of the days.  Every day was the same; eat, check the barricades, look on the Internet, play some games with the sound off to try and distract myself.  I filled up my bathtub, and once the water went out, I'd drink from there when I needed to hydrate.  Meal planning got easier after I was down to just my canned stuff.  The Internet didn't stay on for long, though, which I guess was a blessing because of how many people were sharing their fear and awful experiences in real time.  I did that routine every day until that emergency broadcast came through that no help was coming, and then I knew it was over."
msgstr "我渐渐失去了日期的概念。生活天天重复着：吃饭、检查路障、上网浏览，再玩会儿静音游戏，试图以此分散注意。我把浴缸蓄满了水，一旦停水，口渴时就喝那里的水。当食物只剩下罐头储备时，安排饮食反而变得简单了。不过，网络没能维持多久——这倒未必是坏事，毕竟当时网上充斥着人们实时分享的恐惧与惨痛经历。我就这样日复一日地过着，直到那条紧急广播传来——告知救援不会到来——那一刻，我便明白一切都结束了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I might not have the time.  Hold that thought for later."
msgstr "我可能没有时间。以后再说吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I sure did.  Sorry, just a stupid icebreaker.  Old habits and all that.\"  They sit up.  \"What's up?"
msgstr "是。抱歉，只是个愚蠢的开场白。老习惯了。\"他坐了起来。\"怎么了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I thought I was the only one working for the people here."
msgstr "我还以为自己是这里唯一替他们干活的人。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I'm sorry, that's a bit personal.  Like, you seem alright, but that's kind of heavy stuff, y'know?  Maybe I can tell you another time."
msgstr "对不起，这确实有点私密。虽然你人还不错，但这个话题太沉重了，你知道吗？也许我可以改天再告诉你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I'm sorry.  Too personal?"
msgstr "我很抱歉。太私密了吗？"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I'm sure we'll figure it out once there.  Bring a good weapon and some ammo just in case, if you can; no idea what insanity <the_cataclysm> has brought us this time."
msgstr "我相信我们一到那里就会想出办法的。带上一把好武器和一些弹药以防万一，如果可以的话；不知道这一次<the_cataclysm>会带给我们什么疯狂玩意。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I'm sure."
msgstr "我确定。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I've never really been a prepper, but I was into conspiracy theories.  Not as a participant, just as an observer.  I think information spread is interesting.\"  They pause.  \"I think it was in early March that I started thinking something was wrong.  Like, the riots were bad beforehand, right?  And that just seemed like normal unrest.  But then suddenly you're seeing it happening in other countries where the normal explanations don't work.  So I dug deeper, and once I did, I realized that this had been happening since January, and getting worse since then.  That was when I started to take it seriously."
msgstr "我从来不是一个真正的生存狂，但我喜欢阴谋论。不是作为参与者，而是作为观察者。我认为信息传播很有趣。\"他停顿了一会。\"我想是在三月初，我开始觉得有什么不对劲。比如，暴乱之前就已经很糟糕了，对吧？这似乎是普通的骚乱。但突然之间，你发现它同时在其他国家发生，并且没法正常解释。所以我更深入地挖掘真相，而随之而来，我意识到这种情况自从一月份开始就发生了，而且从那以后变得越来越糟。那是我开始认真对待它的时候。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "If only, huh?  No, not quite.  About five miles away I hit a bad pothole and skidded off the road and got stuck.  That's not a problem on its own, but a few minutes into trying to get it unstuck, I saw a big furrow of dirt coming towards me and decided, you know what, maybe I should get off the side of the road.  So I grab my bugout bag from the cabin and a little food from the bed, and I book it onto the road.  Now, I don't know what this thing was, but it hit the truck from below and *flipped it over*.  That was enough to make me say 'Nope, I can go on foot.'"
msgstr "但愿如此，嗯？没那么简单。大约五英里外，我撞到了一个糟糕的坑洼，滑出了路面，被卡住了。这本身并不是个问题，但在试图解开它的几分钟后，我看到一条大土沟向我走来，于是决定，你知道吗，也许我应该离开路边。所以我从座舱里拿走了我的背包，从后箱上拿了点食物，然后上路。直到现在，我也不知道那是什么东西，但它从下面撞上卡车，然后把它*整个翻过来*。这足以让我说'不了，我可以步行去。'"

#. ~ Description of mission "Active Noise Control"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Investigate Hub 01's radio tower, discover the source of the interference, and fix the problem."
msgstr "调查Hub 01附近的无线电塔，寻找干扰源，并解决问题。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "It took a bit for me to muster the nerve to leave, but I wanted to.  Had to see, y'know?  It was… a shock, zombies just walking in the parking lot.  Like, sure, I could look out the window, but it feels different up close.  I had my knife handy, and I didn't want to make too much noise, so that's what I used.  I stabbed one of my dead neighbors in the neck that day.\"  They smile wistfully.  \"I threw up on my shoes after the first one, but it got easier."
msgstr "我花了好些时间才鼓起勇气离开，但我想离开。总得死个明白，对吧？令人……震惊，丧尸们在停车场里散步。当然，透过窗户能看到，但近距看到感觉非常不一样。我手边有把刀，我不想发出太大的噪音，所以我用那个。那天我刺中了一个早已死去的邻居的脖子。\"他伤感地笑了笑。\"第一次我吐在了鞋子上，但之后越来越容易了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "It took me a few days from there.  I had a heavy load, and it was slow going.  I slept on the road the first night because I was so freaked out by what I saw, but the day after I got the nerves to walk through the woods.  I had a tent, so it wasn't so bad.  Every now and then, I'd run into a zombie, or a wrecked car that still had some of them buckled in.  I left my shotgun behind in the truck, so I got better at using the knife.  It gets easier, y'know?"
msgstr "从那以后我花了几天时间。我带的东西不少，而且走路速度很慢。第一天晚上我就睡在路上，因为我被眼前的景象吓坏了，但第二天我又鼓起勇气穿过树林。我有个帐篷，所以没那么糟糕。时不时地，我会遇到一个丧尸，或者一辆仍有一些丧尸被扣在里面的失事汽车。我把霰弹枪忘在卡车里了，所以我更擅长用刀了。越来越容易了，知道吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Just like that?"
msgstr "就这样吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Just saying hi.  I'll be on my way now."
msgstr "只是打个招呼。我马上就走。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Just the same as you.  Some nobody doing dirty work for scraps.  Uh, no offense."
msgstr "和你一样。为了一点残羹剩饭去干脏活的人。呃，无意冒犯。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Just trying to get some rest.  I don't have anywhere else to stay, so they let me sleep on the couch out here as long as I keep my gun handy."
msgstr "只是想休息一下。我没有别的地方可去，所以他们就让我睡在外面的沙发上，只要我把枪随身放着。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Just vibing."
msgstr "只是享受氛围。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Just wondering if things will get better someday."
msgstr "也不知道情况会不会好起来。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return to Hub 01"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Let's get back home."
msgstr "我们回家吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Let's set up a combat strategy."
msgstr "让我们制定一个作战策略。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "March 30th happened.\"  Cranberry seems shaken, and talks a little louder for a second.  \"You remember that video, right?  That was what set off alarm bells in my head.  That shit was fucking scary.  And at that point I realized, okay, I think things are about to get bad and this is for real."
msgstr "3月30日发生的事。\"克兰伯里似乎仍然有些震惊，声音大了一点。\"你还记得那个视频吧？这就是在我脑海中敲响警钟的原因。那他妈的太可怕了。那时我意识到，好吧，我认为事情会变得更糟，这次是真的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "My truck was still there, and was on half a tank of gas.  I thought, okay, this isn't gonna be easy, but I can pack my food and the things I need to take with me into the truck, and then drive to that building I know about that was so reinforced.\"  They gesture around them.  \"This building.  The Hub.  So I got some stuff into a bugout bag in the cabin and filled up the truck bed, and off I went.  The roads were bad, but I'm not a bad driver.  Zombies are slow."
msgstr "我的卡车还在那里，而且还有半箱汽油。我想，好吧，这并不简单，但我可以把我的食物和我需要带的东西装进卡车，然后开车去我知道的那栋加固了的大楼。\"他指着周围做了个手势。\"就是这栋楼。所谓的Hub。于是我把一些东西放进小屋里的一个逃生背包里，装满了卡车的后座，然后就上路了。路上很糟糕，但我的驾驶技术还不错。丧尸很慢。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "No, no!  It's fine, promise.  It's just been a hot minute, and I'm trying to remember it.  It's been a while.  You sure you want to hear it?"
msgstr "不，不！没事的，我保证。只不过那是很久前的事情了，我正在努力回想起它。已经有一段时间了。你确定想听吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "None taken.  I guess that makes two of us."
msgstr "我不介意。我想这么算的话我们是一对了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Not a whole lot, really.  They made me track down and destroy some government documents a while back.  Obviously I read them first, but it wasn't much.  As far as I know, this place had an experimental computer network before everything went to hell.  What's going on in there now is anybody's guess."
msgstr "真的不算多。前一阵子他们派我去搜寻并销毁一些政府文件，当然我先读了一遍，但是里面并没有什么内容。据我所知，在一切变得糟糕之前，这个地方曾经有个实验性质的计算机网络。现在的情况谁也猜不到了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Now that you mention it, it does seem rather strange."
msgstr "你这么一说，确实有点奇怪。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"People started freaking out.  I did, too.  I don't know how bad things got elsewhere, but shit was flying off the shelves where I lived.  Empty racks at grocery stores everywhere you looked.  I had enough food for a few weeks, so it wasn't a problem for me, but it still shook me up bad.  Every day some horrible new shit was happening somewhere in the world, and things got just worse and worse.  Then that insanity with Rhode Island happened, and once the national emergency came out, I knew that okay, this is happening, it's actually happening.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Did you know that I was still going to work that entire time?  I don't know, it just felt meditative.  I lived in a pretty rural area, so there wasn't the kind of chaos in the cities and congestion on the roads.  I could just take a side road there and have a day of quiet.  Just the woods and whoever else actually bothered to show up that day.  The park closed for visitors closed a day or two before the state of emergency, and it was really peaceful, being there alone."
msgstr ""
"人们开始惊慌失措。我也是如此。我不知道其他地方的情况有多糟，但我住的地方的东西都飞走了。你所看到的杂货店里都是空荡荡的货架。我有足够吃上几个星期的食物，所以这对我来说不是问题，但它仍然让我感到震惊。每天都有一些可怕的新事情发生在世界的某个地方，事情变得越来越糟。然后罗得岛的疯狂事情发生了，而随着国家紧急情况宣告，我就知道，好吧，这正在发生，它确实正在发生。\"\n"
"\n"
"\"你知道我那段时间一直都在工作吗？我不知道，我只是觉得让人深思。我住在美丽的乡村地区，所以没有经历过城市里的混乱和道路上的拥堵。我可以钻进某条小路，在那里安静呆上一天。只有树林和当天凑巧出现在那里的人。公园对游客关闭了一两天，然后就宣布了紧急状态，一个人呆在那里面真的很平静。"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Return to Hub 01"
msgstr "返回 Hub 01"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_guard.json
msgid "Rough out there, isn't it?"
msgstr "外面很难活下去，不是吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "So I figured that this wasn't going to be a problem a few months down the line, right?  Just a flash in the pan.  I had my emergency stock of food in case things went bad for a little while.  Best case scenario, I never have to worry about it, things go back to normal after a bit, and I save some money on groceries for a while.  And I wanted to keep doing this for a few more weeks, but…"
msgstr "所以我想在接下来的几个月里这不会是个问题，对吧？只是昙花一现。我有紧急储备的食物，以防有一段时间情况不好。最好的情况是，我从来不用担心，过了一段时间事情就会恢复正常，我在日常杂货上省下了一点钱。我想再做几周，但是……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "So what's going on?"
msgstr "情况怎么了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Strange bedfellows…"
msgstr "怪异盟友……"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Sure seems like it.  What even was that…?  Eh, doesn't matter.  Let's go back to the Hub; hopefully the tower's working now."
msgstr "看起来的确如此。那到底是什么…？呃，无关紧要了。让我们回Hub去吧；希望无线电塔现在工作正常了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Surprise!\"  They do jazz hands.  \"Sorry.  Well, I'm told that I'm part of a small group right now.  Maybe you were the first."
msgstr "惊喜！\"他比了个爵士手的姿势。\"抱歉。好吧，之前我听说我现在成为小队的一员。也许你才是第一个。"

