msgstr "惊喜！\"他比了个爵士手的姿势。\"抱歉。好吧，之前我听说我现在成为小队的一员。也许你才是第一个。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Thank you for telling me."
msgstr "谢谢你告诉我这些。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return to Hub 01"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Thanks a lot for having my back.  Like I said, I owe you one."
msgstr "谢谢你帮我。就像我之前说的，我欠你一个人情。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Thanks a lot."
msgstr "非常感谢。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Thanks.  I never thought I'd get exhausted of carrying pure gold around, but here we are."
msgstr "谢谢了。我从没想过有一天带着纯金到处走会让我筋疲力尽，但情况就是如此。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "That's quite the story.  You seem to be feeling pretty good, in spite of the world ending."
msgstr "这可真是传奇故事。尽管已经是世界末日了，你似乎也感觉很好。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "That's what the news said, anyway.  It was only about a 20-minute trip from my apartment and sometimes I'd drive past it, so I was curious and I did some research into it.  The only info I could find about it online said that it was a NASA lab for computer research, but that was probably bullshit.  I mean, do you see any NASA logos?  Sure, we got huge steel doors and 15-foot concrete walls, but not a logo in sight.  The building probably goes underground, right?  It's way too small to be a whole laboratory up here."
msgstr "不管怎样，新闻就是这么说的。从我的公寓到这里只有大约20分钟的路程，有时我会开车经过它，所以我很好奇，对它做了一些研究。我在网上唯一能找到的信息是，这是NASA的计算机研究实验室，但那可能是胡说八道。要我说，你在哪里看到NASA的标志了吗？当然，我们有扇巨大的钢门和15英尺(约4.6米)高的混凝土墙，但看不到标志。整栋楼可能都在地下，对吧？这里太小了，不可能是个完整的实验室。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Then the portals happened, and you know the rest from there.  Two days later, the world was over.  There was a lot of chaos in my complex.  I just nailed shut my front door, drew all the curtains, kept my shotgun loaded, and probably slept maybe ten hours total that week.  I don't know if there was someone up in the sky watching over me, but if there was, I sure as hell owe them big time."
msgstr "然后传送门就开始出现了，之后发生的事情你都知道了。两天后，世界末日了。在我的建筑群里发生了很混乱的事情。我只是把前门钉上，拉上所有的窗帘，霰弹枪上膛，那一周大概最多只睡了十个小时。我不知道上天是否有人在庇护着我，但如果有，我肯定欠他很多。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "They don't let you in to sleep?"
msgstr "他们不让你进去睡？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Thinking I should go hunt something soon…"
msgstr "看来我有个狩猎目标了……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Uh… okay.  Who are you?"
msgstr "呃……好吧。你是谁？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Want help with something else?"
msgstr "还有什么需要吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Want help with something?"
msgstr "想要帮忙吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Well, I should get going."
msgstr "嗯，我该走了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Well, never mind."
msgstr "好吧，没什么。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Well, no.  It was obvious they just wanted to get rid of me, but I decided I wanted to show that I was useful.  They tell me to find a crashed drone somewhere in the surrounding area and bring it back here.  No directions, of course.  Y'know, go find this drone in the middle of the woods, it'll be easy.  But I had some tools in my bag, right?  And yours truly has repaired some drones in the park service.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"So it takes me a whole-ass afternoon, but I find their stupid drone stuck in a tree.  I can see the camera's still on, so I pick it up and I tell the lens: 'Hey, you want me to fix it too?'  And I do.  It was just a cracked frame and the wiring to the rotors was sliced up.  The propellers themselves were fine.  So I bring it out of the woods and turn it off.  Then I open up the casing, solder up the wires, and use superglue to hold the frame together, which wasn't perfect, but I figured it'd hold until it got back home.  Then I turned it back on, and wouldn't you know, it immediately starts up and sits there for a minute, like 'What the fuck?  Why am I working again?'  And then it flies away, and I walk my smug ass back home."
msgstr ""
"嗯，没有。很明显，他们只是想除掉我，但我决定，我想证明我是有用的。他们告诉我在周围地区的某个地方找到一架坠毁的无人机，然后把它带回这里。当然，没有方向。你知道吗，去树林里找这架无人机，会很容易的。但我包里有工具，对吧？你们还真的在公园服务部门修理了一些无人机。“\n"
"\n"
"“所以我花了一个下午的时间，但我发现他们的愚蠢的无人机被困在树上。我能看到相机还开着，所以我拿起相机，对着镜头说：‘嘿，你也想让我修一下吗？’我就是这么想的。这只是一个破裂的机架，转子的布线被割断了。螺旋桨本身也很好。所以我把它从树林里拿出来，然后把它关掉。然后我打开外壳，焊接电线，用强力胶将框架固定在一起，这并不完美，但我想它可以坚持到它回家。然后我又打开它，你难道不知道吗，它立即启动并在那里坐了一分钟，就像‘他妈的什么？’为什么我又要工作了？然后它飞走了，我自鸣得意地走回了家。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Well, thanks for offering."
msgstr "谢谢你的提议，还是算了吧。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Well… a little while ago, I set up a radio transmitter in the radio tower not far from here, but apparently it's stopped transmitting.  If you're willing to back me up while I check it out, I'll owe you a favor."
msgstr "好吧……不久前，我在离这里不远的无线电发射塔里安装了一台无线电发射机，但显然它已经停止工作了。如果你愿意在我检查时帮我一把，我欠你一个人情。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "What do you know about our employers?"
msgstr "你对我们这个雇主有了解吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "What food were you canning?"
msgstr "你都做了些什么罐头？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "What was <the_cataclysm> like for you?"
msgstr "对你来说<the_cataclysm>是什么样的？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "Who are you, exactly?"
msgstr "你到底是谁？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Who exactly are you?"
msgstr "你到底是谁？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Whoo-ee, someone was living under a rock, huh?  It was all over the news.  Video on YouTube, it was a livestream of one of the riots in Minneapolis.  A mom was…\"  They hesitate.  \"I don't want to go into detail, but it was real bad.  Real bad.  That's what set off people panicking."
msgstr "哇哦，某人住在石头下面，是吗？新闻上到处都是。YouTube上的视频，是明尼阿波利斯一场骚乱的直播。一位母亲被……\"他犹豫了一会：\"我不想说得太详细，但那真的很糟糕。真糟糕。这就是引起人们恐慌的原因。"

#. ~ Description of mission "Return to Hub 01"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "With the source of the radio tower's interference fixed, return to Hub 01 with Cranberry."
msgstr "解决了无线电发射塔的干扰源后，带着克兰伯里返回Hub 01。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Wondering if the whole world is like this now.  It has to be, right?  I was watching some foreign news channels when everything was going down, and it sounded like things were just as bad there…"
msgstr "我也想知道现在整个世界是否都是这样。一定是吧？我之前看过一些外国新闻频道，一切都在崩溃，听起来那里的情况也一样糟糕……"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Yeah!  Crazy shit.  They sent me to an office building to find a folder with a certain serial and get rid of it.  They didn't even care what was on it.  By the time I got there, though, the building was pretty much a wreck.  The folder had been sitting in a puddle for God knows how long, and there was nothing even remotely legible by then."
msgstr "是啊！疯狂的玩意。他们派我去一栋办公楼，想找到一个带有特定序列号的文件夹，然后把它销毁。他们甚至不在乎上面写着什么。然而，当我到达那里的时候，这座建筑几乎成了废墟。那个文件夹已经在水坑里泡了天知道有多久，那时候连一丁点能看清的东西都没了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Yeah.  Have you noticed how they pay us in these tiny little gold coins?\"  Cranberry holds one up for emphasis.  \"It's bizarre.  You'd think they have a gold mine in there, but no, they don't, so they make me cross the damn world grabbing gold bars.  As far as scrip goes, it seems inconvenient as hell to make."
msgstr "是啊。你注意到他们用来当作报酬的那些小小金币了吗？\"克兰伯里拿起一个来端详道：\"可真他妈奇了怪了。换做是别人得猜他们家有个金矿，但其实他们并没有，所以他们派我翻遍这个该死的世界找些金块来给他们。而且就作为代币而言，制造起来似乎很不容易。"

