msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "Yeah, I surely do.  Here, it ain't much, but oats are easy enough, and good food too."
msgstr "是啊，我确实很喜欢。来，虽然算不上什么大餐，但燕麦做起来简单，而且也是好东西。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
msgid "You know what?  Nevermind.  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "你知道吗？算了。你之前在说什么？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "&Greenwood looks over his their shoulder, briefly glancing around before speaking in a low whisper.  \"Don't tell anyone I said this, but I don't like Helena at all.  Her father was a real nut, he'd rave on and on about an apocalypse he'd prepared for.  He always thought that his church would be the ark to weather the storm, that God would destroy the world by unleashing the armies of Hell; and he wasn't talking about the Second Coming of Christ.  Helena's just as fanatical as he was, and it reflects in her inadequate leadership.  To be honest, I'm highly concerned for some of the people here; they're obsessively zealous with Helena, and harbor a xenophobic hatred of everything.  As in Matthew 15:14, 'They are blind guides.  And if one blind person guides another, they will both fall into a pit'.\""
msgstr "&格林伍德看了看自己的肩膀，在低声说话之前短暂地扫视了一下四周。\"不要告诉任何人我说过这个，但我一点也不喜欢海伦娜。她的父亲是个真正的疯子，他会滔滔不绝地讲述他所准备的启示录。他总是认为他的教堂会成为抵御风暴的方舟，上帝会通过释放地狱的军队来毁灭世界；而且他说的不是基督的第二次降临。海伦娜和他一样狂热，这反映在她不充分的领导上。说实话，我非常担心这里的一些人；他们对海伦娜的狂热，对一切都怀有仇外的仇恨。正如马太福音第十五章第十四节所说：'他们是瞎子的向导。如果一个瞎子引导另一个瞎子，他们都要掉进坑里'。\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Actually, I'm just heading out."
msgstr "其实，我该走了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Alright.  Let's talk about something else."
msgstr "好吧。  我们来谈谈别的事情吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Could I ask you a few more questions?"
msgstr "我可以再问你几个问题吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Could you tell me a bit about this church?"
msgstr "你能告诉我关于这个教堂的一些情况吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Good to see you again, Reverend.  I wanted to talk."
msgstr "很高兴再次见到你，牧师。我想谈谈。"

#. ~ Name of effect type id "godco_confessed"
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Had a Confessional"
msgstr "进行了一次忏悔"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "How may I help you, sister?"
msgstr "我能为你做什么，姐妹？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "I had a pretty comfortable life growing up.  My parents were florists, owned a shop along the main street of town.  They were always so cheery, as if nothing bad could phase them.  When I was about fifteen, I dreamt that the Lord spoke to me; as if urging me to go and spread his Gospel, so I did.  I took odd jobs at several churches for a while, before I went to seminary.  I went between three different churches, before I found this one.  I've been here since."
msgstr "我有一个相当舒适的成长生活。我的父母是花商，在镇上的主要街道上拥有一家商店。他们总是很开心，好像没有什么坏事能影响他们。在我大约十五岁时，我梦见主对我说话；好像在催促我去传播他的福音，于是我就去了。在上神学院之前，我在几个教会打了一段时间的零工。在找到这个教会之前，我在三个不同的教会之间徘徊。之后我就一直在这里。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "I'm looking for work.  Can I do anything for your congregation?"
msgstr "我正在找工作。我能为你们的会众做什么吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "I'm seeking forgiveness, Father.  I've made mistakes in my life that I can never take back."
msgstr "我正在寻求宽恕，神父。我在生活中犯了一些错误，这些错误我再也无法收回了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Nice meeting you, Reverend.  I'd best get going though."
msgstr "很高兴见到你，牧师。不过我还有要忙的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Nice to meet you too, Reverend."
msgstr "也很高兴见到你，牧师。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Thanks for the info, I'd best be going then."
msgstr "谢谢你的信息，那我最好就走了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Thanks for your time, Reverend."
msgstr "谢谢你的时间，牧师。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "The Lord be with you, sister.  You seem new, nice to meet you.  Welcome, and welcome aboard!"
msgstr "主与你同在，姐妹。你似乎是新来的，很高兴认识你。欢迎，欢迎加入！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "The full name is the New England Community Church.  Helena's father started it about twenty years ago.  The flock may be small, but we've always helped each other when times were tough; we're like a family now."
msgstr "其全称是新英格兰社区教会。海伦娜的父亲大约在二十年前创办了它。我们这群人可能很小，但我们总是在困难的时候互相帮助；我们现在就像一个家庭。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "This is the New England Community Church, the congregation of it.  Praise the Lord that we made it through!"
msgstr "这就是新英格兰社区教会的会众。赞美主，我们熬过去了！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "We all came out here when <the_cataclysm> rocked the world.  It's an old retreat Helena bought in the hopes of renovating it, good thing we did."
msgstr "当<the_cataclysm>震撼世界时，我们都来到了这里。这是海伦娜买下的一个古老的度假胜地，希望能对它进行翻新，好在我们做到了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "We all have, sister, we all have."
msgstr "我们都有，姐妹，我们都有。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Well, it's your appearance.  You're… how do I say, significantly different than what most people are used to.  With the sudden appearance of strange phenomenon following the Rapture, some have taken your changes as a mark of demonic corruption, and won't be very kind to you either.  Be wary of this."
msgstr "嗯，这就是你的外表。  你……我该怎么说，与大多数人习惯的有很大不同。  随着被提之后突然出现的奇怪现象，一些人将你的变化视为恶魔腐败的标志，并且不会对你很好。  对此要小心。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "schizo_self_talk"
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json data/json/snippets/schizophrenia.json
msgid "What are you doing out here?"
msgstr "你到儿这来做什么？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "What can I do for you?"
msgstr "我能帮你什么忙吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "What do you think about Helena?"
msgstr "你对海伦娜有什么看法？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "What's wrong with me, if you could say?"
msgstr "如果你能说的话，我到底是怎么了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Where am I again?"
msgstr "我又是在哪？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "Where am I?"
msgstr "我在哪？"

#. ~ Description of effect type "Had a Confessional"
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "You decided to take responsibility for your actions."
msgstr "你决定为自己的行为负责。"

#. ~ Apply message of effect type "Had a Confessional"
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
msgid "You finally got the weight off your chest."
msgstr "你终于卸下了心中的重担。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Could you tell me more about Olwen?"
msgstr "能和我说说更多关于奥尔文的事吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Could you tell me more about Tom?"
msgstr "能和我说说更多关于汤姆的事吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Felicity?  Nice to meet you.  How are things here?"
msgstr "费利西蒂？很高兴见到你。这里的情况如何？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "Good luck with that."
msgstr "那祝你好运。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "He wasn't always like this.  Olwen came not long after we married, he was a great, caring father to her.  A few months before <the_cataclysm> is when he lost it, got in some survivalist circle.  He'd stay up pouring over newspapers and any documents he could find, and wound up quitting his job to study it more.  We didn't see much of him for a while, always in the basement, and took out a chunk of our savings to buy canned goods en masse."
msgstr "他以前不是这样的。我们婚后不久就有了奥尔文，他那时是个伟大的、慈爱的父亲。<the_cataclysm>发生的几个月前，他失去了理智，陷入了一些生存主义者的圈子。他开始熬夜翻阅报纸和他能找到的任何文件，最后还辞掉了工作来进行更多研究。有段时间他老待在地下室里，我们很少见到他，他还拿出了一大笔积蓄购买了许多罐头食品。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Hi Felicity.  Got a minute?"
msgstr "嗨，费利西蒂。有空吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Hi Felicity.  I'm afraid I can't talk right now."
msgstr "嗨，费利西蒂。恐怕我现在没空交谈。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "How's the manuscript coming?"
msgstr "稿子写得怎么样了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
msgid "How's your family?"
msgstr "你的家人怎么样了？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "I don't know.  I've tried talking to him, tried to convince him to give it up.  I think he's stressed out with everything going on, and snapped because of that.  I just want my husband back…"
msgstr "我不知道。我试着和他谈，试图说服他放弃。我想觉得他对发生的一切深感压抑，并因此而崩溃。我只想要我的丈夫回来……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "I suppose we do."
msgstr "我想我们会的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "I'd better get going.  Bye, Felicity."
msgstr "我得走了。再见，费莉西蒂。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "I'll see what I can do.  Bye, Felicity."
msgstr "我看看我能做些什么。再见，费莉西蒂。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "I'm actually from New England, Rhode Island specifically.  I grew up in Providence, the state capital.  It was lovely there, I'd always walk to school and stopped in the park on my way home.  Mom was an accountant for various companies, she went to Rivtech back when it was a startup.  Dad was a baker, ran a shop on the corner of Chalkstone and Mt Pleasant.  It smelled so good when you walked by…  I always wanted to be a writer, but I wound up as a proofreader for Stillwater, a publishing firm.  I met Tom at that office, we got married about three years later."
msgstr "我其实来自新英格兰，确切说是罗得岛，在州府普罗维登斯长大。那真是个可爱的地方，我总是步行上学，然后回家的路上在公园逗留。妈妈是多家公司的会计师，她在 Rivtech 刚成立时就进去了。爸爸是个面包师，在 Chalkstone 和 Mt Pleasant 的拐角开了家店。当你路过时，闻起来真是香……我一直想成为一名作家，但我最终成为了一家出版公司 Stillwater 的校对员。我在那间办公室认识了汤姆，大约三年后我们结婚了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "I'm always good for a talk.  It's nice to have company, even if we don't have much else to offer."
msgstr "我一直都很喜欢聊天。有伴的感觉很好，即使我们没有什么其他东西可以提供。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "I'm still working on it.  I'll have it ready soon."
msgstr "我还在努力，很快就会完成了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "If that's the case, I'll leave."
msgstr "如果是这样的话，我就离开。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Is there any way to get him out of it?"
msgstr "用过什么办法帮他摆脱困境吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
msgid "Is there anything I can do for you?"
msgstr "有什么我可以为你做的吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "It's been nice talking to you, but I need to head out."
msgstr "和你谈话很愉快，但我该出发了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "It's finally finished!  Here, I want you to have a copy of it.  This is my first time writing like this professionally, I hope you enjoy it."
msgstr "终于完成了！来，让你复印一份。这是我第一次像这样专职地写作，希望你喜欢它。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "It's nice to meet you, but I need to head out."
msgstr "很高兴认识你，但我得出发了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Lets talk about something else."
msgstr "让我们谈点其他的事情吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "My family's alright.  I have a wonderful daughter, Olwen; she's an electronics nut, had a great job with it too.  My husband Tom is the crazy one, always rambling on about conspiracy theories, secret agents, all that."
msgstr "我的家人挺好。我有个了不起的女儿，奥尔文；她是个电子迷，在这方面也极有成就。我丈夫汤姆是个疯子，总是喋喋不休地谈论阴谋论、秘密特工之类的东西。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Oh, hi there.  My name's Felicity, nice to see a new face."
msgstr "哦，你好。我叫费利西蒂，很高兴看到一张新面孔。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Olwen's a bright girl, always has been.  She studied electricity and computer science when she was in college, found a job with a research and development firm.  My girl's a fiancee now, her and Julian were going to get married in a few months.  She might teach you something, if you ask."
msgstr "奥尔文是个聪明的女孩，一直都是。她大学时学习电子和计算机学科，之后在科研公司找了份工作。我女儿如今是个未婚妻，她和朱利安几个月后就要结婚了。她也许可以教你些东西，如果你请教她的话。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Thank you, I'm sure it's lovely."
msgstr "谢谢，我肯定会喜欢的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "They're alright, but they won't take kindly to someone with your… appearance.  What can i do for you?"
msgstr "他们很好，但他们不会善待像你这样的……外表的人。  我能为你做什么？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "They're alright.  What can I do for you?"
msgstr "他们都很好。我能为你做什么？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Tom and I wanted to get away from the city, so we found a home up here.  We didn't move again until <the_cataclysm>, when we came here."
msgstr "汤姆和我想远离城市，所以我们在这里找到了家。直到<the_cataclysm>后，我们才再次搬家，来到这里。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "We've been through a lot without much help, it's been difficult to cope.  Still, we put on a happy little face, and some of us pretend everything's all right."
msgstr "我们在没有太多帮助的情况下经历了许多，实在难以应付。尽管如此，我们摆出一副快乐的小脸儿，而一些人装作万事平安。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "What's on your mind?"
msgstr "你在想什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
msgid "Why'd you move out here?"
msgstr "你为何搬到这里呢？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "&Gemma is in deep, silent thought for a moment, before clearing her throat.  \"They read: 'I am the Lord your God, who brought you out of Egypt, out of the land of slavery.  You shall have no other gods before me.  You shall not make for yourself a carved image, or any likeness of anything that is in heaven above, or that is in the earth beneath, or that is in the water under the earth.  You shall not take the name of the Lord your God in vain.  Remember the Sabbath day, and keep it holy.  Honor your father and your mother.  You shall not murder.  You shall not commit adultery.  You shall not steal.  You shall not bear false witness against your neighbor.  You shall not covet your neighbors house.\"  They're written in Exodus 20:1-17, for future reference."
msgstr "&杰玛沉思片刻，然后清了清嗓子。\"他们读到：'我是主你的神，曾将你从埃及为奴之地领出来。除我以外，你不可有别的神。不可为自己雕刻偶像，也不可做什么形像仿佛上天、下地，和地底下、水中的百物。当记念安息日，守为圣日。当孝敬父母。不可杀人。不可奸淫。不可偷盗。不可作假见证陷害邻人。不可贪恋邻人的房屋。\"它们写在出埃及记 20:1-17 中，供将来参考。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Can I help you with anything?"
msgstr "我能帮上什么忙？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Fine then, screw you."
msgstr "那好吧，操你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Got it."
msgstr "知道了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Great to see a new face.  I'm Gemma.  Will you be staying here with us?"
msgstr "很高兴看到一张新面孔。我是杰玛。你会和我们一起待在这儿吗？。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Hello, Gemma.  I'm afraid I can't talk right now."
msgstr "你好，杰玛。恐怕我现在没空交谈。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Hi, Gemma.  How're you doing?"
msgstr "嗨，杰玛。最近过的怎样？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "I always have things on the go: tidying, organizing, cleaning, but I don't complain.  I never complain."
msgstr "我总有事情要忙：收拾整理、组织活动、打扫卫生，但我不抱怨。从不抱怨。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "I heard what it's like out there.  You must be weary from exploring this unforgiving wasteland.  I'm sorry that you're leaving us this soon."
msgstr "我听说过那里的情况。探索这片无情的荒地想必已经令你厌倦了。很遗憾你这么快就离开了我们。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "I meant \"Are there any jobs you know of?\""
msgstr "我的意思是\"你知道有什么工作吗？\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "I want to join the community."
msgstr "我想加入你们。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "I'd better get going.  Nice meeting you."
msgstr "我得走了。很高兴遇到你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json
msgid "I'll see you around."
msgstr "咱们回头见。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'm already staying here.  Nice to meet you."
msgstr "我已经住在这里了。很高兴认识你。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'm feeling alright, just working away."
msgstr "我感觉挺好，就是在工作。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "I'm happy to hear that, Gemma.  I'd best be going."
msgstr "杰玛，我很高兴听到这个。我得走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "It's nice to meet you too, survivor.  It's a tragedy what's become of the New England Church Community, perhaps it'll flourish again someday."
msgstr "我也很高兴认识你，幸存者。新英格兰教会社区已成悲剧，然而终有一天它将再次兴旺。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "It's nice to meet you too, survivor.  It's a tragedy what's become of the New England Church Community, perhaps it'll flourish again someday."
msgstr "我也很高兴认识你，幸存者。新英格兰教会社区已成悲剧，然而终有一天它将再次兴旺。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "It's nice to meet you too, survivor.  It's a tragedy what's become of the New England Church Community, perhaps it'll flourish again someday."
msgstr "我也很高兴认识你，幸存者。新英格兰教会社区已成悲剧，然而终有一天它将再次兴旺。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Its also called the Ten Commandments, if you've heard it by that.  A long time ago, Moses lead the Israelites out of slavery in Egypt, towards the Promised Land.  They broke their Covenant with God, and were cursed to wander the desert for forty years, as opposed to the nineteen days it would normally take.  On the way there, Moses went atop Mount Sinai to speak with God.  He saw a burning bush, and heard the voice of the Lord; who engraved the Decalogue on two tablets of stone."
msgstr "如果你听说过的话，它也被称为十条诫命。很久以前，摩西带领以色列人摆脱埃及的奴役，前往应许之地。他们违背了与上帝的盟约，被诅咒要在仅十九天路程的沙漠中游荡四十年。在去那里的路上，摩西登上西奈山顶与上帝交谈。他看见燃烧的荆棘，又听见耶和华的声音；是祂将十诫刻在两块石板上。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "My flowers look a bit dehydrated, I'd appreciate it if you watered them for me.  These indoor plants are the most calming reminders of life before <the_cataclysm>."
msgstr "我的花看起来有点脱水，如果你能帮我浇水，我将不胜感激。这些室内植物是<the_cataclysm>前生活最安详的回忆。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "My story?  It's been told a thousand times."
msgstr "我的故事？那已经说过上千遍了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Gemma.  I'm just passing through."
msgstr "幸会，杰玛。我只是路过。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Gemma.  I'm seeking asylum."
msgstr "幸会，杰玛。我正在寻找避难所。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Sure.  See ya."
msgstr "确实。那再见啦。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Sure.  Well, bye."
msgstr "确实。那再见啦。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "Thank you.  See you around, Gemma."
msgstr "谢谢你。回见，杰玛。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "There sure is.  Well, bye."
msgstr "肯定的。那再见啦。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "We are all under God's protection here.  Our community, like all moral civilizations, has a set of rules.  Obey the Decalogue, have respect for your neighbors and we'll get along just fine, okay?"
msgstr "在这里，我们皆在上帝保护之下。与所有道德的文明一样，我们社区也有一套规则。遵守十诫，尊重你的邻居，我们将相处融洽，可以吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "What does a dorm leader do exactly?"
msgstr "舍监究竟是做什么的？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "What is the Decalogue?"
msgstr "什么是十诫？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "What was it you said earlier?"
msgstr "你刚才说什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "What's the harsh reception about?"
msgstr "如此严厉的接待是为了什么？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "You are most welcome here.  In the good old days we would've held a ceremony for you.  Oh well, times have changed.  Accept this blanket, you may choose either bed by the window.  If you're hungry, you can go see Simon for a meal, up to one per day."
msgstr "这里非常欢迎你。在过往的美好时光里，我们能为你举办一场仪式。哦，好吧，时代变了。收下这条毯子，你可以选靠窗的任一张床。饿了可以去找西蒙吃顿饭，一天最多一顿。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
msgid "You certainly have the marks of one.  I don't understand how you can go walking around looking like an abomination, cursed by God, and think everything's alright.  I'm not interested in learning, either, so be gone with you."
msgstr "你肯定有一个人的标志。  我不明白你怎么能看起来像一个被上帝诅咒的可憎之人，却又认为一切都好。  我也没兴趣学习，你走吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "&Helena flips through her Bible before stopping.  \"They read: 'I am the Lord your God, who brought you out of Egypt, out of the land of slavery.  You shall have no other gods before me.  You shall not make for yourself a carved image, or any likeness of anything that is in heaven above, or that is in the earth beneath, or that is in the water under the earth.  You shall not take the name of the Lord your God in vain.  Remember the Sabbath day, and keep it holy.  Honor your father and your mother.  You shall not murder.  You shall not commit adultery.  You shall not steal.  You shall not bear false witness against your neighbor.  You shall not covet your neighbors house.\"  They're written in Exodus 20:1-17, for future reference."
msgstr "&海伦娜翻了几页她的圣经，然后停了下来。\"他们读到：'我是主你的神，曾将你从埃及为奴之地领出来。除我以外，你不可有别的神。不可为自己雕刻偶像，也不可做什么形像仿佛上天、下地，和地底下、水中的百物。当记念安息日，守为圣日。当孝敬父母。不可杀人。不可奸淫。不可偷盗。不可作假见证陷害邻人。不可贪恋邻人的房屋。\"它们写在出埃及记 20:1-17 中，供将来参考。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "A generous soul, are we?  That's not what I was expecting, but I'll see to it."
msgstr "一个慷慨的灵魂，可不是么？这可真出乎我的意料了，但我保证会做到的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Alright, I'll go and see what's up."
msgstr "好的，我去看看是怎么一回事。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Corrie and I have finished that solar cart."
msgstr "科里和我已经完成了那辆太阳能车。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Fine then."
msgstr "好吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
msgid "Good to see you again."
msgstr "很高兴再次见到你。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "He had many visions, and he had many secrets.  I don't know all of them, but there was one he was highly vocal about, regarding <the_cataclysm>, that according to him \"The spawn of Satan shall descend upon the Earth, and all will be consumed in death and destruction\".  He never said much else about it, and always had a mortified face whenever someone brought it up."
msgstr "他看到了很多东西，他还有很多秘密。我对这些毫不知情，但有一个他直言不讳，是和<the_cataclysm>有关的。根据他的说法，\"撒旦的产物将降临地球，所有的一切都将在死亡和毁灭中被吞噬\"。他从未提起更多细节，每当有人说起这件事时，他总是一副羞愧的表情。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Here's your money.  Don't spend it all in one place."
msgstr "这是你的报酬。可别一股脑花光了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I am a prophet, like my uncle before me.  He saw <the_cataclysm>, the righteous judgement of God and set about preparing an ark to save us.  He passed before his visions could be fulfilled, and now I carry his righteous banner."
msgstr "我是个先知，就像我之前的叔叔一样。他看到了<the_cataclysm>，神公义的审判，并且着手准备方舟来拯救我们。他在他的愿景实现之前就过世了，现在由我高举他的正义旗帜。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I can't talk right now."
msgstr "我现在没空交谈。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I like what you and Corrie's put together.  I did promise payment for a proof-of-concept, what'll it be?"
msgstr "我可喜欢你和科里一起造出来的那玩意了。之前我说过会给原型机付报酬的，你想要点什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I presume you want me to pay a visit?"
msgstr "我猜你是不是想让我过去拜访一下？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I want Corrie to have some extra rations."
msgstr "我想让科里多领点口粮。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I'll have some icons."
msgstr "我要些圣像。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I'm Helena, the caretaker of this flock.  Who might you be, wanderer?"
msgstr "我是海伦娜，这羊群的牧守者。汝是何人，流浪者？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "I'm glad you could make it here.  May the Lord have mercy on you."
msgstr "很高兴你能来这里。愿主怜悯你。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "I'm glad you could make it here.  May the Lord have mercy on you."
msgstr "很高兴你能来这里。愿主怜悯你。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "I'm glad you could make it here.  May the Lord have mercy on you."
msgstr "很高兴你能来这里。愿主怜悯你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I'm just passing through.  I'll see you around."
msgstr "我只是路过。我们回头见。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "I'm not doing much wandering, I'm staying here."
msgstr "我并未长久流浪，我如今留在这里。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "It certainly seems like it."
msgstr "看起来确实如此。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Just like all the sinners, roaming through Hell."
msgstr "就像所有的罪人一般，在地狱中游荡。"

#. ~ Snippet in category "<done_conversation_section>"
#. ~ Avatar response to an NPC that can be used for TALK_NONE responses.
#. Could be used in a lot more dialogs.  Could also use a lot more variety.
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_rescue_pilot.json data/json/npcs/talk_tags.json
msgid "Let's change the subject."
msgstr "我们换个话题吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Let's negotiate some other time."
msgstr "我们下次再谈这件事吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Oh, I've met them before!"
msgstr "哦，我以前见过他们！"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Okay, I'll see about that later."
msgstr "好的，我稍后去看看。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Okay, I'll see about that.  Goodbye."
msgstr "好，我会考虑的。拜拜。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Olwen's finished the radio transmitter she was working on."
msgstr "奥尔文完成了她正在研究的无线电发射器。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Really?  I'd pay a small sum for information about them."
msgstr "真的吗？我愿意花笔小钱来换取关于他们的情报。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "See ya later, crazy lady."
msgstr "回头见，疯狂的女士。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Stranger, what brings you to our holy home?"
msgstr "陌生人，是什么带你来到我们神圣的家园？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Thank you, I hope he shares that sentiment."
msgstr "谢谢，我希望他感同身受。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Thank you.  I'll see you around."
msgstr "谢谢。我们回头见。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Thanks to my uncle's forethought, we've been blessed by God.  We have plenty of food for ourselves, safety from the hordes of Hell, and the continued protection of the Lord our God."
msgstr "感谢我叔叔的先见之明，我们得到了上帝的祝福。我们有足够的食物供自己享用，免受地狱大军的伤害，并得到我们的主——上帝的持续保护。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "They denied us, they labeled us as a doomsday cult, threw sticks and stones at us, and yet, we were standing resiliently.  Why?  Because we knew God was on our side."
msgstr "他们否认我们，他们给我们贴上末日邪教的标签，向我们扔棍棒和石头，然而，我们却坚强地站了起来。为什么？因为我们知道上帝站在我们这边。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "We are all under God's protection here.  Our community, like all moral civilizations, has a set of rules.  Obey the Decalogue, have respect for your neighbors and we'll get along just fine.  Go see Gemma or Julian for a bed, if one's available.  We do have limited space on our Ark, though."
msgstr "在这里，我们皆在上帝保护之下。与所有道德的文明一样，我们社区也有一套规则。遵守十诫，尊重你的邻居，我们将相处融洽。如果还有空位，你可以去找杰玛或朱利安申请张床位。不过，我们方舟上的空间确实有限。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Well, they're…"
msgstr "好吧，他们是……"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "What do you need?"
msgstr "你想要什么？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Yes, I was just informed of that.  I also heard that she found a large group of people living out in an old evacuation center, who consider themselves merchants.  That would be a good place to resume our spread of the Truth, perhaps we could find others who were faithful before <the_cataclysm>."
msgstr "是的，我刚刚听说这件事了。我还听说她找到了一大群住在破旧的难民中心的人，自称是什么商会的。这将是一处让我们重新传播福音的好地方，也许我们能找到些在<the_cataclysm>前的虔诚信徒。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
msgid "Yes, you seem like a good fit for the job.  I'll pay you a small sum for getting some information about them."
msgstr "是的，你看起来很适合这项任务。我会付给你些报酬，换取些关于他们的情报。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Alright.  Wanna chat?"
msgstr "好吧，能聊聊不？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Always nice to meet a fellow outsider.  How can I help you?"
msgstr "能见到个外乡人总是那么美好。我能帮你什么忙吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "Always nice to meet a fellow outsider.  How can I help you?"
msgstr "能见到个外乡人总是那么美好。我能帮你什么忙吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "Always nice to meet a fellow outsider.  How can I help you?"
msgstr "能见到个外乡人总是那么美好。我能帮你什么忙吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Are you taking care of Arturo?"
msgstr "你在照顾阿图罗吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Could you provide any medical services?"
msgstr "你能帮我看看病吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Do you have any work available?"
msgstr "你这里有什么需要我做的吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Do you want to come with me?"
msgstr "想要和我同行吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "He's an alright physician, but the Church massively overrates him.  They think his 'natural medicine' can cure anything, like he's a magic medicine man.  God created everything, so what on Earth isn't natural?!"
msgstr "他是个不错的医生，但教会对他评价过高了。他们认为他的\"纯天然药物\"可以治愈任何东西，仿佛他是个魔法药师一样。既然上帝创造了一切，那么地球上有什么不是天然的呢？！"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Hi, Jane.  Got a minute?"
msgstr "嗨，简。有空吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "How do you feel about him personally?"
msgstr "你觉得他这个人怎么样？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "I can pay for quality work.  Here it is."
msgstr "我付得起好的医疗服务。给你。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "I could always use more bandages, disinfectant, and the like.  What do you have?"
msgstr "我总是需要更多的绷带、消毒液之类的。你有些什么？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "I do what I can, but he's mostly beyond my skillset.  Coke's a <swear> <name_b>, really messes a person up.  Arturo was on it for several years before he tried to get help, now he has auditory hallucinations; hears voices from nowhere.  Traumatic experiences have a harsher effect on recovering addicts, but <the_cataclysm> is worse than anything we've gone through before."
msgstr "我尽我所能，但他已经远远超出了我的能力范围。快克是一种<swear><name_b>，真的能毁掉一个人。阿图罗在求医之前，已经吸了好几年，现在甚至出现了幻听；凭空听见各种声音。创伤经历对脱瘾者的影响更严重，而<the_cataclysm>比我们之前经历的任何事情都要糟糕。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "I don't have anything right now.  I'll come back with something later."
msgstr "我现在什么都没有。我以后再带些来。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "I don't have anything right now.  Lets talk about something else."
msgstr "我现在什么都没有，我们谈点别的吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/foodguard.json data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
msgid "I have <topic_item>."
msgstr "我有<topic_item>。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "I might have some medicine for the community.  Anything you're missing?"
msgstr "我这里为教会备了一些药。你缺点什么吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "I really don't, actually.  Even my help is thankless here.  Bandaging cuts, setting bones, disinfecting wounds; who needs all that when they can pray anything away?"
msgstr "实话说，我真不需要。即使在这里我干的也是吃力不讨好的活。包扎伤口、固定骨骼、消毒伤口；当他们可以祈祷解决一切问题的时候，谁还需要这些呢？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "I was a physician, one of the more unfortunate people who didn't call in sick during the riots.  I remember it all so clearly, the cuts, bruises, deep bites, then those oily black eyes, caustic yellow blood, spastic fungal growths… it was <swear> gnarly.  Then things descended into all-new levels of fucked up, and some of my coworkers were preparing to just get the hell out.  I followed them."
msgstr "我曾经是一名医生，属于是暴乱期间没能请上病假的倒霉蛋中的一员。我记得很清楚，伤口、瘀伤、深深的咬伤，然后是那些油乎乎的黑眼睛、腐蚀性的黄血、痉挛的真菌生长……太<swear>可怕了。然后事情进展到了一种全新的混乱水平，我的一些同事已经做好了赶紧开溜的准备，我也跟着他们一起溜了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "I'd like to leave, but I've got to take care of Arturo.  He's always low or nearly out of antipsychotics, so I do what I can."
msgstr "我想离开，但我得照顾阿图罗。他用的抗精神病药剩不多了，要么就是几乎没有，所以我得尽我所能。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "I'm doing somewhat well, thanks to my occupation.  The other joinees, well, they're barely scraping by.  It's been tense, and I'm not seeing it change for the better."
msgstr "由于我的职业，我过的还算可以。其他教友，额，他们只是勉强糊口而已。气氛一直很紧张，而我也看不出情况有好转的迹象。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "I've changed my mind.  Let's talk about something else."
msgstr "我改变主意了，我们谈点别的吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Need any help?"
msgstr "需要帮忙么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Nice to meet you too, Jane."
msgstr "很高兴见到你，简。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "No, not by the government."
msgstr "不，不关政府的事。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "No, not really.  I came here after I was split from my friends by a horde of <zombies>.  They let me in after I gave away some food I found.  The church distrusts my profession; I get by helping Kostas."
msgstr "不，算不上好。我是在一群<zombies>把我和朋友分开后才来到这里的。在我捐出了一些我找到的食物后，我得以进来。教会不信任我的职业；我是靠帮科斯塔斯打下手才勉强活下来的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Oh, I don't think we've met before.  My name's Jane, I'm the local doctor."
msgstr "哦，我想我们以前没见过面。我叫简，我是这里的医生。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Personally, I like him.  We've worked together for a few cases, but most people refuse to let me work; they only want to see him."
msgstr "就我个人而言，我喜欢他。我们一起工作过几次，但大多数人拒绝让我看病；他们只想见他。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Sure, I don't see why not.  I've gotta keep my mind off stuff anyway."
msgstr "当然，没什么不行的。反正我现在也得找些能消耗精力的事干。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Sure, I've got some supplies on hand, just give me a minute and I'll look you over.  It'll cost ten icons."
msgstr "没问题，我手头有些物资，稍等一下，我来给你检查一下。费用是十个图标。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Thorazine would go us a long way, but Arturo's having trouble getting it.  They think he's the key and that my help would obstruct him.  Regardless, there's just so much anti-medical sentiment here that I've given up on prescribing anything."
msgstr "冬眠灵可以管上一阵子，但阿图罗很难找到这种药。他们认为他是关键人物，而我的治疗会阻碍他。无论如何，这里有太多的反医情绪，以至于我已经不敢开处方了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Were you evaced'?"
msgstr "你们被疏散了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "What about Kostas?  The Church seems to trust him."
msgstr "科斯塔斯呢？教会似乎很信任他。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
msgid "Would you like to buy any supplies?"
msgstr "你想买些医疗用品吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "&Jeremiah leans his head towards your ear, speaking in a low whisper.  \"To be honest with you, I don't like my mom at all.  She's like a <swear> helicopter, always telling me what to do, where to go, who I can be with.  She never thinks of me as an individual, only some idea of who she thinks I am.  My dad's alright, he's the chef around here.\""
msgstr "&耶利米把头靠在你的耳边，悄悄说道：\"老实说，我一点都不喜欢我妈。她就像一架<swear>直升机，总是告诉我该做什么，去哪里，可以和谁在一起。她从不把我当成一个独立的人，只是她想要的样子。我爸还好，他是这的厨师。\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Darryl should have something for you to do if you like gardening, Jane could use some medical supplies, too.  If you like to be bossed around, Helena probably has a few things that need doing.  I'd just ask around, really."
msgstr "如果你喜欢园艺，达里尔可以给点事你做，简也需要一些医疗用品。如果你喜欢被人摆布，海伦娜可能有一些事情需要做。我只是四处听说到的，真的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Hey, Jerry.  What's up?"
msgstr "嗨，杰里。怎么了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Hey, kid.  I can't stay to talk."
msgstr "嗨，孩子。我不能留下来聊天。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I have a name, you know.  It's Jeremiah, but people just call me Jerry."
msgstr "我有名字的，知道吗。我叫耶利米，但大伙都叫我杰里。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I noticed you're holding a D&D handbook.  Do you play much?"
msgstr "我注意到你随身带着一本D&D手册。你经常玩吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I thought asking about each other's emotions went out of style after <the_cataclysm>.  Uhm, okay then.  I'm fine, I guess."
msgstr "我本认为见面询问对方的情绪在<the_cataclysm>之后就已经过时了。嗯，好吧。我想我还行吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I was in school, like anyone else my age.  Then out of nowhere, my mom pulled me out of school to \"save me\".  I got packed into a bus with my parents and their old-timey friends.  We've been stuck here ever since.  Actually, it's not all that bad.  I'm studying to be a herbalist like Kostas, which is cool I guess."
msgstr "我是个高中生，和其他同龄人一样。然后，我妈妈突然把我从学校拖出来\"救我\"。我和父母以及他们的老朋友一同挤进了一辆大巴。从那以后，我们就一直被困在这里。实话说，情况也没那么糟。我正在学习成为像科斯塔斯这样的草药师，我想这很酷。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I'd like to study herbology with Kostas, it seems like a useful skill these days.  I do feel bad for Jane though, she's a skilled doctor and nobody here cares, they all just think any illness can be prayed away."
msgstr "我想和科斯塔斯一起学习草药学，这似乎是一项有用的技能。不过，我确实为简感到难过，她是一名资深医生，但这里没有人关心，他们都认为任何疾病都可以通过祈祷来消除。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I'll be on my way."
msgstr "我这就出发。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I'll see what I can do for you."
msgstr "我看看我能为你做些什么。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I'm just a traveler, kid.  I won't be staying here for long."
msgstr "我只是个路人，孩子。我不会在这里呆太久。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I'm not exactly new here, kid."
msgstr "我算不上新人了，孩子。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "I've convinced Kostas to take you on."
msgstr "我已经说服科斯塔斯教你了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Is there anything you need?"
msgstr "你还需要什么吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "My take?  You already know how things are.  People are dead, my friends are dead, so yeah.  At least there's no school, the adults just love reminding me that.  You know what?  I kinda miss school."
msgstr "我的看法？你已经知道情况如何了。人们都死了，我的朋友也死了，就是这样。至少没有学校了，大人们总喜欢提醒我这一点。但其实我有点怀念校园了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "No thanks, I'd better get going."
msgstr "不，谢谢。我得走了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "No thanks.  Let's talk about something else."
msgstr "不，谢谢。我们谈点其他的事情吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Oh, uh… you look new.  Didn't think we'd see new people here.  Hey."
msgstr "哦，呃……你看起来是个新人。没想到我们能在这里看到新面孔。嘿。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Sorry, Jeremiah.  I'll be on my way."
msgstr "抱歉，耶利米。我该走了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Sorry, Jerry.  What's up?"
msgstr "抱歉，杰里。怎么了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Sure, I'm up for it."
msgstr "当然，我准备好了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Tell me about your parents."
msgstr "跟我说说你的父母吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "That's great!  Thanks <name_g>, here's the money."
msgstr "干得不错！谢谢<name_g>，这是给你的钱。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Well…  Kostas is a bit unsure about teaching me, for some reason.  If you could change his mind, I'd pay you some \"icons\", what we've started using for money around here."
msgstr "嗯……科斯塔斯有点不太想教我。如果你能改变他的想法，我会付给你一些\"圣像\"，我们已经开始用它当货币了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Were could I find work around here?"
msgstr "我能在这里找到活干吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "What are your parents like?"
msgstr "你的父母怎么样了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "What are your plans after <the_cataclysm>?"
msgstr "你在<the_cataclysm>之后有什么打算吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
msgid "What's your take on the situation here?"
msgstr "你对这里的情况还有什么看法？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "When do you plan on starting that apprenticeship?"
msgstr "你打算什么时候开始当学徒？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "Yeah, I play.  I ran a campaign for a while with some of my friends, we'd play after school.  I don't know where they are now, though.  Do you wanna play some?"
msgstr "是的，我玩。我以前一直和我的一些朋友跑团，在我们放学后。不过我不知道他们现在在哪里。你也想玩一局吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
msgid "You're welcome."
msgstr "不客气。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "&Julian suddenly appears disturbed, and looks away from you for a moment.  \"It's a long story, and not an interesting one at that.  I was a cop before.  You must've heard about those riots and all that.  I'm glad we all managed to make it out alive.\""
msgstr "&朱利安突然显得很不安，眼神避开你了一小会儿：\"那是个很长的故事，一点也不有趣。我以前是一名警察。你一定听说过那场暴乱和之后的事情。我很高兴我们都成功地活了下来。\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Advantages?  All I do is work!"
msgstr "好处？我手头只有做不完的活！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Aight, here are the rules: don't commit sins, don't litter, and try not to die.  Have some mutual respect, capiche?"
msgstr "好吧，这里有份守则：别犯罪，别扔垃圾，尽量别死。相互尊重点，行不？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Alright, let's talk about something else."
msgstr "好吧，我们来说点别的吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Anything I can do to help you out?"
msgstr "我能帮你什么忙吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Go on…"
msgstr "继续……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Hello, Julian.  I can't stay to talk."
msgstr "嗨，朱利安。我不能留下来聊天。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Hey, a new face.  I'm Julian, the guy in charge of this room.  You're planning on sticking around or somethin'?"
msgstr "嘿，一张新面孔。我叫朱利安，目前管着这个房间。你是打算留下还是怎么的？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
msgid "Hey, good to see you again."
msgstr "嘿，很高兴又见到你了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "How did you make it out?"
msgstr "你怎么活下来的？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "I get the picture, screw this."
msgstr "我明白了图片，搞砸了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "I'd rather not talk about it."
msgstr "我不想谈这件事情。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "I'm a joinee actually.  Nice to meet you."
msgstr "其实我已经是教友了。很高兴认识你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss.  I gotta go."
msgstr "请节哀。我得走了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss.  Maybe we should change the subject."
msgstr "我为你的损失感到难过。也许我们该换个话题。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "It's been a struggle, trying to keep this bunch together.  Oh things could be better here, of course.  It could always be, but sometimes we don't even realize how good we have it here."
msgstr "这是份吃力不讨好的活，试图让这群人团结在一起。当然，情况本可以更好。人总是这样，但有时我们甚至没有意识到现状有多好。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Listen, I have some bad news.  I don't personally have anything against you, but many of the people here are very… discriminatory against those who look like you.  I hate to say it, but I'll have to turn you away.  I'm sorry."
msgstr "听着，我有一些坏消息。  我个人并没有反对你的意思，但这里的许多人非常……歧视那些看起来像你的人。  我不想这么说，但我不得不拒绝你。  对不起。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Need anything?"
msgstr "需要什么吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Julian.  I'm just passing through."
msgstr "很高兴见到你，朱利安。我只是路过。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Julian.  I'm seeking asylum."
msgstr "很高兴见到你，朱利安。我正在寻找避难所。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Thank you.  See you around, Julian."
msgstr "谢谢你。回见，朱利安。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Well, I might as well be honest with you.  I ran mostly, ran like the devil was chasin' me.  I was at one of the police stations in town, when we were called out to handle a violent mob on the loose.  When we got there, the people were crazy, smashing and killing everything in their way.  They had these bloodshot eyes and a weird goo in their mouths.  We pulled out all the stops to handle them.  When tear gas wouldn't work, the chief told us to draw guns and kill them all.  We did…  There was so much blood…  That maneuver killed a lot of them, but not all.  One snuck up behind a lady who worked with us, tore a whole section of her spine out.  She never even had time to scream, just slumped over the cruiser door…  So I jumped post and ran, never looked back.  God, I can still hear the cries…"
msgstr "好吧，我想和你实话实说也无妨。我大多数时间都在逃跑，就像魔鬼在追着我一样。当时我在镇上的一个警察局，我们接到通知去管控一群暴民。当我们到达那里时，人们都疯了，用各种方式粉碎和杀害一切。他们双眼布满血丝，嘴里有种奇怪的粘液。我们用尽一切办法来对付他们。当催泪瓦斯不起作用时，警长告诉我们拔枪，把他们全部杀死。我们做到了……留了太多的血……那次行动杀死了很多人，但不是所有人。有一只偷偷溜到一位和我们一起工作的女士身后，把她的脊柱撕了一大截下来。她甚至连尖叫的时间都没有，就那样瘫倒在警车门上……所以我跳船逃走了，再也没回过头。天啊，我仿佛还能听到那种惨叫声……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "What are the advantages of being a dorm leader?"
msgstr "当个舍监有什么好处？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "When I was younger, I used to go to church with my family.  When I started growing up, I saw all this evil around me, people hating and persecuting others, despite the teachings of Jesus; I just stopped going one day, decided to make my own way.  I joined the NECC a few years back to rekindle my relationship with God, get back to who I was."
msgstr "当我年轻的时候，我经常和家人一起去教堂。当我开始长大的时候，我看到了我周围的一切邪恶，人们憎恨和迫害他人，无视耶稣的教导；我只是在某一天停了下来，决定走自己的路。几年前，我加入了新英格兰教会，重新唤醒了我与主的联结，寻回自我。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Why did you join the Church?"
msgstr "你为什么加入教会？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Yeah, I can understand.  See ya later."
msgstr "是的，我能理解。再见。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Yeah, it must be exhausting.  Well, bye."
msgstr "是的，一定很累。好吧，再见。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "You sure?  I mean, you've been traveling for a long time, haven't you?  Alright, it's your decision.  Let me know when you changed your mind."
msgstr "你确定吗？我是说，你已经旅行了很长时间了，不是吗？好吧，这是你的决定。当你改变主意时告诉我。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "You sure?  I mean, you've been traveling for a long time, haven't you?  Alright, it's your decision.  Let me know when you changed your mind."
msgstr "你确定吗？我是说，你已经旅行了很长时间了，不是吗？好吧，这是你的决定。当你改变主意时告诉我。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "You sure?  I mean, you've been traveling for a long time, haven't you?  Alright, it's your decision.  Let me know when you changed your mind."
msgstr "你确定吗？我是说，你已经旅行了很长时间了，不是吗？好吧，这是你的决定。当你改变主意时告诉我。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
msgid "Your name is now on the books.  Here's your blanket, joinee.  Those two beds next to the window, you can choose one of them.  It's safe, don't worry.  I'm armed.  By the way, if you're hungry you can go bug Simon for a meal, up to one in a day."
msgstr "你的名字现在列在名册里了。这是你的毯子，教友。窗户旁边的那两张床，你可以选一张。这里很安全，不用担心。我有武器。顺便说一下，如果你饿了，你可以去找西蒙吃顿饭，一天最多吃一顿。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Alright, fuck you then."
msgstr "好吧，那就操你妈吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you can take in joinees once there's a vacancy?"
msgstr "一旦出现了空缺，你能接受新教友加入吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you tell me about Arturo?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于阿图罗的事情吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you tell me about Corrie?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于科里的事情吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you tell me about Jane?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于简的事情吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you tell me about Jeremiah?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于耶利米的事情吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you tell me about Simon?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于西蒙的事情吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you tell me about Sonia?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于索尼娅的事情吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Can you tell me about Zachary?"
msgstr "能和我说说关于扎卡里的事情吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Do you know where I could find some work?"
msgstr "你知道我在哪能找到活干吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "He was quite reserved when I met him, seemed distant in his thoughts.  Theresa has the answers you are looking for."
msgstr "我第一次见到他时，他还很矜持，沉浸在自己的思索之中。特蕾莎有你想要的答案。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "He's my son, such a wonderful boy.  He's always been the light in my life, and I've tried to teach him well.  We've been a bit distant as of late, but I'm sure he'll come around."
msgstr "他是我儿子，真是个好孩子。他一直是我生命中的光，我一直在努力教他。我们最近有点疏远，但我相信他会回心转意的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Hi, Katherine.  How's it going?"
msgstr "嗨，凯瑟琳。近况如何？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "I hear she knows this and that about electronics.    She keeps herself occupied by doing menial tasks around the camp, looking for payment."
msgstr "我听说她对电子产品了如指掌。她一直忙着在营地四周做些杂活，寻找报酬。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
msgid "I just had some questions."
msgstr "我只是有些问题。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "I understand.  I don't have the answers you are looking for, I'm afraid."
msgstr "我理解。恐怕我没有你想要的答案。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "I worked for the Church, organized charities and filed paperwork.  That's how I met the Founder.  I did so much for everyone, yet they never noticed…"
msgstr "我为教会工作，组织慈善机构并负责文书。我就是这样认识创始人的。我为每个人做了很多，但他们从来没有注意到……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "I'll be on my way then."
msgstr "那我还是走吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "I'll talk to her then."
msgstr "好吧，我会去跟她谈谈。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "I'm not planning to communicate with him, that's for certain.  He can keep his distance with his smug nothingness.  At least he knows how to cut lumber."
msgstr "我不打算和他交流，这是肯定的。他可以保持与他那自以为是的虚无的距离。至少他知道如何伐木。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "I'm sure you've met my husband, Simon.  He was also a volunteer at a homeless shelter, working as a cook.  We were brought together by the hands of fate as some would say.  We have a son together, Jeremiah, the light in my life.  Such a creative and well-behaved boy, I just wish we could find an appropriate woman for him."
msgstr "我肯定你已经见过我丈夫西蒙了。他也是流浪者收容所的志愿者，当厨师。正如有些人所说，是命运之手让我们相会的。我们有一个儿子，耶利米，我生命中的光。那么一个富有创造力又举止得体的男孩，我真希望我们能为他找到一位合适的女士。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "I've been a member of the New England Church Community for a quarter of a century, took part in each and every sermon and gathering they held even while I was carrying my boy Jeremiah.  Not to mention the countless times we visited those filthy homeless shelters and prisons filled with sinners.  I even met the Founder himself.  I can confidently say I'm more worthy to be here than those impostors who leech on us at this camp."
msgstr "我成为新英格兰教会社区的一员的时间已经接近四分之一个世纪了，参加了他们举行的每一场布道和聚会，甚至在我怀着我的儿子耶利米的时候。更不用说我们无数次参观那些肮脏的流浪者收容所和充满罪人的监狱了。我甚至见过创始人本人。我可以自信地说，我比那些在这个营地里依赖我们的冒名顶替者更有资格呆在这里。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "If there's a vacancy.  Even then, there's the decision of which joinee to include.  Those people don't share or respect the same values as we do.  None of them are promising candidates."
msgstr "只在有空缺的情况下。即使如此，也要决定哪一个入会者能加入。这些人没有分享或尊重与我们一样的价值观，他们都算不上有希望的候选人。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "If you're here for an exciting story, you're talking with the wrong person.  Ever since I was born I've lived very modestly.  Did I regret it?  No, it will all be worth it in the end…"
msgstr "如果你来这里是为了一个激动人心的故事，那你可找错人了。自从我出生以来，我就过着朴实无华的生活。我后悔了吗？不，这一切最终都是值得的……"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "It's always a pleasure.  How may I help you?"
msgstr "总是很高兴见到新人。我能为你做什么？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Jesus warned us about false prophets."
msgstr "耶稣警告我们要提防假先知。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "My dear, sweet husband.  He worked as a cook for one of the homeless shelters, that's how we met.  He's always liked to try new things.  He should be in the dining hall, if you want to see him."
msgstr "我亲爱的，亲爱的丈夫。他之前在一家流浪者收容所当厨师，我们就是这样认识的。他总是喜欢尝试新事物。如果你想见他，他应该在餐厅。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/necc/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Katherine."
msgstr "很高兴见到你，凯瑟琳。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
