#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "I don't have a whole lot, but I've got a few things that I could stand to be rid of, too much weight tanks the gas mileage.  I could always use more fuel, food, and clean water if you have any to spare.  Entertainment is also appreciated, it's pretty <swear> boring looking at nothing but road for 10 hours a day."
msgstr "我没有太多，但我有一些我可以忍受摆脱的东西，太多的重量会增加油耗。  如果你还有多余的话，我总是可以使用更多的燃料、食物和干净的水。  娱乐活动也是值得赞赏的，每天花 10 个小时只看马路真是太无聊了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid "I used to travel a lot before <the_cataclysm>, and I've had this camper with me for a while now.  I was at home when the riots started, so I grabbed everything I could from my house and hopped in the camper.  I nearly wrecked on my way out of town when some crazy people tried to smash my van, but I made it out.  I've been on the move ever since."
msgstr "在<the_cataclysm>之前我曾经经常旅行，现在我已经带着这辆露营车有一段时间了。  骚乱开始时我在家，所以我从家里拿走了所有能找到的东西，然后跳进了露营车。  当一些疯狂的人试图砸坏我的货车时，我在出城的路上差点撞车，但我逃了出来。  从那时起我就一直在搬家。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgctxt "npc:m"
msgid "I used to travel a lot before <the_cataclysm>, and I've had this camper with me for a while now.  I was at home when the riots started, so I grabbed everything I could from my house and hopped in the camper.  I nearly wrecked on my way out of town when some crazy people tried to smash my van, but I made it out.  I've been on the move ever since."
msgstr "在<the_cataclysm>之前我曾经经常旅行，现在我已经带着这辆露营车有一段时间了。  骚乱开始时我在家，所以我从家里拿走了所有能找到的东西，然后跳进了露营车。  当一些疯狂的人试图砸坏我的货车时，我在出城的路上差点撞车，但我逃了出来。  从那时起我就一直在搬家。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgctxt "npc:n"
msgid "I used to travel a lot before <the_cataclysm>, and I've had this camper with me for a while now.  I was at home when the riots started, so I grabbed everything I could from my house and hopped in the camper.  I nearly wrecked on my way out of town when some crazy people tried to smash my van, but I made it out.  I've been on the move ever since."
msgstr "在<the_cataclysm>之前我曾经经常旅行，现在我已经带着这辆露营车有一段时间了。  骚乱开始时我在家，所以我从家里拿走了所有能找到的东西，然后跳进了露营车。  当一些疯狂的人试图砸坏我的货车时，我在出城的路上差点撞车，但我逃了出来。  从那时起我就一直在搬家。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "I'll be gone here in a day or two, just stopping long enough to get some supplies and fix anything wrong with the camper."
msgstr "一两天后我就会去这里，停下来足够长的时间去买一些补给品并修复露营车的任何问题。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "Let's take a look."
msgstr "我们来看一下。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that desolate barn"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that collapsed house"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "Sweet."
msgstr "甜的。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that desolate barn"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that collapsed house"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "That's unfortunate."
msgstr "那很不幸。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "What's in that RV of yours?  Couldn't be anything you need, so hand over your stuff."
msgstr "你那辆房车里有什么？  不可能有你需要的东西，所以把你的东西交出来。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "When will you be leaving?"
msgstr "你什么时候离开？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "Where did you say you were going again?"
msgstr "你说你又要去哪里？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "Where was the bunker at?"
msgstr "掩体在哪里？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "Where were they at?"
msgstr "他们在哪里？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "*tips their hat down from their eyes and looks at you blearily.  \"Huh?  Hey, I'm tryin'a sleep here.  I was on night watch."
msgstr "*把帽子从他们的眼睛上摘下来，睡眼惺忪地看着你。\"哈？嘿，我试着在这里睡觉呢。我昨晚守夜了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Actually I had a little more to trade still."
msgstr "稍等，我还有些东西要交易。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Always good to do a little trading."
msgstr "做笔交易总是好的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Are you threatening me?"
msgstr "你这是在威胁我吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Can you give me directions to any of these other survivor groups?"
msgstr "你能告诉我其他幸存者团体的位置吗？"

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Random NPC, non persistent, tells you about being a guard and directs you
#. to free merchants.
#. ~ Random NPC, non persistent, doesn't have much to say.
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Caravan Guard"
msgstr "商队护卫"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Here, I'll mark it on your map.  Feel free to come by and trade, or if you're the type, we might have use for your services as a merc."
msgstr "来，我在你的地图上标出。欢迎随时来做笔交易，或者如果你是那类人的话，我们可能会需要你来做名佣兵。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Hey, thanks.  Well, let's trade."
msgstr "嘿，谢谢。好吧，我们交易吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Hi again.  You want something?"
msgstr "又见面了。你想要点什么吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "How do I get there?"
msgstr "我怎么去那里？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "I can understand that.  Well, let's trade."
msgstr "我能理解。好吧，我们交易吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "I won't try anything if you don't.  Just passing through."
msgstr "只要你不做傻事，我们什么都不会做。只是路过而已。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "I'm a caravan guard, working for the Free Merchants.  I'm an independent contractor though.  Seems like a good way to get safety in numbers and try to find a safe place to settle down."
msgstr "我是一名商队护卫，为自由商会工作。不过我是个独立的安全承包商。这似乎是一个很好的方法，可以在数量上获得安全感，并试着找个安全的地方安顿下来。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "I'm good for the moment, but you can usually find a merc or two waiting between jobs, back at the Free Merchant base."
msgstr "我现在很好，但你通常可以在自由商会基地找到一两个在工作间隙休息的佣兵。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "It's a living, eh?  I'd better get going."
msgstr "这也算是一种生活方式，对吧？我得走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "No offense, but my clients definitely would not like me giving strangers directions to their hideouts.  You'll have to find them on their own terms."
msgstr "无意冒犯，但我的客户肯定不希望我告诉陌生人他们的藏身之处。你必须用自己的方式找到他们。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "No offense, but my clients definitely would not like me giving strangers directions to their hideouts.  You'll have to find them on their own terms."
msgstr "无意冒犯，但我的客户肯定不希望我告诉陌生人他们的藏身之处。你必须用自己的方式找到他们。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "No offense, but my clients definitely would not like me giving strangers directions to their hideouts.  You'll have to find them on their own terms."
msgstr "无意冒犯，但我的客户肯定不希望我告诉陌生人他们的藏身之处。你必须用自己的方式找到他们。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "No, not at all.  Just being cautious.  You know how it gets out here.  We're not looking for trouble.  In fact, if you've got anything worthwhile, maybe we could do a little trading."
msgstr "不，一点也不。只是谨慎而已。你知道它们是怎么出来的。我们可不想找麻烦。事实上，如果你有些值钱货，也许我们可以做点交易。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Nope, just saying hi."
msgstr "不，只是打个招呼。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Nothing much.  Just passing through."
msgstr "没什么。只是路过。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Oh, uh, sorry."
msgstr "呃，嗯，抱歉。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "So you're working for these guys, but aren't one of them?"
msgstr "所以你只是为这些人工作，但不是他们中的一员吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Sup?  Nice to see a survivor.  If you're here for business, talk to the trader."
msgstr "怎么了？很高兴见到幸存者。如果你来做交易的，找商人谈谈。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Sure, I can mark it on your map if you like.  Here."
msgstr "当然，如果你愿意，我可以在你的地图上标出。就在这里。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Sure, let's trade."
msgstr "当然，我们交易吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for chatting.  I'd better go."
msgstr "谢谢你陪我聊天。我该走了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for that.  I'd better go."
msgstr "谢谢你了。我最好走了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the tip!  I'll be on my way."
msgstr "感谢指点！我马上就去。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the tip!  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "感谢指点！你刚才说什么来着？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the tip."
msgstr "多谢你的消息。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks.  What were we talking about before?"
msgstr "谢谢了。我们刚刚在说什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "That suits me fine.  I'll be on my way."
msgstr "我也无所谓。我马上就走。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "That's interesting.  Well, let's trade."
msgstr "这很有趣。好吧，我们交易吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "That's it?  What's your story?"
msgstr "就这样？你的故事是什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "The Free Merchants?  Do they have some kind of trade outpost or anything like that?"
msgstr "自由商会？他们有什么贸易哨站之类的吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "We're just travelers, making a pit stop.  Might be willing to trade a bit, if you've got anything to share.  We're not looking for trouble, there's plenty of that on the roads already."
msgstr "我们只是旅行者，在中途稍作停留。如果你有什么多余的东西，可能还能做笔交易。我们不是在找麻烦，路上已经有很多麻烦了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "We're with a larger group of survivors, working out of one of the old FEMA bunkers.  Folks have taken to calling us Free Merchants, although that sounds kinda on the nose to me.  We know about a few survivor groups and we make regular trips around, sharing supplies back and forth and bringing them home.  We're on the way back now."
msgstr "我们和一大群幸存者在一个旧联邦应急管理局的避难所里工作。大家已经习惯于称我们为自由商会，尽管这听起来有点让我头疼。我们还知道其他一些幸存者团体的位置，我们定期走这条路线，来回分享物资，把大伙完整带回家。我们正在回去的路上。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Well well, another traveler.  Don't try anything, you're outnumbered here and we're well armed."
msgstr "瞧瞧，又一个旅行者。不要尝试做傻事，你在这里寡不敌众，我们都全副武装。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "Well well, another traveler.  Don't try anything, you're outnumbered here and we're well armed."
msgstr "瞧瞧，又一个旅行者。不要尝试做傻事，你在这里寡不敌众，我们都全副武装。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "Well well, another traveler.  Don't try anything, you're outnumbered here and we're well armed."
msgstr "瞧瞧，又一个旅行者。不要尝试做傻事，你在这里寡不敌众，我们都全副武装。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "What's your deal here?"
msgstr "你们在这里做什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Where is 'home'?"
msgstr "那你们\"家\"在哪里？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Yeah, these guys snagged some kind of FEMA evacuation bunker during the early part of <the_cataclysm> and hoard the space.  They don't let anyone else join, but they need supplies, so they send out traders, and those traders need protection, so they send out guys like me."
msgstr "是的，这些人在<the_cataclysm>初就找到了一处联邦应急管理局的避难所，然后就占了下来。他们不让任何人加入，但他们需要补给，所以他们派出了商队交易，这些商队需要人保护，所以他们雇了像我这样的人。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "You looking for work?  I might be hiring."
msgstr "你准备找新工作吗？我可以雇你。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "*chuckles.  \"If you can call it that, sure.  So maybe we should do our best to be better at that than the zombies.  Seems pretty reasonable to me, and it's a pretty low bar to clear.\""
msgstr "*轻轻笑了笑。\"如果你要这么说的话，当然。所以也许我们应该尽最大努力在这方面比丧尸做得更好。对我来说似乎很合理，而且这很容易做到。\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "*chuckles.  \"Lucky for me then it doesn't matter if you believe me.  I do gotta say though, it's funny you and I, a pair of actual real-live zombie hunters, are talking face to face and you think my *survival story* is the unlikely thing.\""
msgstr "*低声轻笑。\"幸运地是，对我来说你相不相信我并不重要。不过我得说，有趣的是，你和我，一对活生生的丧尸猎手，能在这面对面地交谈，而你却认为我的*生存故事*是不太可能发生的事情。\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "*glances your way, then makes eye contact as you move closer to speak.  He is a strong-looking man in his mid forties, his hair greying and his face flecked with stubble and travel dust.  The clothes he's wearing are clearly scavenged, though they fit well, and he has the build of someone who until recently had the luxury of carrying a few extra pounds.  \"Hi there.\"  He presents his hand to shake.  \"You don't look like you belong here.  Name's Bailey, John Bailey.\""
msgstr "*朝你的方向瞥了一眼，在你走近说话时一只盯着你。他是一个四十多岁的强壮男子，头发灰白，脸上布满了胡茬和灰尘。他身上穿的衣服显然是捡来的，尽管它们很合身，而且他的体格看上去像是最近还长胖了几磅似的。\"你好。\"他伸出手来和你握手。\"你看起来不属于这里。我叫贝利，约翰·贝利。\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "*laughs a bit sheepishly.  \"Seems distasteful to keep track of that stuff, doesn't it?\"  He touches a series of notches on his <mywp>.  \"I'm human though.  I'm up to <npc_val:zkc_john> so far.  Seems like a lot to me, especially since I try to avoid actually engaging the enemy if I can help it.\""
msgstr "*有点不好意思地笑了。\"统计这类数据似乎令人厌恶，不是吗？\"他数了数自己<mywp>上的一道道刻痕。\"但我是人类。我已经杀了<npc_val:zkc_john>只。对我来说算是很多吧，尤其是在我尽力避免交战的情况下。\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "*nods as you approach, then smiles and stretches casually.  \"Anything I can do for you, friend?\""
msgstr "*在你走近时点头，然后微笑，随意伸展着身体。\"我能为你做点什么吗，朋友？\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "*raises an eyebrow.  \"I don't know about that.  You should be careful about thinking people who don't make the same choices as you are inferior.  Sure, not everyone's suited to scavenge, but a scavenger's got to have a safe home, too.\""
msgstr "*扬起了眉毛。\"我可不认同这一点。你应该小心些，可别认为那些做出与你不同选择的人是低人一等的。当然，不是每个人都适合拾荒，但拾荒者也得有个安全的家。\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "*rubs his stubble, looking thoughtful.  \"I agree it's important to be independent, but don't forget, working together is what makes us better than the undead.  It's how we got out of the trees and fields, and into civilization.  Anyway, I don't want to talk philosophy at you.  If you're doing well on your own, more power to you!\""
msgstr "*搓着他的胡茬，显得若有所思。\"我同意自力更生很重要，但别忘了，合同协助我们才能比不死人更强。这才能让我们走出森林旷野，走进文明社会。好吧，我现在不想和你讨论哲学问题。如果你一个人过得很好，再接再厉吧！\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "*sizes you up and down, and shakes his head sadly.  \"Darius and I have a good thing going, and a third person would be hard to justify, especially these days.  Trust comes hard.  I'm sorry.  I hope you've got someone to watch your back, but it can't be me.\""
msgstr "*上下打量你，悲伤地摇摇头。\"大流士和我还算合得来，而现在加入第三人很难说得通，尤其是现在。信任很难得。我很抱歉。我希望你能找到人掩护你，但这个人不是我。\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Are you looking for work?"
msgstr "你在找工作吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Can you give me any advice?"
msgstr "你能给我一些建议吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Damn straight.  People should learn to fend for themselves."
msgstr "真他妈的直截了当。人们应该学会自力更生。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Fuck that.  People should learn to fend for themselves."
msgstr "去他妈的。人们应该学会自力更生。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Got time to teach me anything?"
msgstr "有时间教我什么吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Hi John, I'm afraid I can't stay to talk."
msgstr "嗨，约翰。恐怕我不能留下来聊天。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Hi John.  What are you doing here?"
msgstr "嗨，约翰。你在这里干什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "How did you know things were going to go wrong?"
msgstr "你怎么知道事情会变糟糕的？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Huh, well, the short story is, I got my wife and kids out of town in the really, really early days.  She's got great intuition for stuff and when she told me to get ready to leave town, I figured at worst we'd have an unnecessary early spring vacation in my dad's old cabin, you know?  Obviously, turns out trusting her gut saved us all and then some.  Things were still tough, but from what I've heard, I might be the only person left on the Eastern Seaboard who still has his whole nuclear family.  Still got a lot of survivor's guilt for that… still lost everyone else.  Anyway, one thing led to another and we gathered a few other people that we watch out for.  My man Darius, he joined up early on and he and I do the scouting and scavenging and watch each others' backs."
msgstr "哈，好吧，简短的版本是，我在很早的时候就把妻子和孩子们搬出了镇子。她有很强的直觉，当她告诉我准备离开城镇时，我想最坏的情况不过是我们会在我父亲的旧森林小屋里度过一个不必要的早春假期，你知道吗？显然，相信她的直觉拯救了我们一家，还有其他一些人。形势仍然很艰难，但据我所知，我可能是东海岸唯一一个仍然拥有整个核心家庭的人。现在我还带着不少幸存愧疚感……仍然失去了其他亲人。总而言之，自然而然地我们又召集了几个注意到的人。我的手下大流士，他很早就加入了，他和我一起外出侦察搜刮，并互相掩护。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I could use someone like you.  Want to travel with me?"
msgstr "我需要像你这样的人。想和我同行吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I do odd jobs if people need help.  Not on a volunteer basis you understand, but I try not to be unfair about it either.  Lots of people need a bit of help these days, often just with little things a scavenger like me can find for them.  It's easy for folks like you and me to underestimate how scared a lot of people are to go back out in that place.  The situation's bad enough as it is, but these kind of people took refuge back when it was true chaos out there.  Lots of trauma to unpack there.  Anyway, if there's little things I can do for them, I try to help where I can, so long as it doesn't put me in too much danger."
msgstr "如果有人需要，我会打些零工。可不是当志愿者，你得明白，但我也尽量不会乱开价。现在很多人都需要些帮助，通常只是需要像我这样的拾荒者帮他们找些小东西。像你和我这样的人很容易低估其实很多人对回到那个地方是多么害怕。情况已经够糟糕的了，但这些人在当时那种混乱的情况下躲了起来。他们心里有很多创伤需要解开。不管怎样，如果我能为他们做点什么，我会尽力帮助他们，只要这不会给我带来太多的危险。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I don't know, the zombies sure seem to work together to me."
msgstr "我不知道，在我看来，丧尸确实在一起合作对付我。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I don't really know.  Food stocks aren't too bad for me and mine, I found a stock of canned goods early on that will last us for a while yet.  I don't use a gun if I can avoid it, too noisy.  I notice these guys seem to keep a lot of building supplies though, and trying to get a vehicle downtown to loot a hardware store or a lumberyard is suicide, so I think that's where they're going to get my money.  I wonder if they deliver."
msgstr "我也不知道。食品库存对我和我的家人来说都不算太坏，我很早就发现了一批罐头食品，这将够我们吃上一段时间。我尽可能不用枪，太吵了。我注意到这些家伙似乎有很多建筑用品，而试图带一辆车去市中心抢劫五金店或木材厂是自杀行为，所以我想他们可以用这些建筑用品得到我的钱。我只想知道他们能不能送货上门。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I might take you up on that, but for now I've gotta go."
msgstr "我也许会采纳你的意见的，但现在我得走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I'll be straight with you, I don't want to tell you too much about my people, okay?  You seem all right, don't get me wrong, but I've seen some scary fuckin' people out there, who come on all normal and then try to bite your face off when they get you alone.  Everyone's reaction to the world's end is a bit different.  Things are stable with my people now, but we don't really welcome new faces anymore.  I wish it weren't that way.  Maybe if you and I get to know each other better some day, I'll change my mind."
msgstr "我跟你说实话，我不想告诉你太多关于我的人的事，好吗？你看起来还好，别误会我的意思，但我见过一些可怕的人，他们表现得很正常，但当他们和你单独在一起时，他们会把你的脸都咬掉。每个人对世界末日的反应都有点不同。我的人现在情况稳定，但我们不再欢迎新面孔了。我也不希望这样。也许如果有一天你和我能更好地了解对方，我会改变主意的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I'll bear that in mind.  What did you say you were doing here?"
msgstr "我会记着的。你刚才说你在这里干什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "It sounds like you have some past there.  You want to talk about it?"
msgstr "听起来你有些过去的经历。你想谈谈吗？"

#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
#. ~ A survivor who sometimes visits the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "John Bailey"
msgstr "约翰·贝利"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Let's change the subject.  What did you say you were doing here?"
msgstr "我们换个话题吧。你刚才说你在这里干什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Move on\" where?"
msgstr "上路去哪里？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Nice talking to you, I've gotta go."
msgstr "和你聊天很愉快，我也该走了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Not at the moment, thanks."
msgstr "现在不行，谢谢。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Not really, no.  It's old stuff, and there's enough going on.  Let's just say I'm no stranger to loss, either my own or others'."
msgstr "真的没什么，不了。都是陈年旧事，而且又经历了更多。只能说我对于损失并不陌生，不管是我自己的还是别人的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Oh, jeez, yeah.  The world really went to shit, didn't it?  Well, I've seen some weird alien things.  Our rule is 'scared is better than dead'.  If we don't know what something is and how to kill it, we steer wide and clear.  One time I saw this flaming eyeball a long way off, I was scouting from a cell phone tower.  It made eye contact with me and I just started hallucinating shit.  Darius stopped me from falling right off the tower.  Stuff like that is why I think you have to be a bit off your rocker to travel these days unless you have no choice.  Anything we don't know, we turn around and pedal hard.  So far, we haven't met anything our bikes can't outrun."
msgstr "哦，天哪，是的。世界真的变得一团糟，不是吗？我见过一些奇怪的怪物。我们的规则是'害怕总比死了好'。如果我们不知道是什么东西，也不知道如何杀死它，我们就会避开它。有一次，我在很远的地方看到了一个燃烧的眼球，当时我正在一个无线电发射塔上侦察。它和我眼神接触，我就开始产生幻觉。是大流士让我没从塔上摔下来。这就是为什么我认为这些日子你必须有点疯狂才会在外面逛，除非你别无选择。只要遇到任何我们不知道的东西，我们就会掉转车头身，使劲踩踏板。到目前为止，我们还没有遇到任何跑得比我们的自行车快的家伙。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "On your way\" where?"
msgstr "上路去哪里？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "People should learn to fend for themselves, not just get you to hand everything to them."
msgstr "人们应该学会照顾自己，而不是靠你把一切都带给他们。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Same as you, I imagine,\" John shrugs.  \"Checking "
msgstr "我想和你一样，\"约翰耸耸肩。\"我只是看看"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Sometimes, I kinda wonder why other people *didn't* know things were going to go wrong.  Hindsight is twenty-twenty, I guess.  I'll be honest though, as much as I'd like to pat myself on the back, it wasn't me that figured it out.  When the really early riots started out, even though they were way up in the Midwest, my wife just had a bad feeling.  We'd been thinking of a getaway anyway, and I had some time off, so we took it as an excuse to get out to the cabin and wait for everything to blow over.  Here we are.  It wasn't so much knowing how things were going to go, more just straight luck that we trusted our - *her* - gut at the right time and lucked out."
msgstr "有时候，我有点想知道为什么其他人*不知道*事情会变糟糕。事后诸葛亮，我猜。不过说实话，虽然我很想表扬下自己，但这并不是我的功劳。当早期的暴乱开始时，尽管都发生在遥远的中西部地区，但我妻子总有种不好的预感。我们一直在考虑逃走，我刚刚有段时间休假，所以我们以此为借口到森林小屋里等一切都过去。瞧瞧我们现在如何。与其说我们知道事情会怎样发展，不如说我们在正确的时间相信了我们——*她*——的直觉，走了运罢了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Sorry, but that's all I have time for at the moment.  Darius is waiting outside."
msgstr "抱歉，但眼下我没多少时间了。大流士还在外面等着。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Sounds about the same as me, yep.  I'd better get back to it."
msgstr "听起来和我差不多，是的。我们回头再聊。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Sure, I guess.  I don't know if I know anything you don't, you seem like you can handle yourself.  I've made it this far by not engaging whenever possible.  I'm never going to kill all the zombies out there.  Darius and I try not to fight if we can avoid it, and if we can't, we try to always have the advantage.  Numbers, weaponry, terrain.  Zombies are clumsy and stupid so we lead them across bushes and things to trip and stumble.  We take high ground and let them plough into ladders like idiots while we stick 'em with spears from above.  Mostly, though, we try not to be seen.  We use bikes instead of cars because they don't make noise and don't need gas, plus we can take forest trails and things and avoid traffic jams.  Those things are suicide.  We try to avoid the cities, and when we do go close, we stick to the outskirts and raid the outlying houses.  In those, we keep crouched and try to get deep into the building fast, or down into the basement, so that little noises don't carry much and nothing from outside can see us.  Also, zombies being idiots, closing the blinds is a great move.  I always keep a crowbar for opening doors and windows, but I try not to use it if I can avoid it.  Darius can pick locks, which is slower but doesn't make noise.  We get a lot more mileage from raiding gas stations and other rural sites, where if there are a few zombies, we can usually lead them away."
msgstr "当然，我想。我不知道我是否知道些你不懂的事，你似乎能把自己照顾好。我做到这一点是因为尽可能避开战斗。我永远不会试图杀死所有丧尸。大流士和我尽量不打架，只要能避免，如果不能，我们总是试图占据优势。人数，武器，地形。丧尸笨手笨脚，所以我们会领着它们穿过灌木丛，然后被绊倒。我们占领高处，让它们像白痴一样犁进梯子，而我们用长矛从上面刺它们。不过，大多数情况下，我们尽量不被它们发现。我们用自行车而不是汽车，因为它没有噪音，也不需要汽油，而且我们可以走森林小径和其他小路，避开交通堵塞。那里都是自杀陷阱。我们尽量避开城市，当我们靠近时，我们只进入郊区，清扫外围的房屋。在这种情况下，我们会趴低身体，试图快速深入大楼，或者深入地下室，这样少许噪音就不会带来太大麻烦，外界也看不到我们。此外，丧尸是白痴，关闭百叶窗是个高招。我随身带着根能撬开门窗的撬棍，但如果可以避免的话，我尽量不使用。大流士会撬锁，虽然速度较慢，但不会发出噪音。我们通过扫荡加油站和其他农村地区获得了更多油料，如果那里有丧尸，我们也可以把它们领走。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Sure, let's talk trade."
msgstr "当然，我们谈谈交易吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Talk to Darius if you want to know about Darius.  He's a good man, and he won't bite-- ugh, sorry, that's a turn of phrase we should probably retire, hey?  Anyway.  I don't know if we'd have made it through the first days without him.  He gets a bit jumpy around crowds since the riots though, so he's out watching our stuff."
msgstr "如果你想知道大流士的事，就和大流士谈谈。他是个好人，他不会咬人——呃，对不起，我们也许不该再用这种措词了，呵呵？好吧。我不知道如果没有他，我们能否度过最初的几天。自从暴乱发生以来，他在人多的场合总有点神经质，所以他待在外面看着我们的东西。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Tell me about Darius."
msgstr "跟我说说大流士的事吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Thanks, I'll think about it.  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "谢谢，我会考虑的。你刚才说什么来着？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "That is one hell of a life.  You must have some useful skills to teach."
msgstr "这可真是丰富多彩的经历啊。你一定有些有用的技能可以教我。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "That seems like a pretty unlikely story."
msgstr "这听起来似乎是一个不太可能的故事。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "That's a shame.  We'd be a good team.  People like you and I are made of stronger stuff."
msgstr "真可惜。我们可以成为一个好团队的。像你我这样的人浑身都是胆。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "That's a tougher question than you might think.  I've had quite the life.  My dad was a mechanic, and when I was young I used to help around the shop quite a bit.  I started out thinking I was going to get into that line of work, but then I got sidetracked and wound up getting into computers and electrical work for a long time.  Did part of an electrical engineering degree, then decided it wasn't for me and quit that.  Spent a bit of time doing freelance electrical and programming work, then got recruited by a startup that was designing and programming medical equipment.  I was supposed to be a general technician, but through a weird series of events I wound up in sales, then management.  I hated management, and I'd made a big nest egg from my share stock, so I cashed out and tried to retire young.  That was a dumb move, I was bored as hell, so I finished off my degree and started doing on-call teaching work for shop, computers, math, and things like that at a college and high school level.  Just part time, and I spent the rest of my time outdoors, hiking and whatnot."
msgstr "这个问题比你想象的要更难回答。我曾经过得很好。我爸爸是名机械技师，我小时候经常在店里帮忙。我一开始以为自己也会干这行，但后来我改变了方向，很长一段时间都在从事计算机和电气工作。我读了一部分电子工程学位，然后觉得不适合我，就退学了。又花了一点时间做些电子和编程的自由工作，然后被一家设计医疗设备的初创公司录用。我本应该是一名普通技术员，但经历了一系列奇怪的事件，最终当了个销售，然后是管理。我讨厌干管理，而且我从股票里赚了一大笔钱，所以我兑现了，并试图早点退休。这是个愚蠢的举动，我感到非常无聊，所以我完成了我的学位，开始做些大学和高中水平的随叫随到的培训工作，市场、计算机、数学之类的。只是兼职，剩下的时间我都在户外，徒步旅行等等。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "That's for the weaklings.  People like you and I are made of stronger stuff."
msgstr "那是给弱者的话。像你我这样的人浑身都是胆。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What about things other than zombies?"
msgstr "那要是丧尸以外的东西呢？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What are you shopping for?"
msgstr "你都买些什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What did you used to do before?"
msgstr "你以前做过什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What do you know about this place?"
msgstr "你对这个地方了解吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What kind of work are you looking for?"
msgstr "你在找什么样的工作？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Where are you guys located?  Can I join up too?"
msgstr "你们在哪里？我也能加入吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Where are you headed next?"
msgstr "你下一步要去哪里？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Who can say, really?  I don't really have a strong plan.  Depends on how this trip goes.  Once my vehicle is full up, I'll have to head back to my hideout and check on everyone there.  I don't like being gone too long."
msgstr "谁知道呢，真的？我真的没有什么强而有力的计划。取决于这趟旅程的进展。一旦我的车装满了，我就得回到我的藏身处，看看那里每个人的情况。我不喜欢离开太久。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Who is \"everyone\"?"
msgstr "每个人都是谁啊？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Who is \"you and yours\"?"
msgstr "谁是你的家人？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Yeah, I, uh… I know a bit about that stuff.  Hard not to empathize, especially when I know I'm not quite as hard as others, by sheer luck.  Besides, there are so few of us left now.  What's the point in wasting time judging other people for how hard they took the end of the world?"
msgstr "是吧，我，呃……我算是知道一点。很难不去感同身受，尤其是当我知道自己和其他人相比也没那么强时，纯粹是靠运气。此外，我们现在剩下的人太少了。浪费时间评判其他人面对世界末日时不够坚强有什么意义？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "You look like you can handle yourself in a fight.  What's your zombie kill count?"
msgstr "你看起来是那种能在战斗中照顾好自己的类型。你杀了多少丧尸了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "You looking for any kind of work?"
msgstr "你在找什么工作吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "You seem to know a lot about how people feel."
msgstr "你似乎很了解人们的感受。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "You'd do better to talk to the people here about it.  Seems like a bunch of them gathered here in the early days of <the_cataclysm> and managed to make it through.  It's the biggest bunch of survivors I've found yet, but most of them hunker up in the basement.  I can understand the urge.  We've all been through way too much.  They say they don't have room for more people though, so I'm just here to do some shopping, see if there's work to be done, then move on."
msgstr "你最好和这里的人谈谈。似乎他们中的一大群人在<the_cataclysm>刚发生时就聚在这里了，并设法活了下来。这是我迄今为止遇到的最大的一批幸存者，但大多数人都蜷缩在下面的地下室里。我能理解这种冲动。我们都经历了太多。他们说这里没地方容纳更多的人，所以我只是来这里购物，看看是否有工作要做，然后接着上路。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "You've got that right.  People like you and I are made of stronger stuff."
msgstr "你说得对。像你我这样的人浑身都是胆。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Your whole story seems a bit unlikely."
msgstr "你的整个故事听起来似乎有点不太可能。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "the place out, doing a little shopping.  Then I'll be on my way again.  Might see if they have any work that needs done first, if the price is right."
msgstr "，买点东西。然后我就又上路了。可能会看看他们是否有什么需要先完成的工作，价格是否合适。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Actually, I think I'm on the right track here, but you might have some luck finding a little something something back at the Free Merchant base.  They seemed pretty desperate."
msgstr "事实上，我想我的方向是对的，但你可能会幸运地在自由商会那里找到一些东西。他们貌似有点......歇斯底里。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Any progress on getting to the camp?"
msgstr "有消息吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Can you give me directions to that FEMA camp?  I want to go there too if it's so great."
msgstr "您能给我前往 FEMA 营地的路线吗？  如果那里这么棒的话我也想去。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Can you give me directions to where you're going too?  I love cartography."
msgstr "你能告诉我你要去哪里吗?我喜欢绘制地图。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Everything is going to be all right."
msgstr "一切都会好起来的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Good luck with that.  I'll be on my way."
msgstr "祝你好运。  我会上路的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Here, I'll mark it on your map.  I wouldn't bet they'll treat you any differently than us though.  You might try and bring something to trade, they like that."
msgstr "在这儿，我将在您的地图上标记它。不过，我敢打赌他们会以与我们不同的方式对待你。你可能会尝试带一些东西来交易，他们喜欢这样。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Hey man.  Do you have any heroin?  I'm in a bit of a bind."
msgstr "嘿，老兄。你有海洛因吗？我现在很为难。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "I can't tell if you're joking or not, please don't say such things."
msgstr "我不知道你是不是在开玩笑，请不要说这样的话。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "I don't have time for zombie bait like you."
msgstr "我没时间像你一样做僵尸诱饵。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "I haven't been to any refugee center.  Can you tell me where it is?"
msgstr "我没有去过任何难民中心。  你能告诉我它在哪里吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "I love you."
msgstr "我爱你！"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "I think you might need it even more than me.  Here you go."
msgstr "你一定比我更需要它，给你！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid "I'm a refugee, but don't get the wrong idea.  I've got big dreams of settling down after this and starting a big family.  I just need to find the right place and the right person.  Last couple of places didn't work out so well."
msgstr "我是难民，但不要误会。我有一个很大的梦想，就是在这之后安定下来，组建一个大家庭。我只需要找到合适的地方和合适的人。最后几个地方效果不太好。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:m"
msgid "I'm a refugee, but don't get the wrong idea.  I've got big dreams of settling down after this and starting a big family.  I just need to find the right place and the right person.  Last couple of places didn't work out so well."
msgstr "我是难民，但不要误会。我有一个很大的梦想，就是在这之后安定下来，组建一个大家庭。我只需要找到合适的地方和合适的人。最后几个地方效果不太好。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:n"
msgid "I'm a refugee, but don't get the wrong idea.  I've got big dreams of settling down after this and starting a big family.  I just need to find the right place and the right person.  Last couple of places didn't work out so well."
msgstr "我是难民，但不要误会。我有一个很大的梦想，就是在这之后安定下来，组建一个大家庭。我只需要找到合适的地方和合适的人。最后几个地方效果不太好。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "I'm sorry, I should be going before I do something bad again."
msgstr "对不起，我该走了，免得我再做坏事。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Looking good there.  I like your whole setup.  What's your story?"
msgstr "那里看起来不错。  我喜欢你的整个设置。  你的故事是什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Never, that heroin is for me and me alone."
msgstr "不，这海洛因是给我的，只有我一个。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Nice.  Good to see you again.  What do you want from me?"
msgstr "好的。  很高兴再次见到你。  你想从我处得到些什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "No thank you."
msgstr "不了,谢谢。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "No worries friend, good luck to you."
msgstr "别担心，朋友，祝你好运。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "No, I don't have any."
msgstr "不，我没有。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "No, I'm not really with them.  We just got stuck together in the same messed up evacuation place.  This one guy was really nice, but they wouldn't let us stay.  They got there first so they told us we needed to find our own place, but if we got anything they wanted they'd trade some of the stuff they have.  I tried to talk them into helping but they were so cold to me."
msgstr "不，我并没有真正和他们在一起。  我们只是被困在同一个混乱的疏散地点。  这个人真的很好，但他们不让我们留下来。  他们先到了那里，所以他们告诉我们需要找到自己的地方，但如果我们得到他们想要的任何东西，他们会交换他们拥有的一些东西。  我试图说服他们帮忙，但他们对我很冷淡。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Not interested.  I'd better get going."
msgstr "没意思，走了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Nothing, just saying hi."
msgstr "没什么，只是打个招呼而已。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Of course, we're all in this together.  Let me mark that on your map."
msgstr "当然，我们都在一起。  让我在你的地图上标记一下。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Of course.  How do I get there?"
msgstr "当然。我该怎么去那里？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Oh, I wasn't joking <name_b>."
msgstr "哦，我不是在开玩笑<name_b>。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Oh, uh, thanks.  I guess."
msgstr "哦，呃，谢谢。我想。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Please don't hurt us, we're just trying to get to safety."
msgstr "请不要伤害我们，我们只是想安全。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "So you're not attached right now?"
msgstr "你还没结婚吧？"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Such a disappointment…"
msgstr "好失望…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the information.  I'd better go."
msgstr "谢谢你的信息了。我最好走了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the story.  I'd better go."
msgstr "谢谢你的故事。  我最好走了。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "The hard part is getting there."
msgstr "困难的部分是到达那里。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Things must be better at the camp…"
msgstr "营地里的情况一定会更好……"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "This is the beginning of a beautiful thing.  I'm with you."
msgstr "这是美好事物的开始。  我和你在一起。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "We were at the same little evacuation hut, but it was all messed up, just used condoms and broken bottles and lipstick writing on the walls.  We found another group of refugees like us on the road, but they had all been killed, all ripped up, blood everywhere.  We took their food and made it all the way to a big refugee center, but somebody there with a gun told us there was no room, so we're going to a FEMA camp.  They should have more room and supplies.  No guarantees, but it's a chance."
msgstr "我们在同一个疏散小屋里，但一切都乱了，只是用了避孕套和破碎的瓶子，墙上写着口红。我们在路上发现了另一群和我们一样的难民，但他们都被杀了，都被撕裂了，到处都是血。我们带着他们的食物一路来到一个大型难民中心，但那里有人拿着枪告诉我们没有房间，所以我们要去FEMA（联邦紧急事务管理局）营地。他们应该有更多的空间和用品。不能保证，但这是一个机会。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "We're all in this together, looking forward to meeting you there."
msgstr "我们都在一起，期待在那里见到你。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "We're just trying to find a safe place right now.  I think there's a FEMA camp nearby that should have room for us."
msgstr "我们现在只是想找到一个安全的地方。  我认为附近有一个联邦紧急事务管理署 (FEMA) 营地，应该有足够的空间供我们使用。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Well, success I guess."
msgstr "大概是成功了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "What if I want to hurt you?  I'm so good at it and I've had so much practice."
msgstr "如果我想伤害你怎么办？  我非常擅长，而且我已经进行了很多练习。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "What's your situation here?"
msgstr "你这里的情况怎么样？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Why, where were you before?"
msgstr "为什么，你以前在哪里？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Yeah, I guess it's hard all over.  I'd better get going."
msgstr "是的，我想一切都很难结束。  我最好走了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Yes!"
msgstr "好耶!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Yes.  I'll be on my way then."
msgstr "好。那我要走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid "You again.  Any good news?  Haven't heard any in a long time."
msgstr "又是你。  有什么好消息吗？  好久没听到任何消息了"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:m"
msgid "You again.  Any good news?  Haven't heard any in a long time."
msgstr "又是你。  有什么好消息吗？  好久没听到任何消息了"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:n"
msgid "You again.  Any good news?  Haven't heard any in a long time."
msgstr "又是你。  有什么好消息吗？  好久没听到任何消息了"

#. ~ Affirmative response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "You should come with me instead."
msgstr "你应该跟我一起去。"

#. ~ Negative response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "You should definitely come with me instead."
msgstr "你绝对应该跟我一起去。"

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Random NPC, can direct you to the free merchants and nearest FEMA camp.
#. ~ Random NPC, can be recruited away.
#. ~ Random NPC, demands heroin and can accept.
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "refugee"
msgstr "难民"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ", but I'm so hungry."
msgstr "，但我好饿。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "All right!  Let's get going."
msgstr "好的！那我们走吧。"

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ All the beggars have been camping inside the evac shelter because they're
#. too weak and unskilled to make it on their own.
#. ~ This is the only beggar with some skills, sort of the leader.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
msgid "Beggar"
msgstr "乞丐"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Can I ask you something else first?"
msgstr "我能先问你点别的吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Come with me.  Maybe you're not the greatest adventurer, but it's better than living here."
msgstr "跟我来。也许你做不了最伟大的冒险家，但总比呆在这里好。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Get away from me."
msgstr "离我远点。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
msgid "Here, you can have this <topic_item>."
msgstr "给，这个 <topic_item> 归你了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Hey, here, I might have some food for you.  Let me check."
msgstr "嘿，这里，我可以给你点吃的。让我找一下。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I can keep you safe.  I'll take you there myself."
msgstr "我可以保护你的安全。我带你去。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I have a camp of my own, away from here.  Maybe they can't use your skills here, but I could."
msgstr "我在别的地方有个自己建的营地。也许他们这里用不上你，但我可以。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I have a camp of my own, away from here.  Maybe you can't scavenge, but we can use any warm bodies that can lift a tool.  You'd be safer and better fed there."
msgstr "我在别的地方有个自己建的营地。或许你不能拾荒，但任何能拿起工具的活人在我们那都能派上用处，你在那里会更安全，吃得更好。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I have a camp of my own, away from here.  You could come there.  There aren't many people left, we could use anyone regardless of skills."
msgstr "我在别的地方有个自己建的营地，你可以去那里。现在还活着的人不多了，是个人我们都要，不管能力如何。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I hope you'll reconsider eventually.  Bye."
msgstr "我希望你最终能改变主意。再见。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I might have some food for you.  Let me check."
msgstr "我可以给你点吃的。让我找一下。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I really appreciate everything you've done for me, but I don't think you get it.  I can't go out there.  I will die.  I know it's horrible camping out here, but I just can't face that nightmare again."
msgstr "我真的很感激你为我所做的一切，但我认为你还是不懂。我出不了门的。我会死的。我知道在这里呆着很糟糕，但我没法再次面对那个噩梦了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I was a high school math teacher.  It was a good job, I loved it.  Funny enough, it's not super applicable after the end of the world.  I mean, at some point people are going to need a teacher again, but right now they just want food, shelter, and clothing."
msgstr "我是高中数学老师。那是一份好工作，我很喜欢。可笑的是，在世界末日之后，这并没有什么用。我是说，很久很久之后也许人们会再次需要一个老师，但现在他们想要的只是食物，住所和衣服。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I'm sorry, I can't help you."
msgstr "对不起，我帮不了你。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
msgid "I'm sorry, I was wrong.  I can't help you."
msgstr "对不起，我错了。我帮不了你。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I'm sorry, I'm too hungry to make a big decision like that."
msgstr "对不起，我太饿了，做不了这么重大的决定。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I've got some more food, if you want it."
msgstr "如果你想要的话，我还有一些吃的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
msgid "I've talked to the others, and they're all willing to come.  So, you joining us?"
msgstr "我和其他人谈过了，他们都愿意来。你也加入我们吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Let's talk about something else then."
msgstr "那我们再谈点别的吧。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "No problem.  Bye."
msgstr "没问题。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "OK, I'll talk to them too."
msgstr "好吧，我也会和他们谈谈的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "OK.  For now let's talk about something else."
msgstr "好的，我们谈点其他事情吧。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Out there?  That's suicide!  People that go out there don't come back, people who can hold their own… unlike me.  I'd rather take my chances begging for scraps and waiting for someone in the center to die and make room for me, thanks."
msgstr "去外面？那是自杀！每个出去的人都没能回来，那些可是能自己过活的人……不像我。我宁愿在这里求口剩饭吃，等待里面的人死掉一些，为我腾出位置，谢谢。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Please, help me.  I need food."
msgstr "拜托，帮帮我。我需要食物。"

#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Hungry beggar in the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Reena Sandhu"
msgstr "丽娜·桑德"

#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Hungry beggar in the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Teacher"
msgstr "教师"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Thank you so much."
msgstr "非常感谢。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "That's a kind offer of you, but I think I'd rather take my chances here than risking it out there again.  I remember <the_cataclysm>, I'm not in any hurry to face that again."
msgstr "感谢你的好意，但是我宁愿在这里等待机会，也不想冒险离开这里了。我记得<the_cataclysm>，我不想再面对它。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "They won't let me in.  They say they're too full.  I'm allowed to camp out here as long as I keep it clean and don't make a fuss"
msgstr "他们不让我进去。他们说他们太饱了。  只要我保持干净并且不大惊小怪，我就可以在这里露营"

#. ~ Description of effect type "Full"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "This beggar in the refugee center has had something to eat recently."
msgstr "这个难民中心的乞丐最近吃了点东西。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "This is wonderful of you, I really appreciate it."
msgstr "你真是个好心人，我真的很感激。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Well… you have shown that you can survive out there, and you've been able to provide food, so I know you're thriving more than we are here.  All right, I'll tell you what.  I'm not going anywhere without my friends here, we've been through way too much together.  If you can convince Luo, Brandon, and Yusuke to come along, then I'll go."
msgstr "好吧……你证明了你可以在外面生存，还能带来食物，所以我知道你们那比我们这更兴旺发达。好吧，告诉你。我不会抛下这里的朋友去任何地方的，我们一起经历了太多。如果你能说服小罗，布兰顿和雄介一起去的话，我就跟你走。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "Well… you have shown that you can survive out there, and you've been able to provide food, so I know you're thriving more than we are here.  All right, I'll tell you what.  I'm not going anywhere without my friends here, we've been through way too much together.  If you can convince Luo, Brandon, and Yusuke to come along, then I'll go."
msgstr "好吧……你证明了你可以在外面生存，还能带来食物，所以我知道你们那比我们这更兴旺发达。好吧，告诉你。我不会抛下这里的朋友去任何地方的，我们一起经历了太多。如果你能说服小罗，布兰顿和雄介一起去的话，我就跟你走。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "Well… you have shown that you can survive out there, and you've been able to provide food, so I know you're thriving more than we are here.  All right, I'll tell you what.  I'm not going anywhere without my friends here, we've been through way too much together.  If you can convince Luo, Brandon, and Yusuke to come along, then I'll go."
msgstr "好吧……你证明了你可以在外面生存，还能带来食物，所以我知道你们那比我们这更兴旺发达。好吧，告诉你。我不会抛下这里的朋友去任何地方的，我们一起经历了太多。如果你能说服小罗，布兰顿和雄介一起去的话，我就跟你走。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Where else?  I can't fight those things out there.  I'm in terrible physical condition, don't have any useful skills, and I'm terrified of <zombies> and violence.  How am I supposed to find a safe place?"
msgstr "还有别的地方吗？我可打不过外面的那些怪物。我身体状况很差，又没有一技之长，我被外面那些<zombies>和暴行吓坏了。我该怎么找个安全的地方？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Why don't you scavenge your own food?"
msgstr "你为什么不自己出去外面找些吃的呢？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "About that shopping list of yours…"
msgstr "关于你的购物清单……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
msgid "Actually can I ask you something else?"
msgstr "我能问你点别的事吗？"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Any luck?  Bigger ones?"
msgstr "运气怎样？有大一点的吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Are you seriously wearing a dinosaur costume?"
msgstr "你真的就这么穿着恐龙套装吗？"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Brilliant!  You're a true hero.  I'll see if I can find a place to set these up now."
msgstr "太棒了！你是个真正的英雄。我看看能不能找个地方把这些装好。"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgstr "收集 10 个纸板盒"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgstr "收集 10 张大塑料膜"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
msgstr "收集 40 个小纸箱"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgstr "收集 5 个大纸板箱"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
msgstr "收集 200 单位强力胶带"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Cardboard?"
msgstr "硬纸板？"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Did you ask the masters?"
msgstr "你问过这里的主人了吗？"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Did you bring me those last few boxes?"
msgstr "你把最后几个纸板箱给我带来了吗？"

#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Schizophrenic beggar in the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Dino Dave"
msgstr "迪诺·戴夫"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Do you need something to eat?"
msgstr "你需要吃点什么吗？"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Got the little ones yet?"
msgstr "小东西们拿到了吗？"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Gotta start small right?  Little ones for keeping little things safe.  I could use 'em."
msgstr "我们得从小的开始，小纸盒，对吧？小物件需要小盒子保护。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Gotta start small right?  Little ones for keeping little things safe.  I could use 'em.  I need a bunch of 'em.  Little ones, you know?  Can you bring me like… like… forty?"
msgstr "我们得从小的开始，小纸盒，对吧？小物件需要小盒子保护。我需要一堆，小纸盒，明白吗？你能给我拿来……拿来……40个吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Have I told you about cardboard, friend?  Do you have any?"
msgstr "我跟你说过硬纸板的事吗，朋友？你有吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "How's things with you?  My cardboard collection is getting quite impressive."
msgstr "近况如何？我收集的纸箱越来越多了！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I can tell when it has stuff in it, it's got a sandy texture.  But this doesn't.  Thanks again."
msgstr "我知道当里面被下过药的时候，吃起会有点像沙子。但这个没有。再次感谢。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I didn't think so."
msgstr "我不这么认为。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I don't understand."
msgstr "我不明白。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I have it, I have it all, but I can't find a place to put it.  Will you ask the masters?  Maybe?  I've tried but they ignore me."
msgstr "我都有了，我全都有了，但我找不到地方放。你会问这里的主人们吗？可以吗？我试过了，但他们都不理我。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I have it, I have it all, but I can't find a place to put it.  Will you ask the masters?  Maybe?  I've tried but they ignore me.  I just need a place to put it all, a place I can be safe, and not make anyone upset."
msgstr "我都有了，我全都有了，但我找不到地方放。你会问这里的主人们吗？可以吗？我试过了，但他们都不理我。我只需要一个地方，一个安全的地方，一个不会让任何人生气的地方。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I really feel bad sending you on this one, it's dangerous.  Have you found anything?"
msgstr "让你去做这事我感到挺内疚的，这很危险。你找到什么了吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I think I have to get going…"
msgstr "我想我得走了……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I'll have to think on it, Dave, I've done a lot already."
msgstr "我得考虑一下，戴夫，我已经做了很多了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I'll have to think on that, Dave, I've done a lot already."
msgstr "我得考虑一下，戴夫，我已经做了很多了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I'll see you on the rooftop.  Good luck, Dave."
msgstr "我们在屋顶见。祝你好运，戴夫。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I'm building a house out of cardboard.  The sandman doesn't want me to, but I told him to go fuck himself."
msgstr "我正在用硬纸板盖房子。睡魔告诉我别这么做，但我告诉它赶紧滚。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I'm so happy now!"
msgstr "我现在太高兴了！"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "If I can set it up in here I won't need it, but they might drive me out, so I guess I need some plastic just in case.  I don't like it, the sandman can smell through plastic, but I think the cardboard is stronger."
msgstr "如果我能建在这里面的话就不需要了，但是他们随时可能把我赶走，所以我需要一些塑料薄膜以防万一。我不喜欢它，睡魔可以通过塑料闻到气味，所以我认为硬纸板更结实。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "If I can set it up in here I won't need it, but they might drive me out, so I guess I need some plastic just in case.  I don't like it, the sandman can smell through plastic, but I think the cardboard is stronger.  Please bring me some plastic sheets."
msgstr "如果我能建在这里面的话就不需要了，但是他们随时可能把我赶走，所以我需要一些塑料薄膜以防万一。我不喜欢它，睡魔可以通过塑料闻到气味，所以我认为硬纸板更结实。请给我带些塑料薄膜。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "If you don't know who he is, I definitely can't tell you.  He talks to everyone, if you didn't hear him that means you can't be trusted, except to help me out."
msgstr "如果你不知道他是谁，我也绝不告诉你。他跟每个人都说话，如果你没听到他的声音，那就说明你不可信，帮不了我。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Is there anything else I can do for you?"
msgstr "我还能为你做些什么吗？"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "It's all around us… but did you get it in a crude matter form?"
msgstr "它们环绕着我……但你确定拿到它们的时候不是原始物质形态？（注：Yoda大师梗）"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "I… I can see you wearing it.  Why are you wearing that?"
msgstr "我……我可以看到你正穿着它。你为什么穿这个？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Kind of a question's that?  Yeah man, you got cardboard, I got a whole… a whole shopping list.  Got it here."
msgstr "这是个问题吗？是啊，你有纸板箱，而我有一个完整的……完整的购物清单。就在这里。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Maybe somewhere they can't see me?  Where I can just be me?"
msgstr "也许在某个他们看不到我的地方？在那里我可以做我自己？"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Nice, this will do perfectly!"
msgstr "很好，这些特别合适！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "No!  I just got everything together.  I am not leaving, not now.  Everything's finally coming together!"
msgstr "不！我才刚刚把所有的东西收集全。我才不走，不是现在。我终于把它们全部凑齐了！"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "No!  Oh god, no, this can't be happening…"
msgstr "不！天啊，不，这不是真的……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "No, I don't."
msgstr "不，我不。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "No."
msgstr "否。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Nobody's the same, not even twins.  But I'll tell you something.  The big eye looked at me.  When it did, it heard the voices, and it blinked."
msgstr "没有人是一样的，即使是双胞胎。  但我会告诉你一些事情。  那只大眼睛看着我。  当它这样做时，它听到了声音，然后眨了眨眼。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Oh man, but we're so close!"
msgstr "哦，拜托，我们本来都要完成了！"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Oh man, thanks so much my friend.  You won't regret it."
msgstr "哦天啊，非常感谢你我的朋友。你不会后悔的。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Oh this is so great, so great!"
msgstr "哦，这太棒了，太棒了！"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Oh, that's too bad."
msgstr "哦，那太糟了。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Oh, that's too bad.  Guess they're eating it all."
msgstr "哦，那太糟了。我猜他们把它全都吃掉了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Once I saw the full moon, and it was staring right at me - only it couldn't see me, because the sandman kept it away.  Understand?"
msgstr "有一次我看到满月，它正盯着我——只是它看不到我，因为沙人挡住了它。  理解？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Shields?"
msgstr "盾牌？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Sure, Dave.  One last favor, I think I can talk to Smokes about finding you a place to go."
msgstr "当然，戴夫。最后帮你一次了，我想我可以和斯默克谈谈，给你找个能去的地方。"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to call home."
msgstr "和斯默克谈谈给戴夫找个新家的事。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Ten bigger ones now please.  The list doesn't lie.  You've done so well."
msgstr "现在请给我10个稍微大一点的，纸板盒。清单没有说谎，你做得太好了。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Ten bigger ones now please.  The list doesn't lie.  You've done so well.  I got a little more on the list, but we're more than half there."
msgstr "现在请给我10个稍微大一点的，纸板盒。清单没有说谎，你做得太好了。清单上还有几项未完成，但我们已经完成大半了。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Thank you!  I'm sorry, I thought we were done, but we can do this!"
msgstr "谢谢你！对不起，我还以为我们已经成功了，但这次一定可以能成的！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "That's OK, nobody's perfect, ha ha…"
msgstr "没关系，人无完人，哈哈……"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "The roof!  So high!  So lofty!  Come see me there, my friend.  I will not disappoint you."
msgstr "屋顶！那么高！那么高尚！记得来看看我，我的朋友。我不会让你失望的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "The roof!  So high!  So lofty!  I can hardly believe it!  This will be a nicer house than I had before everything went funny.  I can watch out, I'm happy to do that.  And it'll be nice to still have a bathroom!  Come see me there, my friend.  I will not disappoint you."
msgstr "屋顶！那么高！那么高尚！我简直不敢相信！这将是一间我拥有的更好的房子，比这一切变得如此可笑之前还要好。我可以瞭望，我很乐意这么做。而且还能用洗手间！记得来看看我，我的朋友。我不会让你失望的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "The sandman?"
msgstr "睡魔？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "There's so much of it now, and the zombies are afraid of it.  It's kept me safe so far.  The beta rays come from the center point of the zombie, so it hits the cardboard and can't penetrate.  The reflection can stop any further damage."
msgstr "现在有用不完的硬纸板了，而且丧尸们都怕它。至少到目前为止它都保护了我的安全。从丧尸体内会发射出贝塔射线，但一旦击中纸板，就无法穿透。反射射线可以避免任何进一步的伤害。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "These cowards are afraid of me.  They won't let me into their base.  I'm going to build my new house and I won't let them in."
msgstr "那些胆小鬼都怕我。他们不让我进入他们的基地。我要盖我自己的新房子，而我也不会让他们进来的。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "These ones are good, good ones.  They need something to, you know, bind them together.  Surround them, light side, dark side."
msgstr "这些很不错，好东西。还得有些东西把它们绑起来。缠绕它们，一面光明，一面黑暗。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "These ones are good, good ones.  They need something to, you know, bind them together.  Surround them, light side, dark side.  Bring me the Force!"
msgstr "这些很不错，好东西。还得有些东西把它们绑起来。缠绕它们，一面光明，一面黑暗。赋予我原力吧！"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "They keep a lot of this stuff in hardware stores and lumber yards."
msgstr "他们在五金店和木材场放了不少这玩意。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "This is the last thing I need from you.  I've been collecting the other parts myself, it's been easier with more cardboard around.  Can you bring me five more really big cardboard boxes?"
msgstr "这是我需要你做的最后一件事。我自己也一直在收集其他部件，但如果有更多的纸板箱就好了。你能再给我五个那种超级大的纸板箱吗？"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "This is the last thing I need from you.  I've been collecting the other parts myself, it's been easier with more cardboard around.  Can you bring me five more really big cardboard boxes?  Five more cardboard boxes, as big as it gets.  I have a few already stored up, that should be all I need."
msgstr "这是我需要你做的最后一件事。我自己也一直在收集其他部件，但如果有更多的纸板箱就好了。你能再给我五个那种超级大的纸板箱吗？再来五个大纸板箱，有多大要多大。我已经有一些存货了，再来五个应该就够了。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Try looking in cargo storage areas."
msgstr "可以试着去货物仓库找找。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Watch out, he's looking for it too."
msgstr "小心，他也在找。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "We're almost there, now."
msgstr "我们快完成了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "We've done it!  We've solved the list!"
msgstr "成功了！购物清单完成了！"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "We've done it, Dave!  Smokes says you can build yourself a house up on the roof if you want.  You've got to keep it nice and clean, and help out the people down here by looking out for zombies, but you can still use the washrooms and things downstairs when you need to.  What do you say?"
msgstr "我们成功了，戴夫！斯默克说，如果你愿意，你可以在屋顶上给自己盖座房子。但你得保持它的整洁，帮楼下的人们发现丧尸的踪迹，但需要时你仍然可以下楼使用洗手间和其他东西。你说呢？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Well, OK then, Dave.  One last favor, I think I can talk to Smokes about finding you a place to go."
msgstr "好吧，戴夫。最后帮你一次了，我想我可以和斯默克谈谈，给你找个能去的地方。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Well… I had it all pretty together, "
msgstr "好吧……这里一切都被我安排得很好了，"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "What are you going to do with all that cardboard now?"
msgstr "你现在要拿那些硬纸板做什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "What was that about cardboard?"
msgstr "那硬纸板是怎么回事？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "What's next on the list?"
msgstr "清单的下一项是什么？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Why are you sitting out here?"
msgstr "你为什么坐在这里？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Why cardboard?"
msgstr "为什么是硬纸板？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Why don't you leave this place?  Come with me, I could use some help out there."
msgstr "为什么不离开这里呢？跟我走吧，我那里需要你帮忙。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Would you like me to give you some cardboard?"
msgstr "你要我给你一些纸板箱吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Yeah, I'm real hungry and they put drugs in most of the food.  I can see you're not like that."
msgstr "是的，我真的很饿，但他们朝食物里下了药。我看得出来你不是那种人。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "Yeah, I'm real hungry and they put drugs in most of the food.  I can see you're not like that."
msgstr "是的，我真的很饿，但他们朝食物里下了药。我看得出来你不是那种人。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "Yeah, I'm real hungry and they put drugs in most of the food.  I can see you're not like that."
msgstr "是的，我真的很饿，但他们朝食物里下了药。我看得出来你不是那种人。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Yes!  The home stretch!"
msgstr "是的！最后的冲刺！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "You ask me what I can see, but I don't tell you what you see.  Sometimes we have shields up, to protect ourselves."
msgstr "你问我能看见什么，但我不知道你能看到些什么。有时候我们会竖起盾牌，来保护自己。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "You said you were building a house?"
msgstr "你说你在建房子？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "[Schizophrenic] I think I do.  Are we the same?"
msgstr "[精神分裂] 我想我是的。我们一样吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "and I feel bad with all the help you've given me already, but "
msgstr "你给我的那些帮助让我很过意不去，但是"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "now the masters won't let me build my sanctuary.  I know I can't build it in here, they wouldn't allow it.  They won't listen to me when I ask for a safe place.  They just want me to disappear, like the others.  Can you help me figure them out?"
msgstr "现在这里的主人不让我建造我的避难所。我知道我不能在这里建，他们不会允许的。而当我找他们要一处安全的地方时，他们也不会听我的。他们只想让我消失，就像其他人一样。你能帮我解决吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "…What were you saying before?"
msgstr "……你刚才说什么来着？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Actually yeah, I'm always hungry these days.  I don't like taking handouts, but I wouldn't say no."
msgstr "老实说，最近我一直都饿着。虽然我不喜欢被人施舍，但我也不会拒绝。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Aw damn, I was worried you'd say that.  Okay, listen: you've got yourself a deal.  I'll come to your base, but you've gotta get me hooked up with a microscope as soon as you can.  This could be the beginning of something really cool.  Oh, and it should go without saying that I'm not coming unless you can find a place for my friends here in your base.  I'm sure you anticipated that.  Talk them into going and I'm in.  It should be easy, they're a bunch of sweet hearted saps."
msgstr "啊，该死，我就担心你会这么说。好吧，听着：我们成交了。我会去你的营地，但你得尽快给我搞来一台显微镜。这将开始一项可能会很酷的研究。哦，对了，除非你能在营地里给我的朋友们也留个位置，否则我是不会去的。说服他们一起走，我才会加入你。这应该很简单，他们都是一群心地善良的笨蛋。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Do you know about the fungal zombies though?"
msgstr "你知道真菌丧尸吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Does that mean you were part of that back room evacuation I heard about?"
msgstr "那你是不是也被卷入了我所听说的后院的疏散事件里了？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Don't bother with these assholes."
msgstr "别理那些混蛋们。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Don't get me wrong, I hate this place and this situation, and especially the selfish racist fucks that landed me here… but these other losers that landed out here with me?  I like them.  We might be miserable, but we're miserable together."
msgstr "别误会我的意思，我讨厌这个地方和我现在的处境，尤其讨厌那些把我挡在外面的自私的种族主义者……但那些同我一样被丢在外面的卢瑟们呢？我喜欢他们。我们也许过的很惨，但起码是一起惨。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Encroaching alien mushrooms, fungal towers, tough mycelium invading ground and trees, zombies taken over by aggressive mold… Yeah.  It's ugly stuff."
msgstr "异界入侵的蘑菇，真菌塔，坚硬的菌丝侵入地面和树木，丧尸被侵略性的真菌接管……是的。可怕的玩意。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Even without them helping, it's the safest place to squat.  As long as we keep it clean up here and don't cause sanitation problems, they don't mind us sitting around the entryway.  So kind and generous of them, to let us sit here and slowly starve."
msgstr "即使他们不帮我，这里也是我所能呆的最安全的地方。只要我们在保持这里的干净整洁，不引发卫生问题，他们就不会介意我们坐在门口。他们是如此的仁慈和慷慨，让我们坐在这里慢慢地饿死。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Glad you like it.  If I think of something you can do in return, I'll let you know."
msgstr "很高兴你喜欢它。如果我想到什么你能帮忙的事，我会让你知道的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Great!  I'll go see what I can do about that."
msgstr "太好了！我会看看能做些什么。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Heh.  Yeah, that was a great use of my time.  As you can see it really helped my employment prospects.  Yeah, I have a PhD in mycology.  Did my dissertation on signaling pathways in hyphae formation, and a postdoc in plant-fungus communication in rhizomes.  Then I got the job at the bookstore because there wasn't a ton of work for a doctor of mycology, although I'd had a few nibbles before things really got crazy.  Now, people are just breaking down my door to get my sweet sweet knowledge of mold to help them fight the incoming zombie threat."
msgstr "哈哈。是啊，那可花了我不少功夫。如你所见，那头衔真的拓展了我的就业前景，笑。是的，我获得了真菌学博士学位。我的学位论文是关于菌丝形成中的信号通路，博士后研究植株根茎内植物-真菌交互行为。后来我只能在书店打零工，因为真菌学博士能干的工作实在不多，而后直到一切变得疯狂之前我做过的最接近专业的事也就是吃几口蘑菇。现在，大家都疯狂的砸着我家的门，想获得我脑中珍贵的真菌知识，来帮助他们对抗即将到来的丧尸威胁，笑。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "I don't care if you're Chinese.  You can travel with me if you want."
msgstr "我不在乎你是不是中国人。如果你愿意，你可以和我一起旅行。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "I dunno, scientific interest?  If you don't bring me anything, no worries.  I'm positively swimming in entertainment here, as you can see."
msgstr "我不知道，科学探索的精神？即便你不帮我带来，也不必担心。如你所见，我在这里的乐子可不少呢。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "I found a sample of alien fungus for you."
msgstr "我给你带来了一个异界真菌的样本。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "I have a camp of my own, away from here.  No paperwork required.  Want to come?"
msgstr "我在别的地方有个自己建的营地。什么文件都不需要。想来吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "I mean, racism could definitely be a part of it… but you are visibly in poor shape.  They need strong survivor material."
msgstr "我是说，肯定有一部分是种族主义……但你的体型显然不符合要求。他们需要强壮有力的那类幸存者。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "I might have some food for you.  Are you hungry?"
msgstr "我可以给你点吃的。你饿了吗？"

#. ~ Name of effect type id "insulted_luo"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Insulted"
msgstr "被侮辱"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "It just so happens I have a chunk of fungal matter on me right now."
msgstr "真巧，我手头正好有一大块那种真菌。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "It may not be much, but we've got a little community.  We can't live like this forever, but we're safer than out there, and we look out for each other.  One way or another we'll shake things out to something better."
msgstr "可能人不多，但我们是个小社区。我们不能永远这样生活，但我们在这里比在外面更安全，而且我们还互相照顾。不管怎样，我们都慢慢找到一条出路的。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "It'd be dangerous.  What kind of benefit is there from taking a risk like that?"
msgstr "这会非常危险，我冒这个险有什么好处？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "It'd be temporary.  I have a base set up.  There are only a few of us survivors left, we need to work together"
msgstr "那只是暂时的。我已经建了间营地。现在只有我们少数几个幸存者了，我们需要一起干。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Just wanted to get square.  I'd better get going."
msgstr "我只是过来和解的。我该走了。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Like I said, sorry, it's just not happening.  It's not that I don't trust you, it's just that I don't really trust you."
msgstr "我说过了，对不起，不可能。并不是我不信任你，而是我*完全*不信任你。"

#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Angry beggar in the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Luo Meizhen"
msgstr "罗美珍"

#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Angry beggar in the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Mycologist"
msgstr "真菌学"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "No problem.  See you."
msgstr "没问题。回头见。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "No, no I don't, and I'd appreciate you not leaving me hanging on that.  There are fungal zombies?"
msgstr "不，不，我不知道，不过我想你不会和我卖关子的。外面有真菌丧尸吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Oh yeah, that was a hell of a shitstorm.  We were waiting back there for 'processing' for hours and hours, with the sick and wounded.  One guy died, we all thought he was sleeping until he got back up.  That started a panic, gunshots in a closed area, that kind of stuff.  In just a few minutes, a bunch more people were dead.  Then the assholes called it an 'outbreak' and tried to barricade us in… took us way too long to convince the panicking guards that we were alive and needed to get out.  I'll give the one guy credit, Sean: when he found out they'd locked living people in with zombies, he came in himself, as some of the newly dead were starting to get back up, and he held them off for us to escape.  That… that was probably the only actual good thing I've seen since before the end of the world: he owned his error and he put himself in harm's way to make up for it.  Massive respect to that guy.  So, of course, he's a zombie now.  Fuck, thanks for reminding me of all that sunny fun."
msgstr "可不是吗，那真是一场灾难。我们在那里等了好几个小时的\"处理\"，病人和伤员都挤在一起。某个人死了，我们还都以为他在睡觉，直到他重新复活了。这引起了恐慌，有人在狭小的空间里开枪，诸如此类的事。仅仅过了几分钟，就死了更多的人。然后这些混蛋称之为\"丧尸爆发\"并试图把我们封死在里面……我们花了很长时间才说服那些吓坏了的守卫，我们还活着，需要出去。还有肖恩：当他发现他们试图把活人和丧尸关在一起的时候，是他站了出来，当那些刚死的人重新复活站起来时，是他挡住了它们帮我们逃跑。那……可能是我自世界末日发生以来看到的唯一真正的好事：他承认自己的错误，并用最终牺牲自己去弥补。我非常敬重他。哦，当然，他现在已经是丧尸了。干，谢谢你让我又回想起那些大好事。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Oh, come on.  I'm not a random stranger anymore, I brought you that crazy mushroom didn't I?"
msgstr "哦，拜托。我可不算是陌生人了，我给你带来了那种疯狂的蘑菇，不是吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Oh, same old story at first.  I got evacuated on to the local concentration center, then picked up on a repurposed school bus and dragged out here.  Then the chick processing me to get in saw my face and Chinese name and conveniently 'lost' my paperwork.  I was sent out here to wait for further processing, while I watched busloads of people get processed and taken in.  By the time they 'found' it, the place was full up, wouldn't ya know it.  Now I'm stuck out here and they won't consider letting me in."
msgstr "哦，一开始还是同样的老故事。  我被疏散到当地的集中中心，然后被一辆改装的校车接走并拖到了这里。  然后那个让我进去的小妞看到了我的脸和中文名字，很方便地“丢失”了我的文件。  我被派到这里等待进一步处理，同时我看着一车车的人被处理并被带走。当他们“找到”它时，这个地方已经挤满了人，你难道不知道吗？  现在我被困在这里，他们不会考虑让我进去。"

#. ~ Description of effect type "Insulted"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Oh, you went there."
msgstr "哦，你去过那里了啊。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Okay, yeah, that's a bit of a problem.  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "OK，是的，那是个问题，你刚刚说什么？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Okay, you've got my attention.  Listen, do you think you could bring me some kind of sample of these things?"
msgstr "好吧，你这话到让我感兴趣了。听着，你能给我带些样品来吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Ok… see ya."
msgstr "好吧……回头见。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "Oooooh.  Oh.  You did not just fucking go there.  Let's leave the fatties to die, hey?  Wanna know how easy it is to find fucking *thyroid medication* after the apocalypse, asshat?  Besides, there are more skills than heavy lifting needed now… no, you know what?  Screw it.  You're not worth my time."
msgstr "哦哦。哦。可你他妈的也没能进去里面啊。就把我们这些胖子留在外面等死呢，啊？你知道在大灾变之后获得那些该死的*甲状腺激素药*有多难吗，混蛋？除此之外，你知道现在除了干重活的苦力还急需有其他技能的人吗……算了，听好，你去死吧。你不值得我浪费时间。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
