msgid "I was just a laborer till they could find me something a bit more permanent, but being constantly sick has prevented me from doing much of anything."
msgstr "在他们给我找份更长久的差事之前，我现在一直只能当个苦力。但问题是我的病一直好不了，让我很多事都做不顺当。"

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Flavor
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_sickly_laborer.json
msgid "Laborer"
msgstr "劳工"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_sickly_laborer.json
msgid "Please leave me alone…"
msgstr "请让我一个人静静……"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_sickly_laborer.json
msgid "That's sad."
msgstr "那可真糟糕。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_sickly_laborer.json
msgid "Uhm."
msgstr "额。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_sickly_laborer.json
msgid "What could I possibly have that could help?"
msgstr "光有哪玩意有什么能帮到我的？"

#. ~ Player message in an effect
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgid "<npc_name> drops the logs off in the garage…"
msgstr "<npc_name> 把原木丢在车库里……"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid "I'm one of the migrants that got diverted to this outpost when I arrived at the refugee center.  They said I was big enough to swing an axe, so my profession became lumberjack… didn't have any say in it.  If I want to eat, then I'll be cutting wood from now till kingdom come."
msgstr "我一到难民营就被分派来这个哨站。他们说我的块头非常适合挥斧头，所以我就变成了个伐木工……我连说不的机会都没。如果我不想挨饿，我就得一直砍木头砍到下辈子。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgctxt "npc:m"
msgid "I'm one of the migrants that got diverted to this outpost when I arrived at the refugee center.  They said I was big enough to swing an axe, so my profession became lumberjack… didn't have any say in it.  If I want to eat, then I'll be cutting wood from now till kingdom come."
msgstr "我一到难民营就被分派来这个哨站。他们说我的块头非常适合挥斧头，所以我就变成了个伐木工……我连说不的机会都没。如果我不想挨饿，我就得一直砍木头砍到下辈子。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgctxt "npc:n"
msgid "I'm one of the migrants that got diverted to this outpost when I arrived at the refugee center.  They said I was big enough to swing an axe, so my profession became lumberjack… didn't have any say in it.  If I want to eat, then I'll be cutting wood from now till kingdom come."
msgstr "我一到难民营就被分派来这个哨站。他们说我的块头非常适合挥斧头，所以我就变成了个伐木工……我连说不的机会都没。如果我不想挨饿，我就得一直砍木头砍到下辈子。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgid "The rate is a bit steep, but I still have my quotas that I need to fulfill.  The logs will be dropped off in the garage at the entrance to the camp.  I'll need a bit of time before I can deliver another load."
msgstr "开价可能是高了点儿，但要知道，我脑袋上也有指标要完成呢！我会把原木放在营地门口的车库里。每次完工之前我都需要些时间，别太急。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgid "You need something?"
msgstr "有何需求？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgid "[4800 merch, 7d] 100 logs"
msgstr "[12000$，7天]100 原木"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
msgid "[800 merch, 1d] 10 logs"
msgstr "[2000$，1天]10 原木"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
msgid "Bringing in logs is one of the few tasks we can give to the unskilled, so I'd be hurting them if I outsourced it.  Ask around though, I'm sure most people could use a hand."
msgstr "我不想让新手受伤，所以让你们带些原木回来就是我为数不多的选择之一。不过你们可以在附近问问，我相信很多人需要帮忙的。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
msgid "Don't have much time to talk."
msgstr "我可没多少时间聊天。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
msgid "I turn the logs that laborers bring in into lumber to expand the outpost.  Maintaining the saw is a chore, but breaks the monotony."
msgstr "我会把伐木工人们砍下来放在这里的原木加工成木材，来作为前哨站扩建的材料。保养木锯是个苦差事，但算是最不无聊的工作了，因为我可以一个锯齿一个锯齿地数到天黑。"

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Flavor
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
msgid "Woodworker"
msgstr "木工师"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "*shrugs.  \"We got our hands on a few boxes of test strips so that's good.  Being stressed isn't good for conception and I've been pretty fuckin' stressed for a while.  I like our chances a lot better now, that's for sure.  And, well, we've got our own private space at least.\"  She smirks and then blushes slightly, hiding it by fiddling with her baking project."
msgstr "*耸耸肩。  “我们拿到了几盒试纸，这很好。压力对受孕不利，我已经压力很大了一段时间了。我现在更喜欢我们的机会，这是肯定的。而且，好吧，我们至少有自己的私人空间。”  她傻笑着，然后微微脸红，通过摆弄她的烘焙项目来掩盖它。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "*sighs and nods.  \"Making do with what I've got, but yeah.  I can only crank out a couple loaves a day, and can't do anything fun.  Pablo has been talking about setting me up a separate kitchen to really get going, but we've got so much critical work to do, and fresh bread is a luxury, even if it's great for morale.\""
msgstr "*叹息并点头。  “用我现有的东西凑合着，但是，是的。我每天只能烤出几个面包，不能做任何有趣的事情。巴勃罗一直在谈论给我设立一个单独的厨房来真正开始工作，但我们有很多重要的工作要做，新鲜的面包是一种奢侈，即使它对士气很有帮助。”"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "*stands in the middle of a cramped kitchen, covered in flour.  The scene looks reminiscent of easier times, but the illusion is broken as he apron shifts to reveal a heavy machete and holstered pistol on  her belt.  She looks up as you approach, then beams in recognition.  \"Welcome to Dana's Bakery, stranger!\"  She laughs brightly.  \"Glad you made out this way.  What can I do for you?\""
msgstr "*站在狭窄的厨房中央，上面覆盖着面粉。  这一幕看起来让人想起更轻松的时光，但当他的围裙移动，露出她腰带上的一把重型砍刀和手枪时，这种幻觉被打破了。  当你走近时，她抬起头来，然后露出认可的笑容。  “欢迎来到达纳面包店，陌生人！”  她笑得很灿烂。  “很高兴你能做到这一点。我能为你做点什么吗？”"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "*stands in the middle of a cramped kitchen, covered in flour.  The scene looks reminiscent of easier times, but the illusion is broken as he apron shifts to reveal a heavy machete and holstered pistol on  her belt.  She looks up as you approach, then beams in recognition.  \"Welcome to Dana's Bakery, stranger!\"  She laughs brightly.  \"Glad you made out this way.  What can I do for you?\""
msgstr "*站在狭窄的厨房中央，上面覆盖着面粉。  这一幕看起来让人想起更轻松的时光，但当他的围裙移动，露出她腰带上的一把重型砍刀和手枪时，这种幻觉被打破了。  当你走近时，她抬起头来，然后露出认可的笑容。  “欢迎来到达纳面包店，陌生人！”  她笑得很灿烂。  “很高兴你能做到这一点。我能为你做点什么吗？”"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "*stands in the middle of a cramped kitchen, covered in flour.  The scene looks reminiscent of easier times, but the illusion is broken as he apron shifts to reveal a heavy machete and holstered pistol on  her belt.  She looks up as you approach, then beams in recognition.  \"Welcome to Dana's Bakery, stranger!\"  She laughs brightly.  \"Glad you made out this way.  What can I do for you?\""
msgstr "*站在狭窄的厨房中央，上面覆盖着面粉。  这一幕看起来让人想起更轻松的时光，但当他的围裙移动，露出她腰带上的一把重型砍刀和手枪时，这种幻觉被打破了。  当你走近时，她抬起头来，然后露出认可的笑容。  “欢迎来到达纳面包店，陌生人！”  她笑得很灿烂。  “很高兴你能做到这一点。我能为你做点什么吗？”"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "*turns serious.  \"We went inside the dealership to see if they were there.  Owner was still in there.  I… I think he took his own life, maybe figured destroying the brain would keep him from reviving.  It… it didn't.  The shotgun took out enough though, he couldn't, uh, he couldn't really see.  Just this miserable, half-faced… we put him down.  I think we did him a favor, if there was any of him left in there.  Didn't feel wrong going through his pockets.  Gross, but not wrong.\"  She blows out a stream of air, sending a small cloud of flour rising in the air, then shrugs."
msgstr "*变得严肃。  “我们走进经销店看看他们是否在那儿。车主还在里面。我……我想他自杀了，也许认为摧毁大脑会让他无法复活。但……事实并非如此。尽管猎枪已经足够了，他看不到，呃，他真的看不到。就是这么悲惨，半张脸……我们把他放下了。我想我们帮了他一个忙，如果还有他留在那儿的话。通过他的尸体并没有感觉有什么不对。很恶心，但并没有错。”  她吹出一股气流，让一小团面粉在空中升起，然后耸耸肩。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "Any luck with the pregnancy?"
msgstr "怀孕有运气吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "Got any bread for sale?"
msgstr "有面包卖吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "Ha, this thing!\"  She dusts the flour off her hands and tucks a loose lock of hair back behind her ear.  \"You remember, we signed on as caravan hands to get us out here.  Well, we had a bunch of stops along the way first.  We were headed to a little group of survivors that snagged themselves a huge stock of dry food somehow, and passed this trailer sales yard smack dab in the middle of nowhere, nobody to be seen for miles.  Pablo managed to sweet talk the group into taking a rest stop there.  We searched the yard, and a lot of the stuff wasn't suitable, but this baby was ready to go.  Long story short, we got the keys to that vintage truck outside, hitched this thing up, and upgraded our caravan.\""
msgstr "哈，这个东西！”她掸去手上的面粉，把一绺松散的头发别到耳后。“你记得，我们签约成为商队帮手，让我们离开这里。  好吧，我们首先沿途停了很多站。  我们正前往一小群幸存者，他们以某种方式为自己准备了大量干粮，并经过了这个位于偏僻地方的拖车销售场，几英里内都看不到任何人。  巴勃罗设法甜言蜜语地说服大家在那里休息。  我们搜遍了院子，很多东西都不合适，但这个宝贝已经准备好了。  长话短说，我们拿到了外面那辆老式卡车的钥匙，把它挂起来，并升级了我们的大篷车。”"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "Hello, Dana!  What's with the trailer?"
msgstr "你好，达纳！  拖车怎么了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Hey, Pablo!  Dana said you had some plans to build a bakery?"
msgstr "嘿，巴勃罗！  达纳说你有计划开一家面包店？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "Hi Dana, how are things here?"
msgstr "嗨，达纳，这里怎么样？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "How did you get the keys to the truck?"
msgstr "你是怎么拿到卡车钥匙的？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "I'd better go.  See you later."
msgstr "我最好走了。  稍后见。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "It's all propane!\"  She grins.  \"The oven, especially.  We don't need electric, which means we don't need to run the gennie and attract attention.\""
msgstr "都是丙烷！”她笑着说。“尤其是烤箱。  我们不需要电力，这意味着我们不需要运行精灵并吸引注意力。”"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "Nice to see you Dana, I'm just checking in."
msgstr "很高兴见到你，达纳，我只是来看看。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "Not bad.  Much better than before.  Pablo and I have privacy, and the folks here actually appreciate my bread instead of paying me a pittance for it and then taking it to the basement without so much as a 'thanks'."
msgstr "不错。  比以前好多了。  巴勃罗和我有隐私，这里的人们实际上很欣赏我的面包，而不是付给我微薄的钱，然后把它带到地下室，连一声“谢谢”都没有。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "Seems like a tiny kitchen for a bakery."
msgstr "看起来就像面包店的小厨房。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "What made this trailer so good?"
msgstr "是什么让这部预告片如此出色？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "What's with the trailer?"
msgstr "拖车怎么了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "Won't you run out of propane?"
msgstr "丙烷不会用完吗？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "You bet we will.  We've been collecting tanks and have enough for a while, but I'm burning through it faster than the scavengers can bring in more.  Pablo is working out some plans with the others to get me a real wood fired kitchen soon, and that'll also boost my capacity.  Maybe he could give you some scavenging work if you ask."
msgstr "你打赌我们会的。  我们一直在收集坦克，已经够用一段时间了，但我烧毁它的速度比拾荒者带来更多的速度还要快。  巴勃罗正在与其他人制定一些计划，尽快为我提供一个真正的燃木厨房，这也将提高我的能力。  如果你要求的话，也许他可以给你一些拾荒的工作。"

#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Dana is a young woman who survived with her husband, but she was pregnant
#. and lost the baby.  This class def is for after she moves to Tacoma.
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
msgid "baker"
msgstr "贝克"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "*looks up at you from a ledger, takes a moment to place you, then smiles broadly.  \"Great to see you, my friend.  To what do I owe the pleasure?\""
msgstr "*从账本上抬头看着你，花了一点时间给你定位，然后露出灿烂的笑容。  “很高兴见到你，我的朋友。我有什么荣幸呢？”"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Any time!  But I'd better go."
msgstr "任何时间！  但我最好还是走吧。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pass a message to Jenny Forcette."
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Ask Jenny Forcette if she can help Pablo Nunez with his mill designs."
msgstr "询问 Jenny Fortte 是否可以帮助 Pablo Nunez 进行工厂设计。"

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Pablo is a young professional who survived with his wife, but she was
#. pregnant and lost the baby.
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Bookkeeper"
msgstr "会计"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Can't complain,\" he stretches his neck and pops his shoulder.  \"No, really, I can't.  The work is hard, but people here really want to *do* something, not just hide inside and hope someone saves us.  I've been helping doing general labor a bit, but also working out an inventory system for our supplies.  It's already helped us get a few important bits in earlier than we'd have noticed otherwise.  Post-apocalyptic accounting, ha!  Who'd have thought?\""
msgstr "不能抱怨，”他伸长脖子，挺起肩膀。“不，真的，我不能。  工作很辛苦，但这里的人们真的想“做”点什么，而不仅仅是躲在里面希望有人来拯救我们。  我一直在帮忙做一些一般性的工作，同时也为我们的物资制定了库存系统。  它已经帮助我们比我们原本注意到的更早地获得了一些重要的信息。  后世界末日会计，哈！  谁想到呢？”"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Dana said you had some plans to build a bakery?"
msgstr "达纳说你有计划开一家面包店？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Do you know anything about building a 'culinary experience'?"
msgstr "您知道如何打造“烹饪体验”吗？"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get Pablo some fire bricks."
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Find some fire bricks to help Pablo build an oven."
msgstr "找到一些耐火砖来帮助巴勃罗建造烤箱。"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Get Pablo some fire bricks."
msgstr "给巴勃罗一些耐火砖。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Hello, Pablo!  What's with the trailer?"
msgstr "你好，巴勃罗！  拖车怎么了？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Hey, Pablo!  I heard you might be willing to trade for propane?"
msgstr "嘿，巴勃罗！  我听说你可能愿意用丙烷进行交易？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Hi, Pablo!  How are things going here?"
msgstr "嗨，巴勃罗！  这里进展如何？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "I can pass a note to Jenny about helping with the mill designs, if you want."
msgstr "如果您愿意，我可以向珍妮传递一张关于帮助工厂设计的信息。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "I don't mind keeping my eye out for some firebricks for you."
msgstr "我不介意为你留意一些耐火砖。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "I heard you might be willing to trade for propane?"
msgstr "我听说你可能愿意用丙烷进行交易？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "I'm being a bit tongue-in-cheek there.  Really I want some big wood fired ovens, tools for milling grain, tinning and canning equipment, stuff like that.  We'll make flour, jam, pickles, bread, maybe some sauerkraut and things.  All the old school ways of preserving food, from before fridges were commonplace."
msgstr "我在那里有点开玩笑。  我真的想要一些大型燃木烤箱、碾磨谷物的工具、装罐和罐头设备，诸如此类的东西。  我们会做面粉、果酱、泡菜、面包，也许还有一些酸菜之类的。  在冰箱普及之前，所有保存食物的老式方法都是如此。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "If you want the honest truth, only a bit.  It's not much like filing income tax.  Still, I know my way around a spreadsheet and I don't mind staring at numbers all day.  I think people were dubious at first, but now that it's starting to show real value they're coming around.\""
msgstr "如果你想要诚实的事实，只需要一点点。  这与提交所得税不太一样。  尽管如此，我还是熟悉电子表格，并且不介意整天盯着数字。  我认为人们一开始持怀疑态度，但现在它开始显示出真正的价值，他们开始接受了。”"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "I… I honestly don't know why I didn't think of that.  I could even have asked the supply caravans to do it.  If it comes down to it though, I trust you more than them.  Would you mind?"
msgstr "我……老实说，我不知道为什么我没有想到这一点。  我什至可以要求补给车队来做这件事。  如果归根结底，我比他们更信任你。  你会介意的？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Just popping in to say hi.  Talk to you later!"
msgstr "只是过来打个招呼。  我们回聊！"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Keeping inventory is similar to accounting?  Really?"
msgstr "存货和会计类似吗？  真的吗？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "No problem.  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "没问题。  你之前说什么？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Not where you might think.\"  He sets aside his ledger and pulls out a page of bullet-point notes written in neat block letters.  \"Everyone is on board with the idea and the amount of actual building to get it online is small enough that the carpenters are willing to help out, so I don't need any assistance with design.  For the really short term I basically just need materials.  I've been collecting spare wood, but to get a good wood-fired oven I need to secure a source of firebrick.  In the longer run, Dana knows the principles of milling, but I need a resource book if I want to set up a functioning mill, first a muscle-powered one and then a windmill for long term.  I wish I'd thought of asking Jenny.  She's a mechanical engineer, but she would probably know how to get me started at least.  I'm also still looking into how to make a good vermin-proof cellar.  Longer term, I will need to work my way around our reliance on sugar, salt, and vinegar from before the cataclysm, but our stocks of those will hold out for months while I sort things out."
msgstr "不是你想象的那样。”他把账本放在一边，拿出一页用工整的大写字母写的要点笔记。“每个人都同意这个想法，而且将其放到网上的实际建筑量足够小，木匠们愿意帮忙，所以我不需要任何设计方面的帮助。  从短期来看，我基本上只需要材料。  我一直在收集备用木材，但为了获得一个好的燃木烤箱，我需要获得耐火砖的来源。  从长远来看，达纳知道铣削的原理，但如果我想建立一个正常运转的磨坊，我需要一本资源书，首先是一个肌肉驱动的磨坊，然后是长期的风车。  我希望我能想到去问珍妮。  她是一名机械工程师，但她可能至少知道如何让我开始。  我还在研究如何制作一个好的防虫地窖。  从长远来看，我需要解决我们在灾难发生之前对糖、盐和醋的依赖，但在我解决问题的过程中，我们的库存将维持数月之久。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Oh, Dana tells that story better than me.  Basically we found it at an old trailer park and she liked the bakery, so we figured out a way to get it back here.  We definitely earned some cred for coming with our own shelter."
msgstr "哦，达纳比我讲这个故事更好。  基本上我们是在一个旧拖车公园找到它的，她喜欢这家面包店，所以我们想出了一个办法把它带回这里。  我们确实因为拥有自己的庇护所而赢得了一些信誉。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Oh… oh, ok!  It's a good thing you showed me this, my basic guesses missed some important points.  Thanks, this will be helpful for a lot more than just the bakery."
msgstr "哦……哦，好吧！  很高兴你向我展示了这一点，我的基本猜测遗漏了一些重要的点。  谢谢，这不仅仅对面包店有帮助。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Okay, but do you know anything about that?"
msgstr "好吧，但是你知道这件事吗？"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
msgid "Pass a message to Jenny Forcette."
msgstr "将消息传递给珍妮·福赛特。"

