#~ msgid "An iconic 9x19mm pistol, the M9 was the standard issue sidearm of the US armed forces from 1985 until only recently.  It was formerly popular amongst law enforcement before the advent of commercially available polymer-framed handguns and the FBI's adoption of .40 S&W."
