#~ msgid "An incredibly rare German automatic firearm developed by Hugo Schmeisser whilst working under Bergmann Waffenfabrik during 1918; the MP 18 holds the reputation of being the world's first proper and practical submachine gun.  Chambered for 9x19mm and designed for use in close quarters trench-based combat by assault troops, a role in which it excelled, the weapon was outlawed from military use by the Versailles treaty and was relegated to police and counterinsurgency use in the interwar period.  More than likely entering the US as a personal holdover from the Great War, this century-old grandfather to most classic SMGs just might be better off coming out of retirement now that the world's entered the true greatest war."
#~ msgstr "1918 年，Hugo Schmeisser 在 Bergmann Waffenfabrik 手下工作时开发了一把极为罕见的德国自动枪械； MP 18 被誉为世界上第一支真正实用的冲锋枪。  该武器的口径为 9x19 毫米，设计用于突击部队在近距离战壕作战中使用，它在这方面表现出色，但《凡尔赛条约》禁止该武器用于军事用途，并在两次世界大战期间被降级为警察和反叛乱用途。  这位大多数经典冲锋枪的百年老祖很可能是作为第一次世界大战的个人遗留物进入美国的，既然世界已经进入了真正的最伟大的战争，那么退休后可能会更好。"

