#~ msgid "The M17 is an army issued semi-automatic, short recoil operated pistol derived from the SIG Sauer P320."
#~ msgstr "M17的军用版本，一种半自动的短反冲手枪，原型是西格&绍尔P230手枪。"

#~ msgid "The M18 is a compact, semi-automatic, short recoil operated pistol derived from the SIG Sauer P320 Carry, used by US Armed Forces.  Practically the same as its big brother, the M17, in every respect, the M18 features a moderately shorter slide and barrel which terminates at the end of the frame rather than extending partway beyond it like the M17."
#~ msgstr "M18 是一种半自动的短反冲紧凑型手枪，原型是美国军队装备的西格&绍尔 P320 手枪。在各个方面的性能都与它的老大哥M17手枪几乎一模一样，M18手枪有着相对较短的滑套和枪管，末端与枪身末端齐平，而不是像M17手枪一样延伸到枪身之外。"

#~ msgid "The M231 PFW is an adaptation of the M16 assault rifle, designed to be used in the firing ports of the M2 Bradley Infantry Fighting Vehicle.  It does not have a buttstock or front sight post, and the smooth front hand guard does nothing to protect you from the potentially scorching hot barrel collar, making it slightly less than ergonomic.  You could screw it into a firing port if you were so inclined.  The fire selector says only 'SAFE' and 'AUTO'.  You can't help but wonder which one is preferable."
#~ msgstr "M231 PFW 步枪是 M16 步枪的改型，设计用 M2/M3 布莱德雷步兵战车上的射孔。它没有枪托或前瞄具，光滑的前握把根本无法保护你免受灼热枪管的烫伤，这使得它有点不符合人体工程学。如果你想的话，你可以把它拧入装甲车的射孔上。快慢机只能在保险和全自动之间选择，你不禁想说设计这个快慢机还有什么鸟用。"

#~ msgid "The Mossberg 500 is a popular series of pump-action shotguns, often acquired for military use.  It is noted for its high durability and low recoil.  This one is fitted with a 28 inch barrel with sight rib."
#~ msgstr "莫斯伯格 500 霰弹枪是广受欢迎的泵动式霰弹枪系列，通常由军方使用。它以其高耐久度和低后坐力而十分闻名。这款型号采用 28 英寸(约71厘米)枪管以及肋条式瞄具。"

#~ msgid "The Northeastern coyote, a widespread canine pack hunter.  More timid than a wolf, it is an opportunistic feeder and prefers to hunt smaller and weaker prey, but is typically shy around humans."
#~ msgstr "东北郊狼，一种分布广泛的犬科群居猎手。比狼要胆小，是狡猾而爱投机的捕猎者，喜欢捕猎较小较弱的猎物，但在面对人类时一般会胆怯。"

#~ msgid "The SG 556 is a civilian model of the Swiss SIG SG 550 series, manufactured in New Hampshire.  It lacks any automatic fire capability and has a 16 inch barrel, but still retains a folding stock, with the feature of feeding from STANAG magazines instead of the SG 550 series magazines."
#~ msgstr "SG 556 是瑞士 SIG SG 550 系列的民用型号，在新罕布什尔州制造。  它没有任何自动射击能力，有一个16英寸的枪管，但仍然保留了折叠枪托，具有从STANAG弹匣供弹而不是SG 550系列弹匣的特点。"

#~ msgid "The Saiga-12 is a semi-automatic shotgun designed on the same Kalashnikov pattern as the AK-47 rifle.  It reloads with a magazine, rather than one shell at a time like most shotguns.  It is one of the last designs of Mikhail Kalashnikov, and was popular in open division shotgun competitions prior to its ban from import via executive order."
#~ msgstr "Saiga-12 霰弹枪是一把采用了与 AK-47 步枪相同的卡拉什尼科夫布局的半自动霰弹枪。与其他霰弹枪不同，它用弹匣供弹。这是米哈伊尔·卡拉什尼科夫的生前最后设计之一，在被政府行政命令禁止进口之前，它在公开类分区的霰弹枪竞赛中很受欢迎。"

#~ msgid "The Song holds immeasurable power.  A grand symphony could revert the Cataclysm - or accelerate it to a time beyond all.  But with the world looking as is, both options are preferable."
#~ msgstr "歌中有着不可估量的力量。一部宏大的交响乐可以逆转大灾变，或者把它加速到一个超越一切的时代。但鉴于世界的现状，这两种结果都可以接受。"

#~ msgid "The big item I need is an anvil, once I have that I can get a lot of repairs done."
#~ msgstr "我眼下最缺的大家伙是个铁砧，只要有这个我就可以修一大堆东西了。"

#, c-format
#~ msgid "The bite wound on my %s looks bad."
#~ msgstr "我 %s 的咬伤看上去很糟糕。"

#~ msgid "The blackened veins of the creature seem strangely rigid, and you see faint crackles of electricity course across them."
#~ msgstr "这个生物的黑色血管看起来异常僵硬，微弱的电流在其中噼啪作响。 "

#, c-format
#~ msgid "The bleeding of %s stopped"
#~ msgstr "%s的出血已经停止"

#~ msgid "The boss wants your accounting papers, I need them."
#~ msgstr "老板想要你的会计凭证，我需要它们。"

#~ msgid "The broken limb has mended."
#~ msgstr "折断的肢体已被治疗好。"

#~ msgid "The characters on the screen display an obscene joke.  Strange humor."
#~ msgstr "显示屏上的人物展示了一个黄色段子。奇怪的幽默。"

#~ msgid "The creature's heart seems to still be beating, but rather than pumping blood, it strangely reminds you of some sort of biological dynamo."
#~ msgstr "这种生物的心脏似乎仍在跳动，但它不是在泵血，而是奇怪地让你想起某种生物发电机。"

#~ msgid "The default monster hunting experience."
#~ msgstr "默认的怪物难度及物品生成几率。"

#~ msgid "The default: NPCs are rare, but as expected in this ruined world."
#~ msgstr "默认设置：NPC很少见，但正如在这个被摧毁的世界中所预期的那样。"

#~ msgid "The first gun produced by O.F. Mossberg & Sons, the Brownie is a small pocket pistol marketed to trappers during the early 20th century.  Its four barrels can accept .22 Short and .22 LR cartridges."
#~ msgstr "莫斯伯格公司制造的第一款枪械，一种在20世纪早期时为陷阱猎人推出的小型口袋手枪。它的四个枪管可以兼容.22 LR与短型.22口径的弹药。"

#~ msgid "The food you eat is disgusting."
#~ msgstr "你吃的食物令人恶心。"

#~ msgid "The harmful liquid is washed away."
#~ msgstr "温暖的感觉渐渐消失。"

#~ msgid "The helmet's batteries are dead."
#~ msgstr "头盔的电池耗尽了。"

#~ msgctxt "prof_desc_female"
#~ msgid "The last thing you remember was meeting God behind the local restaurant.  Then people started eating each other.  This doesn't feel like a fever dream."
#~ msgstr "你所记得的最后一件事是在当地美食广场后面和上帝谈心。然后人们开始互相吃。这感觉不像是一场狂热之梦。"

#~ msgctxt "prof_desc_male"
#~ msgid "The last thing you remember was meeting God behind the local restaurant.  Then people started eating each other.  This doesn't feel like a fever dream."
#~ msgstr "你所记得的最后一件事是在当地美食广场后面和上帝谈心。然后人们开始互相吃。这感觉不像是一场狂热之梦。"

#~ msgid "The morning ritual of the pre-apocalyptic world, created from coffee cherries through a complex process of seed removal, roasting, grinding, and brewing.  Coffee is substantially richer in caffeine than its rival tea.  With added sweetener for better taste."
#~ msgstr "曾经在世界末日前是一种早晨仪式，咖啡果经过一系列复杂的除种、烘焙、研磨和调制最终得到的饮品。咖啡比它的对手，茶含有更多的咖啡因。加了甜味剂，口感更佳。"

#~ msgid "The multi-cooker argues with you about the taste preferences.  You don't want to deal with it."
#~ msgstr "多功能厨师机和你争辩饭菜的口味表现，你根本不想理会它。"

#~ msgid "The multi-cooker boiled your head!"
#~ msgstr "多功能厨师机水煮了你的脑袋！"

#, c-format
#~ msgid "The multi-cooker needs %d charges to cook this dish."
#~ msgstr "多功能厨师机需要消耗 %d 单位电量来烹饪这道菜肴。"

#~ msgid "The multi-cooker runs away!"
#~ msgstr "多功能厨师机逃跑了！"

#~ msgid "The multi-cooker should be finishing shortly…"
#~ msgstr "多功能厨师机很快就要完工了……"

#~ msgid "The multi-cooker's got a mind of its own!  Look out!"
#~ msgstr "这个多功能炒菜机器人想要把你做成一盆大餐！小心！"

#~ msgid "The oldest and longest-produced shoulder firearm in the world.  Though it fires the weak .22 round, it is highly accurate and damaging, and has essentially no recoil."
#~ msgstr "这是世界上最古老、持续生产时间最长的枪械之一。尽管使用的是弱爆了的.22子弹，它依旧能不时爆发出精准的强力一击。更难能可贵的是，这款枪械几乎没有后坐力。"

#~ msgctxt "prof_desc_female"
#~ msgid "The school never let your club play with the really fun chemicals, the kind that make things go boom, but there aren't any teachers around to enforce the rules anymore."
#~ msgstr "学校从来不让你的俱乐部玩真正有趣的化学物质，那些会爆炸的玩意，但是现在没有老师来执行这些规则了。"

#~ msgctxt "prof_desc_male"
#~ msgid "The school never let your club play with the really fun chemicals, the kind that make things go boom, but there aren't any teachers around to enforce the rules anymore."
#~ msgstr "学校从来不让你的俱乐部玩真正有趣的化学物质，那些会爆炸的玩意，但是现在没有老师来执行这些规则了。"

#~ msgid "The screen flashes blue symbols and scales as the multi-cooker begins to shake."
#~ msgstr "随着显示屏闪过蓝色的符号，多功能厨师机开始振动。"

#~ msgid "The searchlight flares up and establishes a perimeter."
#~ msgstr "军用探照灯亮了起来，照亮了一片区域。"

#~ msgid "The shambling corpses we see all around move in discord.  Their song can be used, but for an Acolyte, this would be needlessly hard.  Be sure to carve an unspoiled living creature."
#~ msgstr "我们到处所见的那些步履蹒跚的尸体都在不和谐地移动。它们的歌仍可使用，但作为一名助手，这将是不必要的困难。一定要用未被污染的完整生物雕刻。"

#~ msgid "The skin feels absolutely turgid, oozing water mixed in with traces of a black liquid where you make your incisions."
#~ msgstr "切口处的皮肤感觉绝对肿胀，渗出的水与黑色液体的痕迹混合在一起。"

#~ msgid "The song can be woven in many forms.  Carved bone charms, weapons and armor all hold immense power, and when the time comes, me and my Kindred shall amass enough Song to restore this world as it was before.  Restore it, or end it.  Makes no difference."
#~ msgstr "歌可以被编织成各种形式。用雕刻的骨制护身符，武器和盔甲都拥有巨大的力量，当时机来临，我和我的血族将收集足够的歌，把这个世界恢复成原来的模样。要么恢复，要么终结。都没有区别。"

#~ msgid "The song is… quiet for now.  Perhaps with time, more notes will be etched in the bones of this world."
#~ msgstr "现在歌……很安静。也许随着时间的推移，更多的音符会刻在这个世界的骨头上。"

#~ msgid "The starter is now stinky and bubbly, and looks ready for cooking."
#~ msgstr "面团现在酸酸的还冒着泡泡，看上去已经准备好用于烹饪了。"

#~ msgid "The starter isn't quite ready to go."
#~ msgstr "酸面团还没发酵好，需要等一会才能用。"

#~ msgid "The water isn't too deep here, it seems to have either pooled here or risen from a pipe leaking nearby.  With a watertight container, you could gather fresh water from here.  Not safe to drink as is."
#~ msgstr "这里水不太深，但是很浑浊，含有有机质。有水密容器的话，可以从这里收集臭水。直接饮用并不安全。"

#~ msgid "The woman you mentioned - Brigitte - why isn't she with you?"
#~ msgstr "你提到的那个女人——布丽吉特——她为什么不跟你在一起？"

#~ msgid "The world may be ending, but the music plays on.  This is DJ Dustbowl, coming right back at you with Dark Days Radio, the soundtrack to the apocalypse.  Tune in for a mix of classic hits, indie tracks, and post-apocalyptic jams.  And remember people, while we may be living in hell, we at least still got good tunes."
#~ msgstr "世↑界↓可能正走向终结，但——音乐仍将继续！我是DJ Dustbowl，带着大灾变音乐专辑《黑暗之日电台》向你走来。跟我一起收听经典热门歌曲、独立音乐和后启示录时代的精彩混响。请记住，或许我们正生活在地狱，但仍拥有美妙的音乐电台。"

#~ msgid "The world seems to sharpen."
#~ msgstr "整个世界看上去都变得更锐利了。"

#~ msgid "Then you shall try again, until you hear."
#~ msgstr "那么你可以再试一次，直到你听到它为止。"

#~ msgid "There are bones to etch, songs to sing.  Wish to join me?"
#~ msgstr "有骨待刻，有曲当歌。想加入吗？"

#~ msgid "There are others who know the power the bones hold, but not all of them are my kin.  Not anymore, at least."
#~ msgstr "还有些人知道骨头中所蕴涵的力量，但并不是所有的人都是我的同胞。至少不再是了。"

#~ msgid "There is always work to be done, song to be woven."
#~ msgstr "总有做不完的事，总有编不完的歌。"

#~ msgid "There is an additional song you could take on, if you'd like."
#~ msgstr "你尚可再唱一首歌，如果你想的话。"

#~ msgid "There's a nagging discomfort in your body, making it hard to focus on anything else."
#~ msgstr "你的身体有一种挥之不去的不适感，让你很难集中注意力于其他事情。"

#~ msgid "There's been rumors.  Folks talkin' about some kind of secret lab, out in the wilds, with survivors in it."
#~ msgstr "最近有些传言。人们在谈论某个秘密实验室，在野外，里面有幸存者。"

#~ msgid "There's been some wolves that keep scaring our chickens and horses, I'd be grateful if you can kill them."
#~ msgstr "这阵子附近一直有些狼，把我们的鸡和马都给吓到了。如果你能杀掉它们，我会十分感激的。"

#~ msgid "These strange flowers have appeared in the wake of the Cataclysm, and their buds can be used for medicinal purposes, like the seeds of the mundane poppy they're named after.  The dirt around it gently churns as its roots writhe beneath the soil, and it's surrounded by an overwhelming floral smell that makes you feel sleepy."
#~ msgstr "这些奇怪的花是在大灾变之后出现的，它们的花蕾可以入药，就像普通罂粟的种子一样，它们是以名字命名的。它们周围的泥土被轻轻地搅动，它们的根在土壤下翻滚，周围弥漫着令人难以抗拒的花香，让你感到困倦。"

#~ msgid "They died when I was very young.  Car accident.  I… don't have any memories of them, but my grandmother raised me as her own."
#~ msgstr "他们在我很小的时候就死了。车祸。我……对他们没有任何印象，但祖母把我当作自己的孩子抚养长大。"

#~ msgid "They just stand there, staring into the void, with a vacant expression on their face.  Barely moving, they will probably fall to the undead horde soon."
#~ msgstr "他们呆呆地站在原地盯着空气，脸上只有空洞的表情。几乎一动不动，应该很快就会被丧尸群吞没。"

#~ msgid "They made their way to this weird spire like structure, I've never seen anything like it, it glistened in the sun like something organic.  I think they could be holding Barry there, I've seen them arrive and leave with other humans."
#~ msgstr "它们进入了一个古怪的尖塔般的建筑，我从来没见过这样的东西，就像是活着一样在阳光下闪闪发光……我觉得它们可能把巴里关在了那里，我见过它们押送着其他人进出。"

#~ msgid "They're not ready yet, you'll have to come back later."
#~ msgstr "他们还没准备好，你得稍后再回来。"

